-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[21] = {
[10500]={"Defeated Ashthrok","Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","Defeat Ashthrok","Habla con Cánnakh","Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Ashthrok, who feels no pain from the deep fires.","'Have you been to The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu?\
\
'Did you know that the deep fires imbue the evil creatures with unheard strengths? Ashthrok is one of these abominations. His feet melt sand! I shall continue my research on the why these creatures of The Rift have made their way to the surface. Be careful out there!'","'You have returned the Fire-troll to The Rift, have you?\
\
'Thank you for your help. I am making progress on my research. It seems that there are many ancient stories about Angmar that have been passed down over the years.'","Roving Threat: Ashthrok, the Fire Seeker","Ashthrok can be found somewhere in Angmar.\
\
You should defeat Ashthrok."},
[10501]={"Bring Bloodtooth's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna","'You did it? I thought you were marching to your death, but that tooth is the size of my fist, so it must be true.'","'You look like a dangerous sort. I have a dangerous job that needs doing, if you're up for a challenge.\
\
'There is a great beast to the east of Zajâna, a jázga of enormous size. She plagues our caravans and our travellers along the Great Road. Locals have taken to calling her Bloodtooth. Some say her mouth is marked in red, though stained by nature or blood I know not.\
\
'It would be a great boon to Kighân to see her defeated. She is quite formidable, larger and tougher than any jázga I've ever seen. It will take a sizeable group - more than a single challenger - to meet her vigour in combat.\
\
'Will you help us see her defeated?'","Nazâkh has asked you to hunt the great jázga plaguing eastern Kighân known as Bloodtooth. It is recommended you fight her with a large fellowship, as Bloodtooth is quite dangerous.","Bring Bloodtooth's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.","Defeat Bloodtooth and collect her mighty fang","Nazâkh has requested your aid in defeating Bloodtooth, a great jázga who roams east of Zajâna. Nazâkh says she has been seen near the watering hole of Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna.","Roving Threat: Bloodtooth Still Hungers"},
[10503]={"Defeated Droghus","Speak with Brangil","Droghus can be found somewhere in Evendim.\
\
You should defeat Droghus.","Droghus, a Gauradan spirit-caller has allied with the Angmarim, in order to find a powerful artifact within the hills of Evendim.","Brangil can be found in Tinnudir.\
\
You should speak with Brangil.","'The Gauredain across the lake are not our allies nor our greatest concern. However, the renewed threat in Annúminas has angered these mountain men. Their high chieftain, Droghus, commands their numbers. You must be careful though, he also has command over wolves as though he were a wolf himself.'","Defeat Droghus","'We Rangers thank you for your efforts. May the mountain slopes once again be quiet and peaceful.'","Roving Threat: Droghus, the Chieftain"},
[10504]={"'This is a dire situation. A Ruthless Dead by the name of Du-kalon has ventured into this Vale. No one knows where he came from and I hear his strength is unequalled. He has begun to take notice from those who followed Drugât and Nerzus. I fear he may be able organize the Dead into the army that Drugât only envisioned.\
\
'Call upon your allies to vanquish Du-kalon before we are all in danger.'","Arvaethor is in the village of Ethring.\
\
You should speak with Arvaethor.","Defeated Du-kalon","'We shall remember you for many years to come. The defeat of the mysterious Du-kalon is truly a heroic feat. It fears me to think what may have happened had he gained command of the Ruthless Dead lurking in Ringló Vale.'","Du-kalon can be found somewhere in Ringló Vale.\
\
You should defeat Du-kalon.","Defeat Du-kalon","Roving Threat: Du-kalon, the Pitiless Dead","Speak with Arvaethor","After the events in the Nimrond caverns, Ringló Vale faces continued threats, including Du-kalon, a Ruthless Dead who takes no pity on the living."},
[10505]={"Othwen can be found in Esteldín.\
\
You should speak with Othwen.","Defeated Dúrlum","Dúrlum can be found somewhere in The North Downs.\
\
You should defeat Dúrlum.","'The enemy forces occupying Fornost have angered and corrupted even the dead. Recently a powerful shade has begun stalking the Fields. The Orcs must have been searching the deepest of tombs. Now even the Orcs are afraid of the one they call Dúrlum. This spirit must be put to rest.'","Roving Threat: Dúrlum, the Disturbed","Speak with Othwen","Defeat Dúrlum","'You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. Thank you, brave ${RACE}.'","The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Dúrlum, a disturbed spirit of Fornost."},
[10509]={"Roving Threat: Gronkerna, the Juggernaut Slave","Defeat Gronkerna","Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Gronkerna, who has become corrupted by the Guaredain over years of enslavement.","'At last, Gronkerna can rest. That creature has endured a fate worse than death for far too long. No Lossoth would ever treat a Mammoth with such disregard as the Guaredain do. I hope that one day we shall put an end to the Guaredain's treachery in the North.'","Ostasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should speak with Ostasänt.","Gronkerna can be found somewhere in Forochel.\
\
You should defeat Gronkerna.","Defeated Gronkerna","'We Lossoth care for our Mammoths. They are a valuable creature for travel and protection from the Northern storms.\
\
'The Gauredain do not hold the Mammoth in as high regard. They corrupt them, raise them with hatred.\
\
'The largest of their Mammoths is Gronkerna. I warn you, this creature is deadly. Its rider can barely control the beast. Sadly this menace needs to be dealt with.'","Speak with Ostasänt"},
[10510]={"Gróthurs can be found somewhere in The Misty Mountains.\
\
You should defeat Gróthurs.","'Stone-giants have no respect for the mountains! They spend all day throwing boulders at each other while trees and animals are flattened and killed without their knowing!\
\
'One particular giant, that we call Gróthurs, has made it impossible to venture through these mountains. Could you talk some sense into that imbecile?!'","Authi can be found in Glóin's Camp in the Misty Mountains.\
\
You should speak with Authi.","Speak with Authi","Beasts of various origins have been causing problems for the dwarves in the Misty Mountains, including Gróthurs, whose endless boulder hurling endangers all mountain explorers.","Roving Threat: Gróthurs, the Stone-giant","Defeated Gróthurs","'How does a dwarf relax when a boulder flies over a peak, right at him? Well, he doesn't!\
\
'Finally, the infernal racket of that stone-giant can make way for the sounds of birds and wind. You have done well.'","Defeat Gróthurs"},
[10516]={"Find and defeat Keterang","Erchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated the Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang, and should now return to Erchar.","The vile Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang, has been sighted throughout Dor-en-Ernil and poses a constant threat to its people.","Keterang has been defeated!","Roving Threat: Keterang, Master of Spirits","Keterang can be found somewhere in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Erchar has asked you to track and defeat the cruel Haradrim sorcerer, Keterang.","'I have heard tell of a mighty sorcerer named Keterang among the forces of the Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil. It is said that he can conjure foul spirits from the very air... can such a thing be?\
\
'His whereabout are unknown, but he cannot be allowed to rally more of the Enemy's forces to his side. I would ask that you seek him out and defeat him before he can rally his men against us.'","'You have dealt a great blow to the Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'With this threat gone, it is my hope that our people will be safer in the days to come.'","Talk to Erchar"},
[10518]={"Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","'Another creature of the darkness falls. What I wouldn't give to study some of that ancient armour.\
\
'I know, it is too much of a risk as the armour was most likely forged and corrupted by an ancient darkness. I would not want to corrupt myself in the process of studying those dark metals.'","Habla con Cánnakh","Defeated Khruthakh","Roving Threat: Khruthakh, the Untiring","Khruthakh can be found somewhere in Angmar.\
\
You should defeat Khruthakh.","Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Khruthakh, who scouts these lands for a lost power.","Defeat Khruthakh","'Khruthakh is most likely a Wight of sorts. This being may be under the control of Ulkharn or some other ancient evil dwelling in the depths of The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu.\
\
'This ancient armour, animated by the darkness of Nûrz Ghâshu searches for something. If we are looking for the same object, this creature should be dealt with soon! My research continues.'"},
[10520]={"'You have done a great deed for the Lossoth. Something dark angers the Gauradan spirits. May Sûri-kylä be spared or be able to defend itself. We shall be ever watchful.'","Evil stirs in the Northern realm, including Krevchal, who leads his Gauradan tribe on violent rampages around the ice bay.","Defeated Krevchal","Ostasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should speak with Ostasänt.","Defeat Krevchal","Krevchal can be found somewhere in Forochel.\
\
You should defeat Krevchal.","'The Gauradan Chieftain known as Krevchal, is on the move.\
\
'His tribe has already murdered many Lossoth over the years. Now that he is out in the open, it is our time to strike.\
\
'I wonder if his movements are connected to these foul winds from the East.'","Roving Threat: Krevchal, the Brutal Chieftain","Speak with Ostasänt"},
[10521]={"Nimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.\
\
You have defeated the Haradrim sorcerer, Luruyak, and should now report your success to Nimithil.","After arriving with the forces at Hata Kebir, Luruyak has wandered Lebennin and sows destruction in his wake.","Luruyak has been defeated!","Find and defeat Luruyak","Roving Threat: Luruyak, Terror of Harad","'I am glad to hear that Luruyak will trouble my people no longer, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Here, I have had a suitable reward prepared for you.'","Luruyak can be found somewhere in Lebennin.\
\
Nimithil has asked you to track and defeat the Haradrim sorcerer, Luruyak.","'I have heard rumblings of a vile sorcerer of Harad who can call forth grim spirits.\
\
'True or not, he might soon rally more to his cause and soon the Haradrim could find their morale bolstered.\
\
'If you and your fellows can discover his whereabouts, I ask that you defeat him swiftly. Let us not allow him time to prove his claims!'","Talk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed"},
[10523]={"The forces of Harad have made their way to South Ithilien and Osgiliath, including Morgrish, a Half-troll who thirsts for battle.","Roving Threat: Morgrish, the Beast from Harad","Defeat Morgrish","'What news have you? Morgrish has been defeated? This Half-troll captain stood for strength within the Haradrim ranks. Though others will rise to take his place, Morgrish's defeat will set the Haradrim forces back long enough for us to strike. The Rangers are thankful of what you and your kinsmen were able to accomplish.'","'A Half-troll captain called Morgrish has led a few of us Rangers to an early death. His strength is unmatched and he is skilled with a sword, overcoming any foe with his tactical finesse. I have often seen him travelling between Haradrim camps, most likely to train and muster soldiers. If you and your kinsmen were able to defeat Morgrish it would indeed strike a blow to the Haradrim forces gathered in South Ithilien and Osgiliath.'","Speak with Nanoth","Morgrish can be found somewhere in South Ithilien or Osgiliath.\
\
You should defeat Morgrish.","Nanoth can be found in Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Nanoth.","Defeated Morgrish"},
[10524]={"Aelnir can be found in the city of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with Aelnir.","'You look weary after your recent battle. May you rest well knowing the good you have done. The people of Western Gondor owe you much for your effects to halt the Eastward march of Azruthor's forces.\
\
'I have been told that this Umbarrim man, Mota, leads this movement. This surely is a great blow to Azruthor's forces!'","Azruthor's forces venture out of Tarlang's Crown including Mota, who seeks to destroy Western Gondor in Azruthor's name.","Mota can be found somewhere in Western Gondor.\
\
You should defeat Mota.","Defeat Mota","Defeated Mota","Speak with Aelnir","'Sorcerers from Umbar hold high rank in Azruthor's forces. It seems that one of their most powerful sorcerers has been sent out to cause destruction in Western Gondor. I fear he may just be a distraction for a much more devious plan. Either way, the Sorcerer Mota should be dealt with.\
\
'I will continue to find out what Azruthor's forces are up to.'","Roving Threat: Mota, the Umbarrim Scourge"},
[10526]={"Find and defeat Render","Render has been defeated!","'I have received word of a great drake that has come down from the mountains.\
\
'It is said that he has preyed only on our goats so far, but such a beast is beyond our control and may soon bring further ruin to our lands.\
\
'Seek him out and defeat him, ${PLAYER}, before he can set flame to any of our settlements that the Corsairs and Haradrim spared. A drake of his size should not be difficult to track....'","Render can be found somewhere in Lebennin.\
\
Milonnen has asked you to track and defeat the drake, Render.","Talk to Milonnen in Ost Anglebed","'You did well to cut down that drake, for his presence filled many of our folk with dread, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I am certain it was no simple task, so take this as your reward.'","Milonnen can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin.\
\
You have defeated the drake, Render, and should now report your success to Milonnen.","Roving Threat: Render, Shadow of the White Mountains","The drake, Render, has come down from the White Mountains, striking greater fear into the already terrified people of Lebennin."},
[10527]={"Talk to Herion","The drake, Ripper, has been sighted throughout Dor-en-Ernil and poses a constant threat to its people amidst the War.","Ripper has been defeated!","Herion can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated the drake, Ripper, and should now return to Herion.","'People have spoken of a great shadow passing overhead - a winged beast beneath the murk of the sky.\
\
'Our scouts tell us it is a drake, and I would ask that you and your fellows hunt it down before it can bring any more ill-fortune to the people of Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
'We have no idea where this... Ripper... has gone, but I would ask that you search swiftly. Go, my friend, for I shall have a great reward waiting for you.'","Roving Threat: Ripper, Bane of the Prince's Lands","Find and defeat Ripper","'Ripper was of great concern to us and you have my thanks for cutting him down. Our lands were besieged by many forces, and that drake only added to our many troubles.\
\
'I shudder to think what may have happened had he set the vale ablaze. Thank you again, my friend.'","Ripper can be found somewhere in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Herion has asked you to track and defeat the drake, Ripper."},
[10528]={"Derrota a Venenorancio","'You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. You have done a great service for the Free Peoples.'","Othwen can be found in Esteldín.\
\
You should speak with Othwen.","The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Rotspittle, a diseased mountain Drake.","Defeated Rotspittle","Speak with Othwen","'Have you seen the Drakes up in the mountains? If you leave them alone they usually won't trouble you. Lately things have changed. There are tales of a Drake who comes down from the Mountains, killing large animals and men! Though I wish it were not true, I have seen some of these corpses. The skin and hair has been burnt, not with fire, but with some sort of putrid poison! Is Angmar corrupting and defiling the mountain Drakes as well?! You must take care of this corrupted Drake before more innocent lives are taken.'","Rotspittle can be found somewhere in The North Downs.\
\
You should defeat Rotspittle.","Roving Threat: Rotspittle, the Corrupted"},
[10530]={"Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","Roving Threat: Shakatrog, the Dreaded","Habla con Cánnakh","Defeated Shakatrog","Defeat Shakatrog","Shakatrog can be found somewhere in Angmar.\
\
You should defeat Shakatrog.","'That Gorthorog was a powerful enemy. I hope that your heroics have gone unnoticed by the enemy. They certainly have not gone unnoticed by me.\
\
'I was discussing The Rift with an old friend and he mentioned that the forgotten city once covered much of the land. What ever we're looking for was most likely lost ages ago.'","Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Shakatrog, who will destroy anything in his path.","'Gertheryg are ancient Trolls. I know you've dealt with Trolls before but prepare yourself if you haven't faced a Gorthorog.\
\
'Shakatrog is a brutal creature. If he finds the ancient power before I do, he will certainly wield it for the will of Sauron. I shudder to think of such things. Please stop Shakatrog from his mission and I will continue to study my old maps and manuscripts.'"},
[10531]={"The forces of Morgul Vale have made their way to South Ithilien and Osgiliath, including Shardrágh, a great siege-beast from Minas Morgul.","Speak with Nanoth","Shardrágh can be found somewhere in South Ithilien or Osgiliath.\
\
You should defeat Shardrágh.","Defeated Shardrágh","Roving Threat: Shardrágh, the Morgul Siege-beast","'Let me share with you information on Shardrágh. He is a massive Morgul-troll, as strong as the great beasts that pull the Morgul seige equipment to war. Shardrágh has been seen wandering South Ithilien then returning to Osgiliath. I am not certain to what this creature's mission is - perhaps he just awaits orders for the Morgul-host to continue its western assault. Something must be done about Shardrágh before he is able use his strength in battle over the days to come.'","Defeat Shardrágh","Nanoth can be found in Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Nanoth.","'You have defeated Shardrágh?! You and your kinsmen have done a great service to the Rangers of Ithilien and the people of Gondor. I shall not forget your deeds.'"},
[10533]={"'A powerful Angmarim sorcerer has journeyed to Evendim. Perhaps he has come to lead an attack upon Annúminas? One thing is for certain: Súnath, this powerful man of Angmar, must be dealt with.'","Defeated Súnath","Speak with Brangil","Súnath can be found somewhere in Evendim.\
\
You should defeat Súnath.","Roving Threat: Súnath, the Treacherous","Brangil can be found in Tinnudir.\
\
You should speak with Brangil.","The nefarious forces of Angmar travel to Evendim in search of powerful artifacts, including Súnath, who commands forces within Annúminas.","Defeat Súnath","'We Rangers thank you for your efforts. May we soon chase the last of the Angmarim out of Annúminas and reseal the city's ancient tombs.'"},
[10535]={"Gellamiel can be found in Ost Galadh.\
\
You should speak with Gellamiel.","Roving Threat: Thorang, the Spirit Armour","Elite lieutenants of Dol Guldur have been seen patrolling the hostile region of Southern Mirkwood, including Thorang, a spirit trapped within deadly armour.","Defeated Thorang","Thorang can be found somewhere in Southern Mirkwood.\
\
You should defeat Thorang.","Defeat Thorang","'The forces of Dol Guldur may outnumber us but our hope outshines all. You have done a great service for the Malledhrim.'","Speak with Gellamiel","'I have seen strange lights in the forest, like a storm in the night. There is a servant of Dol Guldur that wields lightning. This is no creature of the living but some sort of sorcery controlled armour. Thorang has no will of its own. It is a shell of evil-imbued metals controlled by ancient, dark magic. You must break the bond the animates this monstrosity.'"},
[10539]={"Ulkharn can be found somewhere in Angmar.\
\
You should defeat Ulkharn.","Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","'The Rogmul has been defeated?! You are indeed an accomplished warrior!'\
\
'I know not how long and deep the caverns under The Rift stretch. I can only speculate the many nameless foes still lurking down there. I shall continue my research.'","Habla con Cánnakh","Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Ulkharn, who commands this evil for an unknown purpose.","Defeated Ulkharn","'Regmyl are deadly. I am certainly not going near one! I shall leave it up to you if you want to seek out this particular Rogmul.\
\
'Ulkharn seems to be leading the others who left The Rift, but for what purpose? My research continues.'","Roving Threat: Ulkharn, the Commander","Defeat Ulkharn"},
[10540]={"'You bring with you good news and hope that once again The North Downs will be a peaceful place. You have done a great service for the Free Peoples.'","Othwen can be found in Esteldín.\
\
You should speak with Othwen.","Defeat Valikas","Defeated Valikas","'Since some of the Earth-kin have sided with Angmar, their minds have slowly warped. One Earth-kin, called Valikas, walked an even darker path. He trained with the Angmarim and now seeks to corrupt his fellow Jorkyn to the ways of the Witch-king of Angmar. There is no path back to the light for Valikas. He must be dealt with.'","Roving Threat: Valikas, the Misguided","Speak with Othwen","Valikas can be found somewhere in The North Downs.\
\
You should defeat Valikas.","The corruption out of Angmar has angered and misguided many of the creatures in The North Downs, including Valikas, whose temptation of Angmarim riches has blackened his heart."},
[10541]={"Foul, ancient evil from The Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu has made its way to the surface of Angmar, including Vélnas, who seeks a lost power buried somewhere in these lands.","Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","Habla con Cánnakh","Defeat Vélnas","'Vélnas is a creature of nameless evil from an age that time forgot. They say that this creature can look right through you and into your deepest, darkest fears.\
\
'This seer of fear must be dealt with if we are to find this ancient power before anyone else. Are you up for the challenge?'","'A horrid creature such as this nameless abomination has no right to be walking above the ground. You have done much to hinder their efforts in locating this ancient power before I figure out where and what it is.\
\
'I will continue to pour over these old stories and maps.'","Roving Threat: Vélnas, the Seer","Vélnas can be found somewhere in Angmar.\
\
You should defeat Vélnas.","Defeated Vélnas"},
[10543]={"Speak with Authi","In your absence, new threats have come to The Misty Mountains. Authi, an explorer in Glóin's Camp, seeks assistance if he is ever to finish exploring the peaks and caverns of the Misty Mountains.","Roving Threats of The Misty Mountains","Authi can be found in Glóin's Camp.\
\
You should speak with Authi.","'Greetings, I am Authi! You have come at a most fortuitous time.\
\
'I am an explorer by trade, always looking for an interesting artifact or lost treasure. Unlike many dwarves I am happy exploring the highest peak as I am happy exploring the deepest depth. You look like you could assist me. My exploration of the Misty Mountains has been hindered by some creatures on the slopes. Will you help me out?'","Authi requires assistance as The Misty Mountains are once again under threat."},
[10544]={"The Rohirrim tower Súth-torr has fallen to the Easterlings and their leaders. The guards of this tower should be defeated.","Royal Guard","Defeated an Easterling guard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Those were no ordinary Easterling guards you killed at that tower; they were the elite guard for the Nazgûl who serves as general in command in this war on the Wold and Rohan.'","Return to Guthferth, Sergeant of North-torr","Sergeant Guthferth is at North-torr just north of Floodwend.\
\
You should speak with Sergeant Guthferth.","The fallen Rohirrim watch-tower is in the north-east corner of their large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr.\
\
You should defeat the guards of Súth-torr.","Defeat Easterling guards at Súth-torr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10546]={"Después de pensarlo, Alwena cree que el reciente aumento de rufianes en Páramo Rojizo es culpable de su falta de clientela en el Salón de Artesanías.","Rufianes en Páramo Rojizo","'¡Gracias por toda tu ayuda! Mi nuevo guardia vigilará el Salón de Artesanías, ¡y con suerte este malestar que se ha asentado sobre Herne pronto pasará!'\
\
Le dices a Alwena que su nuevo guardia se parece un poco a alguien a quien enfrentaste recientemente en batalla, y ella se encoge de hombros.\
\
'Confío en que todo saldrá bien. Ha pasado página. Y si el joven Edhan pasa por aquí y se pone celoso de mi nuevo guardia, eso es solo una consideración secundaria, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Gracias una vez más. Si deseas ejercer tu oficio en el Salón de Artesanías, eres bienvenido a hacerlo en cualquier momento.'","'¿Puedes hacer algo con los rufianes de Páramo Rojizo? Con menos de esos ladrones y rateros cerca, ¡la gente se sentirá más cómoda frecuentando mi negocio!'","La sorpresa del nuevo guardia es evidente, pero luego adopta una expresión más neutral.\
\
'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:forastero[m]|forastera[f]}. No causes problemas. No querría tener que echarte. La señora Alwena fue muy clara en que este debe ser un lugar seguro para que trabajen los artesanos, y no quiere peleas.'","Tiene cierto parecido familiar, pero tal vez sea tu imaginación","'Gracias por ayudar a eliminar algunos de los rufianes de Páramo Rojizo. Mientras tanto, ¡finalmente logré contratar a un guardia para que vigile en el Salón de Artesanías! Él se asegurará de que la gente se sienta segura mientras trabajan.\
\
'Puedes ir a saludarlo, si quieres. Está justo dentro del Salón.'","'He estado pensando, y creo que el reciente aumento de actividad rufianesca cerca de Herne es en parte culpable de que la gente del pueblo sea reacia a trabajar en el Salón de Artesanías.\
\
'¿Puedes hacer algo con los rufianes de Páramo Rojizo? Con menos de esos ladrones y rateros cerca, ¡la gente se sentirá más cómoda frecuentando mi negocio!'","Habla con Alwena fuera del Salón de Artesanías en Herne","El nuevo guardia contratado por Alwena se encuentra dentro del Salón de Artesanías.","Rufianes derrotados en Páramo Rojizo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Alwena está fuera del Salón de Artesanía en Herne.","Habla con el guardia recién contratado en el Salón de Artesanías","'Oh, nunca nos habíamos visto antes, te lo aseguro. Soy un tipo respetable, por supuesto que lo soy.'","'¡Finalmente logré contratar a un guardia para que vigile en el Salón de Artesanías! Él se asegurará de que la gente se sienta segura mientras trabajan.\
\
'Puedes ir a saludarlo, si quieres. Está justo dentro del Salón.'","Se pueden encontrar rufianes por todo Páramo Rojizo, y son un peligro para la gente de la zona.","Derrota rufianes en Páramo Rojizo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10548]={"'With the destruction of the Orcs' stockpiles of blighted wood, the forces of Dol Guldur have lost a potentially terrible tool in the fight against the Malledhrim.\
\
'You have saved many lives this day, and I appreciate your courage in the face of such danger.'","Destroyed blighted wood pile (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Harchador at Mithechad","Blighted wood stockpiles may be found at Ânghum-maudhûl, south-east of Mithechad along the central road.\
\
Harchador has asked you to find and destroy the Orcs' blighted wood stockpiles.","Ruin the Stockpile","Harchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl.\
\
You should speak with Harchador and let him know that the Orcs' blighted wood stockpiles have been destroyed.","'Desperate for wood to use for spears and other implements, the forces of Dol Guldur have begun to fell trees and gather wood in the Ashenslades. The Orcs believe the wood, when used for weapons, may spread the blight that has affected the trees in the region.\
\
'Will you travel to Ânghum-maudhûl and destroy the Orcs' wood stockpiles? While there is no way to tell whether their hopes may prove true or not, there is no doubt such weapons would bring illness with them.\
\
'Ânghum-maudhûl is located on the southernmost border of the Ashenslades. Follow the central road south-east across the Ashendslades.'","The Enemy's forces of Ânghum-maudhûl have been felling wood in the Ashenslades area in an attempt to procure the blighted wood for spears and other wooden implements.","'Travel south-east to Ânghum-maudhûl and destroy the Orcs' wood stockpiles that can be found scattered throughout the camp.'","Destroy blighted wood pile (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10549]={"Recover tribute baskets stolen from the Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Roamingstar","Defeat Corsair vandals near Roamingstar's glade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","DNT - will not be seen","Ruinous Men","Recovered tribute baskets stolen from the Gilrain (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Corsair vandals near Roamingstar's glade (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'These Men repulse me, ${PLAYER}. They dishonour me and my people and cannot be allowed to hold sway over our waters.\
\
'I hope that soon all of their number are gone from these lands, and that I can return to the Gilrain in peace.'","Corsair vandals and stolen tribute baskets can be found on the outskirts of Roamingstar's glade.\
\
Roamingstar has asked you to punish the Men encroaching on her glade and dishonouring her people.","Yet unpunished for their treachery, the Corsairs of Umbar have laid waste to the lands of Dor-en-Ernil and stolen away the goods of its people.","'Although there are few that believe my sisters and I still dwell in these lands, they have always strived to care for our lands and our rivers.\
\
'These Men from Umbar... they do not honour these lands as the others do. They defile, they steal, and they dishonour and for no greater purpose than their own gain.\
\
'Soon they shall levy their destruction against my waters as well, but already they have taken from my people. Those that still believe pay tribute to me and my sisters with baskets they float down my waters... but the Men have claimed those too!\
\
'I do not know what drives them - be it greed or spite, but they must be punished for the harm done to those that honour us.'","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
You have defeated many of the Corsairs threatening Roamingstar's glade and retrieved the baskets woven for her by the people of Gondor. You should now return to Roamingstar."},
[10550]={"El rostro de este monumento está marcado por lo que parecen ser grandes marcas de dientes, como si varias criaturas humanoides hubieran decidido roer la piedra.\
\
Aunque la mayor parte de la inscripción ha sido destruida, puedes distinguir las palabras 'Ost Ardúlin' en la parte superior del monumento, y al pie la frase: 'para que podamos retirarnos de nuestras preocupaciones y hallar consuelo en tal belleza'","El rostro del monumento está inscrito con palabras desvanecidas:\
\
Duintham\
\
Fundada en el año 1249 de la Tercera Edad.\
\
'En este lugar, el Rey Celebrindor fundó la ciudad de Duintham, para que su gente pudiera cultivar la tierra y alimentar al pueblo de su reino.'","Piedra Fundacional de Ost Ardúlin localizada","Encuentra las Piedras Fundacionales restantes.","Vuelve con Istuienn para contar la historia de tu exploración.","En la portada de este libro está estampado el título: 'De Arthedain y sus Asentamientos.'La cubierta del libro está desgastada, como si muchas manos lo hubieran sostenido. Se abre fácilmente en una página doblada, que dice:\
\
'...En aquellos días, el noreste de Arthedain estaba dominado por cinco grandes asentamientos, conocidos comúnmente como las Cinco Ciudades. Estas eran Henneth Rhún, al sur de Fornost; Duintham, junto a un antiguo arroyo; Carnoglin, en las colinas del norte; Ost Ardúlin, en las tierras de lagos; y Dolindîr, ahora llamada Esteldín.\
\
'Entre los Montaraces de las Quebradas del Norte, alentamos a nuestra gente a visitar las cinco ciudades y descubrir la ubicación de sus Piedras Fundacionales. Es importante recordar quiénes somos...'","Pregunta a Istuienn sobre el Libro de las Cinco Ciudades.","'¿Así que encontraste ese viejo diario?' Istuienn arquea una ceja. 'No es costumbre que quienes no son Montaraces lo hagan, pero si deseas saber más sobre mi linaje, quizás debas emprender el viaje tú mismo.\
\
'El primero de los asentamientos mencionados en el libro se llamaba Dolindîr; hoy lo llamamos Esteldín.\
\
'Vuelve a mí después de encontrar la Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr y hablaremos más.'","Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr localizada","Ruinas de Arthedain","Encuentra la Piedra de Duintham","Piedra Fundacional de Carnoglin localizada","El rostro del monumento está inscrito con palabras desvanecidas:\
\
Henneth Rhún\
\
Establecida en el primer año del reinado de Araphor, hijo de Arveleg.\
\
'La gente se reunirá donde el comercio prospere.'","Has encontrado un libro que describe las Piedras Fundacionales de las Cinco Ciudades de Arthedain. Ahora en su mayoría en ruinas, estas ciudades son: Henneth Rhún, al sur de Fornost; Duintham, junto a un antiguo arroyo; Carnoglin, en las colinas del norte; Ost Ardúlin, en las tierras de lagos; y Dolindîr, ahora llamada Esteldín.","Habla más con Istuienn sobre el Libro de las Cinco Ciudades.","Encuentra la Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr, ahora llamada Esteldín.","Encuentra la Piedra de Carnoglin","Encuentra la Piedra de Ost Ardúlin","'Recuerda, el libro dice que las cinco ciudades eran Henneth Rhún, al sur de Fornost; Duintham, junto a un antiguo arroyo; Carnoglin, en las colinas del norte; Ost Ardúlin, en las tierras de lagos; y Dolindîr, ahora llamada Esteldín.'","Piedra Fundacional de Henneth Rhún localizada","Este antiguo monumento está bien conservado, libre de suciedad y enredaderas. En su rostro hay una inscripción:\
\
'Aquí se alzó antaño la ciudad y Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr, en el reino de Arthedain, que ya ha pasado.\
\
'En este lugar se estableció el refugio de Esteldín, por Arassuil, hijo de Arahad, para que estas tierras nunca más quedaran sin vigilancia.'","Encuentra la Piedra de Henneth Rhún","El rostro del monumento está inscrito con palabras desvanecidas:\
\
Carnoglin\
\
\
\
Fundada en nombre de Malvegil, Rey de Arthedain. Con la habilidad de Thorhaddur el Enano y su parentela fue construida esta ciudad.\
\
'Unidos en propósito, que enanos y Hombres estén siempre ligados por la amistad.'","Piedra Fundacional de Duintham localizada","'Ah, veo que has decidido comenzar el viaje. Muy bien, entonces.\
\
'El libro habla de cinco ciudades: Henneth Rhún, al sur de Fornost; Duintham, junto a un antiguo arroyo; Carnoglin, en las colinas del norte; Ost Ardúlin, en las tierras de lagos; y Dolindîr, ahora llamada Esteldín.\
\
'Has visto la Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr, ahora busca las otras cuatro.'","'¿De verdad? ¿Recorriste las cinco ciudades? Estoy impresionado; no esperaba realmente que lo intentaras.\
\
'A menudo asignamos esta tarea a Montaraces novatos, ya que las bestias que habitan esos lugares hacen que la exploración sea realmente peligrosa. Quizás los Montaraces puedan hacer más uso de tus habilidades en el futuro.'","'Esteldín fue una ciudad conocida antaño como Dolindîr. Encuentra la Piedra Fundacional de Dolindîr y quizás aprendas más sobre lo que mi pueblo fue alguna vez.'"},
[10551]={"'Another fresh recruit? Well you've come to a place in dire need of your aid, ${CLASS}. \
\
'Ever since we arrived, Angmar's forces have made a regular habit of assailing us wherever we travel. There are very few safe places to move. You're here to learn a bit about the Enemy, and I am ready to oblige, but be warned the Enemy travels the Ettenmoors largely unchecked and in great number. You will need to use caution and stealth.\
\
'North of our location, behind the safety of great dark stones, lies the goblin-village of Grothum, a vile place that sits at the east side of the Isendeep Mine, once a dwarf-mine. I need help in defeating those goblins.'","Ruins of Ost Ringdyr","Lieutenant Ingi is at Ost Ringdyr, north and east of Glân Vraig.\
\
Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn directed you to report to Ost Ringdyr to learn about the allies of Angmar's Army from Lieutenant Ingi.","Lieutenant Ingi at Ost Ringdyr may be able to tell you what you can do to support the Free Peoples in the Ettenmoors.","'Your time in the Ettenmoors will be fraught with danger. Angmar's army is bolstered by their own allies, and they are cruel and vicious.\
\
'If you make your way north of Glân Vraig and follow the valley to the east, you will emerge at the ruins of Ost Ringdyr. Inside, you should seek out Lieutenant Ingi. He is a dwarf of great repute who has come to help us. He is handling the assault on one of Angmar's allies.\
\
'To reach Ost Ringdyr, travel north along the edge of the hills and outcroppings that lead towards the Misty Mountains. You will ride through a valley for a short time and emerge on a path guarded by our people. Be wary, the woods are teeming with the Enemy.'"},
[10552]={"'Long have I desired to stand under those arches, and on those bridges. You have given me a wonderful gift on this day, my friend. You have my thanks.\
\
'There is much work to be done, but first this damnable war must be won. Let us hope that the damage from the conflicts to come are minimum. We have much to learn from those who built before.'","'Let us travel the old ways of our forefathers!'","Talk to Gori","Gori Stonesetter se puede encontrar en Amdân.\
\
Gori te ha pedido que hables con él en Amdân.","'I heard that you are heading east, towards the Kibil-nâla. I am Gori Stonesetter, Master Architect. An ancestor of mine worked to build bridges and buildings about the valley in ages past, when Khazad-dûm was still ours.\
\
'I wish to examine the nearby ruins, but I need someone with a strong arm to mind my back. If you are of a mind to help, I would greatly appreciate it.'","Ruins of the Ancestors","Talk to Gori to travel to the ruins","Gori Stonesetter can be found in Amdân.\
\
Gori has asked you to accompany him to the bridge that crosses the Kibil-nâla.","Gori Stonesetter wishes to walk among the ruins his ancestors built ages past."},
[10553]={"Talk to Órug at Leitstáth","Ir a Leitstáth","'${PLAYER}, have you seen any stone-giants about?\
\
'There were rumours that the entrance to Câr Bronach was being blockaded by a group of giants, the Grímklettar. I sent Kúzun and Órug to investigate. I believe they were planning on establishing an outpost, though I have not heard back from them in some time. If you are heading to the eastern reaches of Câr Bronach, will you relay an update of their activities to me?'","Leitstáth can be found in south east Câr Bronach.\
\
You should travel to Leitstáth.","'You must excuse Kúzun, he does not like waiting in this forsaken cold. We can barely keep the fires lit upon these wind-swept slopes. I will tell you what I know about the stone-giants in Câr Bronach.'","Talk to Kúzun at Leitstáth","Órug can be found at Leitstáth.\
\
You should talk to Órug.","Leitstáth, the small encampment of dwarves in Câr Bronach has been tasked with keeping an eye on nearby stone-giants.","Kúzun can be found at Leitstáth.\
\
You should talk to Kúzun.","'Has Mézto sent you? Bah! I wish we had something to report back. Instead we wait for the stone-giants to make the first move. There has been such little movement, one would think the giants are just that; stones, and not giants at all!\
\
'What say you, Órug?'","Rumblings From Leitstáth","Kúzun and Órug greet you as you enter the small encampment"},
[10555]={"Go to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes to the east of Kûr Anzar and search for signs of Orcs.","Return to Numûru in Urmâkh with your report","'I had feared as much. The Orcs are moving from Urash Dâr into Imhûlar. We must bolster our defences to the east before we are over-run. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. This report may have saved countless lives, you have my thanks for your brave and selfless deeds.'","You hear war drums in the distance and smell burning flesh","What remains of the river moves lazily below you","You see Orcs and Orkish weapons strewn about","Go to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes and search for signs of Orcs","Go two-thirds of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout east, towards Urash Dâr.","Go a third of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout south.","Go two-thirds of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout east, towards Urash Dâr","You see nothing but the impressive bridge before you","'Mizâdi's spies have reported an Orc camp sighted near the crossing into Urash Dâr. However, it is not just the Orc encampment nearby that concerns us. Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes, has also been seen occupied by Orkish forces. Make your way to the bridge and let us know what you find. I fear this is only the tip of the spear, and we may soon have two sets of villains and dangers.'","Return to Numûru in Urmâkh with your report.","Go a third of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout south","Make your way to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes, and scout along it. Numûru fears the Orcs are increasing in number and streaming in from Urash Dâr.","Go half of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout north","Rumblings in the East","Go half of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout north."},
[10556]={"'Has resuelto esos dos acertijos preguntándole a alguien, ¿a que sí? ¡Ya decía yo! ¡No hagas eso! Resuelve este por tu cuenta, ¡incluso si la solución requiere hilar fino y pensar con precisión!'","El acertijo restante de Rebuscón","Hunfredo Rebuscón está junto a las ruinas de Tollobel en Tyl Ruinen.\
\
Has obtenido el símbolo de la sierpe de un cofre en Tyl Ruinen. Llévalo de vuelta a Hunfredo Rebuscón si crees que es la solución al acertijo.","Hay cofres escondidos por toda Tyl Ruinen, y uno de ellos contiene la solución al acertijo de Rebuscón.\
\
El acertijo dice así:\
\
Baja estirpe de la prole de Ancalagon\
Garras afiladas y fauces de perdición.\
\
Las lágrimas de Scatha seguro fluirán al ver\
A sus hijos tan bajo caer.","'De acuerdo. De acuerdo. Un acertijo más. Este realmente pondrá a prueba tu saber. De nuevo, te doy una llave de un cofre. De nuevo, te desafío a mostrar aunque sea una milésima parte del genio de Hunfredo Rebuscón, el más sabio de los Sabios.\
\
'Entonces, eh, aquí tienes:\
\
Baja estirpe de la prole de Ancalagon\
Garras afiladas y fauces de perdición.\
Las lágrimas de Scatha seguro fluirán al ver\
A sus hijos tan bajo caer.'","La llave se rompe en tu mano","'¡Ja! ¡Sabía que fracasarías!'","El maestro del saber Hunfredo Rebuscón debe saber algo de las salamandras de Tyl Ruinen, aunque parece que está ocultando algún tipo de secreto.","'Bien. ¿Supones que has ganado? ¡Pues en realidad no has ganado! ¡Ni de lejos! ¡Nunca me vencerás! ¡No a Hunfredo Rebuscón! ¡No!\
\
'Oh, sí, bien. Las salamandras. Ah, lo había olvidado. Bien, ya que reconoces mi grandeza y prominencia entre todos los maestros del saber...\
\
'Supongo que estaría bien compartir mi secreto, ya que has demostrado tu valía... más o menos. ¡Nadie entre mil, ni entre un millón, podría haber resuelto mis acertijos! Así que escucha atentamente...'","Resuelve el acertijo de Hunfredo Rebuscón","Símbolo de la sierpe recuperado","Lleva el símbolo de la sierpe a Hunfredo Rebuscón"},
[10557]={"'Oh, muy bien. Ambos sabemos que has resuelto ese acertijo por pura suerte, pero supongo que te mereces otra oportunidad. ¿Qué? ¿Desafiarme a mí, Hunfredo Rebuscón? ¡Imposible! No estás a mi altura, ¿sabes? ¡No sería justo! Simplemente te daré otro acertijo y otra llave.\
\
Grandes y viles bestias de garras afiladas;\
Pelajes negros y temibles dentelladas;\
Rondan los bosques buscando a sus presas;\
Cuyo tormento acaba en muertes funestas.\
\
'Ese es bastante fácil, ¿eh? ¡Te equivocas si crees que resolver un solo acertijo es suficiente para satisfacerme! ¡No traje todos estos cofres aquí para revelar todo mi conocimiento a la primera pregunta! ¡Si algo caracteriza a Hunfredo Rebuscón es su determinación!'","Lleva el símbolo del huargo a Hunfredo Rebuscón","'¡Bah! El acertijo era demasiado fácil. ¡Incluso un niño lo hubiera resuelto!\
\
'Bien de cualquier manera... ¡los secretos de Hunfredo Rebuscón no son para ti! ¡No te haces una idea de la magnitud de mi sabiduría! ¡El terrible secreto de la salamandras no es para tus oídos!'","'¿Eres incapaz de averiguarlo, eh? ¡Sabía que acertaste el primer acertijo por pura suerte! Busca los cofres que he escondido por Tyl Ruinen... ¡solo uno de ellos tiene la respuesta correcta a mi acertijo!'","El maestro del saber Hunfredo Rebuscón te ha propuesto un segundo acertijo, insistiendo en que si lo resuelves te contará lo que sabe.","La determinación de Rebuscón","Hay cofres ocultos por toda Tyl Ruinen, y uno de ellos contiene la solución al acertijo de Rebuscón.\
\
El acertijo dice así:\
\
Grandes y viles bestias de garras afiladas;\
Pelajes negros y temibles dentelladas;\
Rondan los bosques buscando a sus presas;\
Cuyo tormento acaba en muertes funestas.","Hunfredo Rebuscón está junto a las ruinas de Tollobel en Tyl Ruinen.\
\
Has obtenido el símbolo del huargo de un cofre en Tyl Ruinen. Llévalo de vuelta a Hunfredo Rebuscón si crees que es la solución al acertijo.","Símbolo del huargo recuperado","La llave se rompe en tu mano","'¡Ja! ¡Sabía que fracasarías!'","Resuelve el acertijo de Hunfredo Rebuscón"},
[10558]={"'¿No puedes resolverlo? No eres ${PLAYERNAME:un maestro[m]|una maestra[f]} del saber, ¿verdad? ¡Ja! Busca el cofre que resuelve mi acertijo... ¡los he escondido por toda Tyl Ruinen!'","La ridícula petición de Rebuscón","'Sí, sí, naturalmente, lo sé todo sobre las salamandras. Soy un gran maestro del saber, ¿no es así? ¿O no lo soy? ¡Ja! Es solo una pequeña broma. Por supuesto que lo soy. Todos los Sabios conocen el nombre de Hunfredo Rebuscón. Pero no puedo divulgar los grandes secretos del saber a cualquiera, ¿verdad? ¡No, no, no, no, no! ¡En absoluto! ¿Y cómo puede Hunfredo Rebuscón saber si eres digno? ¿Cómo, me pregunto?\
\
'Probemos con un pequeño desafío, ¿de acuerdo? He escondido varios cofres por toda esta isla. Uno de ellos contiene la respuesta a mi acertijo. Toma esta llave... pero ten cuidado, ¡solo se puede usar una vez! Aquí está el acertijo:\
\
Jirones aleteantes del manto nocturno;\
Bestias horrendas que huyen del sol diurno;\
Moran en sombras, de vuelo taciturno;\
Nublan las estrellas en su viaje nocturno.\
\
No es fácil, ¿verdad? ¡Oh, no! Pero si exploras esta isla de arriba a abajo y de abajo a arriba, ¡seguro que encuentras la solución!'","El maestro del saber Hunfredo Rebuscón debe saber algo sobre las salamandras de Tyl Ruinen, pero parece que esconde algún tipo de secreto. Debe haber alguna forma de hacer que te diga lo que sabe.","Símbolo del murciélago recuperado","Resuelve en enigma de Hunfredo Rebuscón","La llave se rompe en tu mano","Hunfredo Rebuscón está en las ruinas de Tollobel, en Tyl Ruinen.\
\
Has encontrado el símbolo del murciélago en un cofre de Tyl Ruinen. Llévaselo a Hunfredo Rebuscón si crees que es la solución a su acertijo.","'¡Ja! ¡Sabía que fracasarías!'","'¿Hunfredo Rebuscón? ¿Un maestro del saber? Nunca he oído ese nombre. Quizás puedas descubrir lo que sabe... Regresa a Tyl Ruinen e intenta resolver su acertijo, sin importar lo ridículo que pueda parecer.'","Hay cofres escondidos por toda Tyl Ruinen, y uno de ellos contiene la solución al acertijo de Rebuscón.\
\
El acertijo es el siguiente:\
\
Jirones aleteantes del manto nocturno;\
Bestias horrendas que huyen del sol diurno;\
Moran en sombras, de vuelo taciturno;\
Nublan las estrellas en su viaje nocturno.","'¡Ja! ${PLAYERNAME:¡Necio![m]|¡Necia![f]} ¡Ese no es el símbolo correcto! ¡Debería haber sabido que no eras ${PLAYERNAME:un maestro[m]|una maestra[f]} del saber! Oh, espera. Ese es el correcto, ¿no?\
\
'¡Bah! ¡Solo ha sido suerte! ¡Suerte del principiante! ¡Suerte de tontos! ¡Pero no te contaré ya mi terrible secreto!\
\
'Bueno, no es que Hunfredo Rebuscón tenga un terrible secreto, ya sabes; es solo que si lo tuviera, no te lo contaría. ¿Lo entiendes? ¿Lo entiendes?'","Lleva el símbolo del murciélago a Hunfredo Rebuscón"},
[10559]={"Wegil está fuera de la puerta trasera de Snaga-maudhûl.\
\
Debes hablar con Wegil mientras avanzas hacia el este a través de la Gran Excavación.","'Los mensajeros trasgos se encuentran dentro de Snaga-maudhûl. La puerta está justo allí.'","Mensajeros trasgos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Oh! ¡Hola! ¿Acabas de abrirte camino a través de Snaga-maudhûl? ¡Eso es increíble!\
\
'Estoy aquí para ofrecer ayuda en el camino a aquellos que puedan ser emboscados por los trasgos. ¡Es un trabajo realmente nervioso!'","'He visto mucho movimiento entre los mensajeros trasgos en este campamento. No me gusta la cercanía de Snaga-maudhûl al Umbral de Durin, ni el camino hacia el Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
'¡Están observando todos nuestros movimientos y corriendo comunicaciones por aquí y por allá! Temo que muchos enanos que usen los caminos aquí perderán sus vidas a este flujo sin restricciones de información maliciosa.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que deseas apresurarte hacia el este, pero si pudieras hacerme este favor mientras pasas por el campamento, lo agradecería.'","Rumores en los túneles","Los mensajeros trasgos se pueden encontrar corriendo por Snaga-maudhûl, el campamento de trasgos en la carretera oeste de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Debes derrotar a los mensajeros maliciosos para que dejen de informar sobre los movimientos de los enanos por los caminos.","Los mensajeros trasgos han estado ocupados transportando información de un lado a otro sobre los movimientos de los enanos recién llegados a Moria.","Derrota a los mensajeros trasgos en Snaga-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra a Wegil al otro lado de Snaga-maudhûl"},
[10560]={"Rumores del Norte","Glóin explicó con más detalle los escritos encontrados en el legajo de papeles que recuperaste, los cuales mencionaban la visita de emisarios de Angmar.","Devuelve las órdenes a Glóin en su campamento, fuera de la Ciudad de los Trasgos","Glóin te espera en su campamento, justo fuera de la Ciudad de los Trasgos.\
\
Debes llevarle los documentos que recuperaste para que pueda evaluarlos.","Órdenes recuperadas","Recupera las órdenes","La Ciudad de los Trasgos se encuentra al noreste del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Glóin te ha enviado de vuelta a la Ciudad de los Trasgos para encontrar las órdenes que los uruks de Angmar llevan a los trasgos. Deberás localizar el lugar dentro de la Ciudad de los Trasgos donde los uruks se han establecido.","'Como mencioné antes, los papeles hablaban de visitantes del norte, y al principio pensé que se trataba de angmarim, como los que hemos visto arrastrándose por las colinas. Pero parece que los angmarim aquí no tratan con trasgos en absoluto, sino que grandes uruks han venido a la Ciudad de los Trasgos para forzar a los trasgos a servirles.\
\
'Vighar Trotasendas tiene una lista de nombres que los Elfos descubrieron entre esos papeles. Habla con él, y quizás pueda ofrecerte recompensas por algunos de los trasgos mencionados allí.\
\
'También quiero que busques el lugar donde estos uruks visitantes se alojan en la Ciudad de los Trasgos y descubras cuál es exactamente su propósito.'","'Más Lengua Negra. No podemos perder más tiempo, ${PLAYER}. Debemos traducir estas palabras cuanto antes.'","'¿Has recuperado ya las órdenes, ${PLAYER}? ¡Por favor, date prisa!'","'Asegúrate de hablar con Vighar antes de regresar a la Ciudad de los Trasgos. Él tiene una lista con los nombres encontrados en esos papeles.\
\
'Ten cuidado al buscar a los uruks. Cualquiera de ellos podría llevar órdenes para los trasgos, pero puede que haya uno que sea claramente su líder.'"},
[10561]={"Dardúr está en Gondamon, en Ered Luin.\
\
Se te ha indicado que busques la sabiduría del Maestro Rúnico Dardúr.","Como ${PLAYERNAME:Maestro Rúnico[m]|Maestra Rúnica[f]}, has alcanzado tal renombre que has recibido una convocatoria de Dardúr de Gondamon.\
\
Debes buscar a Dardúr para recibir más entrenamiento en tu clase.","'${PLAYER:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]}, . He oído acerca de tu destreza en las artes de la runa grabada. Somos pocos los de nuestro oficio en la Tierra Media, y temo que pronto desapareceremos.'","Habla con Dardúr en Gondamon","Reúnete con Dardúr para continuar tu entrenamiento como Maestro Rúnico","Maestro Rúnico: Significado sobre Significado","Los secretos del saber rúnico se abren ante ti. Capa tras capa de significado yace en ellos, y su poder canta en tu sangre."},
[10562]={"Márus se encuentra en algún lugar dentro de las Fundaciones de Piedra en Moria.\
\
Se te ha indicado buscar la guía del Maestro Rúnico Márus.","Márus te ha hecho llamar.","Habla con Márus en las Fundaciones de Piedra","'Le doy la bienvenida, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'He oído que buscas más conocimiento sobre la creación de runas. Bueno, has venido al lugar correcto.\
\
'Hablemos más sobre cómo podemos ayudarnos mutuamente.'","Maestro Rúnico: El Camino de la Runa de Restauración","Márus te ha convocado para continuar tu entrenamiento como ${PLAYERNAME:Maestro Rúnico[m]|Maestra Rúnica[f]}."},
[10563]={"'¿Élfico, eh? Lo siento, amigo. No puedo ayudarte con eso.'","Regresa con Regin.","Lleva los registros a Regin.","Conocedor de runas","'Sí, puedo leer un poco de élfico. Mi padre era un erudito, y aprendió muchas cosas de Balin. Me transmitió bastante de ello. Déjame echar un vistazo.\
\
'Ah, parece que fue un elfo quien encontró el filón de los enanos en primer lugar. ¡Eso explica esta escritura, y quizás también por qué los enanos de antaño nunca explotaron el filón, pues no habrían querido pedir ayuda a un elfo! Parece que estos registros hacen referencia a un mapa que debió haber estado incluido con ellos. Espero que Regin tenga ese mapa, porque los registros no son lo suficientemente detallados como para valerse por sí solos.'","Regin estará interesado en escuchar este relato.","Regin está en Othrikar, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Los registros antiguos han sido traducidos, pero aparentemente se necesita un mapa para que las instrucciones tengan sentido. Deberías regresar con Regin con los registros descifrados.","Se pueden encontrar enanos por todo Othrikar.\
\
Seguramente alguno de ellos podrá traducir los registros mineros élficos.","Busca a alguien que pueda traducir los registros mineros.","Regin no puede entender las runas en los registros mineros que encontraste. Curiosamente, parecen estar escritas en una escritura élfica.","'¡No puedo descifrar estas runas en absoluto! A menos que me equivoque por completo, creo que esto es algún tipo de escritura élfica.\
\
'Ahora bien, ¿cómo podrían haberse escrito instrucciones para una mina enana en una escritura élfica? ¿Crees que alguien por aquí podría entender este idioma?'","'¿Así que nos falta un mapa, eh? Me pregunto...\
\
'Bueno, gracias nuevamente por tu trabajo.'"},
[10565]={"'Ah, you have returned. Tell me -- are the scouts' numbers reduced?'","Maenhador seeks to disrupt the lines of communication among the Orcs attempting to assault Lothlórien.","Running Interference","Defeated Orc-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The eyes of Moria must be put out...have you dealt with their scouts yet?'","The Orc-scouts can be found running to and fro throughout eastern Fanuidhol, to the north of Talan Fanuidhol.\
\
The scouts that have accompanied the expeditionary force of Moria Orcs into Fanuidhol are quick and clever. They ensure that the Orc-leaders are well-informed, enabling them to make deadly decisions. Maenhador has asked you to put an end to them.","Maenhador is at Talan Fanuidhol, south of Fanuidhol.\
\
You should return to Maenhador with news of your success.","Habla con Maenhador en Talan Fanuidhol","'Greetings to you, friend. Are you here to help in our martial endeavours against the invading Orcs? If so, I have a small assignment for you. The Orcs frequently employ runners and scouts to deliver messages between their camps, and we will hamper their efforts to coordinate their warriors if these scouts are defeated.\
\
'If you would be so kind as to defeat a few of these message-runners, I would be much obliged.\
\
'They have been spotted patrolling throughout the eastern half of Fanuidhol, north of here.'","Defeat Orc-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have done well to disrupt the scouts' patrols, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[10566]={"Talk to Gísling at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld","'Excellent! Their defences are sufficiently weakened now...my men and I will handle this ourselves. These horrid foes will be driven from our lands!\
\
'As for you, my father wishes to speak about another matter.'","Gísling can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld, south-west of Krash-bálum.\
\
You should return to Gísling with news of your victory.","'Since your attack on the fields, the goblin riders have pulled back some of their forces to the half-orc encampment to the north-east of here.\
\
'We cannot allow them to regroup and set siege upon our crofts again. Track them and run them down. Go with haste!'","Defeated goblin riders outside Krash-bálum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gísling has noticed more mounted goblins circling Garsfeld and hopes that you can dispatch them before they are able to launch a full attack upon the town.","Goblin riders can be found circling the half-orc camp, Krash-bálum, to the north-east of Garsfeld.\
\
Gísling asked you to hunt down the goblin riders which have been raiding the crofts.","Running Them Off","Defeat goblin riders outside Krash-bálum (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10567]={"Judging by the light snow cover on the rucksack, you believe that survivors may still be found nearby. After gathering your wits, you decide to set off in search of the Byre Tor refugees.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>","Cerdic has asked you to explore the Balewood in hopes of locating the lost refugees of Byre Tor.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>","The refugees and their belongings can likely be found in southern Balewood off the eastern side of the Orc-roadway.\
\
Cerdic has asked that you venture into the Balewood now that the Warg-riders have passed. He hopes you will find some sign of the Byre Tor refugees that fled into the frozen forest.","You have stumbled upon a snow-covered rucksack in the Balewood. If you move quickly, it is possible you may find some of the refugees of Byre Tor nearby.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.</rgb>","'${PLAYER}, you must travel into the forest before more Warg-riders rally along the path.  If you find any sign of the refugees of Byre Tor, you must aid them if you can. I know not how close they have come to the forest's edge, but if you find anything -- a bag, a scrap of clothing, footprints, or even...one of their fallen -- please search elsewhere nearby.  \
\
'My men and I will hold their attention here along the road. You must go now!'","The rucksack can be found off the eastern side of the Orc-roadway in Balewood.\
\
You have discovered a rucksack belonging to what must be a refugee of Byre Tor, but the owner is nowhere to be found.","Search for any sign of the Byre Tor refugees in the Balewood","The rucksack can be found off the eastern side of the Orc-roadway in Balewood.\
\
The light snowfall on the rucksack leads you to believe that the refugee must still be nearby. You should prepare yourself before travelling deeper into the Balewood.","A small rucksack in the distance catches your eye","Examine the rucksack","You have rescued several refugees of Byre Tor, and they now take shelter in a nearby cave in the Balewood. You should speak to Húna and see if you can aid them further.","'I cannot thank you enough for your aid, ${PLAYER}. We have wandered in the cold and dark for some time now, and many of our number splintered when the Orcs and trees fell upon us.\
\
'Your bravery in aiding us, especially Léodwald, was remarkable. I know not what horrible fates would have visited us had you not intervened. The creatures that roam this forest are those of the most dangerous breeds -- you too should remain here at least for a short time lest they find you again.\
\
'This cave...it is no home of mine, but if it keeps us from harm, we shall make our camp here for now.'","Running Towards Nothing","Talk to Húna in the hidden cave"},
[10569]={"El condestable Vadosalvia espera noticias sobre la implicación de Rurik cerca del centro de Combe.\
\
Parece que Rurik Fennel ha sido un peón involuntario y acosado por los Montebruno.","Rurik Fennel, cerrajero","Rurik Fennel, un cerrajero local, vive en la carretera que va hacia el sur, pasando la posada de la Comba y la Cresta, en Combe.\
\
El condestable Vadosalvia quiere que confrontes a Rurik Fennel por las coincidencias que rodean a los bandidos del Montebruno y por el hecho de que su nombre e iniciales aparezcan en sus cajas y en las cartas que llevan.","'Aunque esto no nos ayuda a abrir la caja ni a recuperar los objetos de valor, habla bien de Rurik. Me apena que sintiera que no podíamos protegerlo... pero con lo que pasó en Archet, entiendo su duda.\
\
Déjame pensar un momento en el nombre que nos dio. Los exploradores van y vienen todo el tiempo... alguno puede haber mencionado haber visto a ese Manzaneda.'","Habla con el condestable Vadosalvia en Combe","'Ve por el camino que va hacia el sur, pasando la posada de la Comba y la Cresta, y enfrenta a Rurik sobre la carta y la caja fuerte que encontraste.'","'Por favor, dile al condestable Vadosalvia que no ayudé a los bandidos intencionadamente. No sé quién es Manzaneda, pero él tiene la llave maestra de las cajas fuertes.'","Habla con Rurik Fennel en Combe","Tras descubrir una carta en el supervisor de los bandidos en la granja del Viejo Bauman, la entregaste al condestable Vadosalvia, quien descubrió que la identidad de \\qR.F.\\q es Rurik Fennel, un cerrajero en Combe.","'Sí, me llamo Rurik. Sí, soy cerrajero. ¿De qué se trata? ¿Una de mis cajas fuertes -- recuperada de un bandido? -- ¿y una carta? Ya veo...\
\
Esperaba haber visto lo último de los Montebruno. Debes entender que no los ayudé voluntariamente. Mi negocio es mantener las cosas bajo llave, así que no suelo hacer preguntas a mis clientes. Completé un pedido de veinte cajas fuertes y, al terminar, los Montebruno vinieron a verme. Uno -- un tipo duro -- tomó mi llave maestra y amenazó mi vida si hablaba. Uno de los otros lo llamó Manzaneda.\
\
Por favor, dile al condestable que cualquier ayuda fue involuntaria, y que solo guardé silencio porque temía por mi vida.'","'Rurik es un cerrajero aquí en Combe. Deberías mostrarle ese recibo y preguntarle por qué los bandidos parecen ser clientes habituales suyos.\
\
Parece extraño que Rurik esté involucrado, es un hombre tranquilo que suele mantenerse al margen. Aun así, debemos investigar cada pista cuidadosamente.\
\
Deberías encontrarlo fuera de su casa en el camino que va hacia el sur, pasando la posada de la Comba y la Cresta.'"},
[10570]={"The trail of rust continues to the north-west...","Talk to King Thorin III","King Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have learned that Karazgar passed into the Grey Mountains in pursuit of Vethúg Wintermind. You should inform King Thorin of what you learned.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'What did you learn of Karazgar's plots in the North?'\
\
You tell King Thorin III that Karazgar has travelled into the Grey Mountains in pursuit of the wounded Vethúg Wintermind.\
\
'Hah! Let him go! Karazgar and Vethúg can bring each other to ruin. I will not involve Durin's Folk in their squabbling any longer! We have defended Erebor! We have defended our home! If Vethúg still dwelt upon the hoards of Thikil-gundu, it is there he can die with the knowledge that he was bested. The sacrifices of Dáin I and Frór have been avenged!\
\
'Now, I must put an end to my kinsfolks' wild thoughts of reclaiming Thikil-gundu....'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Trouble Under the Mountain'</rgb>","Follow the trail of rust towards the Grey Mountains","A trail of rust leads to the north-west...","The trail of rust can be found to the south-west of Ravenhill.\
\
You have discovered a trail of rust leading north-west towards the Grey Mountains and should follow to see where it leads.","Talk to Arcah","The trail abruptly ends along the path into the Grey Mountains, but a lone raven rests nearby...","Search the path into the Grey Mountains for signs of Karazgar","Signal the raven to return to Ravenhill","The lone raven can be found near the path into the Grey Mountains.\
\
You followed a trail of rust and discovered another of Arcah's ravens. You should signal it to return to its kin at Ravenhill.","'It is good to look upon you once more, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Vethúg Wintermind was a cunning foe, but his defeat was a great victory for Durin's Folk. When he fled the battle, I believe he flew for Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep, but where he has gone matters not. If his wounds have not yet ended him, they soon will!\
\
'As for Karazgar, it seems his plots have come to naught... or so he would have us believe. I received word that Karazgar passed near to Ravenhill shortly after the battle against Vethúg was ended. He moved silently among the trees, but even still, Arcah's people spied him from above and said that he made for the Grey Mountains.\
\
'Why did he not come to Erebor to claim his prey? I want to know his purpose in taking that path!'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I have tidings both good and ill.\
\
'Karazgar has gone from the North, and his followers have departed in his wake. When the battle turned, he followed the cold-drake into the Grey Mountains. Vethúg Wintermind must seek to heal his hurts in the Steel Keep of old, but he shall have little time to rest from battle.\
\
'I do not think that the strife between Karazgar and Vethúg is ended. In the mind of one who tames dragons, a weakened foe would be an easier one to break. Who can say if such things will come to pass?\
\
'Tell King Thorin what I have told you and the North shall again know peace.'","In the aftermath of Vethúg Wintermind's attack on Erebor, King Thorin III remains uneasy about Karazgar.","The raven flies towards Ravenhill, but what did it see?","Arcah can be found at Ravenhill.\
\
The raven you found may know where Vethúg and Karazgar have gone in the wake of the attack on Erebor. You should talk to Arcah and learn what it saw.","Karazgar passed near to Ravenhill when he departed the lands of the North.\
\
King Thorin III has asked you to search the lands surrounding Ravenhill for signs of Karazgar's passage into the Grey Mountains.","Óxido y escarcha"},
[10571]={"'Creo que ese ácido será lo suficientemente fuerte para revertir los siglos de daño.'","Recoge glándulas de ácido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Ansurr en Hulwul-nefekh","Obras Oxidadas","Las antiguas ruedas de agua están en gran parte oxidadas y cubiertas de hongos, lo que dificulta su movimiento.","Los gusanos luminosos se encuentran al noroeste, en las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Ansurr te pidió que recogieras glándulas de ácido de los gusanos luminosos. Con ellas, puede fabricar un aceite para restaurar las ruedas de agua.","'El ruido del agua que golpeaba las ruedas era tan fuerte que casi dolía estar aquí, ahora el agua fluye a través de ellas apenas como un goteo. El tiempo y el hongo han atacado las antiguas ruedas.\
\
'Las ruedas están en ruinas, corroídas por la herrumbre y consumidas por las esporas. Para devolverles su pleno potencial, deben ser limpiadas de estas plagas. Busca en las Obras Hidráulicas y tráeme las glándulas de ácido de los gusanos luminosos. Muchos de estos gusanos se han reunido al noroeste. Con esas glándulas, puedo fabricar un aceite que eliminará estas cosas repugnantes.\
\
'Cuando hayas cumplido esta tarea, regresa aquí a verme.'","Glándulas de ácido recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estas glándulas servirán. Esto será justo la cantidad de ácido que necesitamos, y parece que no te has salpicado demasiado tampoco.\
\
'Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}.'","Ansurr está en Hulwul-nefekh, en el centro de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Ansurr estará encantado de ver que has reunido todas las glándulas de ácido que necesita para crear su aceite."},
[10572]={"'You were able to find one of the missives? That is excellent news!\
\
'Now, let me have a look at this....'\
\
Agnar studies the missive you've recovered and compares it to a few of the Orkish orders you collected.\
\
'Ah-ha! There are many inconsistencies between the missive and the other orders, but each mentions the passage called Ushkútoz we recently discovered beneath Zudramdân. It seems that Gorgar plans to send one of his most-trusted lieutenants to Ushkútoz to oversee the destruction of Ifbar-athrâkh and the routing of the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'This may be just what we need to break the stalemate! I shall prepare a plan of attack at once!'","Ruthless and Ramshackle","Agnar Brokentooth can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh.\
\
You have collected many Orkish orders and also recovered a missive from Gorgar the Ruthless. You should deliver them to Agnar Brokentooth.","The Orcs of Gundabad carry many orders into battle, but the most closely-guarded plans of Gorgar the Ruthless are held by his trench-commanders.","Collect a missive from a Gundabad trench-commander","Collect Orkish orders in the trenches around Zudramdân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You find a hastily-sealed missive on the defeated trench-commander","Collected Orkish orders in the trenches around Zudramdân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If I have learned anything about Gorgar the Ruthless, it is that he is cunning in his misdirection.\
\
'The orders held by many of his Orcs are often partly or wholly untruthful, and they exist only to confound the plans of Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'However, my scouts have reason to believe that a few among his forces bear missives written by Gorgar's own hand, and I do not doubt them. It is rumoured that these missives are held by the trench-commanders of Gundabad, but I cannot say for certain if they all carry them.\
\
'I have a task for you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'In addition to collecting orders from the Orcs on the battlefield, you are to find one of these missives and deliver it to me here in Ifbar-athrâkh. If these missives are indeed Gorgar's will, we might learn what few truths can be gleaned from the others Orcs' orders.'","Deliver the missive and Orkish orders to Agnar Brokentooth","Gundabad trench-commanders and Orkish orders can be found in the trenches around Zudramdân in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
In addition to seeking to intercept a missive from Gorgar the Ruthless, Agnar Brokentooth has also asked you to collect Orkish orders from the forces of Gundabad."},
[10573]={"The hillside at Râkh Mathán is home to many Wargs. Their dens extend up into the hills where the beasts are bred and trained by cruel Orcs. These Wargs, and the Orcs who train them, must be cleared out if the woods of Rath Dúath are to ever be safe for Faramir's scouts.","Defeated Rukhuk","You did much to hinder the Wargs in Râkh Mathán. Those who fight for Gondor in the Morgul Vale surely thank you for your efforts.","Warg dens litter the hills of the Rath Dúath, but the wargs are not alone. Orcs have bred and trained the beasts to follow their master's lash.","Defeated wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Rukhuk","Defeat many wargs and warg-masters in Râkh Mathán.","Wargs and warg-masters can be found in Râkh Mathán in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should defeat wargs and warg-masters in Râkh Mathán.","Derrota a los huargos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Râkh Mathán: Howling Beasts","Defeat wargs and warg-masters in Râkh Mathán"},
[10576]={"'Great work, ${PLAYER}. One crisis averted but another remains. Continued threats and enemies still lurk in the cisterns. Unless the tunnels are clear of danger, I won't be able to go into the cisterns any time soon.'","Found the valve gear","Found the valve rod","Repair the main drainage valve","Repaired part of the main drainage valve (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should speak with Rathon.","Find the valve chain","Speak with Rathon","'What brings you to the end of Wellman's Way? I myself am here to see to some maintenance of Minas Tirith's under-workings. The cisterns run throughout much of the city, bringing fresh water from Mount Mindolluin to all the buildings, from the Hall of the Kings to the Keep of the Keys. Many of my workers have traded the cisterns for the wall and now work to defend the city. Do you blame them?\
\
'On my weekly inspection of the cisterns I've come to find this main drainage valve here completely broken. It was in perfect order just last week! I highly suspect sabotage, but who in the city would do such a thing?\
\
'I could use your help as various parts of the valve are missing and I think they may be somewhere in the cisterns. It is a vast cavernous series of tunnels, and a good place to hide something. If I don't fix this valve soon, the lower cisterns could flood!'","Sabotage in the Cisterns","Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and has come to find one of the main drainage valves suspiciously broken.","Find the valve rod","'You found the missing parts to the valve? Good, good! And you say some goblins were lurking about in there? This is indeed dreadful news! I shall alert the city guard to this development.\
\
'Right now, we must fix this master valve so the lower circle does not flood.'","The main drainage valve can be found outside the cisterns on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should repair the main drainage valve for Rathon.","Found the valve chain","Find the valve gear","The missing parts of the main cistern valve can be found within the cisterns.\
\
You should find and collect these parts for Rathon."},
[10577]={"They've taken him into Angar Aragín. We must save him!'","Speak with Razâl near the tower in Kûr Anzar","'Be quick, be quiet and be careful. I will see you all again soon.'","Mizâdi has asked you to accompany Razâl and Numûru on a mission into Kûr Anzar to weaken the Barkhûshim.","Sabotaging Kûr Anzar","'We need to push aside grief. It grants us nothing, and threatens everything. A Shâra's burdens will not wait.\
\
'I have need of your services once more, my friend. Razâl and Numûru have planned a raid into Kûr Anzar this night, to weaken the All-seeing fortifications and weapons, and take back some preciously needed supplies for our people here in Urmâkh. I would ask that you join them, as you can clearly handle yourself in combat.\
\
'Meet with them outside Kûr Anzar this night. The time grows near for our assault on Kûr Anzar directly. This mission will help hasten that day, ${PLAYER}. Speak with me when you are ready to leave.'","Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh when you are ready.","Speak with Razâl near the tower in Kûr Anzar.","Speak with Mizâdi when you are ready to go"},
[10579]={"Lleva las pertenencias robadas a Bahanneth en Talan Fanuidhol","Derrota a los enemigos en Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos han sufrido otra derrota a tus manos, y los Galadhrim se beneficiarán de la recuperación de las pertenencias de sus parientes.'","'Tus esfuerzos en nombre de mis compañeros guardianes de la marcha son encomiables, ${PLAYER}, pero, ay, los Orcos de Moria continúan saliendo del Foso Oscuro y mis parientes continúan pereciendo en la Tierra Media.\
\
'Debo pedirte que te aventures una vez más en Bolg Maufulug y derrotes al enemigo allí. Si encuentras más pertenencias robadas a los Elfos caídos, por favor tráelas también, para que puedan ser devueltas a las familias de los perdidos.\
\
'Bolg Maufulug se encuentra al oeste y un poco al norte de aquí. Cualquier cosa que traigas de vuelta será muy apreciada.'","'¿No has hecho lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? Hay muchos Orcos que derrotar y muchas pertenencias robadas que recuperar en Bolg Maufulug.'","Bolg Maufulug se encuentra al oeste y un poco al norte de Talan Fanuidhol.\
\
Bahanneth te ha pedido que entres en Bolg Maufulug y derrotes a los Orcos allí. También te ha pedido que recojas cualquier pertenencia robada que encuentres.","Los Orcos de Moria han comenzado a reunirse en Fanuidhol para prepararse para asaltar Lothlórien.","Bahanneth está en Talan Fanuidhol, al este y un poco al sur de Bolg Maufulug.\
\
Debes regresar a Bahanneth con las pertenencias robadas que recuperaste y las noticias de tu victoria contra los Orcos.","Cajas de pertenencias robadas recogidas en Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enemigos derrotados en Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saquear Bolg Maufulug","Recoge cajas de pertenencias robadas en Bolg Maufulug (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los Galadhrim estarán agradecidos por cualquier ayuda que nos puedas brindar contra los Orcos de Moria. Cualquier pertenencia robada que puedas recuperar para nosotros también será muy apreciada.'"},
[10580]={"Saqueando Drûmaudhul","Lleva las pertenencias robadas a Bahanneth en Talan Fanuidhol","Bahanneth está en Talan Fanuidhol, al sureste de Drûmaudhul.\
\
Debes regresar a Bahanneth con las pertenencias robadas que recuperaste y las noticias de tu victoria contra los Orcos.","'¿No has hecho lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? Hay muchos Orcos que derrotar y muchas pertenencias robadas que recuperar en Bolg Maufulug.'","Derrota a trasgos, Orcos y Huargos en Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Orcos de Moria han comenzado a reunirse en Fanuidhol para prepararse para asaltar Lothlórien.","'Tus esfuerzos en nombre de mis compañeros guardianes son encomiables, ${PLAYER}, pero, ay, los Orcos de Moria continúan saliendo del Foso Oscuro y mis parientes continúan pereciendo en la Tierra Media.\
\
'Debo pedirte que te aventures una vez más en Drûmaudhul y derrotes al enemigo allí. Si encuentras más pertenencias robadas a los Elfos caídos, por favor tráelas también, para que puedan ser devueltas a las familias de los perdidos.\
\
'Drûmaudhul se encuentra al noroeste de aquí. Cualquier cosa que traigas de vuelta será muy apreciada.'","Drûmaudhul se encuentra al noroeste de Talan Fanuidhol.\
\
Bahanneth te ha pedido que entres en Drûmaudhul y derrotes a los Orcos allí. También te ha pedido que recojas cualquier pertenencia robada que encuentres.","Recoge cajas de pertenencias robadas en Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos han sufrido otra derrota a tus manos, y los Galadhrim se beneficiarán de la recuperación de las pertenencias de sus parientes.'","Cajas de pertenencias robadas recogidas en Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enemigos derrotados en Drûmaudhul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los Galadhrim estarán agradecidos por cualquier ayuda que nos puedas brindar contra los Orcos de Moria. Cualquier pertenencia robada que puedas recuperar para nosotros también será muy apreciada.'"},
[10581]={"Lleva las pertenencias robadas a Bahanneth en Talan Fanuidhol","'¿No has hecho lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? Hay muchos Orcos que derrotar y muchas pertenencias robadas que recuperar en Bolg Maufulug.'","Los Orcos de Moria han comenzado a reunirse en Fanuidhol para prepararse para asaltar Lothlórien.","Bahanneth está en Talan Fanuidhol, al sureste de Mokûrz Gundul.\
\
Debes regresar a Bahanneth con las pertenencias robadas que recuperaste y las noticias de tu victoria contra los Orcos.","Mokûrz Gundul se encuentra al noroeste de Talan Fanuidhol.\
\
Bahanneth te ha pedido que entres en Mokûrz Gundul y derrotes a los Orcos allí. También te ha pedido que recojas cualquier pertenencia robada que encuentres.","Recoge cajas de pertenencias robadas en Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los enemigos en Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Enemigos derrotados en Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cajas de pertenencias robadas recogidas en Mokûrz Gundul (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Saqueando Mokûrz Gundul","'Tus esfuerzos en nombre de mis compañeros guardianes son encomiables, ${PLAYER}, pero, ay, los Orcos de Moria continúan saliendo del Foso Oscuro y mis parientes continúan pereciendo en la Tierra Media.\
\
'Debo pedirte que te aventures una vez más en Mokûrz Gundul y derrotes al enemigo allí. Si encuentras más pertenencias robadas a los Elfos caídos, por favor tráelas también, para que puedan ser devueltas a las familias de los perdidos.\
\
'Mokûrz Gundul se encuentra al noroeste de aquí. Cualquier cosa que traigas de vuelta será muy apreciada.'","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos han sufrido otra derrota a tus manos, y los Galadhrim se beneficiarán de la recuperación de las pertenencias de sus parientes.'","'Los Galadhrim estarán agradecidos por cualquier ayuda que nos puedas brindar contra los Orcos de Moria. Cualquier pertenencia robada que puedas recuperar para nosotros también será muy apreciada.'"},
[10582]={"Bahanneth está en Talan Fanuidhol, al este y un poco al sur de Nardur-stazg.\
\
Debes regresar a Bahanneth con las pertenencias robadas que recuperaste y las noticias de tu victoria contra los Orcos.","Lleva las pertenencias robadas a Bahanneth en Talan Fanuidhol","Saqueando Nardur-stazg","'¿No has hecho lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}? Hay muchos Orcos que derrotar y muchas pertenencias robadas que recuperar en Bolg Maufulug.'","Los Orcos de Moria han comenzado a reunirse en Fanuidhol para prepararse para asaltar Lothlórien.","Nardur-stazg se encuentra al noroeste de Talan Fanuidhol.\
\
Bahanneth te ha pedido que entres en Nardur-stazg y derrotes a los Orcos allí. También te ha pedido que recojas cualquier pertenencia robada que encuentres.","Derrota a los enemigos en Nardur-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cajas de pertenencias robadas recogidas en Nardur-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Tus esfuerzos en nombre de mis compañeros guardianes son encomiables, ${PLAYER}, pero, ay, los Orcos de Moria continúan saliendo del Foso Oscuro y mis parientes continúan pereciendo en la Tierra Media.\
\
'Debo pedirte que te aventures una vez más en Nardur-stazg y derrotes al enemigo allí. Si encuentras más pertenencias robadas a los Elfos caídos, por favor tráelas también, para que puedan ser devueltas a las familias de los perdidos.\
\
'Nardur-stazg se encuentra al noroeste de aquí. Cualquier cosa que traigas de vuelta será muy apreciada.'","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos han sufrido otra derrota a tus manos, y los Galadhrim se beneficiarán de la recuperación de las pertenencias de sus parientes.'","Recoge cajas de pertenencias robadas en Nardur-stazg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los Galadhrim estarán agradecidos por cualquier ayuda que nos puedas brindar contra los Orcos de Moria. Cualquier pertenencia robada que puedas recuperar para nosotros también será muy apreciada.'"},
[10583]={"This ornamented wooden ox would seem to be a shrine of some kind.\
\
Perhaps one of the Rangers of the Grey Company will know more about it.","Talk to a Ranger at Echad Idhrenfair","You found an ornamented wooden ox in the wilds of the Gloomglens. Perhaps it was intended to be a shrine of some kind.","Sacred Bull","'The Algraig herdsmen we encountered in the Windfells are of a tribe called the Uch-lûth -- the Clan of the Ox -- who dwell in Nan Laeglin. It does not seem strange to me that they might worship the oxen, as that is their namesake, but it does seem strange that such a shrine should be found in these forsaken woods, so far north and west of their grazing fields.\
\
'What is more, you tell me that this shrine appears to be in pristine condition, as though it has been visited and cared for recently...perhaps a hermit lives nearby?'","There are Rangers at Echad Idhrenfair to the south-west of the shrine.\
\
You should ask one of the Rangers of the Grey Company about the ox-shrine you discovered."},
[10584]={"Ofrenda a la Corona de Hierro","'Ten, estas son las armas rotas que me trajiste. Lleva los fragmentos y colócalos en los altares repartidos por todo Himbar. Los altos sacerdotes de los Angmarim utilizan estas capillas para honrar al Señor Oscuro de Mordor.\
\
'Con este gesto propinaremos un golpe a su moral y daremos a nuestros amigos el tiempo que necesitan para moverse hacia el norte. Encontrarás a los Angmarim y sus altares repartidos por Himbar.'","'Has derrotado a muchos Angmarim, y eso está bien. Ahora, muestra al resto tu maestría en la batalla colocando las armas rotas en sus altares.'","'Gracias por ayudarnos. Quizá todavía haya esperanza y podamos ganar esta guerra. Los Angmarim se han retirado por el momento, pero temo que pronto recuperen sus fuerzas y se reagrupen.\
\
'Debemos actuar todo lo rápidamente que podamos. Debemos golpearles allí donde residen.'","Los Angmarim, siervos del Señor Oscuro, amenazan a los Montaraces de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Tras haber robado sus armas, debes devolver sus fragmentos a los altares Angmarim para demostrarles tu fuerza.","Coloca las armas capturadas en los altares (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Los Montaraces de Gath Forthnír te esperan en su campamento al este de Carn Dûm.\
\
Has quebrado la moral de los Angmarim con tu demostración de fuerza y determinación. Pasará un tiempo antes de que recuperen su voluntad de luchar.","Los altares de los Angmarim pueden encontrarse por todo Himbar, cerca del camino o dentro de los campamentos Angmarim.\
\
Areneth te ha dicho que una muestra de fuerza podría quebrar el espíritu de los Angmarim leales a Mordor. Te ha pedido que coloques las armas capturadas en los altares de los Angmarim, en señal de intimidación."},
[10586]={"'I must ask your help once more, ${CLASS}. I dare not let Witherbreca out of my sight, but as you can see, she has lost both her saddle and her shoes. Would you ask the people in Ost Rimmon and see if they have any to spare?\
\
'There is a blacksmith here who might have horseshoes. I would begin with him.'","Saddle and Shoes","Gathered deer hide (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dringrod doesn't have any horseshoes or iron to make them. He suggested you gather abandoned tools from the quarry at the back of Ost Rimmon, which he can melt and forge into shoes.","'The quarry is at the far end of Ost Rimmon, opposite the stables from whence you came. Bring back a good handful of the tools that have been left around there, and I'll forge you those horseshoes.'","Return to Bargwen","Gather deer hides (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should go speak with Sithgar now that a saddle and shoes are being provided for his horse.","Talk to Bargwen in Ost Rimmon about acquiring a new saddle.","'Yes, I think the blacksmith is the best place to start. With any luck, he'll have the horseshoes at the ready.'","Return to Sithgar","Gathered abandoned tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You've got them, then? I'll forge them up and shoe the horse myself. Don't you worry.\
\
'Now, the lad will need a saddle, too? Bargwen might help him with that. If we haven't any, she is handy with leather and will work him a new one. She's easy enough to find. You went right by her on your way to the quarry.'","Find the blacksmith in Ost Rimmon and see if he can provide Sithgar with shoes for Witherbreca.","'These hides are good. Well hunted, ${RACE}. I will get this done with as soon as I can. Now leave me to my work.'","Talk to Bargwen","'Look, ${PLAYER}! Witherbreca is fit to ride. Pray only that I am fit to keep her by me from here on out. I must ride - but if you should catch up with the host of Rohan before we reach the Pelennor, seek me there and I shall give you a warm welcome among my own people.'","You should return to Dringrod with the quarry tools you have gathered, so that he can forge them into horseshoes.","'Bargwen should be able to set the young rider up with a saddle, one way or another. Head towards the quarry and you'll find her.'","You should gather deer hides from the deer that can be found by the Firien Wood, in the western Beacon Hills, so that Bargwen can craft a saddle for Sithgar.","'A saddle? Do I look like a stable-hand to you? Just because Dringrod never wants to do a thing but work unpaid and unbidden doesn't mean he can make others do so.\
\
'Besides, you will find nary a saddle in Ost Rimmon, I happen to know.\
\
'Fine! I will make you one, but I will need good leather. We have not any of that either, so you will need to hunt some of the deer found near the Firien Wood.'","Talk to the blacksmith","Help Sithgar reshoe and saddle his unruly horse.","Bring the deer hides back to Bargwen in Ost Rimmon, so that she can craft a saddle for Sithgar.","Return to Dringrod","Gather abandoned tools (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Deer aplenty can be found by the Firien Wood, west of here. Bring me some hides and I suppose I will make a saddle to be rid of this young rider of Rohan.'","'Horseshoes? No, I have none. But if it is for that poor boy from Rohan, I could make him some. Hum! I am short of iron, as well. Why don't you go to the quarry, which is far at the back of Ost Rimmon, and gather some of the tools that were abandoned there. They are beginning to rust and we can put them to better use.'"},
[10587]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}, there remains another matter for us to discuss.\
\
'My apprentice's disappearance is quite concerning, but so too was the loss of my stock. When I awoke the other morn, they had all gone from my stables. If someone thought this a cruel prank, I know not, but they must have been spooked for their tracks away from Middlemead appear to have been made in a frenzy. \
\
'If you would, search the fields to the south. I am sure some haven't travelled far, and it would mean a great deal to me if they were returned to my keeping.'","Found and returned wayward horses to Déorwald (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find and return wayward horses to Déorwald (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horses can be found wandering among the trees and fields to the south of Middlemead.\
\
Déorwald has asked for your aid in recovering his stock. You should find his wayward horses and ride them back to his tent in Middlemead.","Saddled with the Stock","Déorwald struggles to locate his stock after all of his horses were frightened away from their stables in Middlemead.","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. While this is not all of them, it is certainly enough to reopen my shop.\
\
'Curious though, that the only ones you could find were pale of coat. I wonder what has become of the rest...'","Talk to Déorwald","Déorwald can be found in Middlemead at the traders' pavillion.\
\
You have returned many of Déorwald's wayward horses to his keeping. You should now speak to him.","'Have you located all of my horses?'"},
[10588]={"'¿Hay algo en lo que pueda ayudarte?'","Recibiste una carta de un Montaraz llamado Saeradan solicitando tu presencia en su refugio a lo largo del Camino Verde, al norte de Bree.","Entrega la nota que recibiste a Saeradan","La cabaña de Saeradan se encuentra al norte, a lo largo del Camino Verde, entre Bree y las Quebradas del Norte. Encontrarás su cabaña en un pequeño bosquecillo junto a una colina empinada, al este de la granja de Espinar.\
\
Debes ir de inmediato con Saeradan y saber en qué puedes ayudarlo.","${PLAYER},\
\
Te escribo en nombre de mi capitán, Trancos. Mi tarea es vigilar los acontecimientos aquí en las Tierras de Bree y he sabido que has hecho mucho por ayudar a la gente. Tus recientes esfuerzos en Bree llegaron a mi conocimiento cuando supe que ayudaste a un hobbit con un problema de bandidos.\
\
Tus esfuerzos contra los bandidos son admirables, y aunque hayas pensado que habían terminado, lamento informarte que aún no han acabado. Bill Helechal, un ciudadano de Bree, por interés propio pone en peligro la vida de todos los habitantes de esta tierra con sus acciones.\
\
Si quieres, haz el viaje hacia el norte por el Camino Verde hasta mi cabaña. La encontrarás al este de la granja de Espinar, entre Bree y las fronteras de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Saeradan","'Es un placer conocerte al fin, ${PLAYER}. Tus esfuerzos en estas tierras devuelven esperanza donde más se necesita. Solo espero que podamos contar contigo para más ayuda.\
\
'Debemos trabajar con diligencia para deshacer el daño que se ha causado en estas tierras. Ruego que no sea demasiado tarde para comenzar nuestros esfuerzos.'","Llamado de Saeradan"},
[10589]={"Habla con Rúdhan en Gaerond","Paso seguro a Gaerond","Habla con Onora en Gaerond","Rúdhan se siente lo bastante bien como para caminar, pero él y su esposa necesitarán que el camino hacia el norte esté despejado si quieren sobrevivir al resto del viaje.","Muchas son las bestias peligrosas que se interponen entre los refugiados dunlendinos y la seguridad de Gaerond, en la frontera norte del Ángulo del Mitheithel. Has accedido a intentar despejar un camino para que puedan llegar al campamento a salvo.","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. No habríamos podido llegar tan lejos sin ti.\
\
'Sé que aún nos queda gran parte del norte por delante y que el viaje aún no ha terminado, pero sienta bien habernos alejado tanto de los peligros que dejamos atrás. Nos aguarde lo que nos aguarde, Rúdhan y yo lo afrontaremos juntos.\
\
'Gracias por ayudarnos. Eres ${PLAYER:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} para nuestra familia y nuestro pueblo a partir de este día. No tenías por qué ayudarnos, pero lo hiciste, y por ello ambos te estamos agradecidos'.","'No, aún no he dejado el Ángulo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Siempre creo estar listo para partir, y siempre parece surgir algo nuevo! ¡Sin ir más lejos, hace un momento mis flechas han salvado la vida de dos dunlendinos que huían de alguna fechoría en el sur! Un par de semiorcos casi les clavan sus hojas en la carne, pero mi arco ha sido más rápido.\
\
'Se llaman Onora y Rúdhan. Dicen que te conocen y que te deben la vida. Dije que a mí también me la deben, pero hice la broma y me miraron con ojos asustados, así que creo que le dejaré las bromas a mi hermano.\
\
'Deberías hablar con ellos, y luego de verdad debo regresar a Imladris. ¡Pero siempre surge algo!'","'Estamos en deuda contigo, ${PLAYER}, pues el camino a Gaerond estaba casi despejado de los enemigos que temíamos, y sé que fue obra tuya. También agradecemos el rápido arco del elfo que nos recibió, aunque Onora desconfía de él. Si es amigo tuyo también lo será nuestro, con el tiempo.\
\
'A menos que sea propenso a las bromas. Entonces, tal vez no'.","Habla con Elladan en Gaerond","Elladan permanece en el campamento de Gaerond, en el Ángulo.","'Mi pierna ya está lo bastante bien como para poder caminar, ${PLAYER}, pero me preocupa el resto del viaje. ¿Dices que hay un campamento al noroeste, donde unos amigos nos ayudarán como has hecho tú?\
\
'Te confiaré mi vida y la de mi esposa ahora, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, y espero que esa confianza no esté fuera de lugar. ¿Irás por delante de nosotros y despejarás un camino hacia este campamento, este Gaerond del que hablas? Son muchas las amenazas que aún acechan por delante, y es posible que no pueda moverme lo bastante rápido como para esquivarlas. Pero, si despejas el camino, tal vez lo logremos'.","Has despejado el camino hacia Gaerond de muchas amenazas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a muchas criaturas del Ángulo y despeja un camino hacia Gaerond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Rúdhan y Onora han llegado a salvo a Gaerond, pero el futuro que se abre ante ellos está lleno de misterios y peligros."},
[10591]={"Sadreda se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío, en las Fundaciones de Piedra, al noroeste de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas.\
\
Regresa con Sadreda para contarle sobre tu victoria.","'El último paso de tu misión te llevará a un gran peligro. Creo que ese Vigilante Oscuro al que has matado no era más que un siervo de otra criatura a la que llamamos el Capitán Demente.\
\
'Reúne a tus amigos, ${PLAYER}, y dirígete a las Excavaciones Tenebrosas, al sureste de aquí. Una vez dentro, tendrás que usar este amuleto para invocar al Capitán Demente. Busca el altar inmundo y colócalo allí. El Capitán Demente aparecerá de inmediato.\
\
'Libera a Moria del mal repugnante del Capitán Demente y luego regresa conmigo.'","Salvaguarda (Opcional)","El Capitán Demente habita en las Excavaciones tenebrosas, al sureste del Refugio Sombrío en las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Sadreda te ordenó que usaras el amuleto tosco que te dio para invocar y derrotar al Capitán Demente.","Habla con Sadreda en el Refugio Sombrío","'¡Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Tus esfuerzos serán recordados por los siglos venideros.'","'¿Ya está hecho, ${PLAYER}? ¿El Capitán Demente está muerto?'","Invoca y derrota al Capitán Demente","'El Capitán Demente se encuentra dentro de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas, en las Fundaciones de Piedra.'","Capitán Demente derrotado","Sadreda ha descubierto que el Vigilante Oscuro al que mataste no era más que un siervo de una criatura aún más malvada conocida como el Capitán Demente."},
[10592]={"'${PLAYER}, te pediría una última cosa. No sería necesario si estuviera sola, pero con un niño en mi compañía, la situación es diferente. Debería haberlo dejado en Tornhad, pero el muchacho es persuasivo y le encanta escuchar las canciones de los elfos. Si nos hicieras un último acto de bondad, te pediría que exploraras el camino que hay por delante.\
\
'Hay un cruce hacia el este donde este camino se encuentra con otro que va hacia el sur. Antes se han visto huargos por allí, y me gustaría asegurarme de que no estén ahí ahora. Nuestro destino, Tham Lumren, está solo un poco más al este de ese lugar. ¿Podrías explorar el camino y asegurarte de que está libre de peligros? Cuando regreses nos pondremos en marcha.'","No ves ningún huargo, pero deberías continuar más al este por el camino","Habla con Glorfindel","Este es el cruce que describió Ivoreth","Vuelve con Ivoreth a su campamento en el Ángulo del Mitheithel y dile que el camino está despejado.","Continúa tu búsqueda más al este, hacia Tham Lumren","Continúa más hacia el este por el camino hasta Tham Lumren, vigilando cualquier amenaza que pueda dificultar el viaje de Ivoreth y Barhador.","Divisas más adelante a un elfo alto y hermoso, de poderosa presencia, que te llama","Has divisado al señor elfo Glorfindel cerca del puente de Tham Lumren, y te está llamando. Deberías hablar con Glorfindel.","Busca amenazas a lo largo del camino","Sigue el camino hacia el este en dirección a Tham Lumren, hasta el cruce a veces peligroso que describió Ivoreth, mientras vigilas cualquier amenaza que pueda dificultar su viaje.","'¡Saludos y ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]}, ! Vengo recientemente de la Casa de Elrond y me dijeron que podría encontrarme contigo en Haudh Erthaid.'\
\
Su voz es musical y sus ojos brillan con una alegría que llena tu corazón.\
\
'Es bueno que estés aquí, ¡ya que puedes aligerar mis cargas! Estoy vigilando las fuerzas del Enemigo a lo largo de los caminos que rodean Rivendel para cuando nuestros amigos mutuos elijan partir.\
\
'¿También estás salvaguardando este camino? Entonces siento que no necesito repetir lo que ya has hecho, y ahora puedo dirigirme hacia el este del Bruinen. ¡Gracias, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}!'","Ivoreth está preocupada por la seguridad de Barhador mientras viajan hacia el este rumbo a Tham Lumren y te ha pedido que explores el camino que hay por delante.","Le dices a Ivoreth que el camino es seguro y que te encontraste con el señor elfo Glorfindel a las afueras de Tham Lumren.\
\
'¡Oh, son unas noticias excelentes! ¡Sin duda estaremos a salvo! Gracias, ${PLAYER}, por todo lo que has hecho por nosotros. Que te vaya bien en el resto de tus viajes, por muy oscuros que sean los tiempos que se avecinan.'","Vuelve con Ivoreth a su campamento","Salvaguardar el paso"},
[10594]={"Gathered people of Entwade (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Gather people of Entwade (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Léoflad can be found near the waggons outside the Mead Hall of Entwade.\
\
You have spoken to numerous groups of people in Entwade and have sent them to gather at Léoflad's side. You should now speak to Léoflad and inform her that her people are ready.","The people of Entwade can be found throughout the settlement.\
\
Léoflad has sent you to gather the people of Entwade in hopes that they can soon depart for the Eastfold.","Léoflad, wife of Thane Edric, seeks to lead her people south to Eastfold where they will seek safety in the settlement of Aldburg.","Safety for the Meek","DNT -- Will not be seen","'Ho, traveller. Edric has sent you to me? Good, perhaps now we shall be able to depart in some timely manner.\
\
'It has been a great undertaking to uproot the people of Entwade, ${PLAYER}. At my husband's request, I shall aid in escorting them to safety in Aldburg to the south. Many have packed for weeks now, but we cannot afford to wait any longer. I protested when Edric bade me stay in Aldburg as well, but if I cannot return to Kingstead, then I shall aid the people of the Eastfold during my stay. Truly, they face great troubles as well.\
\
'As for you, my people are as ready as they likely ever will be. Would you do me a great favour and bid them all join me here?'","Talk to Léoflad","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You allowed me a chance to finish with other preparations, and now, it appears that everyone is here!\
\
'Keeping them at my side will likely prove more challenging, but worry not, ${PLAYER}, for I have handled far worse!'"},
[10602]={"Usa el Buscador de Instancias para entrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad.","Entra en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad","'Una cara nueva. Debes ser la última víctima de Lágsaith, o lo serás pronto. Ella suele guardar sus relatos dramáticos para los niños, pero incluso los viajeros de paso no se salvarán.\
\
'La expedición a las alcantarillas no fue tan emocionante como ella lo hace parecer. Ella omite por completo los \\qmomentos aburridos,\\q como ella los llamaría, por el bien de un \\qmejor ritmo narrativo.\\q Por lo tanto, se olvida de mencionar la inmundicia que quemamos en el camino.\
\
'Los niños deberían saber que la infección y la plaga no es un asunto para tomar a la ligera. Asegúrate de que Lágsaith tampoco lo olvide.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas.</rgb>","La falta de interés de Lágsaith en mencionar los peligros sanitarios de las alcantarillas molesta a Avlath.","'¿Lágsaith mencionó la inmundicia esta vez? Entonces estoy satisfecho. No quería sonar tan duro antes, pero ella ejerce poder con sus palabras, poder que puede ser usado para el bien.\
\
Que su historia recuerde a los niños que deben mantenerse saludables, porque los seguidores de la Corona de Hierro no son las únicas amenazas a las que nos enfrentamos.'","Lágsaith ha contado, con detalles atroces, la asquerosa inmundicia que ella y sus camaradas encontraron en las alcantarillas.\
\
Debes contárselo a Avlath en Bail Avarc.","Montones de inmundicia no identificable se pueden encontrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas.'\
\
Debes destruirlos.","Sagroth: La atención a los detalles","Habla con Avlath en Bail Avarc","Inmundicia no identificable destruida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destruye la inmundicia no identificable (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10603]={"Usa el Buscador de Instancias para entrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad.","Muestras de líquido fétido recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lágsaith ha descrito con gran detalle el líquido fétido que corre por las alcantarillas.\
\
Debes contárselo a Náchtan en Bail Avarc.","Entra en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad","'Eres un viajero, ¿no? ¿Has visto algo así antes?' Él muestra unas frascos de líquido viscoso y violentamente verde.\
\
'La Corona de Hierro no mantenía bien sus alcantarillas. Recogimos muestras de allí para estudiarlas más a fondo, pero Eávair y Borgach -- Él asiente hacia las dos mujeres cercanas que están en profunda discusión. -- todavía están averiguando cómo descomponerlo y limpiarlo. Estas impurezas deben estar dañando la tierra de maneras que no entendemos.\
\
'Lágsaith adora narrar nuestra expedición, aunque no se detiene en los detalles. Las historias que se transmiten de boca en boca pueden cubrir distancias mayores que las que nosotros mismos podemos viajar. Si ella describiera el líquido fétido a más viajeros como tú, alguien con nueva información podría presentarse y ayudarnos en nuestros esfuerzos.\
\
'Si la buscas para conocer el relato completo, asegúrate de recordarle esto.'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas.</rgb>","Un líquido fétido se encuentra en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas'.\
\
Debes recoger algunas muestras.","Mientras Eávair y Borgach intentan resolver el problema de la limpieza de las alcantarillas, Náchtan dirige sus esfuerzos hacia la difusión de información y, con suerte, obtener algunas respuestas.","'Me alegra escuchar que Lágsaith ha honrado tu solicitud. Tal vez eventualmente cuente estos detalles por sí misma, sin necesidad de recordatorios. Mientras tanto, Eávair y Borgach harán lo que puedan, mientras yo mantengo un oído atento.'","Habla con Náchtan en Bail Avarc","Recoge muestras de líquido fétido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sagroth: Probando las Aguas"},
[10604]={"Usa el Buscador de Instancias para entrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad.","Entra en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad","El diseño de las alcantarillas de Carn Dûm es un desastre. El mapa de Aighrig está en progreso, pero también podría ayudarte a visualizar mejor la historia de Lágsaith.","Encuentra los puntos de cartografía (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Aighrig en Bail Avarc","Puntos de cartografía se pueden encontrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas.'\
\
Debes encontrarlos para completar el mapa de las alcantarillas.","Puntos de cartografía encontrados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Después de nuestras aventuras en el este, es extraño verte aquí en mi tierra natal, ${PLAYER}. Pero eres una visita bienvenida.'\
\
Lukhag emite un chirrido de afirmación.\
\
'Estoy segura de que Lágsaith desea contarte la historia de nuestra expedición, así que no te retendré por mucho tiempo. Pero quizás el conocimiento del diseño de las alcantarillas te permita apreciar más su relato.' Ella te entrega un mapa que ha sido dibujado a mano con cuidado. 'Rastreé nuestros pasos mientras estábamos allí abajo. Lágsaith nunca admitiría esto, pero necesitaba ayuda; su sentido de la orientación es atroz.\
\
Puedes tomar prestado el mapa hasta que Lágsaith termine su relato.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas.</rgb>","Sagroth: Teatro de la Mente","'¿Confías en que el mapa te ayudó? Es rudimentario, sin duda, pero también útil. Sin él, podríamos habernos perdido para siempre.' Una pequeña sonrisa se dibuja en el rostro serio de Aighrig. 'Bromeo. Pero regresar a casa habría sido más difícil.\
\
'El mapa solo muestra una fracción del sistema completo de alcantarillas. Espero que podamos completarlo en futuras expediciones. Después de todo, todavía queda mucho trabajo por hacer.'","Gracias al mapa de Aighrig, el relato de Lágsaith se volvió un poco menos confuso de seguir.\
\
Debes devolver el mapa a Aighrig en Bail Avarc."},
[10605]={"Collect Círgon's model ship of Umbar from his cart","Círgon's cart can be found near the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.\
\
Círgon has offered to let you place one of his ships into the Baths.","Círgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.\
\
You have arrived at the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.","Círgon spends his days sailing the model ships he built with his father, but has become withdrawn from his family in his father's absence.","The Baths of Belecthor can be found to the north in the Fourth Circle.\
\
You have picked up one of Círgon's ships and should now place it in the Baths.","Mílien can be found outside her home in the Fourth Circle.\
\
Círgon has asked you to tell his mother that he will come home for supper once he finishes packing up his ships.","Sailing into Memory","Talk to Mílien","'You made it!\
\
'${PLAYER}, I left one of the ships for you! Would you like to set it in the Baths? You can if you want.\
\
'It'd be great to have someone else here to share in the fun!'","The ship of Umbar is of impressive size and detail for a model...","Meet Círgon at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle","'Look how they float, ${PLAYER}! Father and I built them together, you know. He did most of the work, but I built a lot of the little details. See the tiny Corsair on that one?\
\
'I wonder what it would be like to sail on a real ship. Father said he'd take me to Pelargir someday soon, but I don't know when he'll be home. My uncle, Ristagír, isn't as fond of rivers and seas as Father and me, but he's a skilled craftsman all the same. Don't you see? It runs in my family, ${PLAYER}. I want to be a wood-worker and warrior just like my father!\
\
'Mother wanted me to come home, yes? I'd be glad if you could join us for supper. Allow me a few minutes to pack up my ships and I'll meet you at our house!'","Place the model ship of Umbar in the Baths' waters","Talk to Círgon","'Father and I used to sail our ships every day - they're a little big for the Baths, but it hasn't stopped us yet! \
\
'If you want to join me this time, I'll meet you up in the Fourth Circle by the Baths of Belecthor. It's the big fountain by the bridge to the cisterns - I'm certain you can figure it out.\
\
'The sooner we set sail, the sooner I'll go home - deal? Come on, it'll be fun!'","Círgon is standing near the Baths, where a model ship of Gondor now floats calmly...","The Baths of Belecthor can be found in the northern part of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Círgon has asked you to join him at the Baths of Belecthor where he sails his model ships.","Círgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle.\
\
You have set down the ship in the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.","'You convinced him to hurry home?\
\
'Oh, thank you - thank you!'","The ship floats gently in the waters of the Baths..."},
[10607]={"Las Obras Hidráulicas están muy al suroeste de las Fundaciones de Piedra, en Moria.\
\
Debes matar a muchos gusanos en las Obras Hidráulicas y recoger sus glándulas acre. Cuando tengas suficientes, regresa con Dithrik en las Fundaciones de Piedra.","Adquiere glándulas de gusano luminiscente (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Glándulas de gusano luminiscente adquiridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Echar sal a la herida","'¿Asqueroso, dices? Nunca dije que manejar cosas procedentes de las raíces antiguas de la tierra fuera a oler a margaritas. Si deseas trabajar con olores más agradables, ¡ve con los elfos! Tal vez alguna doncella élfica necesite ayuda para encontrar una flor favorita.\
\
'No, ese trabajo no es para ti ni para mí. Somos Guardianes, firmes y verdaderos. No tememos la oscuridad ni apartamos la nariz ante los olores enfermizos, no cuando hay muros que sostener o buena gente en peligro. Ahora apresurémonos, antes de que pierdan su potencia...'","Regresa con Dithrik en las Fundaciones de Piedra","'Has hecho bien en llegar tan lejos, ${PLAYER}, y en el camino me has dejado sin palabras. Ahora, veamos nuestros preparativos finales antes de enviarte a enfrentar uno de los más antiguos horrores de Moria.\
\
'Las glándulas de los gusanos que se deslizan por las Obras Hidráulicas desprenden un aroma extraño que, según se ha visto, atrae la atención del enemigo. Un pobre enano de la expedición lo descubrió por desgracia cuando ya era demasiado tarde. Si deseas atraer a la criatura ancestral, las cabezas que me conseguiste necesitarán añadirse a las glándulas de estos gusanos luminosos.\
\
'Ve ahora a las Obras Hidráulicas y mata a los gusanos luminosos que infestan ese lugar. Cuando hayas conseguido suficientes, vuelve a mí rápidamente y completaremos tus preparativos finales.'","Dithrik te ha pedido reunir glándulas de gusanos que se encuentran por todas las Obras Hidráulicas.","'Asegúrate de traerme suficientes glándulas de los gusanos que infestan las Obras Hidráulicas. Sin ellas, nuestro cebo no estará completo.'"},
[10608]={"Completa 'Diversión en la feria (intro)'","Cada año se celebra el Festival de la Feria Agrícola para celebrar los largos días y la abundancia del clima cálido. ¡Participa en las festividades para ayudar a difundir el buen ánimo!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>(Hay doce días de misiones de participación en 'Un día soleado de feria' y 'Diversión en la feria'. ¡Planifica en consecuencia!)</rgb>","Completa 'Diversión en la feria (intermedia)'","Puedes encontrar a Campanula Redondo cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta, en La Comarca.\
\
Ve a hablar con Campanula Redondo.","Habla con Campanula Redondo","'¡Dios mío, ciertamente has dado todo de ti este año! Gracias a todo tu arduo trabajo, el festival se llevó a cabo sin problemas.\
\
'¡Espero verte el próximo año, cuando tendré un conjunto completamente nuevo de regalos listos para ti!'","'¡Te doy la bienvenida!\
\
'Si estás aquí para el Festival de la Feria Agrícola, te recomendaría que mires alrededor y participes en muchas de las divertidas actividades que hay por aquí. ¡Si no estás aquí para la Feria Agrícola, tal vez deberías estarlo!\
\
'Para aquellos que participen en muchas de nuestras actividades, podría haber una recompensa esperándote, así que ¡sal ahí!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: esta misión no se puede cancelar.</rgb>","Saludos a los días de la feria","Completa 'Diversión en la feria (final)'","Cada día hay algo que hacer durante el Festival de la Feria Agrícola. ¡Ven y únete a todos y participa en muchas actividades de la Feria Agrícola durante cuatro días!"},
[10609]={"'¡Sí, has encontrado una! ¡Parece que servirá! Es un poco más pequeña que las otras ruedas, así que el viaje será un poco más duro. ¡Pero mientras llevemos esta madera a Puente de Caballetes, no importa!","Recupera la rueda de carro","Mattie Bosquerudo y Noll Tobbit se toparon con los orcos, pero consiguieron escapar ilesos. Su carro sin embargo no corrió tanta suerte y necesita una nueva rueda si van a usarlo para llevar madera de vuelta a Puente de Caballetes.","Rueda de carro recuperada","Las carretas rotas fueron arrastradas por los orcos a su campamento fuera de Nan Wathren.\
\
Algunos granjeros, mientras escapaban de los orcos, fueron asaltados y sus carretas resultaron destruidas. Mattie espera que entre los restos de las carretas de los granjeros encuentres una rueda que pueda usar para arreglar su carro.","'Si no conseguimos una rueda para el carro, esta madera no irá a ninguna parte. Te enviaría a Puente de Caballetes, pero dudo que tengan alguna de sobra. Todo material es preciado allí.\
\
'Pero hay algo de esperanza. Mira, había algunos granjeros escapando de Puente de Caballetes y sus carretas fueron asaltadas por los orcos. Bueno, los suministros fueron robados y los carros se rompieron, pero podría haber alguna rueda de uno de sus carros que podamos rescatar.\
\
'No creo que se llevaran arrastrando los carros hasta Nan Wathren, así que creo que encontrarás los restos en el campamento orco que hay justo al este de aquí. ¡Si encontramos una rueda será allí, diría yo!'","'No creo que los orcos arrastraran las carretas rotas de esa caravana a Nan Wathren, así que yo buscaría una rueda en su campamento al este de aquí.\
\
'De verdad espero que encuentres una, ¡porque sin ella este carro no irá a ninguna parte!'","Lleva la rueda de vuelta a ${NOS}","Rescatar una rueda"},
[10611]={"Find Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home east of Vartúlin","Thórvilon greets you cautiously.\
\
'Though you are an outsider, you have the look of someone capable. I am quite desperate, enough so that I would turn to a stranger for our salvation. This grove you see is dying. My people are dying. My wife... my wife is struggling. She is wearying, fading before my very eyes. I cannot bear it.\
\
'These eyes have seen such sights... countless miracles over thousands of years. Never did I think I would see such nightmares as these. The land cursed, the ground parched, forests as dry and white as bone. All my friends, all those I love, destined to fade and be forgotten.\
\
'I will not fade so easily. I will not let this grove crumble to dust. That is not my path. I have a desperate idea, and you seem capable. Will you help me - will you help our people?'","This odd man before you must be Usakâr","Speak with Usakâr and offer him the oranges","'Milingor? Yes, she is Wearying. But we can make her transition comfortable! I have just the thing.\
\
'Here, take this poultice to her. It is little more than tea, I confess, but sometimes tea is exactly what one needs! At the very least, it is warm and will comfort her.'","Speak with Grove-tender Ulthral about a poultice for Thórvilon's wife, Milingor. She can be found on the higher level of Vartúlin, near the bridge.","Speak with Milingor in her Veróth","Go to the grove Avadhril mentioned east of Vartúlin and obtain some oranges for Usakâr.","Thórvilon has requested your help in searching for a cure to the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight afflicting Vartúlin and greater Imhûlar.","'Lidath mâd, outsider. I am fond of Thórvilon, as I believe his heart is fair, but I do not agree that there is a way to save our people. We are destined to all join in Milingor's fate, and soon, I believe. Nevertheless, Thórvilon is our leader, and I will follow his wishes. If he wishes you to treat with Usakâr, I will tell you how to do so.\
\
'Usakâr is one of the few friends we count among Men. He has always been a loyal ally and friend to the Adúrhid. It is customary for us to send with our envoys to him a gift, part of nature's bounty. As you can see, nature has struggled and her bounty is little more than leaves and ash this season.\
\
'There exists not far from here to the east, however, a small grove of orange trees. When last I walked this orchard, there still were a few oranges clinging to life on one of the orange trees. Bring him a gift of those oranges. I wish I could offer more, but as you can see we barely have anything to give. The southern men have cursed this land. I fear there is nothing we few who remain can do to reverse their savage violence on Favrathór, what was once Laithór, the Emerald Wood, but which is now the Forest of Bone.\
\
'After you have the oranges, continue east along the mountain ridge. Where the mountain meets meadow, there you shall find Dag Usakâra, the home of Usakâr.'","Speak once more with Grove Elder Thórvilon at the edge of Vartúlin.","Speak with Avadhril in Vartúlin","Prune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Picked up oranges from under dying orange trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pruned dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Milingor, Thórvilon's wife, in her Veróth across the bridge from Thórvilon in Vartúlin.","Prune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth.","'Thank you for your kindness. It is hard some days, to bear all the burdens nature has placed upon us. I only wish for Milingor's safety, and the safety and health of all the Adúrhid in this grove. It seems a tall order this day, and most days, however.\
\
'If we are to survive, we need you to convince Usakâr to tell you what he knows of Cúridwan. If you can find her, please, let her know how desperately we need a cure for this Pale Blight. Look around you. This was once Laithór, the Emerald Woods. It has been transformed in a Man's span into Favrathór, the Forest of Bone. So many plants and animals are afflicted with disease. We have held it off for as long as we can, however now it has crept into Vartúlin itself. We have nowhere left to go.\
\
'Avadhril knows more about Usakâr. She often treats with him. She will know how to find him and what boons to bring with you. I believe the Golden Maiden can help us survive. We just need to find her.'","Find Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home. Avadhril mentioned it was east of Vartúlin, where the mountain ridge meets an open meadow.","Speak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and learn more of Vartúlin","'There is a man who treats with us, Usakâr. His ways are strange, but I believe he may have a powerful friend - Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden. She is someone who could help us heal Vartúlin, this grove you see around you. Ever since the southern men made their way through our forests, the trees have started dying, turning hard and white as bone. We call it Lag Dávrit, the Pale Blight.\
\
'I believe it is tied to the southern men, but I cannot be sure. Much of what they do is profane to nature, as they burn and cut the trees and brush they meet, rather than exist within it. I believe Usakâr knows more about the Lag Dávrit, as well as the knowledge of how to contact Cúridwan. She has the power to cure the Lag Dávrit, if she wishes it. I know it in my bones.\
\
'Before you go after Usakâr, would you check on Milingor, my wife? She is behind me, half into the Veróth growing over the bridge. It pains me to see her so. I wish to help her, to stop her Wearying, as she feels it is not her time yet. But yet the Veróth still readily accepts her. I do not wish for her to go yet. Selfishly, I want more time with my beloved.\
\
'Also, if there are any dead branches on her Veróth, please prune them. It is better for her. I cannot do it myself right now. I cannot bear it.\
\
'Perhaps Grove-tender Ulthral has a poultice to comfort Milingor? You should stop there first. She is on the path above me.'","'You bring oranges, so you must be an envoy of the Adúrhid. I keep telling them not to bother sending me fruit, I don't need it. But they, ah, keep to the old ways it seems.\
\
'You are a strange envoy indeed, from the Adúrhid. What's that? Cúridwan? She is a myth! A legend! A terrible cook! Ah, perhaps the cat's out of the bag with that, I suppose. And cats seldom go back into bags once let out. Anyway!\
\
'I have kept Cúridwan's location and identity jealously my own for a very long time. Still, this forest continues to worsen. I know the Adúrhid continue to worsen as well. As the forest goes, so they go. Perhaps it is time to pay Cúridwan a visit after all.\
\
'Don't tell her I called her a terrible cook. She'll be feeding me her blackened chicken pie for months as a punishment. Alright, let's be off then, if you're ready! But keep close! These woods are quite dangerous to outsiders, and many have simply disappeared in them, never to be seen again. I long for the days when a burnt chicken pie was the most dangerous thing I had to dodge.'","Speak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and ascertain what is troubling him.","Speak once more with Grove Elder Thórvilon","Salves for a Ravaged Land, Part 1","'Thorvilon asked you to check on me? He is sweet to ask. And thank Ulthral for me, for this poultice....\
\
'I thought I would undergo the Trothúl, the Wearying, when I was ready to leave this place. I am not ready, little one. I don't want to go yet.\
\
'There is much I would still see and do in this place, with Thórvilon. He tells me to save my energy, that I need to sustain my strength another season and that Cúridwan will soon help us. My strength is fleeting, little one. Each day I see a little less of this grove, my home. Each day I feel increasingly unmoored, less myself.\
\
'I still feel the wind in my limbs, the dry, wheezing breeze. I feel the cold and the heat on my bark. I wish... I wish... I wish many things.\
\
'I love Thórvilon very much. I will hold on for as long as I can.'","Speak with Avadhril to ascertain the details of contacting Usakâr the Hermit.","Pick up oranges from under dying orange trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak with Grove-tender Ulthral in Vartúlin about Milingor's poultice","Speak with Usakâr and offer him the oranges."},
[10612]={"Speak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave","Find your way to the third point Usakâr has marked","'You're ready? Hmm, that is good. You seem to be of stout heart and constitution, which is what this journey and any pies we eat shall require. All right, let's be off!'","Speak with Usakâr and he will mark your map with the route to Cúridwan's home.","Usakâr has agreed to show you the way to the home of Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden, to try to find a cure for the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight sweeping through the woods of Imhûlar.","'If we are to be off, let's be quick about it! This is no time for idle wandering.\
\
'Let me mark the important areas on your map. You must pass through these areas, and in this order or you won't get there at all. I will meet you there. I know several ancient paths that few men remember, and fewer men tread. There we are! I will meet you outside the cave to Kûgrun, Kugêmi's sanctuary.'","A passing group of Ordâkhai has spotted you!","Speak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave.","Find your way to the first point Usakâr has marked on your map.","Find your way to the second point Usakâr has marked on your map.","'Ah, here we are. And right on time, too.'","Speak with Usakâr at Dag Usakâra to mark your map","Salves for a Ravaged Land, Part 2","Find your way to the first point Usakâr has marked","A pack of jackals breaks towards you!","Find your way to the second point Usakâr has marked","Find your way to the third point Usakâr has marked on your map.","Several servals sneak their way near you, looking to pounce"},
[10614]={"Take Cúridwan's salve.","Speak with Cúridwan before you leave","Take Cúridwan's salve","'This is wonderful news! Come, we must return to Vartúlin immediately. I will return with you to Thorvilon. He will be overjoyed - I know he has wished for this day to come for many years. It has been a long losing fight against the Lâg Dávrit for Thórvilon and the Adúrhid, until now.'","'There is one more task we must accomplish, if we actually wish to defeat the Lâg Dávrit permanently. You were probably too young to remember, ${PLAYER}, but the Lâg Dávrit is a recent affliction. It's been here for a little longer than a man's span, afflicting Imhûlar. It came with the Men of Ordâkh, as they made their way north from their strongholds further south.\
\
'I believe their founding stones may have something to do with the Lâg Dávrit. I have sensed a powerful, foreboding energy from them. I believe they must be broken, if the Lâg Dávrit is to be properly defeated, and not merely turned back for a season.\
\
'This salve needs time to complete. The Men of Ordâkh make their camp at Ghat Lor. Destroy the founding stones there. I believe that will rob the Lâg Dávrit of its power. Return here when you are finished. Hopefully by then the salve and my chicken pie will both be done.'","The water shimmers briefly before the current whisks the salve away to Vartúlin","'Perfect timing. The salve just finished, and so did the blackened chicken pie in the oven.'\
\
Usakâr briefly looks panicked. Cúridwan leans in conspiratorially.\
\
'He complains, but he loves my blackened chicken pie.'\
\
She leans out again, and returns to her normal volume.\
\
'I will get the salve for you. It's a shame you both can't stay for dinner.'","Speak with Usakâr in Kûgrun","Salves for a Ravaged Land, Part 4","Return to Cúridwan in Kûgrun","Destroyed Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Use the salve on the river to heal Vartúlin","Speak with Cúridwan before you leave.","Speak with Usakâr in Kûgrun.","'You have done much this day for the Adúrhid. You are quite the potent ally for them. I hope you know I appreciate your efforts as well.\
\
'Here is the other phial of the salve. Use it to purify areas untouched by the waters near Vartúlin, or give it to the Adúrhid for the same purpose.\
\
'Our paths will cross again, my friend. I have seen it. Until then, may your travels be safe and your belly be full. We can scarcely ask for more.'","Curidwan has tasked you with destroying Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found far to the east of Kûgrun.","Cúridwan has tasked you with destroying three great founding stones brought to Imhûlar by the Ordâkhai.","'Ah, yes. Here is the salve. I made sure you got enough for all of Vartúlin. This river you see behind me empties directly into Vartúlin. Take this first phial and dump all its contents in the river behind me. I have a second phial for you as well, to take back to Thórvilon, so he may start the rebuilding process in the forests of Adagím outside of Vartúlin.'","Return to Cúridwan in Kûgrun.","Use the first phial of salve on the river behind Cúridwan's cottage to heal Vartúlin.","Destroy Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10616]={"Thórvilon has gathered with some others around Milingor's Veróth. You should join them.","Speak with Avadhril nearby.","Listen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversation.","Listen to Thórvilon","Comfort Thórvilon.","Speak with Avadhril nearby","'I see now the strength Thórvilon possesses. He has set aside his grief to be present for his people. I don't believe in miracles or sorcerers, friend. There are far too few of both left in this world. But I believe in him. I believe in Thórvilon. I will give what strength I have to him, that Vartúlin might flourish again.'","Listen to Thórvilon.","Salves for a Ravaged Land, Part 5","Comfort Thórvilon","Listen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversation","Join Thórvilon near Milingor's Veróth","Speak with Thórvilon and let him know the good news about finding a cure for the Lâg Dávrit.","Thórvilon turns quickly before you can comfort him"},
[10618]={"Usa la pipa para probar la primera bolsa de hierba para pipa","La hierba para pipa fresca tiene un sabor suave y delicado","La primera bolsa de hierba para pipa está en la mesa.\
\
Deberías recoger algo de hierba para pipa de la primera bolsa.","Tomaste una muestra de la primera bolsa","Usa la pipa para probar la tercera mezcla de hierba para pipa.","Toma una muestra de la tercera bolsa de hierba para pipa","La segunda bolsa de hierba para pipa está en la mesa.\
\
Deberías tomar algo de hierba para pipa de la segunda bolsa.","Deberías usar la pipa que te dieron para probar la hierba para pipa.","'Usa la pipa que te di para probar la primera bolsa de hierba para pipa.'","Tomaste una muestra de la tercera bolsa de hierba para pipa","Tus pulmones arden ante el sabor áspero y denso","Usa la pipa para probar la segunda mezcla de hierba para pipa","La hierba para pipa es algo que los hobbits se toman muy en serio. Un mercado nunca recibiría visitas a menos que tuviera un suministro y variedad adecuados.","'No te avergüences si toses un poco.'","'Esta debería ser un poco más amarga que la primera, pero tener más sabor.'","Prueba la tercera mezcla de hierba para pipa","'¿Así que la primera era suave, la segunda sabrosa y con la tercera no pudiste del todo? ¡Parece que entonces estamos listos para el mercado!'","Esta sigue siendo suave, pero el sabor es profundo y persistente","Prueba la hierba para pipa","'Ahora viene la mejor parte. No se puede sacar un producto sin probarlo y catarlo a fondo. Tienes que asegurarte de que lo que vendes es solo lo mejor.\
\
'He preparado tres mezclas en esa mesa. Una es toda de hierba para pipa recién cortada, otra es toda de hierba para pipa seca, y la otra es una mezcla mitad y mitad.\
\
'Toma esta pipa y prueba las mezclas. Si crees que son buenas, entonces estaré de acuerdo en que se vendan en el mercado.'","Florencia Gamyi está en la Plantación de hierba para pipa de la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Florencia Gamyi querrá saber qué te parecieron las mezclas de hierba para pipa.","Usa la pipa que te dieron para probar la segunda bolsa de hierba para pipa.","Toma una muestra de la primera bolsa","Devuélvele la pipa a Florencia Gamyi","Tomaste una muestra de la segunda bolsa","'Toma una muestra de la primera bolsa.'","'La tercera bolsa se ha secado durante toda una estación; puede que sea demasiado fuerte para los que no están acostumbrados a ella.'","Toma una muestra de la segunda bolsa","La tercera bolsa está en el mostrador.\
\
Deberías tomar una muestra de hierba para pipa de la tercera bolsa.","'Toma un pellizco de la segunda bolsa, una mezcla mitad y mitad.'"},
[10619]={"Derrota al enfurecido del matorral de Adagím","Enfurecido del matorral de Adagím derrotado","Muestreo de los acechadores del pantano","¡Ha llegado un enfurecido troll silvano de Adagím! ¡Derrótalo!","Tu misión es viajar a Lhámuth y recolectar muestras de la Plaga Pálida de los acechadores del pantano para los eruditos de Sul Madásh.","'Eso debería ser suficiente muestras para los eruditos. Regresemos a Sul Madásh.'","Muestras de la Plaga Pálida recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolección de muestras de la Plaga Pálida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10620]={"Okhtâr Ghôlkhas is waiting inside Dâr Laja.\
\
You have paid your respects to the long-departed ancestor by dropping coins to the sea. Hopefully Rashâm has returned the Ghôlkhas armour by now. You should see if Okhtâr has news.","Kheb Hanût is in the north-western corner of Tâkhdar.\
\
The fence, Rashâm, has suggested you search for fallen coins in the black market of Kheb Hanût. He wants to pay a symbolic token of apology for the Ghôlkhas tomb-robbing.","Speak with Okhtâr Ghôlkhas","You let the coins slip through your fingers into the waves","The fence, Rashâm, wishes to return the Ghôlkhas armour, and would like help in paying respects to the noble family from whom it was stolen.","Look for fallen coins in Kheb Hanût (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I would not ask you to waste your own coin-purse on a sentimental errand. It cannot be too difficult to find other coins lying about here. You would be surprised what people allow to go missing.'","A good spot facing the sea is south of the Fisherfold in Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
Rashâm has asked you to drop old coins into the ocean by the Fisherfold in remembrance of a fallen hero whose tomb was robbed.","'I may be a fence, but I respect our funerary customs. The Fisherfold faces the sea. I would think it would be easy to find a good place in the water to respect the departed, even if we cannot place coins over their eyes ourselves.'","Drop the coins into the sea","Sanctified Remains","'So you have paid your respects? Then my conscience is clear. I will find my way inside the Ghôlkhas manor to return the armour. You do not need to know the particulars. By the time you speak with Okhtâr, I will have performed my task, I swear.'","Coins can be found with a bit of searching","The coin is ancient, almost crumbling to dust in your hand (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The most exciting individual crept past my guards, I am told. Do you know how rare it is for any such miscreant to evade my manor's defences? What a tale to tell! I do not much mind; whoever this character was, they seem to have returned my armour to me. This must have been your doing.\
\
'As promised, your reward. Do not tell me of your adventures; I prefer to imagine them!'","'Have you found any scuffed or faded old coins yet? Look around here. I am certain someone long ago might have lost some. I am of the mind we only require two. One for each eye of the departed.'","'The armour Zulkhêma sold me was wrested from a wealthy family's mausoleum, you say? That conniving woman, selling me something at so high a price; I could not sell something so distinctive! I may deal in ill-gained goods, but I am no grave-robber, and I thank you for warning me away. Did this Ghôlkhas family member tell you the location of the tomb, by chance? No, of course not.\
\
'I must find a way to express my apology and return the armour without being noticed. Please bestow some respects to this slain ancestor on my behalf, perhaps tossing them into the sea near the Fisherfold. Find some coins; it is our way.'","Old and forgotten coins will be found in Kheb Hanût, in the north-west of Tâkhdar.\
\
Rashâm would like you to collect some keepsake coins in the black market that no one will miss to represent a funerary token.","Enter Kheb Hanût"},
[10621]={"Ayuda a Maladan con Kergrim de Haudh Valandur","Hay mucho que hacer en las tumbas abiertas del Camino de los Reyes.","Ayuda a Rodlam con Órdenes de la Corona de Hierro","Ayuda a Nimbellas con Ladrones de Haudh Eärendur","Ayuda a Maladan con El cetro de Valandur","Habla con las Nimbellas en el Camino de los Reyes","La santidad de los soberanos","Se han abierto varias tumbas y criptas en el Camino de los Reyes.","'¿Nos ayudarás?'","Ayuda a Nethrandir con El anillo de Arantar","Nimbellas se encuentra en el campamento de Montaraces del Camino de los Reyes.\
\
Nimbellas querrá hablar sobre el trabajo realizado en las criptas abiertas del Camino de los Reyes.","Ayuda a Nethrandir con Saqueadores de Haudh Arantar","Ayuda a Rodlam con Rastreadores de Haudh Eldacar","'Has hecho mucho por ayudarnos a conservar estas tumbas y criptas, ${PLAYER}. Si los gobernantes del más allá aún vivieran, sé que te honrarían y alabarían.'","'Con las amenazas neutralizadas, las criptas exploradas y estas llaves en nuestro poder, estamos listos para adentrarnos en las tumbas del Camino de los Reyes. \
\
'Nos centraremos en las cuatro que has descubierto que se pueden abrir: Haudh Eärendur, Haudh Valandur, Haudh Arantar y Haudh Eldacar.\
\
'Cada uno de nosotros ha dedicado tiempo a investigar estas criptas y a revisar nuestras notas sobre lo que hemos visto mientras estábamos destinados aquí. Hay mucho por hacer.'","Ayuda a Nimbellas con Enterrado en Haudh Eärendur"},
[10622]={"The sand here is damp and contains small clumps of soil","Charzâd is by the old observatory above the city, waiting for you to return to her with your discoveries.","Sand In The Sky","The sand here is coarse and granular","Bring the sand you collected to Charzâd by the old observatory","Collect sand from the spider-haunted ruins east of the city","The sand here is very fine, and sifts easily through your fingers","Collect sand to the west of one of the farms outside the city","Charzâd asked you to collect sand from several different locations outside the city.","'From this observatory, scholars in Umbar Baharbêl once gazed at the skies above, studying the night sky for wisdom. How distant was that age of knowledge? Too long ago for one lifetime, my friend; the observatory was destroyed, and has fallen into ruin in the years since.\
\
'But I have dreamed about the things you might have seen from its balconies and from the rooftop viewing platforms. Will you do something for me? I am a scholar of sorts myself, but my subjects are more terrestrial than those of the folk who once worked in the building above us. Will you take this small leather bag and fill it with sand from several locations east of the city? I will reward you for this work, of course.'","'Thank you for doing as I asked, my friend. Did you observe that the sand you collected from each location possessed its own characteristics?'\
\
You tell Charzâd that some of the sand was damp and some was dry; some was coarse and some was fine; some of the sand was brightly-coloured.\
\
'And yet they were all, in the end, still sand?' Charzâd answers with a raised eyebrow. 'It reminds me of how I envision the stars in the sky. From our position here they all seem to be the same: twinkling dots of light, like jewels affixed to the heavens. But look at this!'\
\
Charzâd reaches into the small leather bag and removes a handful of the sand you gathered. She opens her palm and lets the sand fall, where the individual particles drift and float restlessly on the breeze.\
\
'Like stars,' she says. 'How different might the stars be from each other if we could only see them up close? Might the scholars at the observatory above us have learned the answer if they were not slain, the observatory not shuttered, and their work not lost? I think they might have.\
\
'Thank you for doing this for me, my friend. Not everyone would! I know: I asked them. But take this for your trouble and your time.'","'Will you fill the bag I gave you with sand from several locations east of the city? I will reward you for this work, of course.'","Charzâd stands by the old observatory above the city, musing about the stars in the sky and the sand in the desert.","Collect sand from the hills north-east of the farms outside the city","Collect sand south-east of the farms outside the city, near the river","The sand here shines and sparkles with a variety of colours"},
[10623]={"Lleva la arena blanca a Mundarico Hojarena","Lleva la arena blanca a Mundarico Hojarena en Dwaling","'¿Has encontrado algo de arena ya, ${PLAYER}? El Barandalf está al norte y este de aquí.'","'Deberías poder encontrar arena blanca en las Marismas de Arena al otro lado de la colina.'","Mundarico Hojarena está en casa de Hob Cimacolina en Prado del Toro Bramador en Dwaling, al sur de las Marisma de Arena.\
\
Deberías volver con Mundarico Hojarena para llevarle la arena blanca.","Se necesita arena en el arte del soplado, y la arena blanca de las Marisma de Arena es la mejor.","'${CLASS}, me alegro que hayas venido. Hemos estado intentando reconstruir poco a poco lo que podemos. Ha supuesto mucho esfuerzo pero me temo que pronto será desperdiciado.\
\
'Somos sopladores de vidrio aquí en Dwaling. Siempre ha sido y siempre será así. Bueno, espero que así sea. Nos hemos quedado con muy poco suministro últimamente. La nueva 'gente del pueblo' y las criaturas de las dunas nos impiden aventurarnos demasiado lejos. Apenas tenemos suficiente para terminar el siguiente pedido.\
\
'Solía conseguir arena blanca para el soplado de vidrio de un querido viejo amigo que iba al Barandalf, al noreste de Dwaling, pero se mudó fuera no hace ni una semana. Si pudieras, ve a las Marismas de Arena y consígueme algo de arena blanca. Estaré muy en deuda contigo.'","'Tienes la arena... ¡y justo a tiempo! Mis trabajadores justo estaban terminando con nuestro suministro.'","La arena blanca se puede encontrar en las Marismas de Arena, al norte de Dwaling.\
\
Mundarico Hojarena te ha pedido que recojas algo de arena blanca para él.","Recoge arena blanca (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arena para la llama","Arena blanca recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10631]={"Rhúnelleth te ha pedido que recojas muestras de agua del Jardín emponzoñado y de la Casa de Cristal.\
\
El Jardín Emponzoñado y la Casa de Cristal se encuentran en Carn Dûm.","Debes llevar las muestras de agua que recogiste a Rhúnelleth.\
\
Rhúnelleth se encuentra en Bail Avarc, fuera de Carn Dûm.","Muestras de agua recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Tengo curiosidad por las aguas que fluyen a través de Sant Lhoer, los Jardines emponzoñados de Carn Dûm. Son menos potentes que las del resto de la ciudad, afortunadamente, pero también parecen poseer otros atributos, tanto corruptores como potenciadores para las plantas y criaturas cercanas.\
\
'Toma estas frascos y tráeme muestras de los arroyos que fluyen, para que pueda estudiar el efecto que ha tenido la derrota de Helchgam. ¡Ten cuidado de no dejar que las aguas toquen tu piel! ¿Quién sabe qué venenos aún acechan en esas profundidades?'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados.</rgb>","Sant Lhoer: La corriente de Helchgam","Recoge muestras de agua (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega las muestras de agua a Rhúnelleth","Dentro de los Jardines Emponzoñados de Carn Dûm crecen numerosas plantas, torcidas y corrompidas por las aguas fétidas de los ríos que fluyen por la zona.","'¡Ah, has regresado! Ven, déjame ver qué contienen las frascos.'"},
[10632]={"Sant Lhoer: Resultados de Oganuin","La hechicera angmarim Oganuin se ha encerrado en Bâr Heledh, la Casa de Cristal dentro de Carn Dûm, donde ha estado experimentando con plantas, criaturas y monstruos por igual. Sus creaciones se esconden entre las sombras en los jardines de Sant Lhoer.","Entrega las muestras de carne corrompida a Dolág","'Ah, has regresado. Sé que te he encomendado una tarea macabra. Dame las muestras que has recogido. Las llevaré a mi amigo, y quizás él tenga alguna idea de qué atrocidades se están cometiendo detrás de esas sucias paredes de cristal.'","'Oganuin se ha encerrado en su Casa de Cristal, donde ella y sus seguidores experimentan con plantas y criaturas por igual. He visto algunos de los orcos que han sido sometidos a sus pruebas y los resultados me han impactado profundamente.\
\
Conozco a un maestro cazador que desea estudiar la carne de las criaturas que ha alterado. Tráeme muestras de las criaturas dentro de sus Jardines Emponzoñados y la Casa de Cristal. El conocimiento de lo que ha hecho puede ayudarnos a detener e incluso revertir el proceso.'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados.</rgb>","Recoge muestras de carne (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recogido las muestras de carne que Dolág solicitó. Debes darle estos pedazos sucios lo más rápido posible.\
\
Dolág se encuentra en Bail Avarc, fuera de Carn Dûm.","Dolág te ha pedido que recojas muestras de carne de las criaturas dentro del Jardín Emponzoñado y la Casa de Cristal de Carn Dûm.","Muestras de carne recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10633]={"Quema las coronas de bruja (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has quemado muchas coronas de bruja, y Galasdil estará feliz de escuchar sobre tus esfuerzos.\
\
Galasdil se encuentra en Bail Avarc, fuera de Carn Dûm.","Sant Lhoer: Semillas del mal","En Sant Lhoer, los Jardines emponzoñados de Carn Dûm, crecen numerosas plantas, torcidas y corrompidas por las aguas fétidas de los ríos que fluyen por la zona. Si estas aberraciones logran salir de su jardín húmedo, podrían amenazar a las otras plantas, criaturas y pueblos de la Tierra Media.","'Mae govannen. Mi nombre es Galasdil, y estaba viajando por Nan Amlug cuando me encontré con una planta tan extraña que pausé mi viaje para estudiar su origen. Mi investigación me llevó a través de las tierras arrasadas de Angmar, hasta aquí, a las puertas de Carn Dûm.\
\
En los Sant Lhoer de Carn Dûm crecen numerosas plantas, torcidas y corrompidas por las aguas fétidas de los ríos que fluyen por la zona. Entre ellas se encuentra la corrompida corona de bruja, cuyas semillas se llevan fácilmente con el viento. ¡Incluso ahora veo pequeños copos de semillas flotando por el aire húmedo!\
\
Si eres lo suficientemente valiente como para aventurarte en los Jardines Emponzoñados, quema cualquiera de estas plantas que veas. ¡No deben ser permitidas a propagarse por toda la Tierra Media!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Para avanzar en esta misión, debes usar el Buscador de Instancias (Ctrl+J) para entrar en Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados.</rgb>","Galasdil te ha pedido que destruyas cualquier planta de corona de bruja que puedas encontrar dentro de Sant Lhoer, los Jardines Emponzoñados.\
\
Sant Lhoer se encuentra en Carn Dûm.","'Te doy la bienvenida de nuevo. Puedo ver por el humo que te rodea que has tenido éxito. Que tus acciones eviten que estas terribles creaciones se propaguen por Angmar y más allá.'","Habla con Galasdil"},
[10634]={"Collected tree-sap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The trees of North Ithilien are ripe with valuable sap which Thurindol believes can be made into a sustaining tonic for the soldiers.","Sap-bearing Trees can be found near the Field of Cormallen.\
\
Harvest the sap from North Ithilien trees.","Check tapped trees for tree-sap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Thurindol","Sap Tapper","'${PLAYER}, I have another valuable task for you.\
\
'The versatile flora is not all this region has to offer the willing herbalist. I noticed this morning that some trees have begun to bear a rather curious sap. Harvest this sap for me, and I may be able to formulate potent sustaining tonics for the impending march. There are many fine sap-bearing trees wreathing the Fields of Cormallen.'","Collect tree-sap (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'This sap will prove invaluable as the key ingredient of my new vigour tonic. \
\
'You have helped ensure that the bodies and hearts of the brave Host will remain vigorous and unweary in the face of the Enemy.'","Thurindol can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have gathered a good quantity of tree-sap and should now return to Thurindol."},
[10636]={"Habla con Haflith en Mekhem-bizru","Zapadores orcos derrotados en Uruk-gashan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los zapadores orcos han sido detenidos y la piedra está a salvo por ahora. Esto alivia mi corazón, pero aún queda mucho por hacer. Aún no hemos asegurado que la Piedra de Durin permanezca para las generaciones venideras.'","Los enanos temen que los orcos estén preparando la destrucción de la Piedra de Durin, que marca el lugar venerado donde Durin I miró por primera vez el Lago Espejo.","Zapadores en la Piedra","Haflith se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru, al noroeste de Uruk-gashan.\
\
Haflith querrá saber que los zapadores orcos han sido derrotados, manteniendo la Piedra de Durin a salvo... al menos por ahora.","'La Piedra de Durin es un tesoro de los enanos. Es en ese lugar, mirando el Lago Espejo, donde Durin decidió asentarse y construir Khazad-dûm. La piedra sirve como un recordatorio eterno para todos los enanos de lo que es legítimamente nuestro.\
\
'Tengo miedo por la seguridad de la Piedra de Durin. Los Orcos que salen de Moria han establecido un campamento a su alrededor, y a diario veo a varios de ellos trabajando para reducirla a polvo. Esto no puede ser permitido.\
\
'Dirígete a Uruk-gashan, al sureste de aquí, y derrota a los zapadores orcos alrededor del campamento. Son los que tienen el conocimiento para reducir la piedra a polvo y son la mayor amenaza para nuestro antiguo monumento.'","Los zapadores orcos se encuentran en Uruk-gashan, al sureste de Mekhem-bizru.\
\
Haflith te pidió que fueras a Uruk-gashan y derrotaras a los zapadores orcos que amenazan con destruir la Piedra de Durin.","'¡Apresúrate, imbécil! Si esa piedra es destruida, el Pueblo de Durin podría ser destruido también.'","Derrota a los zapadores orcos en Uruk-gashan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10645]={"Derrota a Sarnemil","'Me alegra tu regreso, ${PLAYER}. No poseo mucho, pero quien ha dado muerte a Sarlug y a Sarnemil merece lo que pueda ofrecerle. Tâl Bruinen es más seguro gracias a tus esfuerzos, y me alegra que así sea.'","La Huida de Sarnemil","Desde las alturas de Cirith Ulunn viste a la sierpe de las rocas Sarnemil huir hacia el sur siguiendo el curso del Bruinen.","Sarnemil está en Torech Ullug, al sur de Echad Candelleth y en la orilla oriental del río, junto a los rápidos que fluyen desde Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Has derrotado a Sarlug y a muchas sierpes de las rocas, pero Sarnemil escapó; sin embargo, la viste huir hacia el sur siguiendo el curso del Bruinen. Deberías descender de nuevo las laderas hasta el Bruinen y buscar hacia el sur por las orillas su guarida.","Has derrotado a Sarnemil","Daervellas está en Echad Candelleth, el campamento élfico en Tâl Bruinen, al norte de Torech Ullug.\
\
Has derrotado a Sarnemil y acabado con la amenaza de sus crías. Ahora deberías volver con Daervellas para darle esta noticia.","Deberías descender de nuevo las laderas hasta el Bruinen y buscar hacia el sur por las orillas la guarida de Sarnemil","Habla con Daervellas"},
[10650]={"The number of Orcs remaining at Minas Rant has been reduced, due to your efforts.","Discover Minas Rant","The tower of Minas Rant can be found at the western end of the stream that cuts across the Norcrofts.\
\
The number of Orcs remaining in the area has been reduced, due to your efforts.","A company of Orcs has taken to the ruins of the ancient tower, Minas Rant, and have begun to use it as an outpost from which to attack the neighbouring homes.","Defeated Orcs in Minas Rant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orcs within Minas Rant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Savage Intruders","Completado","The tower of Minas Rant can be found at the western end of the stream that cuts across the Norcrofts.\
\
The Orcs inhabiting the ancient tower of Minas Rant have begun using it as a base from which to attack the neighbouring homes."},
[10651]={"'Arifael es leal, aunque sea el único gigante que aún lo es.'","El gigante Arifael está en Amon Nendir, al suroeste de Rivendel.\
\
El señor Elrond te ha pedido que hables con Arifael sobre los gigantes que al parecer han jurado lealtad a Angmar y ahora protegen Helegrod para sus nuevos amos.","Salva a Arifael","'Mis propios exploradores no necesitaron acercarse a los muros de Helegrod para ver a varios gigantes en los riscos sobre la fortaleza. Curiosamente, esos gigantes no parecían llevar los emblemas del Señor del Trueno; algún nuevo líder debe de haber tomado el control de este grupo y jurado lealtad al poder que ahora habita en Helegrod.\
\
'No tengo dudas sobre la fuente de ese poder: debe venir de la Tierra de Angmar.\
\
'Hay uno entre los gigantes en quien aún confío: Arifael, en Amon Nendir, siempre amigo de los Elfos de este valle. Siempre ha rechazado a sus primos más beligerantes, aunque le cause dolor y lo obligue a vivir como un exiliado. Amon Nendir está al suroeste del valle. Habla con Arifael y ve si sabe algo sobre los gigantes que habitan sobre Helegrod. Temo que todos los gigantes, salvo Arifael, estén ahora en nuestra contra.'","El señor Elrond solo confía en un gigante: Arifael de Amon Nendir.","'¿Vienes de parte de los Elfos? No todos los gigantes siguen ahora al Señor del Trueno. ¡Storvâgûn es el nuevo líder de los gigantes! Engaña a los gigantes. ¡Traidor!\
\
'Los Elfos deberían preocuparse. Storvâgûn no le teme a nadie, como un verdadero gigante, pero tiene nuevos amigos que le pagan para que haga lo que ellos quieren.\
\
'La vieja ciudad enana en las montañas no es un hogar para gigantes de verdad, sino para los lacayos de los nuevos amigos de Storvâgûn. Eso me pone triste. ¡Debes ayudar!'","'He oído rumores sobre ese Storvâgûn del que hablaba Arifael. Son historias crueles y desagradables.'","'Amon Nendir está al suroeste de Rivendel. Arifael, siempre amigo de los Elfos, quizá conozca las nuevas lealtades de sus primos.'"},
[10652]={"The lumber-yard lies along the road to Fenmarch, north-east of Aldburg.\
\
The panicked Rohirrim woman told you to seek out Guthláf within the lumber-yard.","'I am indeed Guthláf, the former flag-bearer for the king. If you are still hale, you must be a strong ${CLASS}.\
\
'We do not have time to discuss a plan of attack. I overheard the lieutenant of these Orcs threaten to put the orchard to the torch.\
\
'Head south to the orchard and stop him at once.'","Find the back entrance to the lumber-yard","Defeated the Orc lieutenant","Found the back entrance of the lumber-yard","The panicked Rohirrim woman has asked for assistance liberating the lumber-yard from the attacking Orcs.","Talk to Guthláf","Save the Lumber-yard","Guthláf awaits you north of the orchard.\
\
The Orc-lieutenant has been defeated and the orchard is safe. You should return to Guthláf and report the good news.","'I managed to escape before the camp was overrun, but the workers are still there and need your help!\
\
'You may be able to sneak in undetected through the back entrance. Once inside the lumber yard, seek out Guthláf.\
\
'Will you help?'","The orchard lies to the south, within the lumber-yard, east of Aldburg.\
\
Guthláf overheard the Orc's plan to burn the orchard. He suggested that you head to the orchard and defeat the lieutenant of the Orcs there.","A hardy warrior stands ahead...this must be Guthláf","'It was rather fortuitous timing that you arrived when you did. I am not certain that we would have been able to save the lumber-yard without your assistance.\
\
'I am Guthláf, son of Sparhafoc, Thane of Fenmarch. I was once the banner-bearer for Théoden King. Since my recent dismissal, I have been lending aid here at the lumber-yard.\
\
'Now we must put our hands to the task of restoring the lumber-yard.'","Find Guthláf","Guthláf is in the lumber-yard, north-east of Aldburg.\
\
You should speak with Guthláf about how to reclaim the lumber-yard.","The back entrance can be found downhill from the panicked Rohirrim woman, towards the water.\
\
The panicked Rohirrim woman recommended entering the lumber-yard through the back entrance in the hopes of sneaking in unnoticed.","Defeat the Orc lieutenant"},
[10653]={"You have escaped the Taurogrim and rescued Sterkist.\
\
You should talk to Langhár and Sterkist.","The cart belonging to the Beornings was left behind here","Speak with Langhár and complete \\qDeep in the Darkening Wood\\q","'There is no time to delay, ${PLAYER}. I saw them take Sterkist further north. We must pursue them! Go, I will be right behind you.'","You have escaped the Taurogrim and rescued Sterkist.\
\
You should talk to Thorlind.","'Thank you for your help, friend. I cannot say I expected to be kidnapped by mythical wood-trolls on this journey! Our task was to trade with the Elves of Felegoth and then return. Oh, that reminds me, I think many of the things from our cart are scattered about the woods....'","Find Langhár","Saving Sterkist","Habla con Langhár","Langhár has run further into the woods, to the north.\
\
You should find Langhár.","Find any sign of Sterkist","'The Beornings may catch their breath here for a short time, but should not tarry long. I will keep watch, but must soon return to Felegoth. We are still near to danger.\
\
'The Taurogrim have returned and at a time when the spiders have all but vanished. I do not think this a coincidence. They were a dangerous enemy of my people long ago, and we must not allow them to return to force unfettered. I have some more work for you, friend, while we are near to their encampment.\
\
'After you have ensured the Beornings are safely at the Forest Gate, you should report this threat to King Thranduil. I will return myself after I am finished here.'","Sterkist has been taken by the Taurogrim!\
\
You should save Sterkist!","One of the Beornings has been found, but Sterkist is still missing. Langhár needs your help rescuing him from the clutches of the Taurogrim.","'We appear to be safe, for now. You are quite the fighter, ${PLAYER}. Thank you for helping Sterkist. It is about time we move on and return home, I think.'","Talk to Thorlind","The Taurogrim took Sterkist further north.\
\
You should look for Sterkist.","'Sterkist is through here, I am certain! We will surely have to face the Taurogrim inside. Come with me!'","'Hurry, we must save Sterkist!'","The Beorning prints continue in this direction","Talk to Sterkist"},
[10655]={"Musarañas ladronas han robado las manzanas de Habbo Maltaverde.","Has recogido una docena de manzanas de Habbo. Deberías devolvérselas en el centro del pueblo de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree.","'¡Miseria y desgracia! ¡Mis manzanas!\
\
'¡Llevé mi cosecha de manzanas al centro del pueblo para la Feria de los Granjeros, y como puedes ver, ahora no tengo nada, y nada que mostrar por ello! Parece que unas musarañas ladronas vinieron en la noche y se las robaron todas. Algunos habitantes descubrieron la entrada a un gran túnel de musarañas, y seguramente de ahí vinieron.\
\
'¡No pueden haber comido todas esas manzanas en una sola noche, deben estar acaparándolas! Si estás interesado en ayudarme, podrías ir a su túnel y traer de vuelta mis manzanas.\
\
'¡Por favor, salva mis manzanas!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual.</rgb>","Devuelve las manzanas a Habbo Maltaverde","Recupera las manzanas de Habbo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Manzanas de Habbo recuperadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habbo te ha pedido que te aventures en el túnel de las musarañas y salves sus manzanas de su destino incierto. La entrada del túnel se encuentra al sureste del centro del pueblo de Entibo, en las Tierras de Bree.","'¡Bendición, has salvado algunas de mis manzanas! Sabía que no podían haberlas comido tan rápido.\
\
'¡Gracias, camarada!'","Salvando las manzanas"},
[10657]={"Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.\
\
You should speak with Tolwin.","Brotes recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You see signs that the farmers are still alive and should rescue them from the Orcs","Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation","Farmers can be found around Eryn Cordovath.\
\
You should rescue any farmers you find.","'A look-out atop the tower in Crithost has just spotted a band of Orcs heading towards Eryn Cordovath, Talath Anor's prized orchard.\
\
'We have yet to evacuate all the farmers from Eryn Cordovath. You must make haste to the orchard and send the farmers to Crithost at once!'","The farmer thanks you and wishes for you collect saplings if you have the time","Saving the Orchard","The farmer understands and makes her way to Crithost","Travel to Eryn Cordovath and assess the situation.","'I am pleased to report that the farmers have all returned safely to Crithost. You have done well.\
\
'And it is wonderful that you were able to rescue these saplings from the orchard. I am sure that Ceveneth will be more than willing to plant the saplings here in Crithost.'","One of the farmers wishes for you to gather saplings so that Crithost can tend to some of the orchard's crops even if the orchard is lost.\
\
You should gather saplings.","A look-out has spotted a band of Orcs headed for Eryn Cordovath, a nearby orchard that is in the process of being evacuated, and Tolwin wishes for you to ride out there and assist the farmers.","The nervous farmer wishes you luck and scurries to Crithost","The farmer is thankful and urges you to rescue any others","Rescue farmers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Tolwin","Recoge brotes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10659]={"Warn the Dunlending abomination (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Delwin at the Boar-clan encampment","'Thank you for saving our twisted kin. I know that some may have resisted your help. That is all right. It is a sad but foreseen loss.\
\
'I hope that Blaire and the Boar-clan will understand now that these are not monsters... they are just like us. One day, this will never happen again. Thank you for saving our people.'","Warned the Dunlending abomination (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You must save our twisted kinsmen!'","'All of this killing sickens me. Blaire and the others just want to kill anything that moves and has a White Hand emblazoned upon it.\
\
'Well, I will not stand for it. These were once our people. It is not their fault that Saruman wants to make half-orcs and uruks. They did not ask to be made into this.\
\
'Warn our twisted kin and save them. They are not abominations. We need to help them, not destroy them. Go north to Lhan Colvarn and tell them to leave before Blaire and the rest destroy the camp. You may see them as abominations, but I ask you to look more closely.'","Abomination Dunlendings can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment.\
\
Delwin wants you to save the abomination Dunlendings from the killing ways of her companions by warning them to flee.","The Dunlending abomination looks at you with a wary eye, cowering slightly. It is not sure if you mean it harm or help.\
\
As you approach, it tenses, looking at you with a blank stare....","Saving the Twisted","Delwin is at the Boar-clan encampment, south of Lhan Colvarn.\
\
You should return to Delwin and let her know that you have saved many of the Dunlending abominations.","Delwin believes that the abominations are not truly monsters. They were once people. She wants you to speak with them and give them one last chance to escape before the Boar Clan destroys the camp."},
[10660]={"'Small brush fires dot the hill-sides of North Ithilien. We have led several small charges against these flames, yet reports of more come to us at Henneth Annûn each morning.\
\
'This time of the season, a brush fire should be a rare occurrence, and not one we should be dealing with every day. I fear the Orcs lurking in Ithilien are to blame. No doubt they wish to slow us down or strike fear into us by attempting to burn the entire hill-side bare.\
\
'If you encounter any brush-fires, douse them immediately. I know that I can count on you, my friend.'","Saving the Wilds","Talk to Thurindol","Doused the flames (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thurindol has asked you to put out brush fires around North Ithilien.","Thurindol can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
You should return to Thurindol with news of your success.","Douse the flames of burning brush around North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}, your efforts have saved North Ithilien's wilds.\
\
'Any sign of new life is a threat to the Enemy. We must be the sentinels of hope and guard these verdant lands. You have my thanks.'","Brush fires have sprung up across North Ithilien. \
\
Thurindol has asked you to search North Ithilien for brush fires and put them out before they spread further."},
[10661]={"'Los dragonzuelos se encuentran muy al este de aquí, ${PLAYER}, en Dolroth.'","Dragonzuelos derrotados en Dolroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Es cierto lo que he oído? ¿Que estás viajando al valle de Dolroth? Si es así, ¿podrías reducir el número de dragonzuelos que se encuentran allí? ¡Serías de gran ayuda para Gabilshathûr!\
\
'Aunque no son tan peligrosos ni malvados como un dragón, los dragonzuelos comparten al menos una pequeña parte de su amor por las cosas preciosas. En el pasado, los dragonzuelos de Dolroth fueron atraídos hasta aquí, descendiendo en picado y atacándonos. Después de uno de esos ataques, lideré una banda de enanos hacia Dolroth y logramos reducir su número.\
\
'Pero ahora, como estamos presionados por los orcos, no tenemos enanos disponibles para encargarse de los dragonzuelos, y temo que su número vuelva a crecer. Si tú pudieras eliminar a varios de ellos, ¡solo tendríamos una amenaza de la que preocuparnos!'","Los dragonzuelos se encuentran al este de Gabilshathûr, en el valle de Dolroth\
\
Ansurr te pidió que reduzcas el número de dragonzuelos","Amenaza Escamosa","El Guardia Ansurr te contó que en el pasado los dragonzuelos de Dolroth amenazaban a Gabilshathûr. Teme que, al no tener tiempo para reducir su número, vuelvan a representar un peligro.","'¡Bien hecho! Dormiré más tranquilo sabiendo que al menos los dragonzuelos no nos amenazarán por un tiempo. Bueno... eso sería cierto si los orcos nos dieran un momento de respiro.\
\
'Oh, no creas que no estoy agradecido, ${PLAYER}. ¡Nos has prestado un gran servicio!'","Derrota dragonzuelos en Dolroth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Guardia Ansurr está en Gabilshathûr, muy al oeste del valle de Dolroth\
\
Has derrotado a muchos dragonzuelos y deberías regresar con el Guardia Ansurr para informarle de tu éxito"},
[10662]={"Abartârik has asked you to lessen the worm population in Ost Amondal.\
\
Ost Amondal is in southern Belfalas.","Defeated worms in Ost Amondal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should let Abartârik know that you defeated many worms at Ost Amondal.\
\
Abartârik is in Dol Amroth.","'South-east of the city of Dol Amroth are the ruins of Ost Amondal. With the war being over, merchants have begun to travel freely along the road that passes by them once more. However, it seems that the quieter days have led to a clutch of worms moving into the ruins.\
\
'If you are heading that way, take care. If you are inclined to lessen their numbers, even better!'","Scales in Ost Amondal","Defeat worms in Ost Amondal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The ruins of Ost Amondal are home to fierce and dangerous creatures which threaten travel on the nearby roads.","'You've done Dol Amroth a great service this day. Thank you for doing what you could to help make the roads to Dol Amroth safer.'","Return to Abartârik"},
[10663]={"Recolecta escama de sierpe fina (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta escama de sierpe robusta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva las escamas a Melthindir","Deberías recolectar escamas de las sierpes de Ram Dúath. Tales objetos pueden utilizarse para reforzar armaduras débiles y pueden ser de utilidad para los Montaraces de Esteldín.","Recolecta escama de sierpe gruesa (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Melthindir está en Esteldín.\
\
Deberías llevar las escamas que recolectaste a Melthindir.","'Gracias por este regalo, ${PLAYER}. Las escamas se aprovecharán bien para reforzar nuestra armadura.'","Se pueden encontrar sierpes en el paso occidental de Ram Dúath, al noreste de Esteldín.\
\
Deberías recolectar escamas de sierpe en Ram Dúath.","Escamas del Enemigo Terrenal","Escama robusta de sierpe recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Escamas de sierpe finas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deberías recolectar escamas de las sierpes de Ram Dúath.","Recolecta escamas de sierpe","Escamas de sierpe gruesas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10666]={"'It is time, ${PLAYER}. Let us see where the old cold-drake has come to rest.'","'We have arrived, ${PLAYER}. It may be named Skarháld in the Common Tongue, but I know it as Tharrazhâr.\
\
'I know well the history of Tharrazhâr, but I must appear to be an old dwarf, frail of mind, to Ingór and his kinsfolk... at least for now. These walls of stone and azurite... they were wrought by Longbeards! Though I cannot contest it, these Zhélruka have no claim to this fortress.\
\
'I have seen more unfriendly glances fall upon our Stout-axe companions, and so, I think we should press on once we have rested.\
\
'Yet, I have not forgotten that Zádokh Flint-eye spoke of a company of Longbeards in Tharrazhâr. He may have spoken half-truths of Vethúg Wintermind, but who can say what will we find here?'","Dori can be found in Skarháld.\
\
You have travelled to Skarháld with Dori and Company alongside Ingór, son of Vékun, and the Zhélruka. You should now speak to Dori.","Scars of Battle","Talk to Dori at Skarháld","Dori can be found at Dôm Goru.\
\
You have learned that Vethúg Wintermind crashed upon the slopes of Winterstith, one of the Grey Mountains. You should follow Dori to the end of the Bitter Scar to learn the fate of Vethúg Wintermind.","Talk to Dori at Dôm Goru","'So Vethúg has fallen upon Winterstith....\
\
'If what the Zhélruka say is true, Nori has already passed beyond the easternmost mountains to Skarháld, but Winterstith lies not far to the north. From what you have told me, Vethúg must have carved a path of frozen ruin through the foothills of the Ered Mithrin as he fell. Ah, but where does it lead? To Winterstith? To the heart of the Anvil itself? We must find out!\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}. Let us follow the Bitter Scar to its end and see what we discover!'","After learning that Vethúg Wintermind fell upon the foothills of Winterstith, Dori and Company have decided to seek the fallen cold-drake and discover some final proof of his demise."},
[10667]={"Heal wounded Rangers in Henneth Annûn (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Anborn","Wounded Rangers can be found within Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have gathered the kingsfoil and should now use it to heal the Rangers as best you can.","The Rangers of Ithilien lost many of their number in the Battle of the Pelennor Fields. Even as the War rages on, those that survived and returned to North Ithilien are in dire need of healing.","Collect kingsfoil in North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scars of the Pelennor","Kingsfoil can be found in North Ithilien to the west of Henneth Annûn.\
\
Anborn has asked you to gather kingsfoil in the hope that it might be used to heal his fellow Rangers.","'I have a favour to ask of you, my friend.\
\
'Swift was our return to Henneth Annûn at the battle's ending, and we had little time to tend the wounded. We are a hardy folk, but an injury is an injury no matter the Man. A few of our number suffer wounds still, and I hope to heal them before the battle is rejoined.\
\
'The lands of Ithilien are home to many useful herbs and flowers, and among them, kingsfoil. A mere weed in the eyes of many, I know of its restorative properties in the hands of a King... as well as those of an able healer. I have studied the kingsfoil potions and salves you bear, and I believe that you might have the skill to heal my men.\
\
'Search the foot-hills to the west, for kingsfoil has often grown on the slopes beneath Henneth Annûn. When you have gathered as much as you can bear, bring it to my men and heal them as best you can.\
\
'Be swift, ${PLAYER}.'","Healed wounded Rangers in Henneth Annûn (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The wounds of war are not easily healed, and I fear more difficult times still lie ahead... even after our victory at the White City.\
\
'Now more than ever, our resolve must not falter in the face of the Enemy.'","Anborn can be found at Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have healed the wounded Rangers as much as you were able, and should now report back to Anborn."},
[10670]={"Undisturbed cairns lie to the east of Echad Naeglanc, along the southern ridge.\
\
Naeglanc has asked you to scatter ashes before undisturbed cairns in the Bonevales.","'The ashes you spread should prevent more of these abominations emerging from the cairns. Thank you, Duvodiad.'","Scattered ashes before undisturbed cairns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scatter ashes before undisturbed cairns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have spoken with my Dunlending allies, and they seem to have a belief that spreading ashes before the cairns of the dead will prevent the wights from escaping their tombs, though I have many doubts of the veracity of this claim.\
\
'Nevertheless, I have promised that this task will be performed before I leave this place. Will you help me?\
\
'Travel due east from camp, along the southern fork. There you will find the cairns before which you should spread these ashes. When you have done this, find Mair among the cairns.'","Scatter the Ashes","Naeglanc and his allies continue to battle the foul wights arising within the Bonevales.","Seek out an ally among the cairns to the far eastern reaches of the Bonevales.\
\
You should speak with Mair","'You may find an ally among the cairns.'","'Have you scattered the ashes yet?'","Talk to Mair among the cairns"},
[10671]={"'Los trolls de piedra dejaron mucha destrucción a su paso. Probablemente consumieron o desperdiciaron la comida. Las reliquias que estaban almacenadas aquí pueden haberse roto, pero algunas pueden haber sobrevivido.\
\
Busca los barriles rotos esparcidos por los pantanos al sur, en Meluinen, y trae lo que puedas. Sin Lachenn, este claro nunca será lo que fue, pero debemos hacer lo que podamos.'","Provisiones recogidas para Lin Giliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pertenencias esparcidas","Aglardir está en Lin Giliath, el claro en la frontera de la Dehesa del Rey y Meluinen.\
\
Aglardir espera que regreses con las posesiones que recuperaste de las cajas rotas esparcidas por Meluinen.","Busca barriles rotos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Entiendo la necesidad de venganza, pero es más importante para nosotros reconstruir.'","'Que tal destrucción haya llegado a Lin Giliath es algo terrible.'","'No pensé que pudiéramos esperar tanto como lo que has traído, ${PLAYER}; te agradezco tu ayuda.\
Los trolls arruinaron o consumieron gran parte de la comida almacenada aquí, y se perdieron muchas reliquias. Lachenn lamentaría estas pérdidas tanto como nosotros lamentamos su ausencia.'","Aglardir ha asumido la difícil tarea de devolver la paz a Lin Giliath tras el ataque de los trolls de piedra.","'Lachenn querría que restauráramos este claro como era antes.'","'Busca en los pantanos al sur los barriles rotos y regresa con lo que encuentres, ${PLAYER}.'","Lleva provisiones para Lin Giliath a Aglardir","Se pueden encontrar barriles rotos esparcidos por los pantanos que llevan a Taur Gonwaith, al sur de Lin Giliath.\
\
Aglardir te ha pedido que recuperes todas las provisiones que puedas de los barriles que los trolls de piedra esparcieron por los pantanos.","'Gildor Inglorion trajo a nuestra compañía al norte para advertir de un gran mal que se agita en el sur, pero aquí solo encontramos muerte. El guardián de este claro era amigo de muchos de nosotros, un buen Elfo llamado Lachenn; fue asesinado por trolls de piedra antes de que llegáramos, y el refugio quedó en ruinas.\
\
No sé qué hizo que los trolls salieran de Taur Gonwaith, pero debemos reconstruir este lugar lo mejor que podamos, pues es lo que Lachenn nos pediría si estuviera aquí.\
\
¿Venganza? Debe esperar. Los trolls esparcieron las posesiones que estaban almacenadas aquí por todo Meluinen. Busca barriles rotos entre aquí y Taur Gonwaith, al sur. Necesito que me traigas su contenido.'"},
[10672]={"'Caron sent you to find me?\
\
'I do not understand what has happened. Will you please let any of my companions you come across know that I escaped the Dievlig's attack unscathed?\
\
'Thank you, Duvodiad.'","Caron's companions can be found east of his position, possibly near Bledhun's camp.\
\
Caron has asked you to seek out his companions and help them.","Find and talk to Eiluned","Talk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales","'Since you have found my friends, go speak with Bledhun.'","Bledhun is encamped east and slightly north of Caron's companions.\
\
Caron asked you to let Bledhun know that the few survivors of Caron's band are safe.","'Recently, a large army was gathered within the Bonevales, poised to attack the Algraig clans of Enedwaith. However, Yorath, a great Brenin among the clans, summoned the warriors south to Wulf's Cleft to ready an attack against the accursed strawheads.\
\
'Following the withdrawal of the forces, Trehéarn, Brenin of the Dievlig, began attacking all those who would assist outsiders like yourself. My band was scattered throughout the valley.\
\
'Will you seek out those who survived the attack and assist them if possible? Travel east and look among the rocks and hills for my companions. When you have found them, return to Bledhun and let him know we are safe.'","Scattered Companions","'Please, find my friends, ${PLAYER}.'","'I am glad to hear that some of our band survived the Dievlig's brutal attack. I swear that the treachery of the Dievlig shall not go unpunished.'","Several Dunlendings have been assisting members of the Grey Company as they search for a safe and secret path through Dunland. Recently, their camp was attacked, and they have hidden themselves in the valley.","Find and talk to Glundur","'Caron sent you? Then we shall speak.\
\
'We had a peaceful arrangement with the Dievlig at one time. We would bring them goods, and they would allow us to pass unimpeded northwards. Ever since the warriors marched to Wulf's Cleft, the Dievlig have become increasingly hostile to those they saw as duvodiad -- outsiders.  \
\
'They attacked our band, and we were taken unaware...only a small number of us survived.'"},
[10673]={"'It is a strange day when a duvodiad has more kindness than clansmen you have known your entire life. A very strange day, indeed.'","Talk to Andras in the Starkmoor","Aid Andras with The Broken Wheel","Aid Andras with The Smashed Crate","Andras is on the northern road leading out of Starkmoor.\
\
Andras will be pleased to hear that his cart has been repaired and most of his goods returned.","Aid Andras with The Shredded Bag","Andras' caravan has been attacked by Dragon-clan raiders. All of his valuables have been taken. They must be reclaimed if he is to make it to auction successfully.","'If we cannot get this caravan moving again with most of my goods, then I stand no chance to save my clan.'","Aid Andras with The Torn Ledger","The scattered pieces of Andras' caravan are on the northern road in Starkmoor.\
\
Andras asked you to judge the state of the caravan and retrieve whatever goods you can from the Dragon-clan raiders encamped to the east.","'I do not have anything left, I swear! The raiders before you took it all, please do not hurt me! Wait... you do not have the look of rival clansmen.\
\
'My name is Andras. I was taking this caravan to Avardin for the upcoming auction when I was beset by the Dragon-clan. They are an evil lot, and I suspect they answer to Isengard. Saruman is not the friend that he claims to be. There are few who can see through his tangled web of lies, and my clan, the People of the Ox, least of all, it seems. I seek to change that, but to do so, I must be in a position of power. Among the Ox-clan merchants that means money, which I had hoped to raise at the coming auction.\
\
'Please, I ask your help. I have not yet had time to assess the damage to my caravan. If you could check my cart and goods, then venture out against the raiders, I would be grateful. They came from the hill to the east.'","Scattered Delivery"},
[10678]={"Picos enanos recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Aún no has encontrado esos picos? ¡La roca no se va a extraer sola, ya sabes!\
\
'Como dije, busca al sur de aquí, en lo que los Lossoth llaman Norsu-hauta, el lugar al que van a morir los mamuts.'","'Saludos, ${RACE}. Soy Thórth, el jefe de la expedición a las Minas de Arrancahielo, por así decirlo.\
\
'Estábamos esperando un convoy, pero hace poco recibí la noticia de que fue atacado. Ya es bastante grave que transportara provisiones y suministros de armería, que aún podrían conseguirse localmente con algo de esfuerzo. Pero también llevaba picos de minería, y esos no se reemplazan tan fácilmente.\
\
'¿Forjar otros nuevos? ¿Tienes idea del trabajo que requiere un pico enano de calidad superior? ¿Una herramienta capaz de hender la piedra más dura y extraer de ella los metales más preciados? ¡Bah! No. Si queremos sustentarnos con la minería, necesitamos recuperar nuestros picos. Estaban esparcidos por Norsu-hauta, el cementerio de mamuts justo al sur de aquí. Recupéralos y serás recompensado.'","'¿Duramanos? ¡Desde luego que no!\
\
'${PLAYER}, esto es grave. ¡Duramanos en una zona tan remota! Habrá que erradicarlos, a todos y cada uno.\
\
'Al menos has encontrado los picos: un trabajo bien hecho, y doblemente valioso si evitaste que cayeran en manos de esos apestosos Duramanos de barba rala.'","Recoge los picos enanos que quedaron dispersos cuando fue atacado el convoy de suministros con destino a Zigilgund. Thórth dijo que probablemente se encuentren en el cementerio de mamuts cercano y sus alrededores.","Devuelve los picos enanos a Thórth","Dispersos en el cementerio","De camino al puesto avanzado enano de Zigilgund, un convoy que transportaba suministros vitales, especialmente picos de minería, fue atacado y su carga quedó dispersa.","Recoge picos enanos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has encontrado los picos enanos que Thórth te envió a recuperar. Deberías devolvérselos en Zigilgund."},
[10681]={"Habla con Adleithian en el Coloso","Saqueadores de Barad Tharsír","'Tenemos que hacer algo con los saqueadores de tumbas, ${PLAYER}. He hablado con los míos sobre este tema, pero nuestras fuerzas están dispersas. Debemos centrarnos en las amenazas a las tumbas de nuestros antepasados en Men Erain y las criptas de Annúminas, incluso aunque otras zonas corran peligro.\
\
'Al sureste de este Coloso, las brisas del Brandivino azotan las arenas del Barandalf y las dunas de hierba, pero también traen los ásperos gritos y órdenes de una banda de saqueadores de tumbas. Han establecido su campamento en las ruinas de Barad Tharsír, en la orilla opuesta del Brandivino, y temo que a no mucho tardar cruzarán el río a la pacíficas tierras del sur.\
\
'Serás recompensado si puedes derrotar a los saqueadores de tumbas en Barad Tharsír. No podemos permitirles que desvalijen y se lleven nuestro pasado, pero tampoco podemos permitirnos quedarnos de brazos cruzados.'","Adleithian está en el campamento de Montaraces en el Coloso, al noroeste del Barandalf y al oeste de Parth Aduial.\
\
Adleithian está esperando escuchar que has derrotado a los saqueadores de Barad Tharsír.","'Barad Tharsír está al sureste de este Coloso, en el Barandalf, en la orilla opuesta del Brandivino.'","'La promesa de un tesoro saca a relucir lo peor de los hombres.'","Saqueadores de tumbas derrotados en Barad Tharsír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Saqueadores de tumbas derrotados en Barad Tharsír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Barad Tharsír es más seguro gracias a tus esfuerzos.'","Derrota a los saqueadores de tumbas en Barad Tharsír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Adleithian le preocupa que los saqueadores de tumbas hayan tomado el control de las ruinas de Barad Tharsír en el Barandalf.","Barad Tharsír está al sureste del Coloso, en el Barandalf, en la orilla opuesta del Brandivino.\
\
Adleithian te ha pedido que derrotes a miembros de la banda de saqueadores que se ha apoderado de Barad Tharsír.","'¿Has expulsado a varios del contingente? ¡Me complace oírlo y saber que los saqueadores tienen menos control sobre Barad Tharsír!\
\
'¡Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}! Pero no descanses todavía, ya que solo hemos empezado a luchar por recuperar esas ruinas.'"},
[10682]={"Tu misión es viajar a Khazâda y reducir el número de chacales en la zona, así como quemar los cadáveres de los viajeros caídos que han sido profanados por las bestias.","Los carroñeros de nuestros muertos","Los chacales en los surcos se alimentan de los muertos. Es su naturaleza, pero la profanación de los aliados caídos no puede ser tolerada por la coalición.","Derrota a los chacales (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Quema los cuerpos profanados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cuerpos profanados quemados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Buen trabajo aquí. Esos chacales estaban causando muchos problemas. Regresemos a Ub Nishir.'","Chacales derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10684]={"'¿Glándulas olorosas, eh? Muy interesante... no he visto muchas criaturas como estas que posean glándulas de esta naturaleza.\
\
'Tengo una teoría, ${PLAYER}. Quizá puedan utilizarse para atraer a la amenaza que se encuentra en el centro de la plaga del Palacio de Náin, ¿no crees?'","Thórhall espera estudiar la anatomía de los gredbyg para aprender más sobre ellos y poder combatirlos mejor en el futuro.","Los gredbyg pueden encontrarse en una colmena en el Palacio de Náin.\
\
Se te ha pedido que recojas elementos de interés anatómico de los gredbyg para su estudio.","Lleva las glándulas olorosas a Thórhall","Thórhall se encuentra en el pequeño campamento enano de Lamab-dûm, en la Gran Excavación.\
\
Deberías llevarle las glándulas olorosas que has recogido para que pueda estudiarlas.","Olor de la colmena","'¿Has encontrado ya algo de interés en esos gredbyg?'","'Me gustaría aprender más sobre estos odiosos insectos mientras te encargas de expulsarlos. ¿Podrías hacerme el gran favor de traerme cualquier cosa fuera de lo común que encuentres en su anatomía?\
\
'Espero que estudiar a los gredbyg nos proporcione mejores herramientas para combatirlos.'","Has recogido una glándula olorosa de grodbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge glándulas olorosas de grodbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10685]={"Schemes and Misadventures","Deliver Shâr Bârshud's message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar","Speak with Nimasi when you are ready to go","Working with Nimasi, you have traced the banner attacks to a large camp in southern Imhûlar. Investigate the camp without being seen to discover the source of these attacks.","'We must get inside that camp and get close to that main tent in the back. I am sure whoever is in charge will be in there. If we hope to save Surâsh and end these attacks, we need to know who these people are and what they are planning.\
\
'We also must locate Surâsh, but we should only free her after we've scouted the enemy and found out all we can of their plans, as the noise and commotion may waylay any intelligence gathering.\
\
'We must be stealthy as we move. There are too many of them for a frontal assault. Are you ready?'","'I cannot believe Nimasi turned on us. This is most troubling. Most troubling. And the danger to you was grave, I must be better about who I allow into the Subuzûri.'\
\
Mizâdi appears to steel herself. A sudden coldness overtakes her face.\
\
'I don't care how many soldiers the Hûl has proffered him. He has not yet felt the might of the Subuzûri.\
\
'Very well. If it is a war he wants, then he shall have one.\
\
'But I will not allow the people of Kûr Anzar to feel war's cold comforts once more. I will meet him in open battle. War is coming, ${PLAYER}. War is coming to Imhûlar.'","Deliver Shâr Bârshud's message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.","'Are you ready? Steel yourself, we are about to go into the lair of these monsters.'","Speak with Nimasi outside the camp when you are ready to go."},
[10686]={"'Ah, has redactado algunos escritos eruditos. ¡Muy bien! Son fragmentos adicionales de conocimiento que no se perderán para nosotros cuando emprendamos nuestro viaje hacia el Oeste.\
\
'Te agradecemos, ${PLAYER}. No olvidaremos tus esfuerzos en nuestro nombre.'","Entrega tus escritos eruditos a Cachúnir en Rivendel","Cachúnir desea llevar consigo al Oeste tanto conocimiento e historia de la Tierra Media como le sea posible.","'Ha llegado a mis oídos que tus estudios sobre los misterios de la Tierra Media han avanzado considerablemente, ${PLAYER}. Durante largos siglos, quienes habitamos aquí en Rivendel hemos tenido pocas oportunidades de explorar el mundo exterior, y pronto llegará el tiempo en que partamos al Oeste junto a nuestros hermanos.\
\
'Ni siquiera aquellos de entre nosotros cuyas vidas no conocen medida pueden aspirar a comprender todos los misterios del mundo, pero deseamos llevar con nosotros al Oeste tanto conocimiento e historia como nos sea posible; si pudieras ayudarnos en este empeño, te estaríamos profundamente agradecidos.\
\
'Con tal propósito, te pediría que redactes algunos escritos eruditos para nosotros, a fin de añadirlos a nuestras bibliotecas y asegurar que adornen para siempre los estantes de la luminosa Valinor.'","Cachúnir está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Cachúnir te ha pedido que redactes escritos eruditos para preservarlos en las bibliotecas de Valinor cuando los Elfos de Rivendel zarpen hacia el Oeste.","Redacta escritos eruditos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Es cierto que hoy existen asuntos mucho más urgentes en el mundo, pues sombras oscuras se extienden por la tierra y amenazan a todos, pero por grande que sea la oscuridad, el saber que reunimos aquí escapará hacia el Lejano Oeste, donde permanecerá eternamente fuera del alcance del mal... ¡así que no subestimes la importancia de esta tarea!'","Escritos Eruditos — Introducción"},
[10687]={"'I hear that you are a scholar among your other talents, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Do you have any bits of lore that could be turned into a tome of sorts, full of knowledge that will help the people endure this cold climate?'","A skilled scholar such as yourself can help the refugees of Wildermore by scribing a tome of winter survival for them.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","'Ah, this will be very helpful, ${PLAYER}! Thank you for this; it is an honour to read of such deep knowledge of winter and survival.'","Hildelith is in Forlaw.\
\
You have scripted a tome of winter survival, and should now deliver it to Hildelith.","Hildelith has given you a recipe for a tome of winter survival.\
\
You should craft a tome of winter survival for the survivors of Wildermore's bitter winter.","Scribe a tome of winter survival for the people of Wildermore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver the tome of winter survival to Hildelith","Scripted a tome of winter survival (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scholar: Tome of Winter Survival"},
[10688]={"Collect caustic drake-whelp samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kordh Gúrat is located to the south-west of Aslíf, a level below the middle tier.\
\
Hórskur has asked for samples from each type of drakeling there.","'${PLAYER}, hello! I decided it was time to move on from studying the wildlife in Elderslade. After all, it's been many long years since my people have set foot within Gundabad!\
\
'I have been asked to study the two distinct types of drakelings in Kordh Gúrat to the south-west, a level below the middle tier. I'll need a few samples of each, but I haven't been able to get close to them myself. If you could help me procure these samples, it would be much appreciated!'","Collected caustic drake-whelp samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have collected a few samples from each type of drakeling.\
\
Hórskur is waiting for you in Aslíf on the upper tier to return with the samples.","Talk to Hórskur in Aslíf","Collect chilling drake-whelp samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'All of these samples look quite useable, and you've procured enough for me to study. Thank you for your hard work, friend!'","Hórskur's next area of study involves drakelings, but he doesn't have the samples he needs.","Collected chilling drake-whelp samples (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scholarly Study"},
[10689]={"You found the missing scholars. Orthél will want to know of their fate","You see lifeless bodies in scholar's clothing","Return to Orthél with the scholars' notes","You found scholars who have fallen to the blight. See if they have the notes Orthél mentioned to confirm they are the ones who went missing.","Scholars Gone Missing","You find crumpled notes worn by the weather","Inspect scholar","Search for missing scholars","'${CLASS}, you return, though you return alone. Were you able to find the missing scholars?'\
\
You give Orthél the scholars' notes and the unfortunate news. She begins to tear up.\
\
'This is deeply saddening news. My dear friends...\
\
'I do not know what to say but thank you for finding them. I will have the scouts recover their bodies and the recovery of their notes will ensure their sacrifice was not in vain.\
\
'I need some time. Please, take this for your efforts.'","'${CLASS}, I am in need of your help. A group of scholars left the safety of Sul Madásh to study the Pale Blight and try to discover why it is spreading faster these days.\
\
'They have yet to return. I fear the worst, but I cannot venture out and find them myself. If you can search for them and bring them home I would be most grateful.'","You find his notes safely tucked into his satchel","Orthél has asked you to find a group of scholars who went to study the blight outside of Sul Madásh and have yet to return.","Return to Orthél in Sul Madásh with the notes recovered from the missing scholars and inform her of their fates.","You find meticulous notes tucked into her robes"},
[10690]={"King Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have triumphed over Vethúg Wintermind, but at great cost. You should speak to King Thorin III.","Talk to King Thorin III","'The time draws near, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'My scouts have returned bearing ill tidings. Vethúg Wintermind, son of Hrímil Frost-heart, flies for Erebor from the Grey Mountains. He and his brood approach the mountain even now, and I have sent as many warriors as I can spare to guard the gates of Erebor. Many of the Dale-folk have sought refuge within Erebor, and the Elvenking has sent a company of his finest archers to aid us. Thikil-gundu still bears the cold scars of his ire for Durin's Folk, but I will fight to my last breath to ensure Erebor does not come to such an end. All have made ready for the coming of Vethúg, and this time, he will not take us by surprise. We of Durin's Folk will strike him down!\
\
'When you are prepared, we shall join with my warriors before the gates of Erebor.'","'It is over, ${PLAYER}. \
\
'We of Durin's Folk have claimed our vengeance upon one of our greatest foes! Vethúg Wintermind, son of Hrímil Frost-heart, fled the battle gravely wounded and shamed in defeat! Whether he lives still or not, he will not trouble my kinsfolk again!\
\
'Many fought and died bravely before the gates of Erebor, but their sacrifices were not in vain. When the time comes, they shall be laid to rest in tombs of stone.\
\
'There will be many tales told and songs sung of this day, my friend! But where has Karazgar gone? Has his plot now failed?'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Rust and Rime'</rgb>","After spending countless years within Thikil-gundu, Vethúg Wintermind, comes to seek a new vengeance upon Durin's Folk.","King Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
King Thorin III has received word that Vethúg Wintermind draws near to Erebor. When you are prepared, you should speak to the King under the Mountain.","Vástago del invierno","'The time has come, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[10691]={"You are being attacked by fell mirages, seemingly caused by Ishími, the Anguished Wind.\
\
You should defeat the mirages!","It seems that Ishími, the Anguished Wind haunts the Dawn-warden.\
\
You should find the Aradûni officer in charge of the camp.","Unusâli, Sorkamâl, and Hidâti have gone ahead to the Dawn-warden.\
\
You should continue west and find the Dawn-warden.","Talk to Unusâli","'I have met with the Aradûni before. It only makes sense that I go with you. They are yet another people who seek justice against Ordâkh. I trust my people will be good hosts to Mizâdi and her soldiers while I am gone.\
\
'To quickly reach the Aradûni at the Dawn-warden while avoiding the Ordâkhai, we must cross the dry lake-bed. It is a treacherous journey, full of venomous reptiles, wild drakes, not to mention the oppressive heat. In recent months, it has become even more dangerous. There is something... unnatural out there, harrying any who cross. Because of this, we must also travel with Hidâti, our elder Kâparai mystic. She will keep us safe.\
\
'The three of us will go ahead and meet you out there. Look for the dragon bones.'","Unusâli and Sorkamâl will be travelling to the Dawn-warden with you to meet with the Aradûni.\
\
You should talk to Unusâli.","Defeat the mirages","The wind picks up, and with it comes the whispers...","You once again hear the whispering of the Anguished Wind","'We have secured Ahâba and the aid of the Beltáni, but now an even greater diplomatic challenge must be tackled. To the west, the soldiers of Aradûn gather. It is time for my new envoy to prove her worth!\
\
'Unusâli has volunteered to travel with you and Sorkamâl and provide an introduction with the Aradûni stationed at the Dawn-warden. I trust her to keep you safe while you cross the scorched lake-bed. Numûru and I will stay here and organize our soldiers as they arrive.'","Tierra Quemada","To make contact with the Aradûni, you and Mizâdi's envoys must travel west, and cross the perilous dry lake-bed.","Continue to the Dawn-warden","Find Unusâli, Sorkamâl, and Hidâti","Talk to Captain Hanâbu","Unusâli, Sorkamâl, and Hidâti have gone ahead.\
\
You should meet them near Ushumût, the Grave of Serpents.","'I was not expecting visitors... but you do not look like Ordâkhai. Who are you, stranger?'\
\
You explain that you and your fellows are envoys representing Shâra Mizâdi and Renewed Hamât.\
\
'You are with Shâra Mizâdi? Word of her valour has reached us even in Aradûn! Please, make yourself at home in our camp! Though, even we do not find it comfortable. Not with that accursed howling wind!'","'There you are, ${PLAYER}! Unusâli says we are about half-way through our journey. It cannot end soon enough, I say! I did not anticipate tromping through dangerous drake-infested wasteland when I volunteered to serve as Mizâdi's diplomat....\
\
'Wait... do you hear that? Is that the... wind?'","Ishími departs, and the whispering ceases"},
[10692]={"Travel to Dul Râkh","'Greetings, ${CLASS}.\
\
'I gather that you have returned from Dul Râkh successful in your task. I thank you for your help in this fight.\
\
'The Anâkhi and their beasts will be less of a threat for now.'","Nâmi has asked you thin out the number of scorpions in Dul Râkh to the west.","Reached Dul Râkh entrance","Return to Nâmi","Scorpion Extermination","Defeat scorpions inside the cave at Dul Râkh for Nâmi at the Dumûri camp in Urash Dâr.","Return to Nâmi in Urash Dâr and let her know you have thinned the number of scorpions in Dul Râkh.","Defeat scorpions in Dul Râkh cave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nâmi has asked you to travel to the cave in Dul Râkh and thin the number of scorpions in the area.","Defeated scorpions in Dul Râkh cave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${CLASS}, I am glad to see you here. We here have been battling with the Anâkhi in their cave, Dul Râkh, nearby.\
\
'I ask that you help us to turn the tide as we are needed in many places since Utug-bûr was opened. If you can, go to Dul Râkh and find their cave. Inside you must cleanse it of these vicious scorpions that the Anâkhi worship.'"},
[10694]={"Dulgurz se encuentra en Athmadhul, al sureste de Mekhem-bizru.\
\
Ótam te habló de un jinete de huargos particularmente peligroso, Dulgurz, que ya no debe ser permitido vagar por el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío.","'¡Por fin una noche en la que puedo dormir tranquilo, sin el miedo de escuchar esos pasos acercándose a mí! Te lo agradezco.'","'Necesitamos tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Un jinete de huargos nos ataca cada noche, justo al ponerse el sol. No podemos hacer nada para detenerlo, ninguna trampa ha funcionado. Nos está matando lentamente uno por uno.\
\
'Creo que Alrekur le disparó con una flecha la última vez que vino, porque no lo hemos visto durante un par de días, pero no tengo dudas de que su furia está creciendo mientras las heridas de su huargo sanan.\
\
'Dulgurz, el jinete de huargos, debe ser detenido. No podemos seguir viviendo así, sin saber cuándo atacará el jinete de huargos la próxima vez. Dirígete al sureste, a Athmadhul, debería estar recuperándose allí. Pero ten cuidado, la flecha solo lo rozó: no lo subestimes.'","Dulgurz ha sido derrotado","Dulgurz ha aterrorizado a los enanos del Valle del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío desde que establecieron su campamento.","Ótam se encuentra en Mekhem-bizru, al noroeste de Athmadhul.\
\
Ótam querrá saber sobre la derrota de Dulgurz.","Derrota a Dulgurz","Habla con Ótam en Mekhem-bizru","'Por favor. Si Dulgurz nos ataca de nuevo, estoy seguro de que será nuestro último.'","Azote del Valle"},
[10696]={"Maedlathron está en Gwingris, a cierta distancia al noroeste del campamento abandonado.\
\
Deberías llevar la bolsa con hierba para pipa que has encontrado a Maedlathron.","Investiga el camino de la Comunidad","Después de algo de tiempo, Elrond Medio-Elfo envió exploradores a los campos de Eregion para seguir el camino de la Comunidad que partió de Rivendel y asegurarse de que no quedaran signos de su paso que el Enemigo pudiera encontrar.","Bolsa de hierba para pipa recuperada","Habla con Maedlathron en Gwingris","'¿Dices que has encontrado esta bolsa en el campamento? Contiene una piza de hierba para pipa de los hobbits.\
\
'Podría ser que uno de los medianos o el enano la dejara caer. Este descuido podría costarles caro.'","El campamento está enclavado en la base de unos grandes pedruscos, a cierta distancia al sureste de Gwingris, más allá de Sâd Rechu, al sur del camino hacia Pembar.\
\
Maedlathron te ha pedido que busques un lugar que pueda haber sido el campamento utilizado por la Comunidad. Cualquier signo del paso de la Comunidad debe ser eliminado.","Inspeccionando el camino","'Ve al campamento al sureste de aquí y busca cualquier rastro del paso de la Comunidad. Si encuentras algo, deshazte de ello antes de que el Enemigo caiga sobre el campamento.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Mis compañeros y yo hemos llegado recientemente desde Rivendel por orden del maestro Elrond. Teme que los espías del Enemigo puedan seguir los pasos de la Comunidad que partió de Imladris hace poco. La Comunidad que lleva una pesada carga y nos ha ordenado ir tras ellos para comprobar si han dejado atrás algún rastro de paso.\
\
'Para este fin, muchos de mis compañeros se han adelantado para explorar el terreno. Está claro que Aragorn, hijo de Arathorn, todavía viaja con la Comunidad, ya que apenas hemos encontrado rastro. Han encendido pocas hogueras por miedo a llamar la atención del Enemigo, lo que está bien. Sin embargo, uno de mis exploradores me ha informado de que ha visto restos de una vieja hoguera al sureste de aquí.\
\
'Si pudieras, busca ese campamento y averigua si hay más rastros que hayan dejado que pueda revelar la composición de la Comunidad. La hoguera está lejos hacia el sureste, más allá de Sâd Rechu, enclavada entre unas piedras.'"},
[10697]={"You have arrived at the fourth patrol point","The fifth patrol point is east of the fourth.\
\
Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.","'What is this you say? You found a village of strange, halfling-like creatures? But they are not of the halfling people? I must think on this.'","The Rangers of the Grey Company seek to ensure the secrecy of their purpose and their passage through Enedwaith.","Scout the fourth patrol point","The second patrol point is north-west of the first.\
\
Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.","Scout the fifth patrol point","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. It has been long since we spoke with each other at the Haunted Inn of Audaghaim. I must confess that I am relieved to be gone from that place.\
\
'I understand that you are aware of our purpose and would ask for your assistance. It is of utmost importance that our passage remains hidden from the eyes of the Enemy, and for that purpose are we here in the Gloomglens.\
\
'Will you scout the paths of the Gloomglens and learn whether any enemies patrol these lands? Return here when you have completed your patrol and let me know what you have found.'","Scouring the Wood","You have discovered a village of strange creatures","Scout the first patrol point","You have arrived at the third patrol point","You have arrived at the first patrol point","The third patrol point is south-west of the second.\
\
Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.","You have arrived at the second patrol point","'Have you finished your patrol already?'","The first patrol point is north-east of Echad Idhrenfair.\
\
Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.","Scout the third patrol point","Scout the second patrol point","Idhrenfair is at Echad Idhrenfair in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith, north-west of the fifth patrol point.\
\
You should return to Idhrenfair with news of your discoveries.","The fourth patrol point is south of the third.\
\
Idhrenfair has asked you to patrol the paths of the Gloomglens with instructions to keep an eye out for any signs of the Enemy's minions.","Talk to Idhrenfair at Echad Idhrenfair"},
[10698]={"Encuentra la colina al sudeste de las Piedras Aullantes mencionada por Eleri.","'¿Podría otra partida de Uruks permanecer oculta a nuestras torres de vigilancia hasta que estuviera prácticamente sobre nosotros, como ocurrió antes? Más allá de las Piedras Aullantes, hacia el sudeste, una colina se alza sobre la llanura. ¿Puedo pedirte que vayas a esa colina y <rgb=#00FF00>mires</rgb> a la distancia? Puede que no veas nada... pero incluso eso será bueno que lo sepa.'","Desde este punto de observación, la cuenca por la que discurre el Viejo Camino del Sur parece estar en gran medida tranquila.","Eleri te pidió que <rgb=#00FF00>miraras</rgb> a la distancia desde la colina al sudeste de las Piedras Aullantes, al este de Musgovilla.","Habla con Eleri en el lado este de Musgovilla.","'¿Todo parece tranquilo? Eso es bueno, ${PLAYER}, pero no bajaré la guardia. Hay más lugares que vigilar, pues hay varios puntos desde los que los Uruks u otros de su calaña podrían aproximarse.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Mira</rgb> desde la cima de la colina al sudeste de las Piedras Aullantes.","Explora más allá de las Piedras Aullantes.","Preocupada por el reciente ataque de los Uruks contra Musgovilla, Eleri quiere que vigiles si hay más de estas criaturas más allá del cercano campamento de lobos.","Esta parece ser la colina que Eleri describió.","Eleri está en el lado este de Musgovilla, a la vista de la puerta.","'Quiero que entiendas algo, ${PLAYER}, algo que puede ser difícil de creer dadas las circunstancias de la noche pasada. Musgovilla es un pueblo tranquilo. Siempre ha sido un pueblo tranquilo. Los inviernos pueden ser duros si no llenamos los almacenes con suficiente alimento, pero han pasado muchos años desde la última vez que la gente de Musgovilla falló en sus preparativos.\
\
'Por lo general solo hemos tenido que preocuparnos por que los lobos de las Piedras Aullantes se vuelvan demasiado audaces y se acerquen a las murallas, pero los Uruks sueltos en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes lo han cambiado todo. ¿Qué haremos si otro capitán de guerra como Madthrug trae su banda a Musgovilla? ¿Podrían permanecer ocultos de nuestras torres de vigilancia hasta estar casi sobre nosotros, como lo hicieron antes?\
\
'Más allá de las Piedras Aullantes, hacia el sudeste, una colina se alza sobre la llanura. ¿Puedo pedirte que vayas a esa colina y <rgb=#00FF00>mires</rgb> a la distancia? Puede que no veas nada... pero incluso eso será bueno que lo sepa.'"},
[10699]={"'I suppose I should be grateful for the kindness of any willing to aid a wounded man, even if it is from a duvodiad. I received my wounds when a small raiding-party from Gwâl Draig attacked and slew my fellows.\
\
'On the southern shore of the river stands an encampment that these duhirun -- these blackguards -- call home. My party was sent to scout this camp to see if we could rout them from the area. The Draig-lûth butchered the entirety of our sister clan, the Turch-lûth, and now seek our demise as well. Our former brethren from Dunland call us Algraig -- Outliers -- and have ever been our enemies.\
\
'Perhaps you will scout this camp for me? Seek out the entrances and dispatch any guards that you encounter. The camp can be found by following the southern shore of the river to the north and heading due east.'","Scouted the eastern entrance of Gwâl Draig","Defeated Draig-lûth guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scout the eastern entrance of Gwâl Draig","Talk to Gronu at his camp","'The Draig-lûth are a vile and merciless people, and these seem more so than their brethren in Dunland.'","Scouted the western entrance of Gwâl Draig","Scout the southern entrance of Gwâl Draig","The Draig-lûth have created a village on the northern shore of the river, presenting a danger to travellers in the area.","'It is good to hear that Gwâl Draig is indeed the main encampment for the most vile Draig-lûth. Perhaps when more hunters emerge from my clan, the Uch-lûth, we can mount an attack upon these duhirun.\
\
'Thank you for your assistance, Duvodiad.'","Defeat Draig-lûth guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scout the western entrance of Gwâl Draig","Gwâl Draig lies on the southern shore of the river, north-east of Gronu's camp.\
\
Gronu has asked you to scout out the entrances to the camp and dispatch any guards you might encounter.","Gronu is at his camp south-east of Gwâl Draig.\
\
You should seek out Gronu and let him know what lies within the village of Gwâl Draig.","Scouted the southern entrance of Gwâl Draig","Scout Gwâl Draig"},
[10700]={"Explora las Puertas de Tharbad.","Este parece ser el lugar que Eleri describió.","Eleri te pidió que <rgb=#00FF00>mires</rgb> en busca de la marca de la Mano Blanca en las puertas de Tharbad, al noroeste de Musgovilla. Fue muy insistente en que evitaras el combate si los enemigos parecían demasiado peligrosos.","<rgb=#00FF00>Mira</rgb> en las puertas de Tharbad en busca de la marca de la Mano Blanca.","Habla con Eleri en el lado este de Musgovilla.","Los duros gritos de los Orcos pueden oírse dentro de Tharbad, pero no ves señales de la Mano Blanca.","'¿Se ha convertido Tharbad en una guarida de Uruks? ¿Es de allí de donde vino la banda de saqueadores de Madthrug? Esta, entonces, es mi petición peligrosa. Te pido que vayas a las puertas de Tharbad y <rgb=#00FF00>mires</rgb> si hay algún indicio del emblema que llevaba: la marca de la Mano Blanca. Ten cuidado, porque si Tharbad está realmente en manos de fuerzas malignas, quizá sea mejor que pases #-1:{inadvertido[m]|inadvertida[f]} y no entres en combate.\
\
'Tharbad está al noroeste de Musgovilla. Ve solo hasta la puerta, ojo, y no más allá.'","Encuentra las puertas de Tharbad, al noroeste de Musgovilla.","'No me sorprende que haya Orcos arrastrándose por todo Tharbad, pero es bueno oír que no viste la marca de la Mano Blanca mientras explorabas cerca de la puerta. La calaña de los Orcos siempre es una amenaza para los Pueblos Libres, pero fue la organización revelada por la partida de guerra de Madthrug lo que más me preocupaba. Podemos ocuparnos de Orcos, pues ya lo hemos hecho antes, pero los Uruks de la Mano Blanca me parecieron distintos.\
\
'¡Gracias por ayudar a aliviar mis temores con estas misiones de exploración, ! Siempre serás ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} en Musgovilla.'","Eleri tiene ahora una petición más peligrosa para ti, pero si Tharbad sirve de campamento para los Uruks que asaltaron Musgovilla, quiere saberlo.","'Tengo una petición más para ti, , y entonces estaré satisfecha. Esta puede ser más peligrosa que tus exploraciones anteriores, y si dudas en aceptar esta tarea lo entenderé.\
\
'La antigua ciudad de Tharbad está al noroeste de Musgovilla. No ha sido el próspero centro comercial que fue en los días de reinos anteriores durante cientos de años, y ha estado abandonada desde que las aguas de las inundaciones se llevaron los últimos de sus grandes puentes...'\
\
Eleri alza una ceja.\
\
'Abandonada por buena gente, . ¿Se ha convertido en una guarida de Uruks? ¿Es de allí de donde vino la banda saqueadora de Madthrug? Esta, entonces, es mi petición peligrosa. Te pido que vayas a las puertas de Tharbad y <rgb=#00FF00>mires</rgb> si hay algún indicio del emblema que llevaba: la marca de la Mano Blanca. Ten cuidado, porque si Tharbad está realmente en manos de fuerzas malignas, quizá sea mejor que pases #-1:{inadvertido[m]|inadvertida[f]} y no entres en combate.\
\
'Tharbad está al noroeste de Musgovilla. Ve solo hasta la puerta, ojo, y no más allá.'","Eleri está en el lado este de Musgovilla, a la vista de la puerta."},
[10701]={"Eleri cree que el Viejo Camino del Sur es una bendición para Musgovilla, pero si acelera el avance de los Uruks a través de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, quiere saberlo.","'¿Seguirías el sendero que parte desde la puerta norte de Musgovilla hasta que se una con el camino que corre de este a oeste a través de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes? Una vez allí, te agradecería que <rgb=#00FF00>miraras</rgb>, como hiciste antes. Deberías poder ver a bastante distancia, y si hay más saqueadores por la zona quizá logres divisarlos.'","Eleri te pidió que <rgb=#00FF00>miraras</rgb> a la distancia en la intersección del Viejo Camino del Sur con el sendero que sale de Musgovilla por la puerta norte de la aldea.","'¿Dices que no viste señales de partidas de guerra Uruk a lo largo del camino? Son buenas noticias, pues significa que el camino sigue siendo una bendición para Musgovilla y no una maldición, como temía que pudiera llegar a ser.\
\
'Ese camino ha sido clave para la supervivencia de Musgovilla durante toda mi vida, ${PLAYER}. La parte que conocemos comienza en Tharbad y, aunque el propio camino está roto en algunos tramos y oculto por la vegetación, atraviesa la Ciénaga de los Cisnes y continúa hacia Enedwaith. Desde allí entra en las Tierras Pardas, conduce a través del Paso de Rohan y sigue hasta Gondor. Dicen que pasa por Minas Tirith y que finalmente termina en una ciudad portuaria en la costa, aunque nunca he viajado por esas tierras.\
\
'Al norte de Tharbad el camino tiene otro nombre. Se llama el Camino Verde, y solo la gente de Meneldir parece recordar cuando este y nuestro propio Viejo Camino del Sur eran uno y el mismo: el Camino Norte-Sur entre los reinos de Arnor y Gondor. Eso fue hace mucho tiempo, incluso según sus cálculos.'","Algunos tramos del camino están cubiertos de maleza y carecen de adoquines, pero no ves señales de saqueadores.","Habla con Eleri en el lado este de Musgovilla.","'Conoces el camino que atraviesa la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, por supuesto. Comienza de este lado de la antigua ciudad de Tharbad y se extiende hacia el este, pasando por Aguaestancada, hasta llegar a Enedwaith. No lo recorren tantos viajeros como antaño, pero Musgovilla sigue siendo un lugar de descanso protegido para quienes pasan por aquí. ¿Podría también servir para acelerar a los Uruks y a otros de su calaña en sus incursiones?\
\
'¿Seguirías el sendero que parte desde la puerta norte de Musgovilla hasta que se une con este camino? Una vez allí, te agradecería que <rgb=#00FF00>miraras</rgb>, como hiciste antes. Deberías poder ver tanto hacia el este como hacia el oeste a bastante distancia, y si hay más saqueadores por la zona, quizá logres verlos.'","Explora el Viejo Camino del Sur.","Eleri está en el lado este del pueblo, a la vista de la puerta.","Encuentra la intersección del sendero que sale por la puerta norte de Musgovilla y el Viejo Camino del Sur.","Este cruce de caminos es el que Eleri describió.","<rgb=#00FF00>Mira</rgb> a la distancia en la intersección del sendero que sale por la puerta norte de Musgovilla y el Viejo Camino del Sur."},
[10703]={"Ânug-stazg can be found east and slightly north of Mithechad.\
\
Perindúr has asked you to scout out the path leading into Ânug-stazg and the camp-fires at the edges of the camp.","Scout Ânug-stazg","Scouted the western camp-fire","Talk to Perindúr at Mithechad","Scout the western camp-fire","The Orc-camp at Ânug-stazg is the primary sentry-post for the Enemy's forces in the Ashenslades.","Scout the eastern camp-fire","Scout the path to Ânug-stazg","'It appears as if the camp is weaker than we expected. Our hope now is that reinforcements do not arrive soon, or this position may be lost.\
\
'The time may be near to strike out against Ânug-stazg.'","Scouted the eastern camp-fire","'Have you travelled east to Ânug-stazg and scouted the outskirts of the camp?'","Perindúr is at Mithechad, west and slightly south of Ânug-stazg.\
\
You should return to Perindúr with your report of the Enemy's forces at Ânug-stazg.","'A smaller Orc-camp, known as Ânug-stazg, lies to the east of here. It is the primary sentry-post for the forces of Dol Guldur in the Ashenslades. What other forces are stationed there is currently unknown.\
\
'There are three points at Ânug-stazg we would like you to scout: the western camp-fire, the southern path that leads into the camp, and the eastern camp-fire. All of these are found along the edge of Ânug-stazg. Perhaps from those vantage points, you may be able to learn something of the camp's strength.\
\
'When you have completed your patrol, return to me with your report.'","Scouted the path to Ânug-stazg"},
[10704]={"'Wigfast es un explorador audaz, pero necesitará tu ayuda si quiere regresar con vida.'","Encuentra a Wigfast, el explorador en Gazatmur","'¡Ah! ¿Te envía Slagvi? Justo a tiempo — estaba a punto de aventurarme ahí dentro y empezar a cortar cabezas de trasgo yo solo, ¡aunque no estoy bien equipado para algo así!'","Exploración avanzada","Los trasgos han establecido un gran campamento en Gazatmur, lo cual preocupa a los enanos del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.","'Bien, ${PLAYER}, como puedes ver incluso desde aquí, hay un gran campamento de trasgos ahí abajo en Gazatmur, hacia el nordeste. No tenemos fuerzas suficientes para expulsarlos ahora mismo, pero me gustaría que bajaras allí y te unieras a Wigfast, que ha ido a explorar el campamento.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que Wigfast agradecerá ayuda para evaluar la situación allí abajo. Es valiente al ir a explorar, pero no creo que pueda hacer mucho por sí solo.'","El campamento de trasgos se encuentra bajo el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Gazatmur. Se pueden encontrar buenos puntos de observación al norte y al sur del campamento.\
\
Slagvi te ha pedido que explores un gran campamento de trasgos. Te advirtió que evitaras ser visto."},
[10705]={"'¿Así que tampoco han encontrado aún la forma de entrar? Eso juega a nuestro favor.'","Ves unos pocos rastros, pero nada reciente. Parece que los saqueadores de tumbas tampoco han logrado entrar","Encuentra las ruinas de Arthobel","'Creo que un antiguo pariente mío vivió una vez en Arthobel, pero los registros que lo demuestran se perdieron hace mucho tiempo.'","Arthobel está al suroeste del campamento de los Montaraces en el Camino de los Reyes.\
\
Maladan te ha pedido que explores las ruinas de Arthobel para ver si los saqueadores de tumbas las están usando activamente.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> a tu alrededor en busca de signos de actividad","Explorando Arthobel","Has localizado las ruinas de Arthobel","Arthobel se asienta en lo alto de las colinas sobre el Camino de los Reyes. Si los saqueadores lograran entrar, les proporcionaría un punto de vista muy estratégico.","Habla con Maladan","'He estado observando a los saqueadores mientras se movían por las colinas sobre nosotros. Parecen centrarse en dos ruinas principales, Tham Sarch y Tham Laegamon. Por mis días de niño jugando en esas colinas conozco una tercera ruina: Arthobel.\
\
'La torre que se erige allí sería una posición muy estratégica. Podrías ver claramente el Camino de los Reyes debajo de ti, observar las aguas del Baranduin al sureste y, en un día despejado, ver Tinnudir.\
\
'Lo último que recuerdo es que las pesadas puertas de ese lugar estaban bien selladas, y nadie había estado dentro en muchos años. Te pido que te aventures hacia el suroeste, subiendo a las colinas, hasta la entrada y <rgb=#FF0000>mires</rgb> a tu alrededor para ver si notas alguna actividad reciente allí.'","Maladan está en el campamento de los Montaraces en el Camino de los Reyes.\
\
Maladan se alegrará de saber que los saqueadores de tumbas no han conseguido acceder a Arthobel."},
[10706]={"Scout the south-east gate","'If we are to mount an assault on the camp, it would be good for us to know its defences. Upokhir has already drawn a detailed map for me, but you are more experienced with fighting alongside Gondorians. As someone familiar with our tactics and strengths, I would appreciate your perspective. Scout Pahor Boha's entrances and report back to me on what you find.'","The south-west gate has a commanding view of the area. Any attackers will be easily spotted.","Torthril has asked you to scout the Pahor Boha's entrances.\
\
Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.","Scouting Pahor Boha","The south-east gate faces trees and large boulders. These obstacles could be used to hide an approaching force.","Talk to Torthril","You to have scouted Pahor Boha's defences and should report your success.\
\
Talk to Torthril in Ost Arndír.","Scout the south-west gate","Torthril has asked you to scout the defences at Pahor Boha.","'Thank you for report. I will review your findings with my lieutenants and adjust our plans accordingly.'"},
[10707]={"Scout Parth Daenath (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Thranduil","Thranduil can be found at Echad-in-Edhil.\
\
You should talk to Thranduil.","Scouting Parth Daenath","'You did well in this task, but it was only a start. We are known to the enemy. Now we will take that reminder and turn it into a weapon of fear.'","Thranduil has asked you to scout Parth Daenath.","Thranduil requires more knowledge of the Enemies' movements throughout the Corpse-fields of Parth Daenath.","'We have secured much of Parth Daenath, but Sauron's forces still grasp at the edge of the Corpse-fields. I require more men to patrol and scout Parth Daenath. Once you have done this, report back to me. We must make certain our presence is not forgotten if we are to win this war. Let us remind Sauron that he remains opposed, even after so many years of siege.'","Scouted Parth Daenath (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[10708]={"Oathbreakers have appeared across Parth Celebrant. Medwine has told you to scout the camps to the east and west of Idmar's encampment to understand the force they face.","As you scout the west camp, you notice a white tree adorning the garb of the Oathbreakers","Scout the northern Oathbreaker camp","As you scout the east camp, you note a moderately-sized force of Oathbreakers","Talk to Medwine","'I had hoped it would not come to this, but you already know the most of it. Parth Celebrant has been overrun by Oathbreakers, but we have no idea who they are or why they have returned. \
\
'These spirits only appeared here days ago, and my men and I were sent to investigate before things got out of hand. The folk of Stangard were not informed of this matter, but now we have a problem just outside our gates.\
\
'If you would help, I have a task for you. Head to the north and east of the road. One of my men, Medwine, is scouting them out. Speak with him and see if you can find out who these spirits truly are.'","Talk to Idmar","Scouting Shadows","Scout the Oathbreaker camp to the west of Idmar's encampment","'Speak with Medwine and learn if he has discovered anything about the Oathbreakers.'","Medwine is camped outside the Oathbreaker camp in northern Parth Celebrant.\
\
Idmar has advised you to seek out Medwine.","Scout the Oathbreaker camp to the east of Idmar's encampment","Your discovery of a crazed Oathbreaker and the attacks upon his own party have caused Idmar a great deal of concern.","'A white tree? Both you and Medwine have seen this? I do not believe it... they must be Men of Gondor!\
\
'Why would they have returned? The battle fought on this field long ago was a victory... a victory that granted to our kindred all of Rohan. For what purpose would these spirits return?\
\
'This is very puzzling, ${PLAYER}. Give me a moment to consider our situation.'","'Idmar sent you? We have little time for introductions. I, along with another scout, were sent to observe the shades and discover their origins.\
\
'I... think we have found ourselves out of position. The Oathbreakers are needlessly violent... I was chased away this morning when I moved closer -- they wear a white tree, such as the Men of Gondor. But how can that be?\
\
'That is a matter for another time. I do not know what brings you to Parth Celebrant, but if Idmar sent you, you must be willing to help. Please, scout the camps to the east and west of Idmar's camp... we need to know how many of these spirits we are dealing with.'","Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should return to Idmar with news of your discoveries.","As you approach the nearby Oathbreakers, you hear the voice of a man coming from somewhere nearby"},
[10710]={"'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. I have been asked by the Elves of Rivendell to lend them aid in patrolling the furthest reaches of the Trollshaws and keep an eye on the encroachments of the Enemy.\
\
'I need you to head into the area of Tâl Bruinen and scout out the positions that might be used by the Enemy or their allies.'","Scouting Tâl Bruinen","'So, the Gauredain have appeared in Tâl Bruinen, as well? The Elves will not be pleased when they learn of this, if they have not already.\
\
'They would never have moved so far afield save at the prodding of the Enemy -- but what their part is in the greater scheme, I cannot yet say.'","Scouted the Forgotten Monument","Scout the Forgotten Monument","Echad Candelleth lies in Tâl Bruinen, south of the Trollshaws, far to the south and east of the North Downs.\
\
Handarod has asked you to begin your patrol at the camp of Echad Candelleth.","Echad Gauradan lies in Tâl Bruinen, south of the Trollshaws, far to the south and east of the North Downs.\
\
Handarod has asked you to scout the encampment of Echad Gauradan.","The Forgotten Monument lies in the eastern area of Tâl Bruinen, south of the Trollshaws, far to the south and east of the North Downs.\
\
Handarod has asked you to scout the overlook marked by the Forgotten Monument. It provides a commanding view of the surrounding lands.","Echad Candelleth lies in Tâl Bruinen, south of the Trollshaws, far to the south and east of the North Downs.\
\
Handarod has asked you to complete your patrol by returning to Echad Candelleth.","Handarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the west and north of Tâl Bruinen.\
\
You should report to Handarod and tell him what you have seen in the wilds of Tâl Bruinen.","Scouted Echad Candelleth","Scouted Echad Gauradan","Scout Echad Candelleth","Scout Echad Gauradan","Talk to Handarod","Handarod is concerned for the safety of the hidden valley of Rivendell."},
[10711]={"Echad Sûl is a small hill that lies north of Weathertop in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree-land.\
\
Nidgyl has asked you to scout the ruins of Echad Sûl.","Scouted Weatherfoot","Scouting Weathertop","Scout Glumhallow","Scouted Echad Sûl","'The Enemy is on the move... do you know of the hill called Weathertop overlooking the western Lone-lands? The Orcs have raised a number of small camps around its base and launch raids upon travellers and villages from them.\
\
'I need you to scout the area of Weathertop and keep an eye on the strength of the Enemy's forces there. We must watch for an opportunity to strike against them should they lower their guard.\
\
'Weathertop lies far to the east of here.'","'The Orcs continue to maintain their camps, do they? No matter for now, their forces in the Lone-lands are too small to represent a real threat -- yet.\
\
'We will keep an eye on them, though. The Enemy would not have sent them so far afield without reason. They will make their move soon enough.'","Nidgyl is concerned with the movements of goblins, Orcs, and brigands in the surrounding areas.","Weathertop is in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree-land.\
\
Nidgyl has asked you to climb Weathertop itself to examine the surrounding lands.","Scouted Glumhallow","Weatherfoot lies far to the east of Bree-land, near Weathertop in the Lone-lands.\
\
Nidgyl has asked you to scout the Orc-encampment at Weatherfoot.","Nidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Weathertop.\
\
You should report to Nidgyl and tell them what you have seen from the heights of Weathertop.","Scout Weatherfoot","Scout Echad Sûl","Talk to Nidgyl","Scouted Weathertop","Glumhallow is far to the east of Bree-land, near Weathertop in the Lone-lands.\
\
Nidgyl has asked you to scout the Orc-encampment at Glumhallow.","Scout Weathertop"},
[10712]={"Scout the southern section of the camp","Numerous foul smelling cages and siege structures","Zarkul-sulûn is in southern Elderslade.\
\
Laugi has asked you to scout Zarkul-sulûn.","Gunvald is in Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade.\
\
You have enough information to make a report to Gunvald.","Scouting for the Scout","An army would be spotted from far off by anyone in this watch-tower","More cages, supplies, and a dead end","Examine the back of the camp","Another watch-tower, and plentiful supplies","The scout Laugi needs assistance completing his survey of the nearby enemy camp.","Scout the lower camp","Talk to Gunvald","Scout the east portion of the camp","'If Gunvald sent you, then he must trust you. I must return to our base and get this scratch tended to or my wife will never let me hear the end of it.\
\
'I was on my way to scout the camp ahead when I was beset upon by the enemy. Will you go scout ahead and report your findings to Gunvald?'","'Ah, you return! Laugi told me you were checking into the camp for us. My thanks. What have you found?'"},
[10713]={"Handelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should return to Handelen with the report of your patrol.","Patrol the third point in northern Gathbúrz","Talk to Handelen at Thangúlhad","Patrol the first point in northern Gathbúrz","Handelen fears that the Orcs are mustering their forces in the northern reaches of Gathbúrz.","Patrol the second point in northern Gathbúrz","Scouting in Force","'There are still a lot of Orcs down there? I expect there are still hundreds of stragglers wandering back into the encampments after fleeing from the force of our initial assault.\
\
'The real problems will start when the first elements of that eastern army begin to arrive... we must be ready for them.'","'The Orcs of Gathbúrz are a shattered force, but we must continue our forays against them to keep them from regrouping. I am asking the Malledhrim and our allies to mount frequent patrols through the area north of here, skirting their fortifications and engaging any enemies attempting to reinforce those positions.\
\
'Are you up for the task, ${PLAYER}? If so, I bid you good fortune. Return to me when your patrol is complete.'","Patrol the fourth point in northern Gathbúrz","'Our survival here depends upon performing routine patrols to sight the approach of the Enemy.'","You have scouted this area","The first point is north-east of Thangúlhad. The second point is to the north-west of the first, direcdly north of Kúfuzg. The third point is directly north of Thangúlhad, a little south of Búrzkala. The fourth point is just north-west of Thangúlhad.\
\
You should scout the waypoints of the patrol that Handelen has asked you to undertake and defeat any enemies you might find there."},
[10714]={"Complete Quest 'Creatures of the Mire'","Legolas has asked you to scout areas in the Noman-lands and destroy any blighted wildlife you encounter.","Complete Quest 'Culling the Blighted'","Scout the Northern Noman-lands","Scouted the Northern Noman-lands","'${PLAYER}, I look out upon this land and feel a deep sorrow. Where Ithilien is beautiful, the Wastes are blighted and cursed. Evil's taint seeks always to spread, and we must not let that happen. Go out into the Noman-lands and take a closer look. Remove the blight wherever you find it.'","Return to Legolas","Scout the Southern Noman-lands","'Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}. It may seem like your efforts mean little, but I have hope that one day, whether we be here to see it or not, this land will return to its original splendor.'","Complete two quests for Legolas while exploring the Noman-lands.\
\
Legolas has asked you to scout areas in the Noman-lands and destroy any blighted wildlife you find.","Explora la Ciénaga de los Muertos","Scouting the Blight","Legolas can be found at the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
You should return to Legolas.","Find three survey locations around the Noman-lands.\
\
Legolas has asked you to scout areas in the Noman-lands and destroy any blighted wildlife you find.","Scouted the Dead Marshes","Scouted the Southern Noman-lands"},
[10715]={"Scout the north-eastern side of the Circle of Sorrow","The withered gardens smell of rot and decay","The ancient theatre is now a torture pit, a den of great evil","Find the Song-house of Lindalírë","Damrod wishes to patrol the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul to assess the difficulties that the Rangers of Ithilien will have to overcome.","Eyes of the Dead watch your every step","Shadows cast from above darken the Morgul stone","Damrod has asked you to scout the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.","The ancient forge creaks and ghostly sounds echo throughout","Damrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul.\
\
You should talk to Damrod.","Talk to Damrod in Barad Orhant","Scout the western side of the Circle of Sorrow","Find Búrzangh, the Shrouded Forge","'You have learned a great deal about the Circle of Sorrow... and most of it unpleasant. It would seem all these locations, the Hall of Rot, the Shrouded Forge, and the Song-house, all work together to procure a legion of the Dead to serve Minas Morgul. I will send Rangers to these locations with the hope that this plan will be thwarted.'","Find Dâr Grazadh, the Hall of Rot","Scouting the Circle of Sorrow","Scout the north-western side of the Circle of Sorrow","'You are truly an experienced ${CLASS}, and no stranger to adventure or danger. This is why I ask you to scout the Circle of Sorrow for us. We must learn what difficulties we are to face and what obstacles we must overcome. Search the many places and buildings upon the Circle of Sorrow, and then report back to me with whatever you have learned.'","The hall is teeming with the Dead"},
[10717]={"The pass could prove a valuable route of attack for the Haban’akkâ","Investigate Muru Azog","A deadly perch from which trolls bombard those below with boulders","Watch-towers and heavy fortifications bar the road","Investigate Cloudyhead Pass","Investigate Kamaz-kala","'I require your assistance again, friend. The scouts you rescued are recovering from their ordeal. While we wait for their return, we need help covering the other areas they were to inspect.'","With Thrain's scouts recovering, their duties must be taken up by another.","Talk to Sárgo","Scouting the Dale","Investigate Dursh Hûl","Investigate Rung-shakam","'Excellent work, Hermáth. The information you gathered will be instrumental in planning our attacks upon the enemy.'","The Orcs have taken over these ruins","The hills are crawling with the enemy","Sárgo is in Zirakazhâr.\
\
You should return to Sárgo.","Locations to be scouted can throughout Azanulbizar.\
\
Sárgo Stiffbeard has asked you to take over the duties of the scouts that you rescued."},
[10720]={"Complete Quest, The Harlond: Black Hearts","Dindal the scout can be found high up in a secluded look-out, which can be reached by turning north off the east road from Imloth Melui.\
\
You should return to Dindal and let him know all that you have seen.","The Orc forces are camped in the Harlond, on the northern edge of Lossarnach and south of the Rammas Echor.\
\
Dindal the scout has encouraged you to go into the Harlond and survey the Orc forces to learn what can be done.","Complete Quest, The Harlond: Fell Tools","'Hm... yes. Such a great force of Orcs down there. Even you, ${CLASS} that you are, could not stand against them all. And yet, their guard is down. You could harry them from the shadows and cripple them greatly before they even knew you were there.\
\
'Would you brave this deed, ${PLAYER}, for the safety of Lossarnach? I cannot tell you from up here how best it should be done. You should survey the foe with your own eyes, and do what you can.'","Speak with Dindal","The noxious vapours of the Orc defilers' work waft out from the ruined structures","'Truly, ${PLAYER}, keen eyes up high are no replacement for a good head on the ground! Your help against the Orcs has earned our eternal gratitude.'","The Orcs have fully blocked the southern gate. Siege equipment has been constructed here and there along the wall","Investigate the Rammas Echor wall","Investigate the piers","Inspect the northern structure","A large Orc force occupies the Harlond and the Rammas Echor's southern gate.","Look-outs stand at key locations near the Harlond's entrance","Scouting the Harlond","The Harlond's piers are lightly guarded; they clearly expect no trouble from this direction","Complete Quest, The Harlond: Cruel Eyes","Investigate the entrance"},
[10721]={"Mizâdi has asked you to scout the Orc camp near the Span of Danagír, sabotaging the Orkish weapons racks as you go.","Return to Mizâdi in Urmâkh with your report.","Destruye los estantes de armas de orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'How big was it? That is quite worrying. I fear that this incursion is only the tip of a great spear about to plunge into Renewed Hamât. I must think on this more. Nevertheless, thank you. Many would have run from such a sight. It is truly only the valorous that would fight such a beast and live to tell the tale.'","Scout the bend in the Orc camp","Estantes de armas de orcos destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scout deeper in the camp","You see many Orcs milling around the camp","There are fewer Orcs and more weapons here","Scout the entrance to the Orc camp","Scout the back of the camp","Derrota al Devastador Utûgi.","Mizâdi asks you to scout the Orc camp near the Span of Danagír. If possible, destroy the Orkish weapons in their racks.","Scout the back of the Orc camp.","Return to Mizâdi in Urmâkh","'It is not only the Barkhûshim we must contend with. It seems a Shâra can never rest, ${PLAYER}. We have been hearing rumours, reports of odd things near the Span of Danagír to the east. My scouts recount stories of Orcs and something larger... even more sinister. We know not how strong they are or where they come from, but these rumours are quite concerning.\
\
'Go to the Span of Danagír. My spies tell me a band of Orcs has encamped near there. Scout the camp and count their number. If you have the opportunity, destroy their racked weapons so they cannot threaten Renewed Hamât. We have enough to deal with in the Barkhûshim in Kûr Anzar. I will not have another group of villains move towards us. Gather what information you can, and then report back to me. Do not take unnecessary risks. I fear for your safety if my scouts' reports are true.'","You hear an enormous roar as a shiver goes up your spine","There are many Orcs over here, and something large near the back","Derrota al Devastador Utûgi","Scouting the Incursion"},
[10722]={"'Si encuentras trasgos en cada uno de los dos conjuntos de ruinas en el sur de los Pantanos, sabremos que la presencia de trasgos está muy extendida y es una amenaza real. Toma el camino del este desde la plaza del pueblo hasta llegar a la granja de la Viuda Froghorn, luego sigue la línea de cercas hacia el norte un poco. La granja de Swatmidge está cuesta abajo hacia el este, a la vista de los Pantanos de Moscagua.\
\
'Al sur de su granja, una franja de tierra se extiende hacia el pantano y llega directamente al primer conjunto de ruinas. El segundo conjunto está mucho más al este y al sur de esas.'","Las Piedras Hundidas están ubicadas al sureste de la granja de Eldo Swatmidge, al este de Entibo. Las Ruinas de la Cueva de Trasgos están mucho más al este y al sur de las Piedras Hundidas.\
\
El vigilante Hierbaroja quiere que visites dos ruinas en el sur de los Pantanos de Moscagua y derrotes trasgos en cada ubicación para evaluar la amenaza que representan para la seguridad de Entibo.","Bill Musgopié está apostado al sureste de las ruinas de los Pantanos de Moscagua.\
\
Hierbaroja te dijo que informaras tus hallazgos en las ruinas a Bill Musgopié.","'¡Ah, me alegra verte! Hay trasgos en los Pantanos de Moscagua — o eso se ha dicho — y si ese es el caso, necesitamos saber cuántos son. Hay dos conjuntos de ruinas en la extensión sur de los Pantanos. Te pediría que vayas a esas ruinas y derrotes a cualquier trasgo que encuentres. Si hay trasgos cerca de ambas ruinas, tendremos una mejor idea de hasta dónde se han extendido.\
\
'El primer conjunto de ruinas se encuentra al sureste de la granja de Eldo Swatmidge, al este de Entibo. Al sur de su casa hay una estrecha franja de tierra que se extiende hacia los Pantanos y llega directamente a las Piedras Hundidas. Las Ruinas de la Cueva de Trasgos están mucho más al este y al sur de esas.\
\
'Cuando termines, habla con Bill Musgopié. Él y otro miembro de la guardia se han apostado en los Pantanos orientales, justo al sureste de las Ruinas de los Pantanos de Moscagua.'","Habla con Bill Musgopié","'Es como temía, ${PLAYER}. Si los trasgos ya se han extendido tanto por los Pantanos de Moscagua, tienen intención de quedarse.\
\
'Si no fuera por la infestación de arañas en las ruinas del tramo norte de los Pantanos, esperaría que los trasgos se apoderaran de ellas también.'","Trasgos derrotados en las Piedras Hundidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota trasgos en las Piedras Hundidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El vigilante Hierbaroja te ha pedido ayuda para ocuparte de los trasgos que se han instalado en los Pantanos de Moscagua.","Derrota trasgos en las Ruinas de la Cueva de Trasgos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Trasgos derrotados en las Ruinas de la Cueva de Trasgos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Explorando los Pantanos"},
[10723]={"'¿Ringhul envía noticias de Arifael y de sus parientes? No puedo decir que me sorprenda. Intenté viajar a sus salones en el sur y el este, pero tuve que regresar.\
\
'El viaje es peligroso y no recomiendo intentarlo ahora, pero si en el futuro te encuentras viajando por allí, los Elfos de Rivendel agradecerán cualquier noticia que puedas traer.\
\
'Cuando llegue el momento, intenta dirigirte a la Mesa de los Gigantes, un lugar de parlamento en días antiguos... y no viajes solo.'","Las noticias de Arifael fueron motivo de gran preocupación para Ringhul.","La exploradora Gwaemithrin está en las tierras altas al norte y al este de Rivendel, en el campamento de Glóin.\
\
Ringhul te ha pedido que lleves la advertencia de Arifael a Gwaemithrin y averigües qué sabe sobre los gigantes de las Montañas Nubladas.","'El maestro Elrond envió una exploradora a las Montañas Nubladas para observar la actividad de los gigantes. Actualmente, Gwaemithrin está acampada en el pequeño puesto avanzado que nuestros visitantes enanos han establecido al norte de Imladris.\
\
'Lleva a Gwaemithrin noticias de tus aventuras en la vega de Arifael y de los gigantes hostiles allí. Puede que haya aprendido algo más sobre ellos, aunque pensarías que ya habría informado de esto al maestro Elrond si así fuera.\
\
'El campamento de Glóin está al norte y al este de Rivendel. Adiós, ${PLAYER}, y ve con prisa.'","Explorando las montañas","Habla con Gwaemithrin"},
[10725]={"'Es un alivio saber que las fuerzas Angmarim no son tan grandes como temía. Además, aunque sabía que el valle al oeste era hogar de sierpes, no sabía que también había dragonzuelos allí.\
\
Nos has prestado un gran servicio hoy, ${PLAYER}.\
\
Aún queda mucho por hacer antes de estar preparados para enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar.'","Los Montañeses han establecido un pequeño campamento más allá de Ram Dúath","Explora el paso por el Ram Dúath occidental","Melthindir espera tu informe en Esteldín.\
\
Las fuerzas Angmarim han enviado una pequeña compañía de Montañeses a la entrada sureste de Ram Dúath. En la entrada suroeste de Ram Dúath, descubriste evidencia de muchas sierpes y dragonzuelos. Debes regresar con tu informe a Melthindir.","Explorando Ram Dúath","Explora el campamento de los Montañeses en el Ram Dúath oriental","'${PLAYER}, necesito tu ayuda. Como sabes, los orcos atacaron las Quebradas del Norte con fuerza, expulsando a los granjeros de sus hogares y quemando las tierras al sureste. Mientras nuestra atención estaba en los orcos, no notamos a los Montañeses que vinieron después.\
\
Considero Dol Dínen la principal amenaza contra nuestras tierras, pero estamos tan dispersos en las Quebradas del Norte que no podemos determinar completamente la amenaza que representan los Montañeses de Angmar.\
\
Necesito que explores el campamento de los Montañeses al noreste. Desde ese campamento, dirígete al oeste hasta encontrar una formación de extrañas rocas espinosas. El paso continúa al noroeste de esas rocas. Necesito saber qué encuentras en ambos lugares.'","Regresa con Melthindir","El Ram Dúath occidental es hogar de sierpes y dragonzuelos","El campamento de los Montañeses está al noreste de Esteldín. El paso está al oeste del campamento, al noroeste de una formación de rocas espinosas.\
\
Melthindir te ha pedido que explores el campamento de los Montañeses y el paso por el que se acercaron para determinar la gravedad de la amenaza que representan, para que los Montaraces puedan planear una defensa contra ellos.","Orcos salieron de Ram Dúath y arrasaron las Quebradas del Norte. Tras su paso, Montañeses de Angmar cruzaron el paso y acamparon más allá de los acantilados y senderos traicioneros."},
[10726]={"Elladan está más allá de la puerta al este de Dorongúr Espinablanca.\
\
Dorongúr Espinablanca te ha enviado a hablar con Elladan, hijo de Elrond.","Explorando las Ruinas","'Más allá de la puerta al este, encontrarás a Elladan y Dorallas. Elladan está aquí por petición de su padre, investigando un oscuro presagio que atormenta los sueños del Maestro Elrond. Habla con él.\
\
'El Maestro Elrond me ha dicho que es una locura reconstruir este lugar, pero no comparto su preocupación. Búscame si necesitas regresar aquí en el futuro.\
\
'Por ahora, ve con Elladan y ayúdanos a calmar la oscuridad en esta tierra.'","'El Maestro Dorongúr es un buen maestro, pero su corazón está demasiado ligado a esta tierra. Respeto sus esfuerzos por recuperar Edhelion y sé que tiene buenas intenciones, pero hay otros problemas en Ered Luin además de este refugio caído.\
\
'Rezo para que te haya enseñado bien, pues el camino que se avecina es oscuro...'","Habla con Elladan en Edhelion.","'Encuentra a Elladan más allá de la puerta abierta al este. Te he enseñado todo lo que puedo. Que estés bien, ${PLAYER}.'","Dorongúr Espinablanca te envió a hablar con Elladan, uno de los hijos gemelos de Elrond, enviado a Ered Luin para descubrir el significado de la oscura visión de su padre sobre el futuro."},
[10727]={"'In the north-eastern reaches of the Ashenslades, a small Orc-encampment known as Garmadh-maudhûl can be found overlooking the valley below. This encampment is believed to be a staging point for supplies into Dol Guldur.\
\
'There have been rumours that some of the raw materials in this area have been affected by the blight that has swept across the region. Please go to the outskirts of Garmadh-maudhûl and retrieve several satchels of discarded ore and bring them to me, so that we can determine if the ore is blighted in some way.\
\
'Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of here. The ore has been placed in sacks and can be found in the surrounding area.'","Scouting the Stores","Collect sack of discarded ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Eirien at Mithechad","Eirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl.\
\
You should bring the discarded ore to Eirien. Perhaps she will be able to see if this ore has been affected by the blight.","Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of Mithechad.\
\
Eirien has asked you to collect some of the ore discarded by the Orcs of Garmadh-maudhûl.","Scouts of the Malledhrim witnessed the Orcs of Garmadh-maudhûl discarding piles of ore.","'Thank you for recovering these pieces of ore. Interestingly, it appears as if this ore has not been affected by the blight in the region, which makes me wonder why the Orcs discarded it in the first place.\
\
'This does, however, mean that the stores of Garmadh-maudhûl are of high enough quality to be used in making armour and weapons.'","'Travel to Garmadh-maudhûl to the north-east of here. Please retrieve ore that has been placed in sacks and scattered in the area surrounding the camp.'","Collected sack of discarded ore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10728]={"You have found the first patrol point","'Well met again, ${PLAYER}, and a wonder it is to see you here after so long a road. Alas, many of my kinsmen have not made it this far. I have not heard from Braigiar since his start into the Gravenwood and young Amarion failed to return from scouting shortly thereafter... I know not their fates.\
\
'Yet I dare not dwell on such matters, though this journey has left me all but empty, for I have yet to complete my task.\
\
'We find ourselves now before Nan Curunír, and beyond in the tower of Orthanc sits Saruman the Traitor. Looking across the destruction wrought in this vale, it seems clear now that his wisdom has faded, to be replaced by madness. You should make yourself familiar with the land, my friend, for if we are to find our way to Isengard, we must learn its lay ere we are discovered.'","'Patrol Nan Curunír, ${PLAYER}. That is the only way we will know for certain what Saruman has in mind.'","You found the third patrol point","You found the fourth patrol point","Find the first patrol point","You found the second patrol point","Nan Curunír stretches forth beyond Dagoras' camp.\
\
Dagoras has suggested that you scout the southern part of Nan Curunír.","Scouting the Way","Talk to Dagoras at his camp in Nan Curunír","'There is much work to be done here, ${PLAYER}.'","Dagoras is encamped near the entrance to Nan Curunír.\
\
You should return to Dagoras and let him know what you have found.","The Vale of Nan Curunír lies before you. Tales described it as a lush and green valley, but the devastation stretched out before you tells a dark tale. You must learn more of the land before you proceed further.","Find a friend near Nan Curunír","Find the second patrol point","Find the third patrol point","'So, now you have seen some small part of Nan Curunír.\
\
'Among the western hills, a great infestation of goblins and Wargs has taken root. Across the river to the east, an encampment of Orcs -- Uruk-hai this tribe is called. They are strong and do not fear the sun. To the north lies Isengard itself.\
\
'We must proceed carefully, for there are enemies all around us.'","Find the fourth patrol point","Nan Curunír lies to the north of the Ford of Isen.\
\
Grimbold has sent you to the Vale of Nan Curunír and suggested that you might find a friend awaiting you there.","'${PLAYER}, I have heard many dark tidings regarding the purposes and plans of Saruman the White. Long has he been a friend to the Rohirrim -- and even now he holds much sway in the Golden Hall -- but I cannot allay my fears any longer.\
\
'If Saruman has indeed turned against us and allies himself with the likes of the Dunlendings, and even Orcs and goblins, then we must know. Yet I am bound by the strict command of Théoden King not to trespass upon the Vale of Nan Curunír to the North, where lies Isengard.\
\
'Will you go in our stead and learn of the purpose and strength of Saruman, that we may know the depths of his treachery before it is too late? I think you will find a friend near the valley....'"},
[10729]={"'I was supposed to go to the way-crossing west of Tadrent and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> to make sure the roads are clear, but I spent all day looking for that warg and forgot, and now I am too exhausted to make the journey. It's not that far, to tell you the truth, but it is simply too far for me to make the trip in my condition.\
\
'Will you do this for me? I would really appreciate it, and there will be a reward in it for you if you do!'","'Hello there, friend. I was expecting to see my good friend Osbenn! You are here in his stead? Too tired to leave Tadrent, is he? Yes, that happens from time to time. He throws himself into his duties in the morning, and by the afternoon he is exhausted! But his heart is in the right place.\
\
'Well, I am headed that way myself, so there's no reason for you to go all the way back to Tadrent! You say he promised you a reward? Well, I think I can make good on Osbenn's promise, and he will pay me back for it.\
\
'Good day to you, friend. The road is clear, and let us hope it stays that way for a good long while! This kingdom has seen enough of war, and so have I!'","A Gondorian guard coming from the west arrives at the way-crossing","The way-crossing is west of Tadrent.\
\
Guard Osbenn was supposed to go to the way-crossing west of Tadrent and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> to ensure the roads were clear of danger, but now he is too exhausted to make the trip and asked you to do it.","Wait for the newcomer to arrive","Someone approaches along the road.","The road seems clear of danger, but someone approaches","Go to the way-crossing west of Tadrent, in King's Gondor, and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for danger on the road","Guard Osbenn was supposed to scout the way-crossing west of Tadrent, but he is too tired to do it now.","Talk to Guard Dalmann at the way-crossing west of Tadrent, in King's Gondor","'Oh no, I just remembered one more thing I was supposed to do today.\
\
'I was supposed to go to the way-crossing west of Tadrent and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> to make sure the roads are clear, but I spent all day looking for that warg and forgot, and now I am too exhausted to make the journey. It's not that far, to tell you the truth, but it is simply too far for me to make the trip in my condition.\
\
'Will you do this for me? I would really appreciate it, and there will be a reward in it for you if you do!'","Guard Dalmann has arrived at the way-crossing west of Tadrent.","Scouting the Way-crossing"},
[10730]={"Habla con Barachen","Baraches está en su campamento al este del Último Puente, en una colina al sur del camino\
\
Alphlanc te pidió que lleves noticias a Barachen de que ningún mal ha entrado al Bosque de los Trolls mientras ella ha estado vigilando el Último Puente, aunque tampoco ha salido ninguno.","Encuentra la señal de los Elfos","'Este Elfo, Barachen, ha aceptado ayudarme con los problemas que he encontrado aquí en el Bosque de los Trolls. Si quieres, podrías echarle una mano.'","'Si buscas el campamento de Barachen, lo encontrarás al sur. Deja el camino y sigue la pendiente hacia la derecha, mientras asciende por el costado de esos acantilados.'","'Te doy la bienvenida, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, pero debo advertirte: siervos del Enemigo cruzaron el Último Puente y se adentraron en el Bosque de los Trolls hace no menos de dos meses, persiguiendo a una pequeña compañía. Fueron detenidos en el Vado del Bruinen, y la buena gente fue puesta a salvo, pero... no todos los malvados fueron localizados.\
\
'Barachen mantiene un campamento al este, en una colina al sur del camino. Llévale este mensaje de mi parte, si vas en esa dirección: \\qNingún agente del mal ha entrado al Bosque de los Trolls por el Último Puente, pero tampoco ha salido. Sea cual sea el mal que acecha entre las ruinas del viejo Rhudaur... permanece allí.\
\
'Te agradezco esto, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Camina con cuidado y sigue el camino hacia el este hasta encontrar la señal que colocamos para guiar a los amigos al campamento de Barachen. Es difícil pasarla por alto, pues es blanca, a diferencia de la piedra de estas colinas.'","'Barachen tiene un campamento no muy lejos al este, en una colina al sur del camino.  Sigue el camino hasta ver la señal que colocamos para guiar a los amigos al campamento de Barachen.\
\
'Llévale noticias de que el camino sobre el Último Puente sigue despejado, aunque el mal que se infiltró en el Bosque de los Trolls parece seguir aquí.'","Los Elfos colocaron una piedra blanca como señal a lo largo del camino para guiar a los amigos hacia el campamento de Barachen.\
\
Alphlanc te dijo que buscaras una piedra blanca como señal hacia el este, siguiendo el camino.","'¿Traes noticias de Alphlanc? Me alegra que no haya encontrado criaturas malignas, pero los Sabios saben bien que el mal invisible suele ser el peor.\
\
'Aun así, me alegra recibir tus noticias. Si puedes ayudarnos a vigilar la naturaleza en busca de señales de maldad, nos prestarías un gran servicio.'","Las marcas sobre esta piedra apuntan al sur del camino, indicando la dirección del campamento de Barachen.","Alphlanc vigila el camino que cruza el Último Puente, por si algún siervo del Enemigo intenta entrar —o salir— del Bosque de los Trolls.","Explorando lo Salvaje"},
[10731]={"Scout the northern camp","Scout the eastern approach","Scouted the eastern approach","Talk to Harchador at Mithechad","Scouting Ânghum-maudhûl","Ânghum-maudhûl lies to the south-east of Mithechad.\
\
Harchador has asked you to explore the western and eastern approaches to the camp and a small camp directly across from the main rallying point at Ânghum-maudhûl.","In the southern reaches of the Ashenslades, Ânghum-maudhûl stands as the central rallying point for Orcs in the area.","'Please travel to Ânghum-maudhûl, south-east of here, and scout out the forces arrayed against us.'","Scouted the western approach","Harchador is at Mithechad, north-west of Ânghum-maudhûl.\
\
You should return to Harchador and give your report on Ânghum-maudhûl.","'In the southern reaches of the Ashenslades, the Orcs have built a large defensible position surrounding a set of ancient ruins. These ruins are called Ânghum-maudhûl by the Enemy.\
\
'Would you travel to Ânghum-maudhûl and scout the area? There are three specific areas that I wish you to patrol for me: the western and eastern approaches to the camp and a small camp directly across from the main rallying point.\
\
'Ânghum-maudhûl lies south-east of here, along the southern border of the Ashenslades.'","Scouted the northern camp","'Thank you for scouting this dangerous place...perhaps it would be a good target for a distraction, so that our incursions to the north might go well.'","Scout the western approach"},
[10732]={"'Has sido de gran ayuda para quienes vigilamos el Bosque de los Trolls, ${PLAYER}. Recuperar las piedras robadas a los mensajeros de Heithur no fue una tarea sencilla, pero la cumpliste sin queja alguna. Sé que Heithur está satisfecho con tu servicio, y me uno a su agradecimiento.\
\
'Si deseas seguir prestando tu ayuda, quiero que te presentes ante Elladan y Elrohir, los hijos de Elrond. Han establecido un campamento en las ruinas de Thorenhad, al este de aquí y al norte, en las Gargantas del Bruinen, y sé que tus servicios serían bien recibidos. Thorenhad está en lo alto de una colina, al norte de las guaridas de osos de las Gargantas del Bruinen.\
\
'Si sigues la carretera hacia el este, encontrarás el campamento de Narlinn y Fimgris. Ellos podrán dirigirte hacia Thorenhad.'","'Todo ha estado tranquilo. ¡Si me asignaran a Nan Tornaeth, vería algo de aventura!'","Habla con Narlinn","Exploradores en las Gargantas del Bruinen","Narlinn y Fimgris están acampados junto al camino, al este del campamento de Barachen.\
\
Barachen está impresionado con tu habilidad y determinación, y te ha pedido que prestes tu ayuda a los hijos de Elrond, quienes vigilan el Bosque de los Trolls desde su campamento cerca de las Gargantas del Bruinen. Te dijo que Narlinn y Fimgris podrán guiarte hasta Thorenhad, donde residen los hijos de Elrond.","'¿Vienes de parte de Barachen, buscando ayudar a Elladan y Elrohir? Me alegra oírlo, pero antes quisiera pedirte tu ayuda, si tienes un momento...'","Muchos exploradores fueron enviados por el Bosque de los Trolls para vigilar cualquier señal de maldad por orden de Elladan y Elrohir, los hijos de Elrond.","'¡Espero demostrar mi valía ante los ojos de mi doncella Elfa!'"},
[10733]={"Scouts of the Enemy","After the recent attack on Wakenflood, tensions are high at this outpost. The commander wishes to deflect future attacks from Easterlings by ousting the scouts who prowl the bounds.","Find Sergeant Hubyrt at Wakenflood","Sergeant Hubyrt can be found at Wakenflood.\
\
You should find Sergeant Hubyrt and offer your help to him.","'I cannot believe you were able to defeat that party of Easterling scouts! They were a formidable lot, and even the Rohirrim fled before them.\
\
'This was a great deed to prove your strength, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps one brave ${RACE} can help Wakenflood endure this siege. Is there truly hope for us?'","Defeated a scouting party","'Hail, stranger! I am Sergeant Hubyrt; the men of Wakenflood report to me. I am glad to see a new face -- my warriors were forced to defend our outpost as it was attacked by Easterlings last night, and our strength has waned.\
\
'One of my soldiers ventured out this morning and beheld a large encampment of our enemies at the Anduin's edge, but he had to hasten back, for the Easterlings had the same idea.\
\
'Their scouting party is a formidable one, and my man could not face them and survive. They will be able to report our weaknesses unchecked, and we will soon have a great disadvantage, if they are not stopped.'","'Well, you are off to a fine start if you wish to gain favour in Harwick, ${PLAYER}, but I am not through with you yet.\
\
'Your next duty is to report to Wakenflood, and ensure that all is well up at the tower. I will put in a good word for you to Harding next time I see him.\
\
'It will take you a bit longer to earn enough of his trust to receive a welcome in Harwick, but these things do take time. He is a practical man, our Reeve.'","Find and defeat an Easterling scouting party","Easterling scouting parties can be found between Wakenflood and the Easterling encampment at the Anduin's edge.\
\
You should find and defeat an Easterling scouting party.","Sergeant Hubyrt is at Wakenflood, attempting to hold a badly weakened outpost.\
\
You should return to Sergeant Hubyrt with news of the scouting party you defeated.","Return to Sergeant Hubyrt of Wakenflood"},
[10734]={"Talk to Rothulf, who seems to have something important to tell you","'Orc-scouts surrounded us? That is dire news -- and more dire that one escaped, and our leader is hopelessly bewitched. What are we to do?'","Defeated Orc-scouts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Trying to stop us from spreading the word of your little camp, are you?\
\
'Cursed ${RACE}, the Orcs will feast upon the flesh of Man tonight!'","Rothulf suspects that a threatening presence can be found around Wynmar's camp in the south of Thinglad.\
\
You should search for and defeat any threats to the Rohirrim hunters.","'Wynmar has been like this ever since his first encounter with that woman. I think she has bewitched him!\
\
'He pays no mind to the strange sightings and sounds; I have a bad feeling, ${PLAYER}. I feel that we are being hunted as we move south....'","Stop the scouts' leader from sounding the alert","The scout has escaped...this does not bode well for the Rohirrim","Rothulf stands near Wynmar at the southern Rohirrim camp.\
\
Wynmar is distracted by his love for Noriel, but Rothulf has asked for a word with you.","Rothulf is in Wynmar's camp in southern Thinglad.\
\
You should return to Rothulf with the dire news of the escaped scout.","Scouts on the Move","With Wynmar distracted by his admiration for Noriel, Rothulf is deeply concerned about the movements of Orcs on the fringes of the camp.","Defeat any threats to the Rohirrim's camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Alas, alas! Why cannot our folk be friends?'","A hardy leader of the Orc-scouts' initiative is likely somewhere near Wynmar's camp.\
\
You should try to defeat the scouts' leader before he can alert the attackers of the Rohirrim's whereabouts.","Return to Rothulf with news of the Orc-threat","'Please, ${PLAYER}, you must tell me more of Noriel. I would give anything to see her again. I have never seen a maiden so fair nor so bold.\
\
'Do you think her brethren would let me approach their keep again, so that I could speak with her one last time? I am loath to leave these woods!'"},
[10735]={"Murciélagos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jirones de sombra","'¡Ah, ya estás de vuelta! ¿Qué tal fue la caza? ¿Has visto a unas cuantas de esas criaturas agitando a los murciélagos, verdad? Esto no pinta bien.'","'Hay una entrada a una cueva donde se rumorea que hay montones de murciélagos. Cuando llegues al Cruce de Durin gira hacia el sur, y luego al este en el primer pasillo que encuentres.'","Has encontrado la cueva de los murciélagos","Derrota a los morvuls adiestradores de murciélagos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La entrada a la cueva de los murciélagos está al sureste de la entrada de Zirakzigil.\
\
Kalman te ha pedido que des caza a los murciélagos que infestan el Camino de Durin.","'Algo ha estado agitando a los murciélagos desde que hemos llegado. Primero pensé que eran esos trasgos, pero el otro día vi otra cosa... parecía uno de esos merrevail, pero aldgo diferente.\
\
'¡Debemos averiguar qué era en realidad y de paso encargarnos de esos murciélagos! Hay un pequeño puesto avanzado al norte de aquí, la Puerta de las Nubes, cerca de la entrada a Zirakzigil. Ve allí y habla con Kalman para averiguar lo que sabe de los murciélagos.'","Kalman está en el puesto avanzado cerca de la entrada a Zirakzigil, en el Camino de Durin, al noroeste de la cueva de los murciélagos.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Kalman para informarle de que has tenido éxito.","Morvuls adiestradores de murciélagos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Rambi te ha enviado para averiguar la causa del incremento de la actividad de los murciélagos? Sí, nosotros también lo hemos notado.\
\
'Los murciélagos parecen habitar una cueva un poco al sur y al este de aquí. No estoy seguro de qué los ha despertado, pero me imagino que podría encontrarse dentro de esa cueva. Da caza a tantas de esas amenazas aladas como puedas, mientras estás allí.'","Habla con Kalman en la entrada a Zirakzigil","Derrota a los murciélagos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La entrada a la cueva de los murciélagos está al sureste del Cruce de Durin.\
\
Kalman te ha pedido que des caza a los murciélagos que infestan el Camino de Durin.","'La entrada a Zirakzigil está a cierta distancia al norte y un poco hacia el este. Cuando sientas que el aire se vuelve más frío, sabrás que estás cerca.'","Habla con Kalman en la Puerta de las Nubes","Encuentra la cueva de los murciélagos","Algo está agitando a los murciélagos, para preocupación de los enanos de Moria.","Kalman se encuentra en el pequeño puesto avanzado de la entrada a Zirakzigil en el Camino de Durin."},
[10736]={"As you look down, you find a remnant of a fallen branch. The bark appears to be ashen-coloured and smells of decay, though something still speaks of an ancient beauty it may once have possessed.\
\
Perhaps you should bring this to Himeinior at Barad Angol to see if he can tell you anything about the branch.","Himeinior is at Barad Angol, a small camp at a tower overlooking Sâd Doldúr.\
\
You should seek out Himeinior and give him the branch you found. Perhaps he can discern more about what is happening to the trees in the Ashenslades.","Bring the blighted branch to Himeinior","Scratching the Surface","You discovered a blighted branch in the Ashenslades, corrupted by an unknown disease.","'Thank you kindly for gathering such an exquisite specimen, ${PLAYER}. I have gathered several such branches myself, and this is the best of them thus far. \
\
'Sadly, it appears as if this poor branch has been blighted by some form of foul sorcery. It seems as if this sorcery has consumed its life and has left it naught but a husk, bereft of its former glory.'"},
[10737]={"Scroll Delivery","'Would you deliver three scrolls for me? In the village of Iridír to the east, there is an old woman called Amâsu, who has already paid for them.","'I understand that you must continue your travels. Thank you for your company and for indulging me. Are you continuing east? In the village of Iridír there is an old woman called Amâsu. I owe her three scrolls. Would you deliver them for me?\
\
'As busy as I appear, would you believe I have very few customers? Last year I had more work than time. The Great Southern Empire of Ordâkh ruled here until not long ago, and they were my only customers. Sadly, they did not allow our people to learn to read or write, so I am unsure what the future has in store for me.\
\
'Amâsu is a kindly woman, and probably just bought some of my scrolls to be charitable.'\
\
Sûlmur laughs again, but this time you sense discomfort.\
\
'Well, whether she needs them or not, she paid, so the order will be fulfilled. Would you mind? The roads are perilous and I would prefer to stay here.'","'Hello lûkal, what is this?'\
\
She takes the scrolls from you.\
\
'Ah yes, from Sûlmur. Thank you for bringing these. How is Sûlmur, is she well? Has she gone after that handsome rice farmer yet?'\
\
You tell her Sûlmur is well, but has not gone after Turizi yet. Amâsu sighs wistfully.\
\
'Ah well, it is only a matter of time I suppose.'","You have been asked to deliver blank papyrus scrolls to a woman named Amâsu, who is in Iridír, a town in Ambarûl east of Mehêtur.","Deliver the scrolls to Amâsu in Iridír","Sûlmur has blank papyrus scrolls that need to be delivered."},
[10738]={"You should let Abartârik know that you defeated many rats at Hashadir.\
\
Abartârik is in Dol Amroth outside of the Swan-knight's Keep.","Lothíriel has asked you to speak with Abartârik to see what they discovered at Hashadir.\
\
Abartârik is in Dol Amroth outside of the Swan-knight's Keep.","Defeated scurrying Hashadir rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you for taking care of our vermin problem. I know it's not a pleasant task, but they often carry disease and can be a great risk to our citizens.'","Defeat frothing Hashadir rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Abartârik","Scurrying Scamps","Abartârik has asked you to help drive out the rat population that has erupted in Hashadir.\
\
Hashadir is south of Dol Amroth.","Defeat scurrying Hashadir rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Greetings. You say the Lady Lothíriel sent you? I am not sure if this means she trusts you or wishes to punish you.'\
\
The knight chuckles slightly to themself.\
\
'Oh, it's nothing so bad... it just might not be the most enjoyable of tasks. You see, we were successful in driving the invading Corsairs out of Hashadir, but while they fled, they left behind a most undesirable surprise - rats. Rats of the most unusual size, even. Who knew rats could grow so large?\
\
'In any case, our tasks here in Dol Amroth have kept us from cleaning them out, but if you are willing to do so, there is a reward.'","The vermin who have taken up residence at Hashadir stand to pose a serious threat to the citizens of Dol Amroth.","Defeated frothing Hashadir rats (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Abartârik","'Though my father has returned to the governance of Dol Amroth, I am still much involved in seeing to the city's many duties and tasks. One of those tasks is receiving daily reports from our swan-knights who patrol the countryside.\
\
'A recent report on the state of Hashadir has given me cause for concern. I ask that you speak with Captain Abartârik about what they found there. I think you could be of help. You will find Abartârik near the Swan-knight's Keep, probably seeing to the training of their fellow soldiers.'"},
[10739]={"'Yes, I am Odahild, the leader of this village. The tales you have heard of scuttling shadows in the night are true, every word of them, and they have brought a number of adventurers here seeking to learn more.\
\
'They brought this Wizard hither as well. He says you are a friend of his. Perhaps, then, you could kindly ask him to leave? He brings only ill omens with him on this visit!'","Habla con Radagast","Ríkmar has heard troubling stories concerning Blómgard, a small Woodman settlement in the southern reaches of Laerlad.","Odahild can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Odahild, the leader of Blómgard.","Travel to Blómgard in Laerlad","Radagast can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Radagast.","'We always meet in less than ideal circumstances, ${PLAYER}! Have you noticed? I certainly have. Do you know that some folk believe my arrival actually draws these problems with them? Preposterous, I know, but people do think so nevertheless!'","Find Odahild, the leader of Blómgard","Blómgard can be found at the edge of the southern wood of Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin.\
\
You should travel to Blómgard and see if you could be of any help there.","Scuttling Through the Narrows","The folk of Blómgard barely seem to notice you","Odahild is deep in conversation with Radagast, the Brown Wizard","'Listen well, ${RACE}. I have heard troubling rumours from the south, and I would share them with you. They may be the falsest of lies, but then again they might be true. I cannot judge, so I leave it to you.\
\
'These tales come from Blómgard, a village to the south, in Laerlad. They speak of shadows in the night and a frightful scuttling sound upon the roofs of the village. Now, I have not spoken with their leader Odahild since the Elves gave these woods to us, but she is not one to speak falsely. There are good men and women in that village, and if we can save them from this creeping danger we should do so! And if these are just tales, well, at least we will know for certain.'","Talk to Odahild, leader of Blómgard"},
[10740]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow time to expire</rgb>","Consume food or drink (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER} from far away lands! We are pleased that you can join us in our celebration!\
\
'Here you will find a sport that any and all may participate in, regardless of age! While we are few, we have prepared a marvelous eating contest. The point is simply to consume as much food as you are able in the time allotted.\
\
'Be careful, though... some foods may slow you down! We shall begin soon. Speak to the Event Coordinator when your are ready to begin.'","'You must have come hungry! A voracious eater and our victor!'","Consumed food or drink (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Event Coordinator is standing next to Wulfherr.\
\
You should speak with the Event Coordinator when you are ready to begin.","Tables with food may be found outside the gates of Scylfig.\
\
Eat as much food as possible before time runs out.","Talk to Event Coordinator","'Are you ready to begin? Good!\
\
'There are four tables... you may eat or drink from any of them. You are in competition with these good folk, so be as quick as you can!'","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","'The people of Wildermore have much to be thankful for, ${PLAYER}, despite the destruction wrought by the giant Núrzum. The folk of Scylfig celebrate by holding a small festival outside their town.\
\
'You should go there at once and join the festivities. I hear that they are holding an eating contest outside the gates of their city. The survivors are few, but their hearts are emboldened!\
\
'A friend of mine, Wulfherr, is overseeing the festivities. He will be able to provide you with everything you need. Let me know when you are ready to go to Scylfig, and I will arrange your travel.'","Speak with Wulfherr or Gyric.","Scylfig: A Celebration Feast","The people of Scylfig celebrate the end of the giant Núrzum.","Gyric is waiting for your decision in Forlaw.\
\
You should speak with Gyric when you are ready to travel to Scylfig in the Writhendowns and talk to Wulfherr to join the festivities.","Talk to Gyric to travel to Scylfig in the Writhendowns and speak with Wulfherr","<rgb=#FF0000>Time has expired</rgb>","'You should speak with Wulfherr when you arrive in Scylfig.'","Talk to Wulfherr or Gyric."},
[10741]={"'The people of Wildermore have much to be thankful for, ${PLAYER}, despite the destruction wrought by the giant Núrzum. The folk of Scylfig celebrate by holding a small festival outside their town.\
\
'You should go there at once and join the festivities. I hear that they are holding a demonstration of mounted archery in the form of a race. Whether you are skilled or not, you should try your hand at it.\
\
'A friend of mine, Wulfherr, is overseeing the festivities. He will be able to provide you with everything you need. Let me know when you are ready to go to Scylfig, and I will arrange your travel.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires Mounted Combat</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not allow time to expire</rgb>","Use the Scylfig bow","Used the Scylfig bow","Points: ${NUMBER}","Gyric is waiting for your decision in Forlaw.\
\
You should speak with Gyric when you are ready to travel to Scylfig in the Writhendowns and talk to Wulfherr to join the festivities.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Talk to Gyric to travel to Scylfig in the Writhendowns and speak with Wulfherr","<rgb=#FF0000>Time has expired</rgb>","Scylfig: Target-shooting","The people of Scylfig celebrate the end of the giant Núrzum.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires Mounted Combat</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>","Use the bow Wulfherr gave you to obtain your skills.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>","'You should speak with Wulfherr when you arrive in Scylfig.'","'So, Gyric sent you? Indeed, we do have much to be thankful for. While the giant wrought terrible damage upon our village, he is dead and we are alive. That is all the motivation we need for celebrating.\
\
'We are hosting a demonstration of mounted archery in the form of a race. Take this bow and mount your war-steed. Follow the targets around and up the mountain and back down to the road, shooting targets as you go. I will score your performance. Green targets will yield one point, while blue targets will earn you five. Keep an eye out for the rare red targets -- often on high ledges -- for they will yield ten points.\
\
'If you reach one hundred points, you will earn a reward! The race is timed, so you must hurry!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This quest requires Mounted Combat</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>","Targets may be found throughout the course in the Writhendowns.\
\
Destroy targets to gain points towards the success of the celebration event.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest auto-completes upon beating the course.</rgb>"},
[10742]={"The goblin-cave lies to the north of Cadthorn's position, along the ridge.\
\
Cadthorn has asked you to collapse the entrance of the goblin-cave.","Collapse the cave entrance","'Thank you for lending Cadthorn your aid. With the entrance to the goblin-cave collapsed, it should be some time before they are able to attack any more of our patrols or messengers.'","Cadthorn and his companions were attacked by goblins as they journeyed to Forthbrond from Edoras with important messages.","Ardwyn is at Forthbrond, south of the goblin-cave.\
\
Cadthorn asked you to return to Ardwyn with news of your success.","'The goblins that attacked my companions and I emerged from a cave to the north of here. We had no warning before they were upon us, and in such numbers that we had no chance.\
\
'I fear that others will suffer the same fate if the goblins are permitted to retain their hiding hole. If you would, go to their cave and collapse the entrance, then return to Ardwyn at Forthbrond and let him know that one threat has been removed.'","Collapsed the cave entrance","Seal the Path","Talk to Ardwyn at Forthbrond"},
[10743]={"El túmulo de Thorún ha sido sellado","'Es un destino terrible que los cuerpos de gente sencilla como los Hombres del Bosque sean obligados a servir al Enemigo...'","El túmulo de Brungúr ha sido sellado","'¿Has sellado las puertas de los túmulos, ${PLAYER}? Bien hecho. Solo nos queda expulsar a los espectros malignos que aún deambulan por las Hondonadas Enmarañadas... entonces tal vez la paz regrese a esta parte del bosque.'","Sella el túmulo de Thorún","Sellando los túmulos","Ivorel teme que los daños causados por los maestros demacrados no puedan revertirse, pero los túmulos deben sellarse para evitar que más Muertos emerjan y amenacen a los Malledhrim.","Los túmulos se encuentran al noreste del campamento de Ivorel.\
\
Ivorel te ha pedido que cierres los túmulos de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y coloques sobre ellos sellos de manufactura élfica para impedir que los espíritus malignos de Morgoth se alcen como espectros.","Sella el túmulo de Brungúr","El túmulo de Mordeloth ha sido sellado","Ivorel se encuentra en su campamento, al suroeste de los túmulos.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Ivorel con la noticia de tu éxito.","Habla con Ivorel en su campamento","Sella el túmulo de Mordeloth","NO DEBERÍAS VER ESTO","'Las inscripciones que me has descrito hablan del gran esfuerzo dedicado a la construcción de Dol Guldur como morada del Nigromante. Muchos hombres fueron traídos desde el lejano Este, y trabajaron en sus piedras bajo una labor cruel más allá de lo soportable. Cuando morían de agotamiento, eran enterrados en los túmulos de aquí para continuar su servidumbre eternamente como guardianes finales.\
\
Aún siguen siendo sus siervos, y ahora son llamados para frenar nuestro avance hacia la torre, animados por los espíritus malignos de Morgoth; pero muchos permanecen todavía sin despertar, y debemos asegurarnos de que no surjan en mayor número. Debemos sellar estos túmulos para que sus ocupantes permanezcan en ellos para siempre.\
\
Cerrad los túmulos y colocad estos sellos sobre ellos. Estos sellos me fueron entregados por Agorin antes de abandonar Ost Galadh, pues sospechaba que estos túmulos serían perturbados. Ahora te los entrego.'"},
[10745]={"Derrota a los soldados de Moria en Snaga-maudhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jarmárr quiere eliminar el campamento de trasgos recientemente descubierto. Snaga-maudhûl es una amenaza para todos los que viajan desde la Puerta de Acebeda hacia el resto de Moria.","Habla con Wegil en el lado nordeste de Snaga-maudhûl","Wegil se encuentra en el lado nordeste de Snaga-maudhûl, vigilando el camino.\
\
Deberías encontrarlo y hablar con él.","'¡Eh, tú! ¿Estás herido? No, ya veo que no. Pero parece que has herido a muchos trasgos durante tu breve estancia en Snaga-maudhûl, ¡y te lo agradezco!\
\
'Estoy aquí para ayudar a los viajeros que puedan verse obstaculizados en el camino al pasar por ese podrido campamento de trasgos, pero como parece que tú ya los has neutralizado, ¡te ayudaré a continuar tu camino!'","'Me alegra que haya aquí ${PLAYER:un guerrero[m]|una guerrera[f]} mejor que yo para causar estragos entre estos pequeños e inquietantes engendros. Su campamento supone una amenaza total para todo el tránsito desde el Umbral de Durin hasta el Mirador de la Gran Excavación y más allá.\
\
'Todos los enanos que entren en Moria pasarán por aquí, ¡y no podemos permitir que Snaga-maudhûl se alce bajo el camino! De paso, , trata de reducir este malicioso nido de trasgos.'","Sellar la puerta","'Los trasgos deben ser expulsados de Snaga-maudhûl si queremos recuperar Moria para los enanos.'","Soldados de Moria derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El campamento de trasgos se encuentra en los túneles más allá de la grieta sobre las escaleras orientales.\
\
Los enanos quieren poner fin al dominio de los trasgos en los túneles inferiores para garantizar la seguridad de su posición."},
[10746]={"'Lleva las hierbas a Othrikar. Los enanos las necesitarán.'","'Gracias por entregar estas hierbas, ${RACE}.'","'Las hierbas de los Jorthkyn nos ayudarán contra Angmar y los Duramano.'","El intendente Orgrin está en Othrikar, al noroeste de Rusfold.\
\
Iivari te ha pedido que realices una última tarea para él: desea que entregues una alforja de hierbas a Orgrin, el proveedor en Othrikar, como cumplimiento de un pacto entre los Hijos de la Tierra y los enanos.","Existe un pacto entre los Suuri-lehmä y los Enanos de Othrikar, por el cual cada uno brindaría ayuda al otro.","'Los Rauta-lehmä no tienen honor. Con tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}, les hemos enseñado el significado de la palabra.'","'Eres una buena amistad de los Suuri-lehmä y de los enanos.'","Lleva la alforja de hierbas de Iivari al intendente Orgrin","'¿Eh? ¿Qué es esto? Ah, las hierbas prometidas por los Jorthkyn. ¡Gracias por traerlas!\
\
'Son aliados extraños, ¿no? Pero estos tiempos son peligrosos, y cualquier fuerza que podamos reunir para detener el avance de Angmar es bienvenida.\
\
'Los Jorthkyn parecen tener una extraña afinidad por las plantas, aunque no cultivan cosechas... No estoy seguro de dónde aprendieron tal saber, pero ahora es de gran valor para nosotros. Muchos de nosotros sin duda seremos heridos en las batallas que se avecinan, y las cataplasmas que pueden hacerse con estas hierbas son potentes para sanar.'","'Nos has ayudado bien, ${PLAYER}. El momento de la batalla está muy cerca ahora.\
\
'Una última cosa te pido: lleva esto a Othrikar, las minas enanas al noroeste de aquí, y entrégaselo al intendente Orgrin. Esta alforja contiene muchas hierbas curativas que hemos reunido como parte de nuestro pacto con los enanos de allí, quienes también nos ayudarán.\
\
'Que te vaya bien. Puede que no nos volvamos a encontrar.'","Sellando el Pacto"},
[10747]={"Los dos enanos, Knakk y Kafli, deberían encontrarse en algún lugar al este, en los alrededores o más allá del territorio de los orcos.\
\
Te han pedido que encuentres a los enanos Knakk y Kafli.","'Kafli y yo intentamos escabullirnos entre los orcos... ¡y casi lo conseguimos! Creo que fue ese collar que llevaba lo que lo delató. Brillaba bastante.\
\
'Cuando salimos del campamento de la compañía, le dije que lo escondiera en un bolsillo o algo así, pero se negó, pensando que alguien se lo arrebataría mientras no lo tuviera en la mano. No puedo creer que perdiera la vida por esa cosa.'","'Nuestra compañía de la Guardia Orca no llegó muy lejos antes de separarse. Acampamos aquí una noche, pero luego surgieron discusiones sobre qué hacer con las hordas de orcos en el camino. Los dos enanos que se dirigieron a las cavernas del sur iban bien preparados, pero los dos que se dirigieron al este, directo al territorio de los orcos, me tienen preocupado. Por favor, ${PLAYER}, ¿puedes buscarlos y asegurarte de que han llegado a su destino?\
\
'Se adentraron directamente en el corazón del territorio de los orcos, creyendo que había un camino seguro entre los campamentos de esas tribus.'","Knakk y Kafli se dirigieron hacia el este cuando la compañía de enanos se separó al pie de las escaleras de la Guardia Orca. Consideraban que los orcos no eran más que un pequeño obstáculo y que podrían abrirse paso a través de su territorio y acampar al otro lado de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.","Busca a los enanos que se dirigieron hacia el este","En la mano fría y rígida de este enano hay un medallón bellamente tallado a mano. Tras manipularlo un rato, te has dado cuenta de que no es un medallón normal y que no se abre con facilidad. Deberías llevárselo al compañero de este enano caído, que tal vez continuó sin él y debería encontrarse en algún lugar al este.","En busca de los desaparecidos","Recogiste el medallón que Kafli sujetaba cuando murió.","Knakk debió de continuar después de que Kafli cayera en manos de los orcos, pero quizás no esté muy lejos. Seguro que no habría querido abandonar a su amigo...","Aquí yace Kafli... ¿eso que tiene agarrado en la mano es un collar?","Encuentra a Knakk"},
[10749]={"Rastreadores de Haudh Eldacar","Habla con Rodlam en el Camino de los Reyes","Acaba con Angmarim en Haudh Eldacar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Angmar ha mostrado interés por Haudh Eldacar.","'Tienes que retrasarlos mientras buscamos la razón por la que están aquí.'","'A diferencia de Haudh Arantar, donde los Angmarim se limitan a saquear y destruir la cripta, el registro en Haudh Eldacar parece mucho más metódico. Hasta ahora se ha sacado muy poco.\
\
'Lo que sea que estén buscando allí debe de ser de gran importancia para su propósito aquí en Annúminas.\
\
'Debemos retrasarlos mientras descubrimos cuál es su objetivo. Si logras expulsar al grupo que está registrando el interior, eso nos daría un tiempo muy valioso.'","Angmarim derrotados en Haudh Eldacar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Haudh Eldacar se encuentra al suroeste del campamento de los Montaraces, en el Camino de los Reyes.\
\
Rodlam te ha pedido que te adentres en Haudh Eldacar y derrotes a los Angmarim que se encuentran allí.","Rodlam se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces, en el Camino de los Reyes.\
\
A Rodlam le interesará saber que derrotaste a muchos Angmarim en Haudh Eldacar.","'Aún no conozco su objetivo final, pero sé que lo hemos retrasado, aunque solo sea un poco.'"},
[10753]={"Bráthi the Master Prospector is in search of rare treasures in Gundabad.","Collected dwarf-made treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Thank you! These lost treasures are indeed a thing of beauty and each has a story to tell! Well done!'","Collect dwarf-made treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deliver the dwarf-made treasure to Bráthi","'There are a fair number of old trinkets and treasures to be found in Gundabad. I am sure there are some to be found in forgotten chests and on the corpses of unlucky adventurers. If you recover any on your travels in Gundabad, I would very much like them, my friend!'","Searching For Treasures","Dwarf-made treasure can be found on chests, packs, and corpses throughout Gundabad.\
\
You should return to Bráthi when you have collected enough dwarf-made treasures."},
[10755]={"You have arrived at Talan Brethil","You have arrived at Talan Fanuidhol","'Have you seen the Great Eagles of the Misty Mountains? They are a sight to behold.'","You scan the horizon, but do not see any Great Eagles","Searching for Eagles","You have arrived at Talan Gwilith","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> into the distance from Talan Gwilith","Talk to Cúvroval at Talan Revail","Cúvroval has received orders that every flet must be on the look-out for a sighting of one of the magnificent Great Eagles who hail from the northern Misty Mountains.","Cúvroval is at Talan Revail, north-east of Cerin Amroth.\
\
You should return to Cúvroval to report that empty skies were all you saw from the telain.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> into the distance from Talan Fanuidhol","The sky is empty of any Great Eagle, as far as you can see","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> into the distance from Talan Brethil","You are unable to spot any bird larger than a hawk","Talan Brethil is to the south-east of Talan Revail, along the banks of the Anduin. Talan Gwilith and Talan Fanuidhol are well west and a bit south of Talan Revail, along the border of Fanuidhol where the Orcs have recently emerged from Moria.\
\
Cúvroval wants you to go to three of the telain and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> into the distance from atop all three of them to search for a Great Eagle in the sky. She was not told why this look-out had to be kept, only that it was essential.","'Nothing? You are certain? Ah well.\
\
'The truth is, I have no idea why any of the Great Eagles should be paying us a visit at this time anyway.'","'Whence hail you and wherefore come you here, brave ${RACE}? To have come this far into the Golden Wood, you must have earned the trust of the archers who guard our borders. That is why I feel able to ask you for aid: I have orders that I fear I cannot fulfil alone. Will you help?\
\
'Have you ever sighted one of the majestic Great Eagles who hail from eyries north of the High Pass in the Misty Mountains? Well, my orders are to keep a stringent look-out for one of them -- it is not my privilege to know why. Will you go to the nearby Telain -- Talan being our word for the platforms in the trees that you call flets -- and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for them?\
\
'Talan Brethil is south-east of here, along the banks of the Anduin. Talan Gwilith and Talan Fanuidhol are well west and a bit south of here, along the border of Fanuidhol, where the Orcs have recently emerged from Moria.'"},
[10756]={"Searching for Erkenbrand","Marton is destroyed! You should search for survivors who might yet be nearby","'I do not know where Erkenbrand would go after the Fords of Isen fell. Perhaps with Grimbold back to the town of Grimslade, or perhaps to Marton which lies closer to the Gap. Or perhaps elsewhere.\
\
'I urge you to begin your search in Marton, for many men bear news thither as soon as they have news to bear. Good luck to you, ${PLAYER}! I know I will see you again soon.'","Gather news of Erkenbrand in Marton","'Where is my husband Gladsúnu? Have you come to tell me of him? Is he in good health? When can he come back? He is Thane, and we need him!\
\
'He has been holding the fords, but the fords were lost. Please, tell me of my husband!'","You have decided to begin your search for Erkenbrand in the town nearest the Fords of Isen: Marton.","Marton is north-west of Helm's Dike in the Westfold.\
\
You should head to Marton to begin your search for Erkenbrand and the other missing lords of the Westfold.","It is likely that any survivors from Marton fled north of town into the trees and stony hills.\
\
You should search north of Marton in the stony hills for any refugees who may have survived.","Find survivors who escaped Marton","This part of the woods looks to have many promising hiding spots...."},
[10757]={"'¿Has encontrado ya ese manantial? Hawkling dijo que estaba justo al oeste de la entrada del Bosque Viejo. ¡Realmente podríamos usar esa agua!'","'¡Gracias por traer esa agua... realmente la necesitábamos!'","'Es una buena cosa lo que has hecho, trayendo esa agua a tu amigo.'","La entrada del Bosque Viejo está al este, y el campamento de Adso está al norte desde allí. \
\
Adso te envió al Bosque Viejo a buscar agua, pero sin nada en las manos. Baya de Oro te ha dado un cubo en el que llevar agua de vuelta al campamento de Adso y te ha concedido permiso para sacar agua de su estanque, pero advierte que el Bosque es peligroso.","Habla con la hermosa mujer en el manantial","'¡Gracias, ${PLAYER}! Nos has ahorrado mucho tiempo y problemas. No desperdiciaré más de tu tiempo con esto. Si necesitamos más, enviaré a mis cazadores al manantial.\
\
'Toma esto como pago por tus esfuerzos. Debo volver al trabajo.'","Encuentra el manantial","'Tienes que llevar esa agua a tus amigos, pero ten cuidado. El Bosque puede intentar obstaculizarte.'","Graham Larkspur desea hablar contigo de nuevo.","Graham Larkspur es uno de los trabajadores de Adso. Él y sus compañeros se están quedando sin agua y necesitan ayuda para reponer su suministro.","'¿Has traído ya ese agua? Nos estamos quedando muy cortos, y este es un trabajo sediento. ¡Por favor, apúrate!'","'Hemos estado trabajando bastante duro en este edificio durante algún tiempo, y es un trabajo sediento, pero parece que nuestro suministro de agua se está agotando. \
\
'Uno de nuestros cazadores encontró un manantial en las partes norteñas del Bosque Viejo donde el agua es particularmente dulce y refrescante. Algo extraño de encontrar en un bosque tan miserable y sombrío. Ve al suroeste hacia el Bosque Viejo y mantente en los bosques del norte. El manantial es un lugar hermoso... difícil de perderse en ese bosque lúgubre. \
\
'Agradecería que pudieras traer esa agua para mí lo antes posible. Odio quedarme sin ella antes de que regreses. El Bosque se está volviendo peligroso, oigo, así que querrás tener cuidado.'","Has traído el agua de vuelta a Graham Larkspur","Al encontrar el manantial al que Graham Larkspur te envió, notaste a una mujer hermosa pero de aspecto extraño de pie debajo del roble en la orilla occidental del río. Quizás ella posea los medios para que lleves agua de vuelta al campamento de Adso.","Recoge el cubo","Hay una mujer extraña y hermosa de pie cerca del manantial","'Fue algo amable lo que hiciste, trayendo esa agua a tu amigo hobbit.'","La entrada al Bosque Viejo está al sur del campamento de Adso. El manantial se encuentra hacia el oeste dentro del bosque. \
\
Graham Larkspur te ha pedido que traigas agua del manantial que sus cazadores encontraron.","'Has venido de lejos por agua y hacia un peligro que no conoces. Es cierto que el agua de mi estanque es la más dulce, y con gusto compartiré, pero el Bosque es salvaje e indómito, poco amistoso con aquellos que no pertenecen.\
\
'Toma este cubo y saca agua de mi estanque. A menos que tus amigos beban demasiado ávidamente, esto durará mucho más que el agua de los pozos de Bree.\
\
'Ten cuidado en tu viaje de regreso al Camino, no sea que el Bosque te atrape. Mi Tom es el Maestro, pero está ocupado con sus asuntos y puede que no venga a salvarte. Que te vaya bien.'","Buscando manantiales frescos"},
[10758]={"Frustrated at her failure to locate the Dubarâkh, Girhâzi needs a moment to herself and sent you to talk to Amâsu instead.","Talk to Girhâzi","Complete Instance: Searching for Hope","'Please excuse Girhâzi's behaviour. I have noticed that when she does not wish to feel pain, she recasts it into anger. It has been so since Ukhâx and her boys were taken from her. Her pain is something she will eventually have to face, but let us not worry ourselves about it today.'","'I am unsurprised that Khûldim lied to us. I only wish it had not been so. Curse it all, now we have no hope of finding the Dubarâkh! That coward got himself killed when he could have gone home to Ordâkh! What a fool! He lied to us for no reason but to deprive us of something we want.'\
\
You can see her sadness shifting into anger.\
\
'I will never understand why people hate us so. Leave me be, I need to think. Talk to Amâsu if you must talk to someone.'","Talk to Amâsu","You accompanied Girhâzi to explore the abandoned salt mine of Ashunûg in search of the Dubarâkh. Instead of a library, you found a cult and Khûldim Umûn found death at the hands of his would-be rescuers.","Khûldim Umûn has informed Girhâzi that the Dubarâkh is inside an abandoned salt mine. You are invited to join them as they search the caves for the lost library of Ambarûli culture and history.","Searching for Hope","Talk to Girhâzi when you are ready to travel to the salt mine in search of the Dubarâkh.","'I could not have gotten this information without you, ${PLAYER}. Would you like to come with us to search this salt mine? I will gather some Dumûri volunteers and get Khûldim ready to be moved. Let me know when you are ready and we will be on our way.'","'You are ready to go on this expedition? Then let us be off.'"},
[10759]={"You should return to Thranduil in Felegoth.","'Hold, ${PLAYER}. The spider flees, but look closely. The wound you have given it has in return given us a trail of blood to follow. If we keep our distance, we might follow this fleeing spider back to Iphantemel's den.'","Track the wounded spider","Thranduil's chief hunter, Thorlind, has also been on Iphantemel's trail.","'While you sought proof by way of trap, I bade my chief hunter, Thorlind, to search these woods he knows so well for other signs of the spider Iphantemel. He, too, has just returned and bears tidings we should hear.'","Find the spiders by the Rhachló","Search for Iphantemel's den","An old rocky pass leads downward into a shadow-covered gorge","The trail of spider blood begins near the banks of Rhachló and will hopefully lead right to the den of Iphantemel.\
\
You should track the wounded spider.","Thorlind has spotted spiders harvesting sap along the river-banks of the Rhachló.\
\
You should seek out the spiders that Thorlind found.","'Torech Emel is where old Iphantemel hides? I wonder how long the ancient thing has hidden there, where no Elf's foot ever treads. She will be on her guard, I do not doubt, but we know she may be provoked.\
\
'Let us make preparations against her brood.'","The dripping trail of blood from the spider continues deeper into the forest","Approach one of the spiders","The wounded spider flees!","Talk to Thranduil","Searching for Iphantemel","Talk to Thorlind","'Far and wide have I wandered through our woods, and now I well and truly believe the spiders have gone. This should be glad news, but instead it troubles me. At long last, when I was full weary and on the brink of giving up, I happened upon a group of spiders by the banks of the Rhachló, gathering sap from a gnarled and wounded tree.\
\
'They were too great in number and I dared not go closer, but with your help we might come closer and learn more, either by capture or chase.'","Thorlind has spotted spiders harvesting sap along the river-banks of the Rhachló.\
\
You should approach one of these sap-harvesting spiders.","You should talk to Thorlind, in Felegoth, about what he has found.","A spider has noticed you!","'I think we have found what we sought, ${PLAYER}. See how webs entangle the way ahead. Yea, I can even hear her brood moving to and fro down there.\
\
'Come, we should report back to King Thranduil. The brood is too much for the two of us alone.'","You should talk to Thorlind by the banks of the Rhachló.","You should talk to Thorlind where he stands just outside Torech Emel."},
[10760]={"Mincham is at his camp north of the barrows.\
\
You should return to Mincham and deliver the intact corrupted phial you collected.","The foetid liquid you discovered in the barrows of the Lich Bluffs may yet provide a clue to the mystery of the Dead in that place.","Return to Mincham with the corrupted phial","'Perhaps if you can find an intact phial of this liquid, I may be able to determine its source.'","Wights can be found in great numbers among the southernmost barrows of the Lich Bluffs.\
\
Mincham has asked you to try and recover an intact phial of the foetid liquid from the wights of the Lich Bluffs.","'This liquid you recovered may yet provide us a clue as to the forces behind the raising of the wights in the Lich Bluffs. I have heard of only a few creatures with such power, one of whom is the Witch-king of Angmar, but he is accounted for.\
\
'Perhaps if you can secure an intact phial of this liquid from one of the wights, I may be able to determine something of its origin.\
\
'I have seen many wights wandering among the barrows in the southern hills of the Lich Bluffs.'","Collected an intact corrupted phial","'The delivery of this phial is a grim but important discovery. It appears that these phials are being used to corrupt the bodies of the fallen in the Lich Bluffs. It may also partially be the cause of the corrupted cairn-stones.\
\
'We must work quickly to unravel who is behind this plot.'","Searching for Signs","Collect an intact corrupted phial from the wights of the Lich Bluffs"},
[10761]={"The path north will be difficult but if there are survivors, you must try and rescue them.","The injured farmer can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should kneel and listen to what the injured farmer has to say.","'Quick, a farmer from Talath Anor has come to the North-gate. He is injured and could use some comforting. Please, go to this man and find out what brings him here!'","You should patrol the road north and search for survivors in Talath Anor.","This Easterling appears to have been slain recently.","Searching for Survivors","A slain body nearby catches your attention","Ingold can be found at the northern gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","Patrol the road north and search for survivors","Approach and examine the body","Speak with Ingold","'So, Cair Andros has fallen and much of Talath Anor is in ruins. I had heard the rumours but did not wish to believe it so.\
\
'If there are indeed more Gondorians holding out in Talath Anor, we must rescue them. ${PLAYER}, now is the time to part ways.\
\
'You must search Talath Anor for any survivors.'","You see no signs of survivors yet and should press on","Ingold has learned of an injured farmer who has made his way to the North-gate!","The farmer's breaths are short but his words are heavy","Continue to patrol the road north and search for survivors","The slain body is located on the road in Talath Anor.\
\
You should examine the body.","<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> and listen to the injured farmer"},
[10762]={"The water in the channel is calm and warm","Not a bad place to swim, but it is quite public","Searching for Swimming Spots","Swim in the southern cove","Swim off the south-western beach","This is a nice, quiet place to swim","The water is warm and perfect for swimming","The water is cold and the waves are a bit much","Swim at the west side of the harbour","Merkhâma has asked you to test various swimming spots around Furtherholm and then share your opinions with her.","Visitors often ask Merkhâma where the best places to swim are, but she doesn't know.","'I must linger here and be available to guests who ask for help. Many ask for advice on where the best swimming places are, and I admit I do not know! I stand here all the time!\
\
'Were you to take some time to explore the island and test out places to swim, I will reward you when you return and tell me what you learned.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","You have tested various swimming spots around Furtherholm. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon and share your opinions with her.","Talk to Merkhâma","'So ${PLAYER}, how was the swimming?'\
\
You tell her that the water is warmer where it is shallow and it's easier to swim where there are less waves - and advise her on where these places are.\
\
'Thank you, you have been of much help. As a mariner, I usually prioritize staying on the boat and not ending up in the water. I do not understand people who go in the water on purpose, but when they ask, I will repeat what you have told me. You have my thanks!'","Swim in the northern channel","Swim off the western beach"},
[10763]={"'So ${PLAYER}, how was the swimming?'\
\
You tell her that the water is dangerous and visitors will surely drown. Currents could pull you away, waves could pull you under, and the sea is full of deadly creatures that can bite or sting you.\
\
'Well, to be honest, you are not wrong! As a mariner, I usually prioritize staying on the boat and not ending up in the water. I do not understand people who go in the water on purpose, but when they ask, I will need something to tell them. I suppose I can just tell them to be cautious and choose a swimming place with safety in mind. Many thanks for your help!'","Searching for Swimming Spots","Swim in the southern cove","The water is deep and people are just watching you possibly drown!","This would be a lot nicer if the water was more shallow","Swim off the south-western beach","Merkhâma has asked you to test various swimming spots around Furtherholm and then share your opinions with her.","It's all right here, but way too deep","Swim at the west side of the harbour","There is entirely too much water here!","Visitors often ask Merkhâma where the best places to swim are, but she doesn't know.","'I must linger here and be available to guests who ask for help. Many ask for advice on where the best swimming places are, and I admit I do not know! I stand here all the time!\
\
'Were you to take some time to explore the island and test out places to swim, I will reward you when you return and tell me what you learned.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","You have tested various swimming spots around Furtherholm. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon and share your opinions with her.","Talk to Merkhâma","Swim in the northern channel","What a dangerous place - this was a mistake!","Swim off the western beach"},
[10766]={"Celethon asked you to help them collect seashells by the seashore.\
\
Collect seashells on the beach near Linhir.","This seashell seems to be prettier than others, though whether it counts as 'double-pretty' remains to be seen","Celethon examines each shell with what appears to be a jeweller's loupe before tucking them in his pockets.\
\
'The shells aren't for me, they're for my mum.\
\
'Every summer, Miss Túrith would make a necklace out of shells and give it to my mum, but Miss Túrith still hasn't come home from the war. Mum's really sad about it, so I want to try making one instead.\
\
'I promise I'll come home soon. Please don't tell my mum what I'm doing here. I want it to be a secret.'","Collected seashells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have collected enough seashells.\
\
Talk to Celethon on the beach near Linhir.","Seashells by the Seashore","'Let me guess, he was collecting seashells again? He's been at it for days. He thinks I don't notice the growing pile hidden in his room.'\
\
Sadness creeps into her voice.\
\
'Did he tell you about Túrith? It took so long for him to warm up to her after his father passed, but now he can't imagine a world without her. Neither can I.\
\
'She left to join the fighting at Minas Tirith. She still hasn't come home. I begin to worry she never may, and I think he fears the same.'\
\
She sighs and takes a moment to gather herself.\
\
'I should talk to him about this.\
\
'Thank you, adventurer, for your help.'","Collect a pearlescent seashell","Talk to Celethon","You have secured a promise from Celethon to return home. It's time to tell Meligrien.\
\
Talk to Meligrien in Linhir.","Talk to Meligrien","Collect seashells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Mother worries too much. I'm old enough to be on my own!\
\
'What am I doing here? I need to collect some seashells for... reasons. If you help me find some, I'll go home sooner rather than later.'\
\
You agree to help.\
\
'Hooray! In addition to a few normal shells, could you find some unique ones, too?'","Collect a vibrant seashell","This seashell seems sufficiently pearlescent","Collect a 'double-pretty' seashell","This seashell seems sufficiently vibrant","'Hello, friend. May I ask you for a small favour? My son is supposed to be helping me with some chores, but he's nowhere to be found. I suspect he's gone to the beach again, along the coast south of town. Could you tell him his mother is worried about him and that he should come home? His name is Celethon.'","Meligrien would like for you to check on her child near the beach along Linhir's southern coast.","Meligrien has asked you to look for her child, Celethon. She suspects he can be found by the beach near Linhir.\
\
Talk to Celethon.","'I'll be home soon, my Meligrien, Celethon. Wait just a bit longer.'"},
[10768]={"'¡Vaya, vaya! ¡Te has congelado hasta los huesos, ${PLAYERNAME:querido[m]|querida[f]}! ¡Debería haber sabido que era mala idea enviarte a Helegrod! ¿Encontraste alguna de las monedas del viejo Storvâgûn?\
\
'¡Así que la historia era cierta! ¡Lo sabía!\
\
'Me temo que no tengo bufandas ni capas que ofrecerte, pero quizás esto te sirva'","Storvâgûn aparece durante el Festival de Yule en Jefe del Pasado: Storvâgûn.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión solo puede progresarse en el nivel 2 de Jefe del Pasado: Storvâgûn. Además, solo puede completarse una vez por Festival de Yule.</rgb>","Entrega las monedas de oro viles a Verbena Manoverde en Risco Invernal","Estacional: Las Riquezas de Storvâgûn","Monedas de oro viles obtenidas de Storvâgûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Verbena Manoverde se encuentra en Risco Invernal.\
\
Has juntado unas cuantas monedas de oro viles y ahora debes entregárselas a Verbena Manoverde.","'¡Hola! ¿Qué tal lo estás pasando en el Festival de Yule?\
\
'Hay mucha comida y algo de teatro... ¡Qué maravilla! Pero ahora que lo pienso... Oí una historia curiosa de uno de los clientes de Farol Escarchado. ¿También la has oído?\
\
'¿No? Bueno, cuenta que hubo una vez un viejo y codicioso gigante llamado Storvâgûn que vivía en lo alto de Helegrod. Era tan codicioso que decidió hablar en nombre de todos sus amigos y hacer un trato con unos Hombres del Norte de lo más desagradables. Y lo que es peor, todos sus amigos estuvieron de acuerdo, ¡salvo uno! Ese, Arifael, era un gigante diferente... ¡un gigante amigable! Así que Arifael encontró nuevos amigos y los envió a detener al viejo Storvâgûn para que dejara de ser tan egoísta. ¡Y luego se llevaron todo su tesoro!\
\
'Ahora que lo digo en voz alta... creo que he olvidado la moraleja del cuento. ¡Pero estoy segura de que la hay!\
\
'En fin, se dice que el viejo Storvâgûn vuelve para contar sus riquezas en lo alto de Helegrod durante el Festival de Yule. No sé si creerlo, pero si fuera cierto, ¡apuesto a que ${PLAYERNAME:un aventurero[m]|una aventurera[f]} valiente como tú podría robarle algunas monedas sin que se diera cuenta!\
\
'Te recompensaría bien, pero si decides ir a buscar su oro, ¡no me culpes si también te encuentras con el gigante!'","Los Hombres de Angmar otorgaron grandes riquezas a Storvâgûn. Aunque muchas de sus baratijas portan la corrupción del Rey Brujo de Angmar, los aventureros valientes podrían descubrir las riquezas más preciadas de Storvâgûn."},
[10769]={"Recoge monedas de oro ensangrentadas de Naruhel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Extiendes las monedas que has reunido. El Sargento Tom las acepta y asiente solemnemente.\
\
'Estas son sin duda las mismas monedas de las que habló aquel juglar. Gracias, por atreverte a entrar en ese lugar terrible con la esperanza de ayudar al pueblo de las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
'Aquí, toma este obsequio. Es lo menos que puedo hacer. ¡Disfruta el resto del Festival de Primavera!'","Las monedas de oro ensangrentadas pueden obtenerse derrotando a Naruhel una vez al día durante el Festival de Primavera en Jefa de las Cámaras: Naruhel.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión solo puede progresar en Tier 3 de Jefa de las Cámaras: Naruhel. Además, solo puede completarse una vez por Festival de Primavera.</rgb>","Has recogido monedas de oro ensangrentadas de Naruhel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estacional: Las Monedas de Naruhel","El Sargento Tom se encuentra en el Recinto del Festival, en los Campos de Caballos de Bree.\
\
Has reunido varias monedas de oro ensangrentadas y ahora debes entregárselas al Sargento Tom.","El Sargento Tom ha oído relatos de aventureros que enfrentaron a Naruhel la Doncella Roja y quiere que le lleves pruebas de tus hazañas.","Entrega las monedas al Sargento Tom en el Recinto del Festival","'¡Hola! ¿Disfrutando del Festival de Primavera? Si te sientes con valentía, tengo un encargo perfecto para ti.\
\
'Un día, estaba comiendo y bebiendo en el Poney Pisador cuando escuché a un Juglar contando historias. Narraba el caso de un manantial corrompido en lo profundo de Garth Agarwen, una fortaleza en las Tierras Solitarias. Se dice que una doncella del agua llamada Naruhel vive allí, y que cayó debido a la sangre derramada en sus aguas durante las guerras entre Angmar y el Reino del Norte.\
\
'En el pantano hay una serie de monedas de oro que fueron entregadas como ofrenda a la doncella del río. Lamentablemente, estas monedas, al igual que la criatura misma, se han oscurecido por la sangre derramada en la zona.\
\
'Ya que la esperanza brota eterna, nuestra esperanza es que puedas purificar a esta criatura de la corrupción que infecta estas tierras. Si me traes monedas que lleven la señal de su aflicción como prueba de tus actos, ¡te recompensaré por tus esfuerzos!'"},
[10770]={"Recoge monedas forjadas con hierro de la Falla de Thrâng (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Hola! ¿Disfrutando del Festival de verano? Oye, si te sientes valiente, tengo un trabajo para el que serías perfecto.\
\
'Un día, estaba disfrutando de una comida y una bebida en el Dragón Verde, y escuché a un Músico contar algunas historias. Contó la historia de un grupo de montaraces y aventureros que entraron en una gran falla en las tierras malditas de Angmar, y enfrentaron todo tipo de horrores. Dicen que el pozo era tan profundo que el suelo mismo estaba tan caliente como el hierro en una forja, y era hogar de gigantes de fuego y orcos en llamas.\
\
'¡Orcos en llamas! ¿Puedes creerlo? Yo no podía, pero luego, sacó una moneda muy inusual. Era oscura, y tenía un brillo peculiar. Hierro de la Falla, dijo que era, hecho del metal y obsidiana de ese horrible lugar. ¡Eso despertó mi interés!\
\
'Estoy escuchando rumores de que la Falla se ha abierto nuevamente, y aventureros como tú están desafiando las profundidades. Si me traes algunas de estas monedas como prueba de esta historia, te recompensaré por tus esfuerzos.'","Las monedas forjadas con hierro de la Falla se pueden ganar derrotando a Thrâng una vez por día durante el Festival de verano en Señor de los cofres: Thrâng.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión solo se puede avanzar en el nivel 2 de Señor de los cofres: Thrâng. Además, esta misión solo se puede completar una vez por Festival de verano.</rgb>","Entrega las monedas a Campanula Redondo en el Árbol de la Fiesta","Campanula Redondo ha escuchado la historia de aventureros que se atreven a entrar en la Falla de Nûrz Ghâshu y le gustaría que le trajeras evidencia de este terrible lugar.","Monedas forjadas con hierro de la Falla recogidas de Thrâng (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estacional: Las monedas de la Falla","Tienes en tus manos las monedas que has reunido. Campanula las acepta, una amplia sonrisa se extiende por su rostro.\
\
'¡Estas son sin duda las mismas monedas que vi ese día en el Dragón Verde! ¡Así que la historia era cierta! Gracias, por haber desafiado ese terrible lugar por el bien de la curiosidad de esta vieja hobbit.\
\
'Aquí, toma este regalo. Es lo mínimo que puedo hacer. ¡Disfruta el resto del Festival de verano!'","Puedes encontrar a Campanula Redondo en el Árbol de la Fiesta en la Comarca.\
\
Has recogido varias monedas forjadas con hierro de la Falla y ahora debes entregárselas a Campanula Redondo."},
[10771]={"Carne de Res Sazonada con Coliflor — Introducción","El Maestro Cocinero también es el escribiente de la Sociedad de los Mathoms, y ha estado tan ocupado que no podrá preparar la próxima cena de la Sociedad.","Lleva la carne de res sazonada con coliflor a Baldwin Colazorro","'¿Has conseguido carne de res sazonada con coliflor? ¡Me has salvado! No sé cómo agradecértelo, ${PLAYER}.'","Recoge carne de res sazonada con coliflor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Baldwin Colazorro está en la Casa de los Mathoms, en Cavada Grande, en la Comarca.\
\
Baldwin te ha pedido que le traigas carne de res sazonada con coliflor para los cocineros de la Sociedad de los Mathoms.","'¡Hola, hola! Mi nombre es Baldwin Colazorro, hijo de Brombard Colazorro... él es el encargado de la Casa de los Mathoms, ya sabes. Soy uno de los miembros más importantes de la Sociedad de los Mathoms; estoy a cargo de supervisar la recolección de los deliciosos platos del menú para nuestras extravagantes cenas de la Sociedad, además del etiquetado y la limpieza de varias de las secciones más importantes de los almacenes de la Casa de los Mathoms.\
\
'Hemos tenido algunos problemitas: con tantos aventureros llegando con nuevos mathoms, ¡jamás había visto tantos en toda mi vida! El viejo Grisin insiste en que todos los tengamos clasificados y ordenados antes de pensar en el menú de la cena... una tontería, si me preguntas.\
\
'Nuestro Maestro Cocinero lleva tanto tiempo encerrado en el sótano de la Casa de los Mathoms que empiezo a temer que haya olvidado cómo cocinar. Y lo que más me preocupa es que quizá no tenga tiempo de preparar su especialidad, carne de res sazonada con coliflor, para nuestra próxima cena.\
\
'¡No podemos celebrar la cena sin algo para servir! ¿Crees que podrías conseguirnos carne de res sazonada con coliflor? Harías un gran servicio a la Sociedad de los Mathoms.'","'¿Encontraste ya carne de res sazonada con coliflor?'","Carne de res sazonada con coliflor recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10774]={"'¿Sabes una cosa, ${PLAYER}? ¡Creo que estoy listo para reunirme contigo de vuelta en Lothlórien! Te esperaré delante de Caras Galadhon, y quizá encontremos comida de verdad, porque mi estómago no para de quejarse.'","'Oh, sí he visto a tu lince. Pasó por aquí corriendo, tiró los papeles de esta mesa y continuó hacia el este. Ya no está en Ost Galadh.'","Willem Bigotes está junto a una alforja sucia que parece haber sido propiedad de un orco. El lince te mira con orgullo, y recoges la alforja.\
\
Le echas un vistazo rápido al interior, y su contenido te hace reír pese a ti mismo. Decides llevársela a Bingo en la Posada Embrujada.","'Acabo de regresar de Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}, y vi algo realmente peculiar. Había un lince luchando contra orcos justo dentro de la puerta de Fennas Guldur, al sureste. Mientras me alejaba sigilosamente, vi al lince subir por una pendiente hacia el norte, justo detrás del muro.\
\
'Si buscas a esta curiosa criatura, deberías dirigirte al sureste, a Fennas Guldur, y luego subir la pendiente hacia el norte una vez cruces la puerta. Si es enemigo de los orcos, ¡debe de ser amigo de la Hueste Dorada!'","'No creo que tu amigo el lince siga en Audaghaim. Ha ido a otra parte del Gran Bosque Verde.'","El estómago de Bingo le ha hecho completamente imposible concentrarse en seguir escribiendo su libro, y necesita que hagas algo respecto a esta situación de hambre.","Bingo quiere encontrarse contigo fuera de la puerta de Caras Galadhon, en Lothlórien.\
\
Bingo ya ha visto suficiente del Bosque Negro y ha decidido viajar contigo de vuelta a Lothlórien.","Willem Bigotes te mira con orgullo. ¿Quizá la alforja contiene algo útil para Bingo, después de todo?","Bingo está en la Posada Embrujada, situada en los Troncosombríos del Bosque Negro.\
\
Has recuperado una alforja orca encontrada por Willem Bigotes, y deberías llevársela a Bingo.","'Veo que has regresado. ¿Qué opinó tu amigo de las aventuras de la Hueste Dorada en el Bosque Negro?'\
\
Le explicas a Calengoth el engaño de Bingo y le transmites las sinceras disculpas del hobbit. El Elfo asiente solemnemente, aunque con una sonrisa en los labios.\
\
'Bingo debe de tener una opinión muy pobre de la inteligencia de los Elfos si creyó que realmente me engañó con su treta. No fue así. Pero hace falta un gran corazón para admitir algo así, y mi negativa a llevarlo a través del río no fue por malicia, sino por preocupación por su seguridad. Acepto sus disculpas.\
\
'También puede que tenga la solución a su hambre. Dale este pequeño paquete de lembas, junto con mis mejores deseos. Creo que lo primero curará su hambre y lo segundo aliviará su culpa, pues imagino que esta última es la verdadera fuente de su maldición, y una vez perdonado, espero que esté bien. ¡Esa es mi impresión!'","'Vi al lince que buscas. Corría a gran velocidad hacia el sureste, en dirección a Fennas Guldur. Si cruzó la puerta y está ahora al otro lado del muro, no lo sé.'","Willem Bigotes está dentro del muro exterior de Dol Guldur, subiendo una pendiente al norte de Fennas Guldur.\
\
Has encontrado a Willem, y parece que él ha encontrado una alforja sucia de algún tipo.","'¡Sí, vi a tu lince! Pasó corriendo delante de nosotros, no sin antes saltar sobre esta mesa y esparcir los papeles por todas partes.\
\
'No se quedó. Corrió hacia el este, saliendo de Ost Galadh.'","Calengoth está en los muelles de Lothlórien, al oeste de Imlad Lalaith.\
\
Bingo cree que ha caído víctima de una maldición que le provoca punzadas de hambre antinaturales, y quiere que pidas disculpas a Calengoth por el engaño que permitió al hobbit cruzar el río hacia el Bosque Negro.","'El lince que sigue a tu amigo Bingo no se quedó en la Posada. Creo que estaba buscando comida y se marchó hacia el este.'","Encuentra a Willem Bigotes en algún lugar del Bosque Negro","Habla con Calengoth en los muelles de Lothlórien","Regresa con Bingo a la Posada Embrujada con la alforja que encontró Willem","'Acabo de regresar de Dol Guldur, ${PLAYER}, y vi algo realmente curioso. Había un lince luchando contra orcos justo dentro de la puerta de Fennas Guldur, al este. Cuando me alejaba a escondidas, vi al lince subir por una pendiente hacia el norte, justo detrás del muro.\
\
'Si buscas a esta extraña criatura, deberías ir hacia Fennas Guldur, al este, y luego subir la pendiente al norte una vez cruces la puerta. Si es enemigo de los orcos, ¡debe ser amigo de la Hueste Dorada!'","'No he visto ningún lince que coincida con tu descripción en el Bosque Ahogado. Quizá deberías viajar al noreste y preguntar si alguien en Ost Galadh ha visto algo.'","Lleva el paquete de lembas a Bingo fuera de Caras Galadhon, en Lothlórien","'Hemos vuelto a tierras más agradables. Es un alivio dejar atrás el Bosque Negro, pero... bueno, hay algo que me preocupa.'\
\
La expresión alegre de Bingo ha desaparecido. Parece bastante afectado.\
\
'¡Es este apetito mío! ¡A nosotros los Boffin nos gustan tantas comidas como a cualquiera, y no me es ajeno escabullirme a la despensa para tomar uno o dos bocados entre comidas! Pero este hambre es más punzante que cualquier otra que recuerde. Me puse a pensar qué me ha hecho tener tanta hambre, y me di cuenta de que comenzó aproximadamente cuando cruzamos el río hacia el Bosque Negro.\
\
'¡Hay algo antinatural en esto! ¿Es una maldición? Para ser maldecido tienes que haber hecho algo malo. ¿No dijo Adolinda algo sobre un gran mal en su pasado? Pues bien, estuve pensando y, aunque no diría que he hecho nada especialmente malvado, no fui honesto con Calengoth, ¿verdad? Usamos el engaño para conseguir que nos dejara cruzar el río. ¿Es este aumento de hambre una maldición por mi mal comportamiento?\
\
'¡Tienes que ir a ver a Calengoth en los muelles y disculparte por mis mentiras, ${PLAYER}! ¡Temo desfallecer por esta maldición si no lo haces!'","'Le conté a Willem nuestro problema, y salió corriendo. ¿Puedes preguntar por la Posada a ver si alguien sabe qué ha sido de él? ¡Imagino que ha ido en busca de un segundo desayuno, y te agradecería muchísimo que lo trajeras de vuelta con él!'","Recoges la alforja orca, y Willem ronronea satisfecho","'¿Calengoth aceptó mis disculpas? ¡Maravilloso, maravilloso! ¡Me alegra oírlo! ¿Y esto qué es? ¿Lembas? Qué interesante. Parece un tipo de pastel, aunque algo sencillo. ¿Es un regalo de Calengoth?'\
\
Bingo da un pequeño mordisco y lo saborea un momento.\
\
'¡Ah! ¡No esperaba que fuera tan delicioso! ¡Y tan saciante! Vaya, este lembas ha curado por completo mi maldición, si es que realmente lo era. Es agradable tener el estómago lleno; ahora estoy listo para viajar por el Gran Río en busca de nuevas aventuras.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La próxima semana: 'Las Riberas del Gran Río' (Nivel recomendado: 70)</rgb>","'Vi a ese lince correr hacia el este. Se movía con mucha prisa.'","Bingo está fuera de la puerta de Caras Galadhon, en Lothlórien.\
\
Calengoth te dio un pequeño paquete de lembas para entregárselo a Bingo y también perdonó al hobbit por su engaño.","Bingo toma con cuidado la alforja orca.\
\
'¿Qué es esto? ¿W.W. encontró esta alforja para mí? ¡Qué detalle! ¿Crees que contiene comida? La bolsa parece bastante deteriorada, pero veamos... pequeños trastos... trozos de metal doblado... esto está bastante peludo...'\
\
De repente Bingo da un salto hacia atrás y deja caer la alforja sobre la mesa. Tras un momento, empieza a reír.\
\
'¡Hay patas de araña aquí dentro! Willem, ¿pensaste que estaba descontento por lo POCAS patas de araña que trajo ${PLAYER}? ¡No era eso en absoluto! ¿Por qué todos quieren que pruebe estas cosas tan desagradables? ¿Sabes una cosa, ${PLAYER}? Creo que estoy listo para regresar a Lothlórien. Te esperaré delante de Caras Galadhon, y quizá encontremos algo de comida de verdad, ¡porque mi estómago se queja muchísimo!'","'¡Este estómago vacío me ha hecho completamente imposible concentrarme en seguir documentando nuestra estancia en el Bosque Negro, ${PLAYER}! Me alegra que hayamos podido darle a Adolinda un respiro temporal de su maldición, pero el hecho es que su receta para el desayuno incluía patas de araña, y aunque soy incapaz de hacer algo contra la maldición, sí está en mi poder rechazar un desayuno de patas de araña peludas. ¡Patas de araña para mí, no, gracias! ¡Puaj!\
\
'Le conté a Willem mi descontento y mi hambre, y salió corriendo. ¿Puedes preguntar por la Posada a ver si alguien sabe qué ha sido de él? Supongo que ha ido en busca de un segundo desayuno, ¡y agradecería muchísimo que lo trajeras de vuelta lo antes posible!'","'¡Tienes que ir a ver a Calengoth a los muelles y disculparte por mis mentiras, ${PLAYER}! ¡Temo consumirme por esta maldición si no lo haces!'","Recoge la alforja que encontró Willem y dile que regrese a la Posada Embrujada","'Creo que sí vi a tu lince, desde lejos. Lo vi bastante hacia el este, en dirección a Dol Guldur. Corría directo hacia la puerta de Fennas Guldur, pero fui atacado por orcos y no vi si llegó a entrar.'","'¿Willem Bigotes? ¿Qué clase de nombre es ese?\
\
'Rodelleth me dijo que vio un lince corriendo hacia el sureste, en dirección a Fennas Guldur, pero yo no lo vi.'","'Bingo debe de tener una opinión muy baja de la inteligencia de los Elfos si creyó que realmente me engañó con su treta. No fue así. Pero hace falta un gran corazón para admitir algo así, y mi negativa a llevarlo a través del río no fue por malicia, sino por preocupación por su seguridad. Acepto sus disculpas.\
\
'Tal vez también tenga la solución para su hambre. Dale este pequeño paquete de lembas, junto con mis mejores deseos. Creo que lo primero curará su hambre y lo segundo aligerará su culpa, pues imagino que esto último es la verdadera fuente de su maldición, y una vez perdonado, espero que esté bien. ¡Esa es mi impresión!'","Habla con Bingo fuera de Caras Galadhon, en Lothlórien","'¡He visto al lince que buscas! Pasó corriendo delante de los tres en dirección al este. ¡Desordenó los papeles de esta mesa! Creo que buscaba algún tipo de comida, pero no quedó satisfecho y salió corriendo por Ost Galadh tras una breve búsqueda.'","Ves una figura familiar delante de ti: ¡Willem Bigotes!","Segundo Desayuno","Willem Bigotes está en algún lugar del Bosque Negro. Si preguntas por la Posada Embrujada y por otros lugares del bosque, quizá puedas averiguar adónde se ha marchado el lince.\
\
Bingo quiere que encuentres a Willem Bigotes y lo envíes de vuelta a la Posada Embrujada, ¡con desayuno si es posible!","'¿Encontraste a Willem? ¿Le dijiste que te siguiera de vuelta aquí?'"},
[10775]={"Talk to Andur","'Did you only just get here, ${PLAYER}? It seems that I caught up to you very quickly!\
\
'I give you my gratitude again for taking a chance and trusting me. Most people would have slain me where I stood in the desert. You have given me a second chance at life, and I will not squander it. Thank you, my friend.'","Find Andur","You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, but the donkey is wounded. Andur is caring for the donkey and has asked you to collect the semi-precious stones from the pebbles for him. You have collected the stones, and should now talk to Andur.","'It is good to see Andur has returned unharmed. I could use his help with many odd jobs and errands, and I will gladly employ him for as long as he would like to stay. Not to say that you were not good help, ${PLAYER}, but I imagine that you will soon be moving on.'","Talk to Tibira in Western Khanâg","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}, did you find Andur?'\
\
You fill her in on recent events, secretly still not entirely sure if Andur can be trusted to not steal the stones and the donkey.\
\
'Oh, speaking of, there he is now!'","Second Chance","Collect colourful stones from the loose gravel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, but the donkey is wounded. Andur is caring for the donkey and has asked you to collect the semi-precious stones from the pebbles for him.","'You have collected the stones? Thank you ${PLAYER}, we will be able to leave that much sooner now. She is almost better and will be fit to walk before long. Thank you once again for your help, ${PLAYER}. I will take the stones and will be off to Western Khanâg shortly.'","'${PLAYER}, what are you doing here? No matter, I could use your help. The donkey got stung by an usan-kûni, and I have been tending to the animal. The poor thing is in much pain, but I must try and keep her still to prevent the venom from spreading from her leg to other parts of her body. I think she will be fine, we only need a little more time to rest.\
\
'I have not yet been able to collect any of the coloured stones for which Tibira sent us seeking. Since you are here, would you mind doing that while I keep the donkey calm? That way when she is ready to move on, we can head back to Western Khanâg immediately.'","You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You returned to Tibira and as you were giving her an update, Andur arrived. You should talk to Andur.","Tibira gave a donkey and some supplies to Andur, formerly a soldier of Ordâkh and then a bandit, and sent him to collect some of the semi-precious gemstones that can be found in the desert. She says he should have returned by now and has asked for your help in finding what became of him.","'${PLAYER}, I had hired a man named Andur, who said he was your friend, to collect gemstone pebbles. I gave him a donkey and some supplies and sent him to an area east of here, where I know the colourful stones can be scooped up from the gravel.\
\
'He has not yet returned, and I worry that he perhaps got lost or ran afoul of some beast in the desert. Would you mind looking to see what became of him?'\
\
Though you want to think the best of Andur, you can't help but wonder if the man perhaps took Tibira's donkey, never to return.","You have found Andur in the hills east of Western Khanâg, exactly where he is supposed to be. You should talk to Andur.","Collected colourful stones from the loose gravel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You returned to Tibira and as you were giving her an update, Andur arrived. You should continue talking to Tibira.","Andur is supposed to be in the hills east of Western Khanâg. You should go there and look for him.","Bring the colourful stones to Andur","You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You should return to Tibira and give her an update.","Talk to Tibira","Andur found!"},
[10776]={"A wily merchant is displeased by the opening of the roads which pass by Ost Amondal.","'Hurry, now hurry! Bring them to me! Ah, thank you. Thank you. What a burden this has become. I will sadly have to pass along the increased cost of supply to my buyers, alas.'","Retrieve secret stashes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Balgam","'Bah! Just as I expected! I knew it was just a matter of time.'\
\
The stranger glares at you and then lets out a breath, deflating.\
\
'My apologies, I am only about to lose my entire supply of goods to cursed adventurers like you who are sure to come wandering by now that the roads are open. Say, I don't suppose you are looking for some coin?\
\
'These roads used to be known to only a few, and I have used them for years to transport my goods across Belfalas. I had been using the nearby ruins as a way point, where I would stash goods, but now that it's overrun by worms, I cannot get near enough to retrieve them. If you go fetch my crates for me, I will make it worth your time. Just... hurry up before anyone else comes along, will you?'","Secret Stashes in Ost Amondal","Retrieved secret stashes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Balgam has asked you to retrieve crates that he has stashed about the ruins of Ost Amondal.\
\
Ost Amondal is in southern Belfalas.","You have managed to retrieve a great many of Balgam's stashed crates.\
\
You should deliver them to him outside of Ost Amondal, in southern Belfalas."},
[10777]={"'¿Está hecho, ${PLAYER}? ¿Ha sido desterrado el espíritu?'","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Ahora que el espíritu maligno ha sido derrotado, la piedra rúnica ya no estará sometida a su corrupción. Has realizado una gran hazaña al devolver esta piedra enana a su antigua gloria.\
\
'Cuentas con el agradecimiento de todos los Barbiluengos, ${PLAYER}. Tómate un merecido descanso y acepta tu recompensa. Te has ganado ambos.'","Usa la piedra rúnica para invocar a Helegfan","'Debemos devolverle a esta piedra rúnica su poder de antaño, ${PLAYER}. No hay duda de que una fuerza maligna la ha corrompido. Existe un espectro sombrío llamado Helegfan, conocido por complacerse en la perversión de todo lo bueno, y esta piedra apesta a su vil corrupción.\
\
'Según las últimas noticias, Helegfan se ha establecido en la Sala Decimosexta, al norte de aquí. Usa la piedra rúnica para invocarlo y destrúyelo.\
\
'Vuelve cuando la tarea esté cumplida y veremos si es posible disipar la corrupción.'","Márus ha determinado que la piedra rúnica que encontraste ha sido corrompida por un espíritu maligno en las profundidades de Moria.","Habla con Márus en el Refugio Sombrío","Secretos largamente olvidados (opcional)","'Usa la runa para invocar a Helegfan, ${PLAYER}.'","Márus se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío, al sur de la Sala Decimosexta.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Márus con noticias de tu victoria.","Helegfan puede encontrarse en la Sala Decimosexta, al norte del Refugio Sombrío, en el extremo sur de Nud‑melek.\
\
Márus te ha pedido que entres en la Sala Decimosexta y derrotes al espectro sombrío Helegfan para purificar la piedra rúnica de la corrupción del espíritu.","Derrota a Helegfan","Helegfan ha sido derrotado"},
[10778]={"Rúni, a Lore-master from Erebor, has journeyed to the Grey Mountains seeking lost history and knowledge. He suspects that even the fortress of Skarháld may hold secrets.","This chest is empty","Bring the old maps to Rúni","There is nothing useful in this chest","'Well now, I remember you! Did we briefly speak of dragons in Erebor not too long ago? Ah yes, that is what I thought!\
\
'I have come to Ered Mithrin seeking lost history and knowledge. There is much of dwarf culture buried here in the mountains. I suspect that even this fortress, Skarháld, may hold some secrets yet. Have a look around and perhaps we will find something that the Zhélruka have not!'","Old chests may be hidden in Skarháld.\
\
You should search any old chests that you find in Skarháld.","You found an old map!","Whatever was in here is just dust now","Secrets of Skarháld","Rúni can be found in Skarháld.\
\
You should bring the old maps to Rúni.","Rúni pores over the old maps.\
\
'Oh, this is too good not to share. I will have to show the Zhélruka as well! Do you know what these maps contain? One map is of Thikil-gundu, an old keep north-west of here.  Another map is of Glitgróf, a mine to the north. The third map is of Stormlind, a crafting hall north-east of here. These maps will assist in planning expeditions. You have found something very helpful, very helpful indeed!'","That may have been food once...","Search old chests (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","There is nothing of interest in this chest"},
[10779]={"Spakorth can be found at the Stout-axe barracks on the central level of Lûghash.\
\
You have discovered the location of the King of the Stout-axes by reading the missives and should now deliver them to Spakorth.","You have gathered three missives from the Order of the Eye and should now read them.","This missive details rumours concerning the fates of the Rings borne by the Nazgûl...","Deliver the missives to Spakorth in Lûghash","Collect a missive from a Mordath expedition-leader","Read the Order of the Eye missives (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Collect a missive from a Dor Amarth expedition-leader","You wrest a piece of parchment from the fallen expedition-leader...","This missive details artifacts rumoured to be held in a secret vault within the Black Pits of Mordath...","Collect a missive from a Lûghash expedition-leader","'For my part, I have but one task for you, and it is one of dire importance to my folk, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Men of the Order of the Eye have been searching Dor Amarth and the ruins of Barad-dûr for Sauron's artifacts since his fall, and they have taken careful note of all they have found as has Mistress Zôreth.\
\
'One of my folk, Sversting, once told me of a rumour shared with him by Mistress Zôreth. She told him that King Greytooth was still held within the deeper dungeons of the Dark Tower, but she would speak no more of it when the rumour spread among us.\
\
'I must know if the Mistress spoke true - does my King still live?\
\
'The Order has sent expeditions all across Dor Amarth - from the deepest depths of the Black Pits of Mordath to the very gates of Lûghash!\
\
'I would ask that you seek out their leaders, and see if they bear any missives or orders that speak of King Greytooth!'","Secrets of the Order","The Order of the Eye has sent many of its followers into Dor Amarth hoping to uncover the resting places of Sauron's most powerful artifacts.","'King Greytooth lives? Seventy-eight years he has been gone... and for seventy-eight years we have been without hope. Perhaps those days shall soon be behind us!\
\
'Mistress Zôreth claimed he was still imprisoned by Sauron after all these years, but one detail in this missive has left me uneasy. You see, my folk have never been sent to seek him. I... I cannot recall a single expedition to rescue him from the Dark Tower. What attempts to free him could this missive speak of?\
\
'That is a question I shall have to ask the Mistress, I think.  Where her efforts failed, we must now succeed.\
\
'It is time King Greytooth is freed from Barad-dûr and returns to lead his folk!'","Order of the Eye expedition-leaders can be found patrolling outside Lûghash, upon the broken plains of Dor Amarth, and among the ruins of Barad-dûr that have sunken into the Mordath.\
\
Spakorth has asked you to retrieve missives from the Order of the Eye expedition-leaders searching the lands of Dor Amarth. Spakorth hopes they might reveal the whereabouts of the lost King of the Stout-axes.","This missive warns of Mistress Zôreth's motivations and her attempts to free a dwarf-king from Barad-dûr..."},
[10780]={"Defeat a Barkhûshim sorceress in Kûr Anzar","'This is quite the day, my friend. Quite the triumph. And you killed Rokóbu?'\
\
Mizadi lets out a long, loud whoop of triumph.\
\
'That will prove to be a severe blow to Okhíso. We still have much to do before we can declare victory, but this is a huge first step. Without your bravery, I fear we would have been lost, ${PLAYER}. You have my thanks.","Mizâdi has asked you to lead the charge to secure the lower ward of Kûr Anzar. Once successful, Mizâdi can set up a foothold outside Kûr Anzar.","Secure the Landing of Kûr Anzar","Report your success to Mizâdi in Urmâkh.","Find and defeat Rokóbu in Kûr Anzar","Defeat Barkhûshim skirmishers in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Barkhûshim champions in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated a Barkhûshim sorceress","Report your success to Mizâdi in Urmâkh","'We are close to retaking Kûr Anzar and driving the loathsome Barkhûshim out. Soon we will reunite all of Hamât under our banner of hope. Kûr Anzar is the key.\
\
'We need to seize a foothold in Kûr Anzar, from which we may strike at the heart of Okhíso and his twisted realm. You are to be the point of our spear, ${PLAYER}. It's time to make our move. We ask that you move through the lower portion of the city and drive their forces back in the lower ward. We know Okhíso's loathsome aide, Rokóbu to be leading them. If you get the chance, plunge your sword into his chest for me. Now is the time that Hamât rises again!'","Rokóbu lets out a strangled cry and collapses, defeated","Ready yourself for battle, then move swiftly into Kûr Anzar and defeat the forces of the All-seeing. Find and defeat the loathsome Barkhûshim leading them, Rokóbu. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.","Defeated Barkhûshim champions in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Barkhûshim skirmishers in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10781]={"Sectarios del que todo lo ve derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Kûr Anzar te debe una. Ahora que la batalla se ha ganado, se te quiere de regreso en Urmâkh.'","Destruye las fortificaciones y derrota a las fuerzas del que todo lo ve.","Asegurando Kûr Anzar","Encuentra y derrota a Usóhi, líder de los invasores Barkhûshim","Derrota a Usóhi, líder de los invasores Barkhûshim","Fortificaciones del que todo lo ve destruidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destruye las fortificaciones del que todo lo ve (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Los partidarios del que Todo lo ve atacan Kûr Anzar! Destruye sus fortificaciones de fortuna y repulsa las fuerzas invasoras de Barkhûsh.","Derrota a los sectarios del que todo lo ve (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Usóhi deja escapar un gruñido y levanta su bastón en desafío hacia ti"},
[10782]={"Collected relics of Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Idmar","Securing Our Past","The brigands are located in the large camp to the south. It is likely that the thieves who carry these relics will be hard to detect, even among their fellows.\
\
Idmar has asked you to recover relics of Gondor from the brigands in Parth Celebrant.","Collect relics of Gondor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Well done, ${PLAYER}. While I am certain that more relics are still missing, I am overjoyed to have these back in our hands. The history of Rohan is rich, and it is worth preserving.\
\
'I will have these sent to Stangard...thank you.'","Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should bring the relics you recovered to Idmar.","'Collect the relics of Gondor for me, ${PLAYER}.'","Idmar has considered Doron's plea and has chosen to take action against the brigands of Parth Celebrant.","'Aye, I believe it is time that we dealt with the brigands. They have been plaguing us for some time now, and recently, they have amassed a sizeable force. Turmoil within Stangard has prevented us from launching a proper assault on their camp, but you may be able to aid us in that regard.\
\
'We know that they have been stealing a large number of relics from Ost Celebrant and bringing them to their camp south of here. I wager the Oathbreakers have startled the brigands even more than they have us...there can be no better time to press the attack.\
\
'I will send word to Stangard to gather more support. As for you, fight your way into their encampment and retrieve the relics. These Men deserve no such treasure and will pay dearly for their crimes.'"},
[10783]={"Ves un destello de acero.\
¡El Capitán de la tripulación de los Leales está bloqueando tu camino!","Regresa a tu barco con los suministros","Debes derrotar al Capitán de los Leales para poder regresar a tu barco.","Recoge los suministros recuperables que han llegado a la playa para que no caigan en manos de los Herederos de Castamir.","'¿Los has derrotado, ${PLAYER}? ¡Eso estuvo cerca! Ven, regresemos a Umbar Baharbêl!'","Cajas de suministros recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Corsarios leales a los Herederos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota al Capitán de los Leales","Recoge las cajas de suministros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Un barco que transportaba armas y suministros se ha hundido y la carga está llegando a la costa en las Islas del Escudo. Recoge los suministros recuperables para que no caigan en manos de los Herederos de Castamir.","Regresa a tu barco con los suministros que has recogido.","Asegurando el botín","Derrota a los corsarios leales a los Herederos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10786]={"Asegurando el Agua","Prueba la muestra de agua de la Cuencasangre","La pasta se dispersa en el agua, dándole un tono marrón que es mejor no describir con más detalle.","'¿Has recogido las muestras de agua? Necesitamos tres en total, cada una tomada más y más río abajo, lejos de la Cuencasangre.'","Murig podría usar tu ayuda para asegurar agua para los exploradores guerreros.","Has puesto a prueba todas las muestras de agua.\
\
Habla con Murig","Muestras de agua del río reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Murig está junto a la orilla del río, cuesta abajo desde la Cuencasangre.\
\
Habla con Murig","Prueba la muestra de agua tomada lo más lejos posible de Cuencasangre","La mezcla se hunde hasta el fondo del agua sin dispersarse en absoluto.","'Claramente, la tierra de Cuencasangre tiene algún efecto en el agua. Por ahora, me aseguraré de recoger agua más abajo del río para garantizar que sea apta para mí y mis camaradas. Quizá cuando Marget complete su sangrienta labor, las aguas alrededor de Cuencasangre se vuelvan más agradables.\
\
'¡Regresaré a nuestro campamento en breve! Gracias por tu ayuda.'","Murig necesita muestras de agua de distintos puntos a lo largo del río.\
\
Recoge agua de la orilla del río.","Prueba la muestra de agua tomada a una distancia moderada de la Cuencasangre","Habla con Murig","Reúne muestras de agua del río (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Qué sincronización! Acabo de terminar de preparar la mezcla.'\
\
Murig ordena las muestras de agua que recogiste en tres recipientes separados. Luego te entrega tres bolas de una sustancia curiosa.\
\
'Añade un trozo de esta... pasta, a cada recipiente. Observemos los resultados.'","Murig ha dispuesto tres recipientes de agua.\
\
Prueba cuál de los recipientes tiene el agua más limpia usando cada uno de los tres recipientes.","'Debes de ser de quien la Instructora Eluna me habló. Sí, sé que ya debía haber regresado a informar, pero aún no he completado mi trabajo. Mi tarea es encontrar una fuente confiable de agua para nuestro grupo de exploración. Con un río tan grande cerca de nosotros, pensé que sería sencillo. La presencia de Cuencasangre complica las cosas. Me preocupa que su proximidad pueda contaminar el agua de algún modo. Estoy trabajando en una mezcla que Deryn me enseñó a preparar. Cuando se añade al agua, puede ayudar a determinar si es segura para beber o no. ¿Podrías recoger muestras de agua para mí?'\
\
'La primera muestra debe ser de la orilla del río, cerca de Cuencasangre.\
'La segunda muestra debe ser más río abajo desde Cuencasangre.\
'La tercera muestra debe ser aún más lejos río abajo. Ya entiendes la idea.'","La pasta se dispersa un poco, enturbiando ligeramente el agua."},
[10787]={"Talk to Glóin at Annâk-khurfu","'Well done!\
\
'Thanks to you, my scouts have returned to Annâk-khurfu no worse for the wear. The Gabil'akkâ stand ready to march on Mount Gundabad.\
\
'I count myself fortunate to have you at my side, ${PLAYER}. Let us see what tomorrow brings!'","Aid Glóin with 'Beyond the High-threshold'","Securing the Approach","Aid Glóin with 'After the Fall'","Aid Glóin with 'At the Gates'","Glóin can be found in the keep of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
Glóin has asked you to aid him and his scouts in securing the approach to Mount Gundabad.","'By order of Prince Durin, I have sent a number of my scouts across Elderslade to prepare the way for the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'None of us know what awaits us at Mount Gundabad, and it is a fool's hope to think Gorgar the Ruthless is not also keenly aware of that fact.\
\
'You are a skilled warrior, a practised adventurer, and wise to the dangers that lurk in unexplored territory. And so, I would have you aid my scouts, ${PLAYER}.'","Glóin has sent several scouts into Elderslade to aid the Gabil'akkâ in securing the approach to Mount Gundabad."},
[10788]={"Saruman's forces have used their black powder to create an opening at the culvert and have begun to infiltrate through the gap in the wall. \
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Full</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Worker defeated\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Moderate Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Too much time has passed before sealing the culvert \
* Every 15 seconds after the initial time penalty","A worker has been defeated (${VALUE}/3)","Seal the culvert opening with rocks (${VALUE}/18)","Securing the Culvert","The Orcs have blasted a hole into the culvert upon the wall and are infiltrating through the gap. Assist the Rohirrim workers as they attempt to seal the opening to prevent further enemies from getting through the defences.","Protect the workers from being defeated (${VALUE}/3)"},
[10789]={"Saruman's forces have used their black powder to create an opening at the culvert and have begun to infiltrate through the gap in the wall.  The Rohirrim labourers must be defended as they work to seal the culvert with nearby stones.\
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Partial</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Major Merit Gain</rgb>\
* Defeat Madhash\
* Defeat Vogalash\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Labourer defeated\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Moderate Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Excessive time has passed without the culvert being sealed (5 minutes)\
* Additional time has passed after the initial penalty (every 20s)","Seal the culvert opening with rocks (${VALUE}/18)","A worker has been defeated (${VALUE}/4)","Securing the Culvert","The Orcs have blasted a hole into the culvert upon the wall and are infiltrating through the gap. Assist the Rohirrim labourers as they attempt to seal the opening to prevent further enemies from getting through the defences.","Do not allow labourers to be defeated (${VALUE}/4)"},
[10791]={"Sót se encuentra en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, al suroeste de Katûb-zahar.\
\
Deberías llevarle el tomo que has encontrado. Estará deseando examinarlo.","'Tus esfuerzos no pasarán desapercibidos, ${PLAYER}. Este texto será devuelto al Pueblo de Durin.'","Algunos de los antiguos archivos del Pueblo de Durin se encuentran en la Gran Excavación, o eso dice un diario que encontraste en el camino.","Encuentra el tomo antiguo","Tomo antiguo encontrado","Esta página del diario describe la esperanza de alcanzar las antiguas bibliotecas de Khazad-dûm, conocidas como Katûb-zahar. El enano que poseía este libro buscaba un antiguo texto que, según se rumorea, detalla los métodos antiguos de combinar el mithril con otros metales, junto con muchos otros secretos sobre su correcta forja.\
\
Parece una búsqueda digna. Deberías continuar la misión del enano caído.","'¿Encontraste un diario en el camino cuyo objetivo era recuperar este libro? ¡Increíble! Pero...\
\
'¡Ay! Los años y la vil alimaña que infesta Khazad-dûm no han sido nada clementes... ¡tantas páginas están arruinadas!\
\
'No importa. Con el tiempo suficiente, estoy seguro de que podré recomponerlo, ¡aunque me lleve años!'","Asegurar la biblioteca","Lleva el tomo antiguo a Sót en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación","La biblioteca llamada Katûb-zahar indicada en el diario se encuentra al norte de Gazatmur, al nordeste del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Deberías buscar el tomo antiguo en las antiguas bibliotecas de Khazad-dûm."},
[10792]={"Dilûsu has asked you to help him deal with another group of brigands nearby that have been attacking people trying to flee.","'I have reports that the fiends in Zikrum-dûl have been dealt with. I trust I have you to thank for that, ${CLASS}.\
\
'This road will now be safer for people in need... for now, that is.'","Dilûsu has asked you to help him deal with a group of brigands near Zikrum-dûl who have been attacking people as they flee the Orcs.","'Ah, fortunate timing, ${CLASS}. You look like a capable adventurer.\
\
'People here could use your help if you are willing. A group of brigands nearby in Zikrum-dûl has been preying on the weak as they flee the demons in the area.\
\
'It is a step too far for them to be attacking and robbing folk who are trying to escape this cursed land. They must be stopped if you find yourself in the area.'","Return to Dilûsu near Zikrum-dûl","Defeated brigands in Zikrum-dûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat brigands in Zikrum-dûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Securing the Outskirts","Return to Dilûsu now that you have made the area safer from the brigands."},
[10795]={"'At long last, Edoras sees fit to send anyone at all to the Wade. Perhaps Éowyn is a bolder leader than her uncle...'","Talk to Thane Edric","Securing the Wade","Thane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead.\
\
Éowyn has asked you to travel to Entwade to assist Thane Edric in securing the Wade as his people evacuate to a more defensible shelter.","As Théoden King rides to war with Saruman, Éowyn commences her efforts to gather the people of Kingstead to Edoras.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest will fail if you complete 'In the King's Wake' before speaking to Thane Edric.</rgb>","'With my uncle Théoden bringing the war to Saruman, there remain a great many things to do in the Westemnet.\
\
'To the east, the river-fort of Entwade lies along the Entwash's shores, and has held the Wade for years innumerable. Thane Edric commands the post and holds but a few men in his service. The White Hand has pressed into the King's lands as of late, and the cost of losing the Wade would be unknowable.\
\
'I have many matters to attend to in my uncle's stead, but I know this is a task for which your skills are suited. If you would aid me, I will have your steed readied for the journey at once.'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: When you accept this quest, you will immediately travel to Entwade in Kingstead.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: This quest will fail if you complete 'In the King's Wake' before speaking to Thane Edric.</rgb>","'Why came you here?'"},
[10797]={"Celebrandir está en Gwingris, al norte de Glâd Ereg.\
\
Celebrandir está esperando las semillas que has conseguido.","La corrupción que ha afectado a Glâd Ereg y la destrucción provocada por los siervos del Enemigo han arruniado el bosque.","'Me temo que los esfuerzos que has realizado en el sur no serán suficientes para repeler la corrupción que el Enemigo ha traído a Glâd Ereg. El mal ha calado demasiado profundo.\
\
'Para reparar el daño que nuestros enemigos han causado, necesitaremos replantar los acebos que han sido devastados por los trolls y sus viles métodos.\
\
'Marcha hacia el sur, hacia el bosque, y encuentra semillas de acebo en los arbustos que crecen bajo los árboles que se encuentran allí. Tráemelas de vuelta y encontraremos la oportunidad de asegurarnos de que el bosque prospera.'","Consigue las semillas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Semillas para el futuro","'¿No has podido recoger suficientes semillas, ${PLAYER}?'","Lleva las semillas a Celebrandir en Gwingris","'Puedes encontrar semillas de acebo en los arbustos que crecen bajo los árboles al sur de Gwingris. Tráeme tantas como puedas y quizá podamos sanar al bosque.'","'Estas semillas son la esperanza del bosque, ${PLAYER}. Te lo agradezco, pues tus esfuerzos podrían marcar la diferencia para el futuro de Glâd Ereg.'","Las semillas de acebo pueden encontrarse en los arbustos que creen bajo los árboles en Glâd Ereg, al sur de Gwingris.\
\
Celebrandir te ha pedido que has consigas semillas de acebo, para que pueda replantar el bosque.","Semillas conseguidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10799]={"Seedlings can be found throughout the Vale of Nan Curunír.\
\
Dagoras asked you to gather up the seedlings struggling to survive in the Vale of Nan Curunír.","Bring the seedlings to Dagoras' ally","Collected seedlings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect seedlings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Have you collected the seedlings, ${PLAYER}?'","'Farewell, little Orc. You have chopped your last tree! Hoom! Hom...!\
\
'...Hrmm?'\
\
'One moment now, ta-rum. Perhaps I have been too hasty. You are not an Orc, are you, even if you do rather look like one?\
\
'${RACE}, you say? Well, that is new then, and what do you have there? Why I know these little ones! I raised their mother, down in the Vale, hoom, before the Orcs came with their axes.\
\
'You had best introduce yourself then, little ${RACE}.'","Seeds of Hope","The ally Dagoras mentioned might be up the ridge to the north-east from Dagoras' camp.\
\
Dagoras asked you to bring the seedlings to Dagoras' mysterious ally.","'While I was scouting to the east of here, I thought I saw some kind of movement among the trees upon that slope, but I could find no figure moving about, nor any tracks to indicate what it might have been.\
\
'I have a growing suspicion what it is though, and it may be much to our advantage. This may sound queer to you, but I suggest that you carefully gather up some of the seedlings trying to gain purchase in the devastated Vale and carry them with you up towards that ridge.\
\
'And if I were you, I would handle them with the utmost care....'","Dagoras has hinted that there is a potentially powerful ally to be found in Nan Curunír, but he was unwilling to say much of it."},
[10800]={"Devuelve las semillas conservadas a Gailthin","El bosquecillo del que habla Gailthin está a poca distancia de ella.\
\
Gailthin te pidió que buscaras entre los montones de hojas alguna semilla conservada que pueda usarse para restaurar el bosque a su antigua belleza.","'Una vez más leeremos el saber de nuestro pueblo bajo las ramas de estos árboles, gracias a ti.'","Los árboles de Edhelion, dormidos desde la partida de los Elfos, dejaron caer sus semillas hace mucho tiempo. Los Elfos del refugio creen que aún hay vida en las semillas conservadas que se encuentran entre los montones de hojas bajo las ramas secas.","'El don de la vida, eso es lo que representan estas semillas. Me alegra que tus esfuerzos hayan dado fruto. Saber que recuperaremos la belleza y el conocimiento de Edhelion me llena de alegría, y siempre recordaré tu ayuda. Gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Semillas del Pasado","'Saludos, ${CLASS}. Quiero hablar contigo sobre un asunto importante para mí. Hace mucho tiempo, cuando esta ruina era un lugar hermoso, cuidaba los bosques y guardaba el saber de Edhelion. He regresado para ver que este lugar sea restaurado a la belleza y reverencia que una vez tuvo. Mis esfuerzos para recolectar y catalogar el saber no van bien. Peor aún, la plaga que afecta a los árboles me ha dejado con poca esperanza...\
\
Sin embargo, la esperanza nunca se pierde del todo, así que te pido tu ayuda. Estos árboles tienen semillas resistentes, y si alguna ha sobrevivido a los años, se encontrará entre las hojas esparcidas alrededor de sus troncos.\
\
Sé que debes probar tu valor contra las criaturas que ahora acechan los árboles, así que espero que esta pequeña tarea no obstaculice tus objetivos. ¿Me ayudarás?'"},
[10801]={"Free Razâl from his bonds so you both can escape","Investigate the outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of Razâl","Razâl, Mizâdi's trusted scout, hasn't reported back in a day. Investigate the eastern outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of Razâl. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.","Free Razâl from his bonds so you both can escape before the Barkhûshim notice you.","'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. We are in need of someone with your rare talents. My best scout, Razâl, has not reported back to Numûru in the past day. He was scouting Kûr Anzar, and I fear the Barkhûshim, those twisted adherents to the Church of the All-seeing, may have captured him.\
\
'You seem like you can handle yourself, perhaps better than some warriors I might send. Please, find Razâl for me. He was sent to the eastern outskirts of Kûr Anzar, to map the movements of the Barkhûshim. If he has been captured, it is likely there you may find him, or some clue to his whereabouts. We need every soldier we have, particularly one with Razâl's talent for burgling. Please, if you find him, order him to report back to me immediately. He is one of my best warriors, but he takes such foolish risks sometimes.'","Scout the third outlook into Kûr Anzar","'I am grateful to you. As you can see, Razâl made it back safely. Hopefully he is a bit wiser for the wear, but he escaped with his skin due to your valour, so for that I am in your debt. Thank you for seeing to this task. I have another, larger task for you when you are ready. One that is suitable for someone of such skill.'","You have found Razâl. Free him quickly!","Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh","It's difficult to see clearly, but you finally count twelve All-seeing from your vantage point","Scout the second outlook into Kûr Anzar","Seeing the All-seeing","Find the three locations Razâl mentioned on the western outskirts north of where he was captured and scout Kûr Anzar from each of them.","Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh.","Scout the first outlook into Kûr Anzar","It's hard to see between the crumbling walls, but you finally count ten All-seeing cultists","Mizâdi's trusted scout, Razâl, has gone missing. She has asked you to search the western outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of his whereabouts.","You count nine Barkhûshim moving along the winding path into Kûr Anzar"},
[10802]={"Viznak directs you to return to Rhadrog and Faeron in Zajâna, convinced that the Blight Lady they pursue has arrived here in Adagím.","After speaking with Rhadrog, he is resolved to seeking out Lhaereth and asks that you inform Faeron at the fountain in Zajâna.","'Our road southward has not been in vain. If the tidings prove true, then the one we have long hunted may at last be near. Let us turn our path east and press on into the very heart of the blight.'","Seek the Citadel","Speak with Rhadrog at Zajâna","'You must hurry to my bodyguards. They will want to know. They may want to help. Be quick, I will wait here and study more.\
\
'They are still in Zajâna.'","'That wretched imp yet finds new ways to confound my expectations. If indeed there is truth in the rumour that Lhaereth has come, seeking to reap some vile gain from the pestilence that defiles this land, then we must learn her whereabouts with all speed. Go now—tell Faeron what has passed. I shall make ready to depart.'","Viznak is concerned that the Blight Lady has come to these lands. He directs you to return to Rhadrog and Faeron at Zajâna.","Speak with Faeron near the fountain in Zajâna"},
[10803]={"Biblioteca de Tham Mírdain encontrada","'Encuentra la Biblioteca de Tham Mírdain, ${PLAYER}... es de la máxima urgencia.'","Los elfos de Echad Mirobel han rastreado a las fuerzas de Angmar en Eregion hasta una antigua biblioteca.","Encuentra la Biblioteca de Tham Mírdain","Buscador de conocimiento","La Biblioteca de Tham Mírdain se encuentra en Mirobel, en la región suroeste de Eregion.\
\
Ornras de Echad Mirobel te ha pedido que encuentres la entrada a una antigua biblioteca.","'Hemos rastreado las armas de los herreros hasta una antigua biblioteca cerca de Mirobel, en Tham Mírdain. Adéntrate y encuentra este lugar. Estoy seguro de que en su interior aguardan misterios aún mayores.'"},
[10804]={"'Well, my little fellows! You shall have your deeds completed!'","'Now, my little fellows, where be you a-going to, puffing like a bellows? What's the matter here then? Tell me what's your trouble!\
\
'You need to play the instances? Naught worse that that, eh? That can soon be mended.'","By completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Seeker of Knowledge","Buscador de conocimiento","Grants completion of quest: Seeker of Knowledge","Talk to Javatar to complete Seeker of Knowledge"},
[10805]={"'Debemos aprender más sobre el poder que ha corrompido la Arboleda Retorcida y que ahora se filtra hacia el bosque que la rodea. Es oscuro y maligno, pero no sabemos nada de su origen.\
\
'Ve a la Arboleda Retorcida y reúne cualquier planta enferma o muerta que encuentres. A partir de ellas, quizá pueda determinar a qué nos enfrentamos en verdad.'","'¿Me has traído los miembros caídos de los árboles de la arboleda? Esto debería darme una mejor idea del poder que ahora infecta ese lugar oscuro.'","Recoge ramas podridas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva las ramas podridas a Lithuifin","'Ten cuidado mientras exploras la Arboleda Retorcida. Se ha convertido en un lugar oscuro, con un odio vil hacia todo lo que vive, y debemos averiguar de dónde ha surgido esta plaga.","Lithuifin está en las Agujas de la Linde, en la orilla noroeste del lago Evendim.\
\
Debes llevarle las ramas podridas que has recogido.","Ramas podridas recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Necesitaré más de las plantas moribundas que sin duda cubren la Arboleda Retorcida antes de poder decirte más sobre lo que aflige al bosque. Ahora ve.'","La Arboleda Retorcida está al suroeste de las Agujas de la Linde.\
\
Lithuifin te ha pedido buscar indicios del poder que ha corrompido la Arboleda Retorcida. Te pidió recoger ramas podridas y llevárselos.","Ramalarga cree que algún poder maligno podría estar retorciendo el bosque con fines oscuros.","En busca de respuestas"},
[10806]={"You freeze in your place as a pain enters your chest. The cold stone conjures unbidden words to swell up inside you. Unknowingly you say 'power' followed by 'Borangos,' and 'Dúrossul.'\
\
You close your eyes to cope with the pain and an image of an armoured Rogmul towers over you next to a volcanic vent. Your eyes shoot open as the images burn away.\
\
Able to breathe again, you gather your thoughts. It seems the watching stone assumes you want to forge a treaty with Borangos and has shown you one of his lieutenants to speak to instead.","'What purpose have you within the sacred realm of Borangos? Speak now and I shall show mercy and merely throw you to the flames below.'","The Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should return to the Watching Stone.","Destroy a more prominent vent and defeat Dúrossul","Return to the Watching Stone","Vents can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should destroy vents to attract Dúrossul's attention.","The watching stone is motionless and the air smells strange and foul.\
\
You feel a sense of searching and piercing eyes all around you.","Destroy vents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed vents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dúrossul appears before you!","Seeking Dúrossul","The Watching Stone unwillingly divulges more information about the structure of Borangos' forces in Nargroth. You can use this to your advantage.","Defeated Dúrossul"},
[10807]={"'Me preguntaba cuándo enviaría Unnarr a mas aventureros. Tenemos mucho de qué hablar.'","'Salve, ${PLAYER}. Si buscas gloria entre los Enanos de la Mansión de Thorin, necesitamos mas aventureros resistentes para ayudarnos en nuestra lucha contra los malditos Duramano. Si tienes interés, busca a Tórth fuera del Cuartel de la Piedra Azul.'","Tórth se encuentra fuera del Cuartel de la Piedra Azul, cerca de la cascada en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
El Capitán de Guardia Unnarr te ha pedido que hables con Tórth para ayudar en la lucha contra los Duramano.","'Tórth está fuera de los barracones del Cuartel de la Piedra Azul. Date prisa ahora.'","Buscando Gloria","El Capitán de Guardia Unnarr te ha pedido que hables con Tórth fuera del Cuartel de la Piedra Azul."},
[10810]={"Destroy a more prominent pillar and defeat Nargúr","The watching stone is motionless and there seems to be a fine dust coating the air.\
\
You feel a sense of dread and piercing eyes all around you.","Seeking Nargúr","Defeated Nargúr","Pillars can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should destroy pillars to attract Nargúr's attention.","Nargúr appears before you!","The Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should return to the Watching Stone.","Destroyed pillars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to the Watching Stone","You freeze in place as a pain enters your chest. The cold stone conjures unbidden words to swell up in you. Unknowingly you say 'power' followed by 'Borangos,' and 'Nargúr.'\
\
You close your eyes to cope with the pain and an image of an armoured Rogmul towers over you next to an ornate pillar. Your eyes shoot open as the images burn away.\
\
Able to breathe again, you gather your thoughts. It seems the watching stone assumes you want to forge a treaty with Borangos and has shown you one of his lieutenants to speak to instead.","'You have desecrated this realm! Borangos has tasked me with putting an end to your foolish missions. What beast of Mordor or beyond do you serve? You speak no words? Then I must turn you to ash.'","Destroy pillars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Watching Stone unwillingly divulges more information about the structure of Borangos' forces in Nargroth. You can use this to your advantage."},
[10811]={"Seeking Narthalum","Destroy statues (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy a more prominent statue and defeat Narthalum","The Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should return to the Watching-stone.","Destroyed statues (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to the Watching Stone","'What creature dwells, unwelcomed in Nargroth? Have you a message for Borangos or are you simply pathetic and lost? I have not the time for this trifle!'","The watching stone is unmoving and silent.\
\
You feel a sense of confusion and piercing eyes all around you.","Statues can be found in Nargroth.\
\
You should destroy statues to attract Narthalum's attention.","Defeated Narthalum","You freeze in place as a pain enters your chest. The cold stone conjures unbidden words to swell up in you. Unknowingly you say 'power' followed by 'Borangos,' and 'Narthalum.'\
\
You close your eyes to cope with the pain and an image of an armoured Rogmul towers over you next to a vile statue. Your eyes shoot open as the images burn away.\
\
Able to breathe again, you gather your thoughts. It seems the watching stone assumes you want to forge a treaty with Borangos and has shown you one of his lieutenants to speak to instead.","The Watching Stone unwillingly divulges more information about the structure of Borangos' forces in Nargroth. You can use this to your advantage.","Narthalum appears before you!"},
[10812]={"Cam Barroso está en su casa, en el centro de Bolgovado.\
\
El primer ingrediente que Hyacinth Tuk te ha enviado a buscar es el salitre. Te ha sugerido que vayas a ver a su amigo Cam Barroso, un criador de cerdos en Bolgovado.","En busca de salitre","'Por favor, ve a Bolgovado y pide a mi amigo Cam Barroso el salitre que necesito.'","'¿Salitre? Tengo montones. Pero te diré una cosa, también tengo otros problemas.\
\
'Ya que estás aquí, te voy a pedir que te ocupes de ellos por mí antes de enviar ese salitre a casa de Hyacinth.'","'Bueno, si la vieja urraca está dispuesta a pagar, supongo que tendré que complacerla.\
\
'Primero te enviaré a buscar salitre. Mi amigo Cam Barroso, el criador de cerdos de Bolgovado, suele tener algo. ¡Tiene los fosos de estiércol más grandes de toda la Comarca!\
\
'Cam me avisará cuando necesite el pago, así que no necesitarás llevar dinero contigo. Apenas usa salitre.'","Dado que Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón pagó para adquirir los ingredientes de sus fuegos artificiales, Hyacinth Tuk te ha reclutado para ayudarla a reunirlos."},
[10813]={"Find signs of the Malledhrim's passing at the Gostannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is clear that a great battle was fought at the Gostannon and that the Malledhrim were the clear victors, for the Orc-camp lies in ruin. However, we must learn whether this is the route the Host took eastwards, for if it is, then it would likely be the safest route for any reinforcements that may follow.\
\
'Travel to the Gostannon and seek any signs you may find of the Malledhrim's passing, then return to me with your report. I do not imagine you will encounter much resistance from the Orcs there...they appear to be in disarray after their loss.'","'You found these weapons throughout the area and even on the eastern side of the Gostannon? Then the Malledhrim did indeed take that route. This, then, shall be our road for reinforcements and supplies.'","Collected a weapon of the Malledhrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Have you found no sign of the Malledhrim's passing at the Gostannon?'","Seeking Signs","The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continuing presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.","The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.\
\
Dannaswen has asked you to patrol the road to the Gostannon in order to determine the strength of the Enemy there.","Bring the Malledhrim weapons to Dannaswen atop Amon Angened","Dannaswen is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.\
\
You should bring the Malledhrim weapons you found back to Dannaswen and explain where you discovered them.","'The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}; when you have finished your patrol, return to me.'"},
[10814]={"Return to Rusgwen","Consigue madera cortada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should bring the cut wood you gathered back to Rusgwen in Calembel.","'Welcome back! Huh, you found far more wood than I expected. My apologies for underestimating you!'","Rusgwen has asked you to gather cut wood from the tree dotted areas around Calembel.","A maker of barrels in Calembel needs help gathering chopped wood from the surrounding forests.","'Greetings! I am Rusgwen, maker of fine barrels and crates. If you are looking for work, I am in need of someone to collect wood outside the city's walls. Fear not, for I shan't ask you to chop it yourself. I did that already yesterday and left it there to dry a bit.\
\
'No sense in my lugging it back up the hill when I can pay coin to have some dolt – uh, that is, some fine individual to gather it for me.'","Seeking Slats","Madera cortada conseguida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10815]={"Teodoro Tojo está buscando sus tesoros robados.","Teodoro Tojo, un buscador de tesoros con experiencia, está buscando muchos de los tesoros que le fueron robados en sus numerosas aventuras.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión será eliminada de tu registro cuando finalice el evento asociado.</rgb>","Habla con Teodoro Tojo en Bree, Rivendel o en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Teodoro Tojo está buscando sus tesoros robados y puede encontrarse en Bree, Rivendel y en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Debes hablar con Teodoro Tojo.","Teodoro Tojo, un buscador de tesoros con experiencia, está buscando los muchos tesoros robados a lo largo de sus aventuras.","Completa 'El Bugan del Tesoro'","¡Buscando a los Bugans del Tesoro!","Completa 'El Bugan del Tesoro' (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'El gran Teodoro Tojo, buscador de tesoros y trotamundos de vasta experiencia, a tu servicio. En todas mis aventuras y extensas expediciones en busca de reliquias invaluables, no me di cuenta de que algunas habían desaparecido. ¡Esos Bugans son un grupo astuto, siguiéndome y robando todos mis logros virtuosos!\
\
'Tú has hecho una gran hazaña. ¡No, la mayor hazaña! Pues has recuperado algunos de mis tesoros perdidos y puesto en su sitio a esos molestos Bugans. Sin embargo, aún queda más de mi tesoro extraviado por ahí. Lo sé porque lo he documentado cuidadosamente, por mí mismo. Si lo recuperas todo, te otorgaré una gran recompensa.'","Teodoro Tojo está buscando sus tesoros robados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Los Bugans del Tesoro pueden encontrarse en muchas de las Instancias de Escalado.</rgb>"},
[10817]={"Search for orders of Azruthor in Tarlang's Crown (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","These orders detail a plan for the Havens of Belfalas","These torn orders focus on the Anfalas to the west","Search for any further communication between Azruthor and the Scourge","'We need to push deeper into their encampment, ${PLAYER}... and that is no simple task.\
\
'Their defences are considerable, and we know little of their plans in the Crown. Dol Amroth cannot field the men to confront such a foe with so many of our number gone to the east, and without knowledge of their intent, it is ill-advised at best to move against them in force.\
\
'I have known the Corsairs to be slovenly men, and should they possess orders from Azruthor, it is likely that they may have left them within reach of you and your allies. Return to me with what you discover, and let us hope they are as careless as they seem!'","The missive before you contains detailed information about Azruthor's forces in Tarlang's Crown, including a planned assault into the Anfalas to the west. Finally, it concludes with a vague, ominous mention of the Scourge's plans for Gondor.\
\
You decide to continue looking over these notes for much may be learned from them that could aid the people of Gondor.","DNT -- will not be seen","The Heirs of Castamir have a yet unknown plan for Tarlang's Crown, and Harnion seeks to expose it by stealing their orders.","Orders can be found through the main Corsair encampment in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Harnion has asked you to seek out orders from Azruthor in an effort to learn more of the Heirs' plan in Tarlang's Crown.","These orders seem to focus on the sacking of Blackroot Vale","Seeking the Heirs","A missive to Azruthor can likely be found in the largest tent in the Corsair encampment in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
You have found numerous plans for the Corsairs amidst their camp, and should now search for any missives to Azruthor himself."},
[10818]={"Has encontrado a los dunlendinos cerca de Nímbarth.\
\
Deberías hablar con su líder, Meriona.","'¿Riderch mandó a un duvodiad para vigilarnos? ¡Bah! ¿No confía en nosotros?'\
\
En ausencia de Riderch, la mujer te mira a ti. Pasan unos segundos hasta que se calma y suspira.\
\
'A lo mejor estoy siendo... impulsiva, como diría él. Si de verdad quieres ayudarnos, que así sea.'","Dos exploradores toman sus armas, pero el tercero niega con la cabeza para detenerlos","Riderch te ha pedido que busques a sus exploradores cerca de Nímbarth.\
\
Nímbarth se encuentra al noreste del campamento de Siempreviva.","Habla con Meriona","'¿Has visto a mi gente? Iría a buscarles yo, pero...' Se señala las vendas y sonríe irónicamente. 'Después de lo que ha pasado en Nímbarth, dudo que quieran rescatarme de nuevo.\
\
'¿Podrías asegurarte de que están bien? Deberían haber vuelto ya a Nímbarth, al noreste.\
\
'Nuestra líder es una mujer llamada Meriona. Tendrás que perdonarla a ella y a los demás por ser desconfiados contigo, pero así funcionan las cosas con ellos.'","Un explorador dunlendino herido se ha separado de su gente.","Encuentra a los dunlendinos cerca de Nímbarth","Buscando a los exploradores"},
[10819]={"Vuelve junto a Reynold Potts","Puedes encontrar al profanador Blogmal en las ruinas de la ciudad de Fornost, al este del campamento de los cazatesoros.\
\
Reynold Potts te ha pedido que mates al profanador Blogmal para poner fin a la corrupción de la fauna local.","Reynold Potts está en el campamento de los cazatesoros de Fornost.\
\
Potts estará aliviado de saber que el profanador Blogmal ha encontrado su final a tus manos, acabando con la amenaza de su influencia corruptora.","'Estoy profundamente aliviado de que hayas acabado con ese profanador. Si la plaga que causó estaba llegando a los animales, no habría tardado mucho en llegar hasta nosotros también.'","Buscando la fuente","Derrota al profanador Blogmal","Reynold Potts sospecha que los orcos Blogmal tienen un profanador entre sus filas, envenenando las tierras de su alrededor y causando terribles desfiguraciones en los animales de pasto.","'Una corrupción tan vil... Parece que las pobres bestias han sido envenenadas. Yo diría que por el agua y los pastos contaminados. No hay duda de que detrás está la mano de algún orco, y de uno astuto, al parecer.\
\
'He oído hablar de los profanadores y de los envenenadores entre los orcos. ¿Crees que los Blogmal cuentan con uno de ellos entre los suyos?'","Has derrotado al profanador Blogmal"},
[10820]={"El gran almacén de madera de Sejer-tharâkh alberga una enorme reserva de madera de gran valor que la Guarnición de Hierro desea utilizar en la recuperación de Moria. Además de la madera, Torfi de la Guarnición de Hierro pretende obtener los registros conservados en Sejer-tharâkh para comprender mejor a los artesanos enanos de épocas pasadas.","Recoge registros de entrega (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los enanos de Khazad-dûm fueron en otro tiempo poderosos mercaderes, comerciando con pueblos a ambos lados de las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
'La información contenida en estos libros de registro nos brinda la oportunidad de reencontrarnos con nuestros antiguos socios comerciales y comenzar el proceso de restablecernos como mercaderes de gran prestigio una vez más.'","Lleva los registros de entrega a Torfi","'Tengo un encargo para ti, ${PLAYER}. Se dice que muchos registros se guardaban dentro de los muros de Sejer-tharâkh, pero se perdieron cuando Moria cayó ante el Azote de Durin.\
\
'Te pediría que buscaras esos libros de registro durante tu incursión en Sejer-tharâkh y me los trajeras. Cuanto más aprendamos de nuestro pasado, más conocimiento tendremos para expulsar a los orcos de Khazad-dûm.'","Sejer-tharâkh: Una historia de madera","La entrada a Sejer-tharâkh se encuentra en Mezer-serej.\
\
Torfi te ha pedido que entres en Sejer-tharâkh y busques cualquier libro de registro antiguo que permanezca en el almacén.","'¿Cómo va tu búsqueda? Sin duda el almacén está en mal estado, pero espero que encuentres algunos documentos intactos.'","Registros de entrega recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10821]={"'Saludos. Soy Torfi de la Guarnición de Hierro, encargado de la recuperación de Sejer-tharâkh. En su interior hay un vasto almacén de madera que podríamos utilizar para comenzar las reparaciones por todo Khazad-dûm.\
\
'Por desgracia, no podemos reclamar este almacén hasta haber acabado con los intrusos que se encuentran dentro. Quizá, con tu ayuda, podamos sembrar el terror entre ellos y expulsarlos.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que estos intrusos tienen un líder, alguien -- o algo -- que los mantiene bajo su control. Entra rápidamente en Sejer-tharâkh y elimina al enemigo que comanda a los demás.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La Guarnición de Hierro ha creado una distracción, atrayendo a la mayor parte de los intrusos fuera de las profundidades de Sejer-tharâkh. Te permiten el acceso durante una hora, tiempo durante el cual podrás entrar y salir libremente de Sejer-tharâkh para completar las tareas que se te han encomendado.\
\
Sin embargo, una vez transcurrida la hora, la Guarnición de Hierro ya no puede garantizar tu seguridad y bloqueará el acceso hasta que pueda reunir de nuevo fuerzas para lanzar otra ofensiva que aleje al enemigo de Sejer-tharâkh.</rgb>","Habla con Torfi en Mezer-serej","'¿Y tu tarea? No pierdas tiempo... ¡acaba con quien lidera a los intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh!'","La entrada a Sejer-tharâkh se encuentra en Mezer-serej.\
\
Torfi te ha pedido que derrotes al líder de los intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh.","Sejer-tharâkh: Todo acaba bien","Con una base establecida en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, la Guarnición de Hierro ha comenzado la recuperación de los almacenes, bibliotecas y minas olvidados de Moria. El almacén de madera de Sejer-tharâkh es uno de esos lugares.","'Bien hecho, bien hecho.\
\
'Tras la derrota de su líder, ya hemos observado desorden entre los intrusos restantes. La Guarnición de Hierro no debería tener ninguna dificultad para recuperar este almacén.'","Derrota al líder de los intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh","Se te ha acabado el tiempo...","Has derrotado al líder de los intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh","Torfi se encuentra en Mezer-serej.\
\
Tras la derrota de su líder, la moral de los intrusos de Sejer-tharâkh se ha debilitado. Deberías regresar con Torfi y comunicarle tu victoria."},
[10822]={"Habla con Torfi en Mezer-serej","Sejer-tharâkh: Golpear y hendir","La Guarnición de Hierro se esfuerza por recuperar los olvidados almacenes de Moria. Por orden de sus superiores, Torfi intenta expulsar a los intrusos de Sejer-tharâkh. Como sus intentos anteriores no han tenido éxito, Torfi ha recurrido a otros aventureros de Moria para ayudarle en su tarea.","Derrota intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Pareces ser un guerrero más capaz que yo. Claro que solo lo admitiré entre nosotros dos. ¡Un enano debe mantener su reputación!\
\
'Ahora que los intrusos en Sejer-tharâkh han sido reducidos, podemos explorarlo más a fondo. Afortunadamente, esto significa que vamos adelantados respecto a lo previsto, y por ello mereces una recompensa.'","Torfi se encuentra en Mezer-serej, en las salas orientales de Zelem-melek.\
\
Deberías regresar con Torfi para recibir una recompensa por tus esfuerzos.","La entrada a Sejer-tharâkh se encuentra en Mezer-serej.\
\
Torfi te ha pedido que le ayudes a limpiar Sejer-tharâkh de los intrusos que hay en su interior.","Intrusos derrotados en Sejer-tharâkh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Nosotros, la Guarnición de Hierro, hemos comenzado la labor de recuperar Moria de las repugnantes criaturas que ahora la habitan. Mis superiores me han encargado liderar los esfuerzos para recuperar Sejer-tharâkh de los intrusos que se encuentran en su interior.\
\
'Creyéndome algo competente en combate, hice todo lo posible por expulsar a los indeseables que había dentro. Por desgracia, disto mucho de ser un guerrero de renombre y me vi obligado a retirarme. Tú, en cambio, pareces tener lo necesario para enfrentarte a toda clase de bestias u orcos. ¿Podría contratarte para que me ayudes en mis esfuerzos?'","'¿Has completado ya tu tarea? Hazlo y regresa conmigo cuando hayas terminado.'"},
[10823]={"'Ah, just the ${RACE} I wanted to see. You look to be quite a useful sort, so I have no qualms asking you to do a bit of dirty work for me.\
\
'You see, the workers here have never been overly fond of my policies. They can feel however they wish, but if I hear of them stirring up any trouble or complaining to folks, that will mean trouble for them.\
\
'Gareth Rust is the one who seems to be the most upstart among his peers. You must go spy on him and convince him to talk to you. If he says anything out of place, the rascal won't have a job!'","Tell Gareth Rust of the Mayor's desire to expose him","'What sorrow and what joy this winter has brought me! I can hardly believe my ears, ${PLAYER}. By what providence has the mayor decided to give me another chance at life?\
\
'You are so good to deliver this message to me. My outlook does not seem so bleak now.'","Gareth Rust and Daley Utteridge are in the workers' area in Winter-home.\
\
You should tell the workers of your success in manipulating the mayor. Things are looking up for the workers of Winter-home!","Gareth Rust is in the workers' area in Winter-home, ever toiling.\
\
You should tell Gareth Rust that the mayor wants you to spy on him so he will lose his job.","Ted Ives is ecstatic about this turn of fate","Jack Judson is ecstatic about this turn of fate","'Hurrah! Hurrah! I cannot believe it! I've been hoping every moment that some luck would come my way, and it has at last!'","Defend yourself from the banker of Frostbluff","Find out what the mayor wants from you","Tell Jack Judson that he may have his old job back","Your search is over; all evidence of the mayor's corruption is on this receipt","The mayor is in the town of Winter-home, in Frostbluff.\
\
You should return to the mayor with the evidence you collected of his corruption.","'Oh, good ${RACE}! Thank you. I can feel it -- you have had a great part in this gift that you now bring me from Mayor Goodnough.'","'You have done a wonderful thing, ${PLAYER}. We workers don't have much, but we scraped together what we could. Please, accept these gifts as tokens of our gratitude.\
\
'But know that we will not forget you, or the great deeds done this day. If we ever have opportunity to give you proper thanks, you can rest assured that we will.'","'What's that you have there?'\
\
The mayor looks at the paper in your hand and pales in alarm as he realizes that you know everything about his irresponsible investing while the folks of his town go hungry.\
\
'W-what are you going to do with that?! Surely you don't mean to tell our innocent visitors of this... do you? Please... I will do anything you ask if you just put that paper back where it belongs, hidden away....\
\
'What do you want? What share of the profit will appease you?'","Guard Frostway has been driven off... but the door of the fort opens of its own accord","The mayor wants you to betray the workers, but you would never stoop so low!","'You fool. By challenging this fort, you are challenging the mayor. I think he will send you to the stocks for this, once I knock you out. And he'll find out whoever sent you here, stranger.'","Tell Barrett Nowell that he may have his old job back","A piece of paper has swirled into your hand as the banker of Frostbluff fled from his post.\
\
You should examine this piece of paper.","Talk to Gareth Rust of all that you have achieved on behalf of the workers","The banker has been driven off... and a curious piece of paper swirls into your hand as he flees","'Don't look to me for advice, ${PLAYER}. It's not my role to choose or help you choose. You must look inside yourself and do what you think is right, for yourself or for others.'","The beggars, now re-hired for the former positions, are around the town.\
\
You should quickly tell the beggars that their period of despair is at an end at last.","'Ha! The mayor is right to send a spy. But you are a friend to us workers, and that is a great boon.\
\
'I have reason to believe that the mayor uses the extra funds from our lowered wages and over-time for unsavoury transactions and doesn't invest it in making our town better.\
\
'I have seen Guard Frostway coming to town at night to collect money and forms to bring to the fort down by the lake. Will you go investigate down there? The mayor will fire me on sight if I leave my post.'","'You nosey patrons should mind your own business and stay in the festival area! You're out of bounds, ${RACE}, and out of your depth!\
\
'So you're intent on sticking your nose where it don't belong? The mayor pays me good money to make sure folks like you don't dig up any unwanted dirt!'","The mayor stands in the centre of Winter-home, overseeing the events of the Yule Festival.\
\
You should speak with the mayor and find out what he wants from you, though it sounds like he has a sleazy scheme brewing.","Bring the proof of the mayor's corruption to Mayor Goodnough","Examine the piece of paper dropped by the banker","Barrett Nowell is ecstatic about this turn of fate","Regina Judson is ecstatic about this turn of fate","Use the door to gain access to the store-house","Tell Ted Ives that he may have his old job back","Investigate the fort in Frostbluff where the mayor stores his funds and records","The fort on the frozen lake is east of Winter-home in Frostbluff.\
\
You should go to the fort on the frozen lake and find what evidence you can of the Mayor's corruption, as Gareth Rust is sure the town's money is being put to corrupt use.","'Surely... surely you are joking. How can this be? Has the mayor grown a heart? I'll not count my blessings -- I will go to work at once!\
\
'This is wonderful news...!'","Tell Bill Hyde that he may have his old job back","Tell Regina Judson that she may have her old job back","Bill Hyde is ecstatic about this turn of fate","Sometimes you must put others before yourself, especially when those others have great need. Charity is a wonderful thing!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends.</rgb>","'You... you give me my life back with your news. I don't know what to say. Can it really be true, ${PLAYER}? Can the mayor have grown a heart?\
\
'What a wonderful day. Things are turning around for this town; I can feel it.'","'I'll give you the short of it: the mayor is feeling a little suspicious of the workers and wants someone to spy on them to see what's afoot. What you make of this is for you to decide, but I would talk to the mayor if I were you. See if what he has to say is to your liking.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: The rewards for both of these mutually-exclusive quests are UNIQUE to each quest. Please choose your quest carefully!</rgb>","You demand that the mayor sets the wages right for the workers, and gives the beggars back their jobs","Self-sacrifice: Support the Poor"},
[10824]={"Collect Númenórean relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Porókho has told you that there are places in Ilmabiri where relics of ancient Númenor can still be found. He said that if you bring him some, he will give you coin for them.","Collected Númenórean relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Listen, if you are not opposed to... acquiring items, I have a proposition for you.'\
\
He scratches his beard thoughtfully as he considers you.\
\
'These sewers are one of the oldest parts of the city. They were built by Men of Númenor, and the fact that they are still working today is a testament to their knowledge and skill. You can see their influence in much of the architecture. There are some areas of Ilmabiri where Númenorian relics can still be found. If you come across any, bring them to me, and I will give you some coin in exchange for them. I think you can find some to the east.'","Selling History","'Oh thank you, my friend, these are in excellent condition. You have really come through for old Porókho today!'","Porókho believes Númenórean relics may be found in the eastern part of Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You should go there and collect them.","Talk to Porókho","You have collected Númenórean relics found in the sewers. You should bring them to Porókho at Hêbatokh, his camp in Ilmabiri."},
[10826]={"Cartas de enanos recuperadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Listein en la Puerta de las Nubes","'Por favor, ${PLAYER}, haz lo que puedas para recuperar esas cartas...'","'Tenemos muchas tradiciones, ${PLAYER}, y esta no es la menos importante. Cuando marchamos hacia la batalla, llevamos con nosotros una carta. Si caemos, esa carta será devuelta a casa por los supervivientes, si queda alguno.\
\
'Muchos de nosotros hemos venido a Moria, y algunos han caído... Parece que las merrevail han descubierto las cartas y disfrutan perversamente el conservarlas como trofeos de su victoria contra nosotros. El honor de nuestros guerreros y la paz de sus familias requieren que recuperemos estas cartas del enemigo y las devolvamos a casa. ¿Podrías ayudarme a recuperar estas cartas?\
\
'Si te encuentras con alguno de nuestros caídos en el Camino de Durin, investiga el cuerpo para ver si tiene la carta. Tráeme de vuelta cualquier carta que encuentres antes de que los merrevail se apoderen de ellas.'","'Esas cartas deben ser encontradas y llevas de vuelta a casa. Se lo debemos a nuestros caídos.'","Envíalos de vuelta a casa","Listen está en la Puerta de las Nubes, cerca de la entrada de Zirakzigil.\
\
Deberías llevas las cartas de los enanos de vuelta a Listein.","'¿Has recuperado las cartas de los caídos? Te lo agradezco, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Los mensajes que contienen estas cartas traerán un cierre triste, pero muy necesario para el duelo de sus familias. Me aseguraré de que lleguen a salvo al Umbral de Durin.'","Las merrevail que rondan los túneles de Khazad-dûm han robado muchas cartas de los enanos que han caído en combate en el Camino de Durin.","Recupera las cartas de los enanos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las cartas pueden encontrarse en las merrevail que han saqueado los cuerpos de los enanos caídos en los salones del Camino de Durin.\
\
Listein te ha pedido que reclames las cartas de los enanos antes de que las merrevail se las lleven."},
[10827]={"Eirien is at Mithechad, south-west of Garmadh-maudhûl.\
\
You should return to Eirien and let her know that Ukhurk has been defeated and his standard destroyed.","'At the heart of Garmadh-maudhûl, the leader of the Orcs there, a creature named Ukhurk, rallies his troops beneath his horrible standard.\
\
'Perhaps if you were to journey to Garmadh-maudhûl and dispatch with Ukhurk? Cast down his standard and drive fear into the hearts of his followers.\
\
'Garmadh-maudhûl lies to the north-east of here... be wary on your journey.'","Ukhurk and his standard can be found in Garmadh-maudhûl to the north-east of Mithechad.\
\
Eirien has asked you to defeat Ukhurk, leader of the Orcs at Garmadh-maudhûl and cast down his standard.","In the deepest reaches of Garmadh-maudhûl, the Orc-leader Ukhurk rallies his troops.","Talk to Eirien at Mithechad","Defeat Ukhurk","'Seek out Ukhurk in Garmadh-maudhûl and defeat him. Destroy his standard and strike fear into the hearts of his minions.'","Defeated Ukhurk","Destroy Ukhurk's battle-standard","Destroyed Ukhurk's battle-standard","Sending a Message","'Through your dedicated efforts, the leadership of Garmadh-maudhûl has been defeated and his forces have been thrown into disarray for the time being.\
\
'Hopefully, our efforts will assist those who seek to disrupt the forces of Dol Guldur.'"},
[10828]={"'¡Muy bien, ${PLAYER}! Has completado mi desafío y puede que hayas frustrado los planes que los orcos de Moria estaban urdiendo con sus combatientes de retaguardia más poderosos.\
\
Acepta esta recompensa con mi agradecimiento y con la certeza de que tu victoria es digna de una canción.'","'No basta con limitarse a rechazar a los orcos, ${PLAYER}. Si quieres que los juglares canten tus hazañas, debes hacer algo más que simplemente ganar la batalla, ${CLASS}. Necesitas lograr algo verdaderamente digno de una canción.\
\
Mientras sigas luchando por Lórien, idearé desafíos adicionales que merezcan perdurar en las canciones; si completas uno de ellos, me aseguraré de recompensarte además de lo que te dará Belvagor.\
\
Dos temibles enemigos fueron vistos acechando en la retaguardia durante la última batalla: Narshpug, un uruk de mal carácter, y Grakâmâb, un poderoso troll. No fueron llevados al frente, lo que me hace pensar que los reservan para algún propósito; en cierto momento abandonaron el campo de batalla. Si logras derrotar a uno de ellos antes de que se marche y además consigues ganar la batalla, habrás superado mi desafío.'","Narshpug derrotado","Grakâmâb derrotado","Desafío del Centinela I","Rilhathel se encuentra en Caras Galadhon, esperando saber si has completado su desafío con éxito.","Habla con Rilhathel en Caras Galadhon","Rilhathel está decidida a cantar canciones sobre tus esfuerzos en defensa de Lórien y te ha planteado un desafío además de simplemente rechazar a los orcos: derrotar a uno de los dos combatientes de retaguardia que aparecen en el campo de batalla.","Derrota a Narshpug o a Grakâmâb antes de que abandonen el campo y aun así gana la batalla.","'Narshpug y Grakâmâb fueron vistos en la retaguardia durante la última batalla y en algún momento abandonaron el campo. Si puedes derrotar a uno de ellos antes de que se marche y aun así ganar la batalla, habrás completado mi desafío.'","Rilhathel te ha pedido no solo ganar la batalla por Lórien, sino también derrotar a Narshpug o a Grakâmâb antes de que abandonen el campo de batalla.","Completa con éxito la Batalla de Lórien"},
[10829]={"'No basta con limitarse a rechazar a los orcos, ${PLAYER}. Si quieres que los juglares canten tus hazañas, debes hacer algo más que simplemente ganar la batalla, ${CLASS}. Necesitas lograr algo verdaderamente digno de una canción.\
\
Mientras sigas luchando por Lórien, idearé desafíos adicionales que puedan perdurar en las canciones; si completas uno de ellos, me aseguraré de recompensarte además de lo que te dará Belvagor.\
\
Mi hermana Limhendeth siempre ha tenido aprecio por Belvagor y me ha expresado su preocupación por que pueda resultar herido en las próximas batallas contra los orcos. Mi desafío para ti es el siguiente: no permitas que Belvagor sufra ni el más leve rasguño. Es un elfo valiente y fiel, y querrá luchar en uno de los pasos, pero por mi hermana, asegúrate de que no resulte herido. Debes ganar la batalla sin que Belvagor sufra ninguna herida grave para completar mi desafío.'","'¡Muy bien, ${PLAYER}! Has completado mi desafío, y mi hermana Limhendeth se alegrará al saber que su querido Belvagor no ha sufrido daño alguno.\
\
Acepta esta recompensa con mi agradecimiento y sabiendo que tu victoria es digna de ser cantada.'","'Mi hermana Limhendeth aprecia mucho a Belvagor y quedaría destrozada si resultara herido. Si puedes evitar que sufra cualquier herida grave y aun así ganar la batalla, habrás completado mi desafío.'","Desafío del Centinela II","Habla con Rilhathel en Caras Galadhon","Rilhathel está decidida a cantar canciones sobre tus esfuerzos en defensa de Lórien y te ha planteado un desafío además de repeler a los orcos: evitar que Belvagor sufra heridas graves.","Rilhathel se encuentra en Caras Galadhon esperando saber si has completado su desafío con éxito.","Completa con éxito la Batalla de Lórien","Evita que Belvagor sufra daños graves y aun así gana la batalla.","Rilhathel te ha pedido no solo ganar la batalla por Lórien, sino también evitar que Belvagor sufra heridas graves."},
[10830]={"'Enviemos un mensaje a los orcos, ${PLAYER}, devolviéndolos a Moria humillados. Si logras ganar la batalla en menos de treinta minutos, habrás superado mi desafío.'","Rilhathel está decidida a cantar canciones sobre tus esfuerzos en defensa de Lórien y te ha planteado un desafío además de repeler a los orcos: ¡ganar la batalla en treinta minutos!","Completa con éxito la Batalla de Lórien en menos de treinta minutos","Gana la Batalla de Lórien en menos de treinta minutos","'No basta con limitarse a rechazar a los orcos, ${PLAYER}. Si quieres que los juglares canten tus hazañas, debes hacer algo más que simplemente ganar la batalla, ${CLASS}. Necesitas lograr algo verdaderamente digno de una canción.\
\
Debemos enviar un mensaje a los orcos, ${PLAYER}. Debemos demostrarles que no están a la altura de los defensores de Lothlórien, ¿y qué mejor manera de hacerlo que rechazarlos con la mayor rapidez?\
\
Si logras ganar la batalla en menos de treinta minutos, habrás completado mi desafío.'","Gana la batalla en treinta minutos","'¡Muy bien, ${PLAYER}! Has completado mi desafío, ¡y ahora los orcos sabrán lo superados que están!\
\
Acepta esta recompensa con mi agradecimiento y sabiendo que tu victoria es digna de ser cantada.'","Habla con Rilhathel en Caras Galadhon","Rilhathel te ha pedido no solo ganar la batalla por Lórien, sino hacerlo rápidamente: ¡en treinta minutos!","Rilhathel se encuentra en Caras Galadhon esperando saber si has completado su desafío con éxito.","Desafío del Centinela III"},
[10833]={"'These knives were carried by the Cargûl who guard the Watchers of Dol Guldur? They are not morgul-blades, though they are indeed of a similar make. Unfortunately, I do not think they can be used to negate the power of the watchers... however, there may be another way.\
\
'I can bind these blades as tokens that you may keep upon you. They are still evil things, I fear, but so long as you carry them, the watchers will not be able to distinguish you from their own dark servants, thus you should be able to pass them unmolested.\
\
'That is the best I can do for you, I am afraid. Lady Galadriel cannot cross the river without leaving Lothlórien defenceless, and Mithrandir is lost to us. I do not know of any other who might be strong enough to break the power of the watchers.'","Talk to Handelen at Thangúlhad","Search Cargûl sentries for clues","'Have you seen the sentries, ${PLAYER}? I do not refer to the Orcs, of course -- there is little challenge in avoiding the eyes of Orcs. I refer to the ones carved of stone, with unblinking eyes that strike your will with a crushing darkness if you should stray too close.\
\
'We have quickly learned to stay away from them as much as we may, but they make manoeuvering through Gathbúrz difficult, and I imagine the inner walls of Dol Guldur are likewise defended. We must find a way to defeat their power if we are to achieve our goals here.\
\
'The robed Cargûl have been seen tending to these stone sentries on occasion... if you could approach close enough to defeat one, then perhaps you might be able to find something to aid us against the stones.'","Agorin is at Ost Galadh in Emyn Lûm, west of Thangúlhad.\
\
Handelen instructed you to bring the engraved dagger you found to Agorin, the Malledhrim Lore-master in Emyn Lûm.","There are many watching stones placed in and around Dol Guldur, guarded by Cargûl sentries. Anyone who foolishly approaches too close to one of these stones is struck with a black curse that sunders the will.","'So you found these knives upon the Cargûl? I am not certain if they can help us or not. They look similar in make to the dread morgul-blades carried by the Nazgûl....\
\
'I think you had best bring this to Agorin in Emyn Lûm. She might have some insight as to what might be done with them.'","'In truth, I had not imagined that the watchers would be so powerful that even Agorin cannot answer them. This will be a serious thorn in our sides as we do battle for control of Gathbúrz.\
\
'Still, at least she found a way for you to avoid their power. I shall have to see if we can get our hands on a few more of those blades....'","'It is said that the watching stones of the Enemy are possessed of fell spirits and that the Cargûl which guard them were once knights of Eärnur of Gondor... you would do well to be wary.'","Handelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should bring the engraved dagger you found to Handelen.","'Agorin may know something of what you found... speak with her at Ost Galadh at once!'","Watching stones and their Cargûl sentries can be found throughout Gathbúrz.\
\
Handelen has asked you to defeat a number of the Cargûl sentries found near the watching stones in Gathbúrz to learn if a way might be found to protect the Malledhrim from the effects of the stones.","'Return to Handelen, ${PLAYER}... he will wish to know what we have learned.'","YOU SHOULD NOT SEE THIS","Found an engraved dagger","'It is said that the satching stones of the Enemy are possessed of fell spirits and that the Cargûl which guard them were once knights of Eärnur of Gondor... you would do well to be wary.'","Sentries of Dol Guldur","Bring the engraved dagger to Agorin","Handelen is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should return to Handelen and tell him what you have learned from Agorin about the Watchers of Dol Guldur.","Talk to Handelen in Thangúlhad"},
[10834]={"'Have you dealt with the sentries?'","'Saruman's remaining sentries will spend more time looking out for themselves than looking for intruders... for a while, at least.'","Defeat White Hand sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","White Hand sentries can be found near the Pillar of the Hand, not far from Dagoras' camp.\
\
Dagoras has asked you to defeat several of the sentries guarding the southern end of Nan Curunír.","Talk to Dagoras at his camp in Nan Curunír","'We stand here on the edge of the Vale of Nan Curunír, at the north end of which lies the stronghold of Isengard. Saruman's schemes hatch from here, and he guards it jealously.\
\
'Nearby, you will find the Pillar of the Hand. Around it are arrayed a number of sentries -- strange and unpleasant, I think they may be more of these queer half-orcs we have been seeing of late.\
\
'They stand watch over the road leading into the Vale, and if we are to untangle Saruman's plots unhindered, we will need to weaken their guard.'","Defeated White Hand sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dagoras is at his camp in Nan Curunír.\
\
You should tell Dagoras that many of the White Hand sentries have been driven off.","Unusual half-orcs wearing the mark of the White Hand are guarding the southern end of the Vale of Nan Curunír.","Sentries of the White Hand"},
[10836]={"'You have my thanks for keeping the people of Arnach safe, ${PLAYER}. It is yet another thing my sister could not manage without my help. You see, she and her husband lead Arnach, but that is a story of which I do not wish to speak more.\
\
'It is strange, indeed, that the Haradrim would more readily set siege to Arnach instead of fording the Erui at the Crossings. Why would they march directly into superior numbers instead of hastening to the East?\
\
'I believe this might be a matter for you and Lord Angbor to investigate.'","'It is a grim day, traveller. My men and I have held out here for hours now, and the Haradrim continue to push their advance against Arnach. We have held them back for hours now, but I grow concerned that their numbers shall soon overwhelm us.\
\
'They stalk the road to Tumladen, and we in turn have barricaded the bridge into Arnach. \
\
'Would you lend us your aid? If even one of my men can rest as you defend the bridge, it would bolster our resolve for the coming assaults.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Othor must not be defeated</rgb>","'My men have spotted the Haradrim approaching from the west. We must drive them back!\
\
'Are you ready, ${PLAYER}?'","Serpents at Minlos","You have defended the bridge into Arnach!","Talk to Othor","'I thank you for your aid, ${CLASS}. That should break their assault for some time!\
\
'This assault troubles me, though... for what reason would the Haradrim throw themselves against the walls of Arnach instead of passing across the Erui? We have not the men to guard the Crossings, and could not repel their advance there.\
\
'Return to the Lady, and tell her of my concerns. I do not believe we should leave this matter to speculation.'","Talk to Lady Terenis","Othor can be found at Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have successfully defended Arnach from attack and should now speak to Othor.","Othor can be found at Minlos in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
Othor has asked for your aid in defending Arnach from the Haradrim. You should speak to him when you are ready.","Lady Terenis can be found in her hall in Tumladen.\
\
Othor has asked you to return to Lady Terenis and warn her of the Haradrim forces readying to cross into Lossarnach.","In spite of their dwindling numbers, the Haradrim forces in Upper Lebennin are poised to spill forth into Lossarnach through the settlement of Arnach."},
[10837]={"El teniente de la Mano Blanca se encuentra en Gazatmur, al noreste del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Debes derrotar al teniente de la Mano Blanca.","Informa a Wigfast de la presencia de la Mano Blanca","Derrota al teniente de la Mano Blanca","Este escudo de trasgo lleva la marca de la Mano Blanca, algo extraño de encontrar en Moria... o quizás no tan extraño. Seguramente un sirviente de la Mano Blanca está cerca, responsable de agitar el mal en Gazatmur. Si ese sirviente es eliminado, quizás la presencia de los trasgos se disipe en la Gran Excavación.","'¿Marca de la Mano Blanca y un enemigo Uruk detrás de todo esto? Es una noticia extraña, y no estoy seguro de qué pensar al respecto, pero suena como un asunto completamente desagradable. Me alegra que hayas puesto fin a esto, ${PLAYER}.'","Wigfast está en su escondite cerca de la entrada de Gazatmur.\
\
Debes buscar a Wigfast e informarle sobre la corrupción de la Mano Blanca que descubriste y eliminaste de un solo golpe.","Siervo de la Mano Blanca","Un Uruk al servicio de la Mano Blanca ha aparecido en el campamento de trasgos de Gazatmur. Claramente, planea someter a los trasgos a su voluntad y conducirlos contra los enanos del Mirador de la Gran Excavación en gran número.","Derrotado el teniente de la Mano Blanca"},
[10838]={"'You managed to deal with a few more of those apprentices? Good.\
\
'I do not know where he procured all of these servants, but Saruman is going to need a fair number of replacements by the time you are through with them.'","Isengard is littered with strange devices which have some role in Saruman's preparations for war. These machines are frequently maintained by goblins or by human apprentices who have been trained in their operation by Saruman.","Defeat Apprentices of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dagoras is within the Ring of Isengard.\
\
You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.","'I have spotted a number of strangely-robed Men wandering about, occasionally tending to those devices.\
\
'They are some sort of apprentices in Saruman's service. Without them, he will have more trouble running Isengard. Will you see if you cannot deal with a few of them quietly?'","Servants of Saruman","'It seems like there is no end to those foolish enough to throw in their lot with the forces of darkness.'","Defeated Apprentices of Saruman (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Dagoras within the Ring of Isengard","Saruman's apprentices can be found in Isengard.\
\
Dagoras has asked to you to hunt down any of Saruman's apprentices that you come across in Isengard."},
[10841]={"Free captured Longbeards from Caivád Sâr (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Múta","Captured Longbeards can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
Múta has discovered several Longbeards held captive in Tûr Ágal. You should free them.","Freed captured Longbeards from Caivád Sâr (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Servants of War","'Listen to me.\
\
'There must be more at work here than I thought. The leader of these Dourhands is not an honourable sort—that much is certain. I have seen dwarves led in chains through Tûr Ágal, and the Dourhands mock them and yank at their beards. But not one of the Zhélruka or my kin have been taken... it is only Longbeards!\
\
'I don't know why the Longbeards have drawn the Dourhands' ire, but nothing good can come of it. I would not leave the Longbeards to suffer in such a place. They must be freed before it is too late!\
\
'Would you do this for me, ${PLAYER}?'","Although they seem curiously uninterested in the Stout-axes and Zhélruka, the Dourhands have captured several Longbeards and taken them as prisoners and servants at Caivád Sâr.","'You honour me, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'In the mind of the Stout-axe, there is no fate worse than imprisonment. When our business here is finished, let us leave this wickedness behind.'","Múta can be found in Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr.\
\
You have freed all of the captured Longbeards that you could find. You should return to Múta."},
[10842]={"While scouting Elderslade, you have discovered a settlement of Angmarim still loyal to the Iron Crown.\
\
Although the Witch-king of Angmar has been defeated, these remnants of Angmar continue to spread their wickedness through Middle-earth.\
\
You should defeat the Angmarim of the Iron Crown who dwell in Caivád Sâr, and its tower, Tûr Ágal.","You have defeated many of the wicked Angmarim of the Iron Crown dwelling in Caivád Sâr, and its tower, Tûr Ágal.\
\
The Iron Crown remains the last vestige of Angmar's resurgence, but it, too, shall meet its end in time.","Siervos de la Corona de Hierro","You have defeated many of the wicked servants of the Iron Crown dwelling in Caivád Sâr, and its tower, Tûr Ágal.","Servants of the Iron Crown can be found in Caivád Sâr and Tûr Ágal.\
\
You have discovered a settlement of wicked Angmarim still loyal to the Iron Crown at Caivád Sâr. You should defeat the Angmarim of the Iron Crown dwelling in Caivád Sâr, and its tower, Tûr Ágal.","Although the Witch-king of Angmar has been defeated, servants of the Iron Crown dwelling in Elderslade continue to spread their wickedness through Middle-earth.","Completado","Defeated servants of the Iron Crown in Caivád Sâr and Tûr Ágal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat servants of the Iron Crown in Caivád Sâr and Tûr Ágal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10843]={"'What evil summons forth wights and fell hounds must have great power indeed. We shall have to be cautious.'","Defeat Cun Annun (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'A large pack of fell spirits the Algraig clans call Cun Annun have settled among the hills and valleys of the Lich Bluffs recently. These creatures are fearsome and are an indication of a darker power at work.  \
\
'Can you seek out Cun Annun in this area and defeat any that you might find? They can be found roaming to the south and east of my camp.\
\
'Be wary, ${PLAYER}, for they are no ordinary hounds. The Cun Annun are demons of the ancient world.'","A large pack of Cun Annun haunt the barrows of the Lich Bluffs, presenting a danger to those that would call Enedwaith home.","Talk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs","Servants of the Master","Mincham's camp is south and slightly east of the large Gondorian ruins in the Lich Bluffs.\
\
You should return to Mincham and let him know that you have located and dispatched a pack of Cun Annun.","Defeated Cun Annun (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cun Annun can be found in the southern reaches of the Lichbluffs. \
\
Mincham has asked you to find and defeat as many Cun Annun as you are able.","'Thank you for dispatching these insidious creatures. I fear that their arrival may give credence to tales of a darker force at work in the Lich Bluffs.'"},
[10845]={"Grimmar is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
Fríthild told you to speak with Grimmar and obtain the signets with which to summon the Thanes of the Broadacres.","Talk to Grimmar in the Mead Hall of Stoke","'Welcome, stranger from afar! It is seldom that we greet travellers, even from other parts of Rohan. May I offer you some wine or ale? Indeed, I was about to sit down to a meal...would you join me?\
\
'What is this? Ah! I did not think I would see this signet in my lifetime! My father granted it to Edmar, Fríthild's husband, to use in the event Stoke needed our aid.\
\
'Tell me what has transpired that would bring Fríthild to such a need....'","Gained entrance to the Mead Hall of Oserley","Serving the Summons, Part I","'Welcome, stranger from afar! It is seldom that we greet travellers, even from other parts of Rohan. May I offer you some wine or ale? Indeed, I was about to sit down to a meal...would you join me? Or perhaps you are upon a greater errand?'","'So Reeve Fríthild has decided to summon the thanes? I recommended that she do so days ago, but I understand her concerns. It may well be that Ordlac and Tordag will be unable to come in time.\
\
'Nevertheless, here are the signets of Oserley and Torsbury. Fríthild told you of Ordlac, but not of Tordag. The Thane of Torsbury is brave and a mighty warrior, but he is not the most clever man. It took much for him to accept Fríthild -- a woman -- as Reeve when her husband perished, but since she broke his nose in a brawl, he has been a faithful retainer.\
\
'May fortune smile upon you as you deliver these tokens. Go to Oserley first.'","Bring the signet of Oserley to Ordlac","Gain entrance to the Mead Hall of Oserley","Oserley lies along the road north-east from Stoke.\
\
Fríthild has asked you to deliver a signet to Ordlac of Oserley, summoning him to her aid.","'Greetings, stranger! What news from beyond?\
\
'What? Stoke is under siege? Aye, you must speak with Thane Ordlac at once! You have leave to enter the Mead Hall.'","'${PLAYER}, I know what needs to be done, but I confess that I hesitate to do so. If we are to send aid to Théoden King, we must first break the siege upon Stoke...but to do that, we must muster the Thanes of the Broadacres, and I have no doubt that they, too, face the threat of assault.\
\
'Nevertheless, it must be done. Speak with Grimmar, and he will provide you with signets to take to my thanes. Each signet bears the crest of their households, and they will know that it means we are in dire need of aid.\
\
'Not far to the north-east lies Oserley, where dwells Ordlac. It is settled on an embankment leading down to the Entwash, so they may have not yet seen the smokes of the fires here. Ordlac is a pleasant fellow and likely will be the most ready to join our cause. You should go to him first.'","Stoke is crowded with refugees from outlying farms and even bordering parts of Kingstead and the Stonedeans. Livestock and horses join the press. All the while, Reeve Fríthild struggles to secure her town against the White Hand's siege.","Thane Ordlac is within the Mead Hall of Oserley.\
\
Éoric afforded you access to the Mead Hall of Oserley to speak with Thane Ordlac."},
[10846]={"Apparently, Tordag was forced to retreat from Torsbury, for this is his encampment","Tordag is at his encampment just north of the road between Torsbury and Stoke.\
\
Fríthild sent you to bring the signet of Torsbury to Tordag, summoning him to Stoke's aid.","Serving the Summons, Part II","Your duties done at Oserley, it is time to continue your mission for Reeve Fríthild.","'My muster is complete. I have not a large force, but my garrison is prepared to march to Stoke's defence.\
\
'I suggest that you make for Torsbury at once...they are likely to be in more dire straits than Oserley. I would take as straight a route as you may, for you will not want to come there too late.\
\
'I shall send Dudsig with a handful of my finest warriors to assist at Torsbury, while I myself lead the remainder of my garrison to Stoke. May fortune go with you, ${PLAYER}!'","Torsbury lies to the west of Oserley, near the border of the Stonedeans.\
\
Ordlac bade you hurry by the straightest route to Torsbury to aid Tordag and bring him Fríthild's summons.","'Are you blind? Can you not see that we are in the midst of a war council? I have not the time to....\
\
'What? The signet of Torsbury? That can only mean that Stoke is under siege. May Saruman the White burn forever in the fires he has kindled, curse his mangy hide!'","Torsbury has been overrun. There are signs that Tordag retreated south and east","'What do you want? I am busy.'","Bring the signet of Torsbury to Thane Tordag"},
[10847]={"Viaja al Bosque de los Trolls y encuentra un caballo en Thorenhad.","'Cosas...'","Habla con Roheryn en los establos de Rivendel","Roheryn se encuentra en los establos de Rivendel.","'TBD'","Un caballo en Ost Guruth desea tener una audiencia contigo.","Encuentra el caballo en Ost Guruth","Sesión - Rivendel"},
[10848]={"Atrapacaballos Ongbúrz derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","¡Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:derrotado[m]|derrotado[f]} y te retiras hacia los Campos de Caballos!","Encuentra un caballo de los Montaraces en Esteldín","Sesión — Esteldín","Habla con la montura del Montaraz en Esteldín","Trampa para caballos destruida","'¿Qué te ha traído a un lugar como este? Este no es sitio para ninguna criatura en su sano juicio, pues estoy en el borde mismo de la guerra, con el humo de muchos fuegos llenando el aire.\
\
'El Enemigo ha puesto recientemente su atención en las monturas; usa trampas para desgarrarnos o rompernos las patas. Estos mecanismos perversos deben ser destruidos, pero ten cuidado, seguramente estarán protegidos. Una vez que una montura queda atrapada, los enemigos intentan emboscar al jinete antes de que el caballo pueda liberarse.\
\
'Pareces capaz de valerte mejor que la mayoría de los caballos que he conocido. ¡Por favor, ayúdanos a destruir las trampas para caballos y a quienes las colocaron!'","El enemigo está usando terribles trampas para caballos, y pueden encontrarse en los pasos hacia Dol Dínen.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si te derrotan o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a la Granja Hengstacer.</rgb>","'Los Montaraces aquí, y nosotros las monturas especialmente, te agradecemos haber destruido las trampas que nuestros enemigos colocaron. Ya has probado el sabor de la guerra, y parece que no ha quebrado tu espíritu. Estás hecho de buena madera y espero volver a verte pronto.'","Sientes que un conflicto en Esteldín te atrae de alguna manera, como si tu propósito estuviera ligado a él. Buscas un caballo que pueda instruirte sobre tácticas y estrategias de guerra desde la perspectiva de una montura.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotada[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a la Granja Hengstacer.</rgb>","Los sonidos y olores de la guerra ahuyentarían a la mayoría de los caballos, pero a ti te atraen como una polilla a la lumbre. Buscas encontrarte con un caballo acostumbrado al conflicto, con la esperanza de que pueda darte alguna pista sobre tu propósito...","La montura del Montaraz se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotado[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a la Granja Hengstacer.</rgb>","Destruye las trampas para caballos","Derrota a los atrapacaballos Ongbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Se te acabó el tiempo!"},
[10849]={"¡Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:derrotado[m]|derrotado[f]} y te retiras hacia los Campos de Caballos!","Destruir los trofeos que dejó el enemigo ha apaciguado tu furia, por ahora. Una fuerza poderosa intervino para ahuyentar a esta criatura, y quedó gravemente herida hasta morir aquí.\
\
Antes no podías percibirlo porque el hedor del mal llenaba tus fosas nasales. Al regresar al cadáver, sientes la otra energía, distinta de algún modo.\
\
Permanece aquí como una ola en retirada que deja pequeños charcos sobre la arena. ¿Qué pudo haber hecho esto a una criatura tan poderosa? Debes encontrar la fuente de esta energía.","Examina una vez más la montura negra caída","Un olor maligno te atrae hacia lo profundo del Bosque de los Trolls","Una poderosa fuerza dejó una energía misteriosa alrededor del cadáver de la montura negra, como una ola en retirada que deja pequeños charcos en la arena.\
\
La montura negra no pudo haber llegado muy lejos tras sufrir una herida tan grande. La fuente de un poder así debe encontrarse en algún lugar del Bosque de los Trolls.","Los trofeos dejados por la montura negra caída y su jinete han sido destruidos.\
\
Con tu furia apaciguada, la curiosidad te invade. ¿Qué pudo matar a esta montura, y hacia dónde se dirigía su jinete?","Has destruido una parte de armadura negra","Trophies of the evil steed can be found in the area where it met its death.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.</rgb>","Tus fosas nasales se dilatan ante un olor maligno en el aire. Te sientes ${PLAYERNAME:impulsado[m]|impulsada[f]} a encontrar su origen, ${PLAYERNAME:ansioso[m]|ansiosa[f]} por enfrentar lo que sea que descubras...","Has destruido un trozo de tela negra","Sesión — Bosque de los Trolls","¡Has encontrado la fuente del mal!","Destruye un fragmento de armadura negra","Encuentra la fuente de aquello que ahuyentó a la montura negra","Tus sentidos agudos te atraen hacia una fuente de mal detectada en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotado[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a los Campos de Caballos.</rgb>","Has encontrado la fuente del mal que te atrajo hasta aquí. Este fue una vez un caballo criado para servir a las fuerzas de Sauron. Existen muchos caballos al servicio del Enemigo, pero esta criatura era la montura de un Nazgûl, uno de los Nueve.\
\
El hedor del mal aquí aviva un fuego que nunca antes habías sentido, y sabes que este caballo era un archienemigo. Su muerte es agridulce; habrías preferido enfrentarte tú mismo con él.\
\
El enemigo dejó fragmentos de armadura y tiras de capa. Destruir estos trofeos del mal saciará tu ira ante la existencia de semejante criatura. Busca por la zona y destruye los trofeos de este enemigo caído.","¡Se te acabó el tiempo!","Has encontrado el Vado del Bruinen, la misma fuente del poder que envió a los caballos de los Nueve a su perdición","Destruye un trozo de tela negra"},
[10850]={"'Últimamente he deseado una hierba rara que no he probado en edades. Solía encontrarla solo en lugares muy altos, pero no donde hiciera demasiado frío. Creo que podría encontrarse en la cumbre más elevada de estas tierras, en lo alto de la Cima de los Vientos. ¿Podrías ir allí y recoger unas pocas para mí si las encuentras?\
\
'Mi amo y yo solíamos viajar con frecuencia, y tomé cariño a esta hierba. Ha pasado mucho tiempo desde que me ha llevado más allá de estas ruinas. Quizá pronto volvamos a recorrer la Tierra Media como solíamos hacerlo.'","'¡Gracias por saciar mi apetito por estas hierbas que tanto extrañaba! Mi amo ha estado ocupado con los importantes sucesos que se desarrollan aquí, pero se alegrará al recordar nuestros viajes cuando vea estas hierbas. Son exactamente lo que buscaba; no sé cómo agradecerte lo suficiente.\
\
'Tal vez ya lo sepas, tal vez no, pero parece haber algo especial en ti. Mi amo y yo hemos viajado por muchos lugares de la Tierra Media a lo largo de los años, y he conocido a muchos caballos en mis viajes. Rara vez he encontrado una montura con tu espíritu, o que desprenda tal aire de autoridad...'","Los corceles de los Campos de Caballos mencionaron a un misterioso caballo acompañado de un mago con especial afinidad por los animales, ambos residentes en las Tierras Solitarias.","Derrota a los crebain emboscadores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Encuentra hierbas en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos","La hierba rara que busca el caballo de Radagast solo crece en lugares de gran altitud. El único sitio lo bastante alto en millas alrededor de Ost Guruth es la cima de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotada[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a los Campos de Caballos.</rgb>","Has encontrado hierbas.","¡Has encontrado el caballo de Radagast en Ost Guruth!","Crebain emboscadores derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}).","¡Se te acabó el tiempo!","Lleva las hierbas de vuelta al caballo de Radagast","El caballo de Radagast se encuentra en Ost Guruth.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotada[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a los Campos de Caballos.</rgb>","Dirígete a Ost Guruth y encuentra allí un caballo","Sesión — Cima de los Vientos","Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:derrotado[m]|derrotada[f]} y ahora te retiras hacia los Campos de Caballos","Hay un caballo en Ost Guruth que sientes la necesidad de buscar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si eres #-1:{derrotado[m]|derrotada[f]} o se acaba el tiempo, regresarás a los Campos de Caballos.</rgb>"},
[10851]={"You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should use your Diplomatic Words to convince Góramul Sai to leave.","Check on your daughters","My daughters should be in bed at this hour, but I noticed that my youngest, Khêjiba, was missing. I asked my eldest, Lokóya, if she knew where she was.\
\
'She said she was bored and went to explore. I tried to stop her, but she ran off before I could block the door. I think she went to the garden. Sorry, mother. Please don't be too angry with her.'","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should find Otibúk in the southern bed-chamber.","Listen to the conversation","'I assume you overheard some of that. Mizâdi's rebels approach from the East while the upstart servants of Aradûn approach from the West. Our enemies are nearly at our doorstep. We must strike before they form an alliance and encircle Emax Dûl.\
\
'But do not worry, I will oversee our forces and ensure we are victorious. We cannot abandon Emax Dûl. We cannot fail the Hûl. We cannot abandon Emax Dûl. We cannot fail the Hûl...'\
\
Góramul seems momentarily entranced. He snaps back to normal when he hears someone else enter the room.","Talk to Lokóya","Use your Diplomatic Words to convince your husband","Session: Life on the Other Side","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should use Icy Glare on Ratúlko the Bloody to let him know how you feel.","I asked Khêjiba who she was speaking to, growing increasingly concerned.\
\
'I don't really know. We call her the Pale Lady. She talks to me sometimes.'\
\
I was alarmed, and asked if my other daughters knew about her.\
\
'Yes. She talks to all three of us. I've seen her staring at Otibúk before, too. Do you think she can help him?'","My husband's lapdog does not deserve my attention","Otibúk's condition is much the same. His whole body glistens with sweat, fighting both his wounds and an ever-returning fever. He occasionally thrashes in the bed, softly moaning. Is he having nightmares of the battle? I could not know, and was being consumed by my helplessness. How can a mother watch her son suffer so?","Find your husband","Talk to your sister","Find Khêjiba in the central garden","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should hear Góramul Sai's response.","Eavesdrop on your husband's conversation","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should return Khêjiba to the northern bed-chamber.","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should approach Góramul Sai and listen to the conversation.","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should hear what Dark Priestess Barkhuráni has to say to Góramul Sai.","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should talk to Dark Priestess Barkhuráni in the banquet hall.","I inquired as to just who this dark ally is, and why I was not made aware of an important guest in the palace before this.\
\
'My apologies, sister! I would have thought your husband would have informed you. If he has not explained, he must not want to trouble you with it, and I would not want to displease the Sai.\
\
'All you need to know is we have a powerful ally on our side, who will ensure a prosperous future for us and the empire.'\
\
She flashes an innocent smile, but does not elaborate any further.","My family and I only recently arrived in Emax Dûl. Life was not so different at first, trading one palace for another, but recently something has changed. Of late I felt a growing unease, as if something was hidden from me. Two days ago, I decided it would be necessary to act, to save the lives of my children.","Góramulâ's eyes welled with tears. Somewhere inside, he knew he was losing the fight, both for Mûr Ghala and for his own mind.\
\
'Kotráka... I am sorry.'","Use your Icy Glare on Ratúlko","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should talk to Góramul Sai in the banquet hall.","Listen to your husband's words","I demanded answers. Yes, my husband is the crown prince, but something was deeply wrong, and I would not allow it to threaten my children.\
\
'You forget yourself, Kotráka. I have everything under control.'","I asked Lokóya if she knew about the Pale Lady. She turned white as a sheet at the mention of the name.\
\
'I... Yes. I don't know what she is or what she wants. She has appeared to all of us. Aunt Barkhuráni warned us not to mention her to anyone, so I haven't....'\
\
She starts to cry.\
\
'Mother, I'm afraid to leave our bedroom! Can we please go back to Ordâkh?'","Check on your son","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should find your daughters in the northern bed-chamber.","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should find Khêjiba. She is hiding somewhere in the royal living quarters.","Talk to your husband","You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.\
\
You should find Góramul Sai in your shared bed-chamber, to the rear of the living quarters."},
[10853]={"Coloca la trampa (Opcional)","Drâgh se encuentra en la Gran Escalera, al este de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo y al noroeste del Refugio Sombrío, en las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Derrota a Drâgh en la Gran Escalera para evitar que siga interfiriendo en la expedición de los enanos en Moria.","Derrota a Drâgh","Regresa con Armbeald en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo","Drâgh ha sido derrotado","Armbeald se encuentra en la Guardia Orca, al noroeste de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Regresa con Armbeald y cuéntale que Drâgh ha sido derrotado gracias a tus esfuerzos y a los de tus amigos.","'¿Ya terminaste?'","El líder de los orcos de la Mano Blanca, Drâgh, se encuentra en la Gran Escalera de Moria, sembrando el terror por donde pasa. Uno de los enanos de la expedición ha sido asesinado, y Armbeald te ha pedido que vengues al inocente acabando con ese malvado enemigo.","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. ¡Sin duda te mereces esta recompensa!'","'Tu última misión será derrotar a Drâgh. Reúne a tus amigos, ${PLAYER}, pues no será una tarea fácil.\
\
'Lleva esta efigie a la Gran Escalera y convoca al orco cruel que supone una amenaza enorme para el pueblo que desea recuperar el hogar que le corresponde por derecho. No quiero que siga hostigando a los pueblos libres de Moria.\
\
'Regresa a mí cuando hayas logrado desterrar a esta criatura, ${PLAYER}. Espero que tus flechas vuelen certeras y lo derriben de una vez por todas, para que no nos cause más problemas.'"},
[10854]={"Set to Task","Speak with Akúlhun at Gramsfoot","Speak with War-tyrant Akúlhun about available tasks.","The War-tyrant has a set of tasks for you and offers rewards if you can complete them.","'A new recruit, eh? Good. Take this. It's a list of tasks that need doing. Make yourself useful and I will see you rewarded and marvel as you rise through the ranks of my war-host. Or, be like so many other, maggots. Useless. Pathetic. Unworthy.'","'The battle goes on, recruit. We need every body in the field to be upright and capable. If you think you are ready to take the fight to the enemy, then speak with the War-tyrant. He's got a list that'll keep you busy.'"},
[10856]={"Wynfor has fashioned three traps from the avanc-jaws that you brought him and wants you to set them out for the mysterious intruder.","You have used up all the traps and should return to Wynfor","'We do not need any unwelcome guests creeping about.'","'I will take this string and stretch it here... and here....'\
\
Wynfor works for a few moments, then is satisfied.\
\
'Aye, this will do. See! I have made of this avanc-jaw a trap! It will snap shut on the leg of its unsuspecting prey, and this intruder will find it much more difficult to evade capture!\
\
'Let me make a few more, and... all right. I will give you these three traps. Set them in the vicinity of those footprints you found, and we will see if this unwelcome intruder strays into our trap! Use up the bundle of traps and return to me.'","'Thank you for helping me guard the village.'","You found footprints on the far shore of the lake, north-west of the eyot and beneath the cliffs west of the shore, and now Wynfor wants you to set three traps he made at those locations.\
\
Wynfor has given you three traps he has made, and he wants you to set them in the vicinity of the footprints you found earlier.","Placed snap-jaw traps on the ground (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wynfor is in Tûr Morva.\
\
You have set the traps for Wynfor and should now return to him.","Find a suitable place to set the traps near the footprints","Talk to Wynfor at Tûr Morva","'Set those three traps near where you found those footprints, ${PLAYER}. We will catch this intruder with one of them, then we will see what she has to say for herself! Use up the bundle of traps and come back here.'","This would be a suitable place to set the traps.","'I am not as spry as I used to be.'","Place the three snap-jaw traps near the footprints until you have used them up (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Setting Traps","You have placed the snap-jaw traps in Tâl Methedras, as Wynfor wanted.","'You set the traps? Good. We do not want anyone sneaking around who should not be here.\
\
'I wonder if that was enough traps? I may see if your Ranger friends will help me collect more avanc-jaws.'"},
[10857]={"Hojas desafiladas recogidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Puedes encontrar las viejas hojas desafiladas esparcidas por el Ala Norte. No necesitas buscar demasiado.'","Las hojas desafiladas se encuentran en los armeros en el Ala Norte del Umbral de Durin.\
\
Debes recoger varias hojas desafiladas para restaurarlas en la forja recién encendida.","Usa la forja para restaurar las hojas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, hola, ${PLAYER}! Hemos tenido un comienzo difícil aquí, sin duda, pero ¿no es este un momento emocionante? Ya hemos excavado estas forjas tan impresionantes.\
\
'¿Te gustaría ayudarme a montar el taller? Ten cuidado... los fuegos están calientes. ¡Los enanos de Moria sabían lo que hacían cuando construyeron esto!'","Has restaurado las hojas desafiladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Poniendo en marcha el taller","Athils busca ayuda para poner en funcionamiento una vieja forja en el Ala Norte.","Recoge hojas desafiladas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Athils se encuentra en el Ala Norte del Umbral de Durin, supervisando el trabajo que se realiza allí.\
\
Debes llevar las hojas recién restauradas a Athils.","'Ah, eso es un buen trabajo, buen ${RACE}! Puedo decir que esto fue forjado en Moria -- la mejora ya es notable. Espero con ansias el trabajo que se hará aquí.'","Lleva las hojas recién restauradas a Athils","La forja del Ala Norte se encuentra cerca de Athils.\
\
Debes usar la forja para restaurar las hojas que has recogido."},
[10858]={"Habla con Robbo Moliespalda","'Ah, these are just the thing, ${PLAYER}! If these don't help us sound great, I don't know what will! I'll make sure they end up in the proper hands.\
\
'I saw Hollur talking to Polla while you were gone, and I think she'd like another word with you when you have the time.\
\
'We are so close now, my friend!'","The Hall of Air can be found in the northern section of the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Polla is displeased, but willing to try a different theatre at Gord's request. You should meet the Cloudyheads at the Hall of Air.","Search the markets of Minas Tirith for ornate instruments (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The sound of Hollur's drumming is a bit muffled, but still acceptable...","Hollur's drums are nearly muted by the wind coursing along the theatre's edge!","Hollur's drumming can be heard clearly","Polla Stoutley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith.\
\
Gord Dunley has requested that the band perform in another space as he feels his voice is lacking in the Stone Theatre.","'Thanks for all the help so far, ${PLAYER}. I know it's been a bit frustrating to be shuffled around like this, but I think our troubles are finally resolved! I spoke to Hollur and Gord about choosing another theatre, and I was able to arrange something very special for us after speaking to one of the local players.\
\
'I won't spoil the surprise just yet, but we're going to perform in the best theatre in Minas Tirith.\
\
'Care to guess which one?'","You have found a fancy theorbo with fine strings and intricate detailing","Talk to Polla Stoutley","Talk to Hollur","Displeased with the theatre in the First Circle, the Cloudyheads have chosen to explore another before putting on their show.","'Oh, Gord...\
\
'If he thinks that trying another theatre will make a difference, so be it. Goodness knows, we've had enough trouble at this one.\
\
'I know of another theatre in the Fifth Circle named the Hall of Air. We'll pack up and travel there in a few moments. \
\
'We need to resolve this soon or the war will be at our doorstep before we get the chance to play... Do meet us there when you are ready!'","You have found a lute with a detailed grille and beautiful maple shell","'Hullo again, my friend!\
\
'On my long walk to the Hall of Air, I had quite the thought! These instruments we have are old and more than a bit warped from our long journey to Gondor. Can you imagine how great we might sound with what the very best the craftsmen of Minas Tirith have to offer?\
\
'Yes, yes, I know. The instrument does not make the player, but humour me!\
\
'Please, ${PLAYER}. Here is some gold - take it down to the markets and see what you can find!'","Gord Dunley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith.\
\
Gord Dunley has voiced concerns about performing in the Stone Theatre and Polla has asked you to investigate.","'Well, we're still talking - so I'll take that as a yes!\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. It'll be worth your while, I promise.\
\
'The Cloudyheads are a good bunch, and we take care of our own! To that end, Gord wished to speak to you about some sort of matter. He wouldn't be specific, but then again, I've come to expect that from him. If I were to wager a guess, he might be a bit apologetic for such a terse introduction.\
\
'Why don't you go speak to him and find out?'","Robbo Gristback is in the Hall of Air in Minas Tirith.\
\
Hollur has asked you to speak to Robbo about an idea he had on the way to the Hall of Air.","You have found a fine horn crafted of steel and plated with gold","Polla Stoutley can be found in Hall of Air.\
\
You have delivered the instruments to Robbo in the Hall of Air. Robbo has informed you that Polla would like to talk to you.","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I am sorry for the manner of my introduction... I did not wish to come across so dismissively.'\
\
You inform Gord that Polla knew that he would say something like that.\
\
'She truly knows me, doesn't she? I was a bit distracted by the crowd, you see, but I am beyond the initial shock of their gathering - I assure you. You seem to be helping out, and if Polla's happy, I'm happy.\
\
'I'll not mince words - the Stone Theatre will not work for our performance. My voice sounds abysmal in the space, and it seems a waste to perform in such conditions.\
\
'I was hesitant to bring this up with Polla as it has been a problem in the past as well, but perhaps if you do, she'll be more receptive.\
\
'What do you say, my friend?'","Ornate instruments can be found at various markets in Minas Tirith.\
\
Robbo Gristback hopes to purchase instruments of finer make to help his band put on a better show in Minas Tirith. He has provided the gold and has asked you to peruse the markets of the City.","The Hall of Air can be found in the Fifth Circle.\
\
Polla Stoutley has asked you to sit in various seats in the Hall of Air to help Hollur ensure that the sound is even throughout the theatre.","Robbo Gristback can be found in the Hall of Air in the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You have acquired several new instruments for the Cloudyheads and should now deliver them to Robbo.","Hollur can be found in the Hall of Air.\
\
You have tested various seats in the theatre and much to your dismay, it seems there is a wide range of quality in the available seating.","'It is as I thought then...\
\
'This will not work for us either. We'll either have to travel back down to the Stone Theatre or perhaps there's another we still haven't tried. Don't you worry, I'll speak to Polla about it.\
\
'In the meantime, I think Robbo wanted to talk to you about something.'","'Ah, you made it, ${PLAYER}! This City is too big for its own good, if you ask me!\
\
'I decided it was best to humour Gord's request and take a look at the Hall of Air. Between you and me, he's always been worried about his voice. I know the theatre won't make any difference, but if it helps him perform, I'll hold my tongue.\
\
'This theatre is a bit smaller, but I think it will do. Why don't you talk to Hollur? He's always keen on testing the acoustics of a space before performing, so you might be able to aid him.'","Setting the Stage","Talk to Gord Dunley","Listen to Hollur from seats in the Hall of Air (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have found an ornate drum depicting the Tree of Gondor on its head","Meet the Cloudyheads at the Hall of Air","'Hah, ${PLAYER}, glad you're still with us!\
\
'It seems to me that this theatre has an odd shape to it, and I am curious how our instruments might sound in such a lofty place. I asked Gord to help, but he is in something of a foul mood and I know better than to press him.\
\
'You could aid me greatly if you would sit in several different seats throughout the theatre and tell me how clearly you can hear my playing.\
\
'Hopefully my fears are unfounded, but I have a bad feeling about this one.'","You have found the band busily exploring the theatre...","Deliver the instruments to Robbo Gristback","Polla Stoutley can be found in the Hall of Air in the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You have arrived at the Hall of Air and should now talk to Polla.","Hollur can be found in the Hall of Air.\
\
Polla has asked you to speak to Hollur about testing the theatre's acoustics.","Talk to Polla Stoutley in the Hall of Air"},
[10860]={"'Bien, es algo bueno que el asunto de los lobos esté solucionado. Nunca podría haber terminado con la cosecha con los lobos acechando y cazando en mis tierras.'","'Menuda historia sera esta, con esos lobos cruzando el Brandivino y gente expulsándolos. Tendré que decirle al viejo Ronald en Dwaling que me escriba una carta para contarle todo esto a mi primo Sam!'","'Esta carne servirá perfectamente, ¡ahora todo lo que tenemos que hacer es tender la trampa! Como le decía a la gente del pueblo, vi la manada al noreste de aquí. Si vas en esa dirección, deberías ver algunos lobos jóvenes, y el más grande no andará muy lejos.\
\
'El gran lobo seguramente esté oculto en una cueva o agujero cerca de la manda... eso es al menos lo que suelen contar las historias. Podrías intentar colocar la carne fuera de su cueva para atraerlo.\
\
'Intenta no usar toda la carne, eso sí. No me importaría almorzar unas cuantas lonchas de alce frito.'","Habla con Hal Gamyi","Has conseguido el cebo que Hal Gamyi te sugirió que usaras para atraer al líder de los lobos.","'Todavía no puedo creer que fueras capaz de vencer a este lobo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Vaya historia que tengo para contar la próxima vez que vaya al Dragón!'","'Los lobos deberían estar justo al norte de Avenal en el Peñasco del Sedo. ¡Deberías darte prisa en encargarte de los lobos antes de que empiecen a cazar aquí en el pueblo!'","Colmihueso derrotado","'¿Ya has matado al lobo?'","Hal Gamyi está en el centro de Avenal.\
\
Debes volver con Hal Gamyi con las noticias de tu victoria.","Mata a Colmihueso","Tendiendo la trampa","El campamento de los lobos se encuentra al noreste de Avenal.\
\
Ahora que has traido la carne de alce, Hal Gamyi sugiere que es hora de tener la trampa para el gran lobo colocando la carne fuera de su cueva."},
[10861]={"'Tus esfuerzos en favor de los Eglain son nobles, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, pero considero que nuestro peligro es mayor de lo que pensábamos. ¿Llevan una bandera con la marca de una mano blanca? Los bandidos y rufianes comunes no ostentan tal emblema. La marca de la Mano Blanca me indica que sirven a un señor más poderoso.\
\
'Sea cual sea su propósito, esas criaturas no pueden tomar pie en el Norte. No pertenecen aquí. Si puedes entrar en Naerost y matar a Hontimûrz, su líder, y a sus guardias, quizá los demás huyan.\
\
'Hontimûrz se dio a conocer cuando nos envió regalos macabros acompañados de sus amenazas garabateadas. Creo que has venido a vengar esa ofensa y a devolver la fe a los Eglain.'","Corta la Mano Blanca","Naerost se encuentra justo al este de la Cima de los Vientos, al norte de Hunulf Mascador.\
\
Hunulf Mascador teme que los semiorcos sirvan a un poder mayor, quizá incluso a Mordor. Te ha pedido que entres en Naerost y derrotes a su líder y a sus guardias con la esperanza de que los demás huyan.","'Me ahorraré los detalles macabros de la entrega que nos hizo Hontimûrz. Basta saber que la depravación de esas criaturas demuestra que no son Hombres. Son algo totalmente bestial y destructivo. Hemos anhelado una oportunidad de venganza, y parece que tu llegada puede traer esa oportunidad.'","Derrota a los guardias de Hontimûrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a Hontimûrz","'Ah, ¿entonces los semiorcos no huyeron? No importa... el agarre de la Mano Blanca se ha aflojado. Creo que no nos volverán a molestar, gracias a ti.\
\
'Tus esfuerzos en favor de los Eglain no serán olvidados, ${PLAYER}.'","Guardias de Hontimûrz eliminados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A la sombra de Amon Sûl, en el borde de Nain Enidh, yacían unas ruinas arnorianas. Esas ruinas ofrecían a los Eglain de Ost Guruth abundante material para comerciar con coleccionistas de las Tierras de Bree... hasta la llegada de semiorcos procedentes del sur.","Hunulf Mascador espera tu regreso en su campamento al este de Minas Eriol, al sur de Naerost.\
\
Aunque los semiorcos no huyeron, su líder y sus guardias han sido derrotados. Debes volver a informar a Hunulf Mascador.","'Puedo recuperar mis fuerzas de nuevo, gracias a todo lo que has hecho.'","'Siempre te recordaremos, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Hunulf Mascador","Hontimûrz ha sido derrotado"},
[10862]={"Lady Raenemel is at her house in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place.\
\
You have found Lady's Raenemel's house and she is outside. Now you should talk to her.","'Speak with her, ${PLAYER}.'","Return to Lady Raenemel's house","Stroll to the garden near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.","'I have some words that I wish to say to you... over there.'","Stroll up onto the wall near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.","'Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, right by the Finding Place.'","The Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.\
\
The mysterious woman stands before the Old Guest-house, talking to Bergil.","'Speak not until we are back at my home. I must think!'","'Do you know why I took you on this stroll? To explain to you how I would not budge. How I would remain a watchful statue, above and far off, and help only as I may from the shadows.\
\
'But, I know not how, in endeavouring to explain myself, I have budged. Relented! I am a clouded pool, I am a troubled heart, but I cannot help but feel that beyond this pain I feel lies, might I call it... hope?'","Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place.\
\
Bergil wants to take you to Lady Raenemel's house.","Here is the spot where the goblins broke into the cisterns","'You will not believe your ears, ${PLAYER}. She says it was she who placed all the things in the Finding Place. But I think that also - ah, never mind that. You should speak to her yourself.'","Talk to Bergil","Learn more about what happened in the Cisterns and the mysterious woman you found there.","You can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle.\
\
The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further. Use the stones you've gathered to block up the hole.","Walk to the fountain by the Baths near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.","Talk to Lady Raenemel","'Up the stairs to the wall-walk, where we may have a view.'","Lady Raenemel dashes ahead and begins to speak with Bergil in hushed tones","Return to Raenemel's home","'${PLAYER}, there is something I must say. An explanation is in order. But no, not here.\
\
'Walk with me.'\
\
Lady Raenemel nods southward down the street.","You can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle.\
\
The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further.","'Go on, if that's what she wants. I'll be all right.'","Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place.\
\
Lady Raenemel wishes to speak with you alone.","Stroll with Lady Raenemel","Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place.\
\
Lady Raenemel wishes to speak with you alone... outside her home.","'Over there, where there is a small garden beside the path.'","'Do you doubt that I tutored the Steward's sons? Many years had I laboured in the Houses of Lore, and after my sons perished in Lord Denethor's bid to retake old Osgiliath, he was wise and kind and generous in charging me with his own sons.\
\
'Few have seen my face in the years since they left my tutelage. Indeed, I have rarely left my chambers. But when I discovered the prizes I left in that crevice being taken not by the season or the month, but by the day - or more often - I found ways of watching the takers without being seen.\
\
'Like you, I have watched over these children. Only, in my own way, and you must understand that. This is what I am trying to impart to you. My own way.'","Lady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\
\
Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.","Several Mendings","'I have always loved the fountains outside the Baths. Let us stroll over there.'","Lady Raenemel beams.\
\
'Speak with the boy, ${PLAYER}. He will tell you all.'","You have arrived at Lady Raenemel's house","'Here is the ${CLASS}. Bergil, would you be good enough to stay here a moment? This ${RACE} and I must speak alone.'","Gathered a stone (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place.\
\
You should follow Lady Raenemel back to her house.","Block up the breach","'She lives just around the way from the Finding Place! How many times have we gone past her, and never known!'","Return with Lady Raenemel to her home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.","Continue to stroll up on the wall near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.","'Why look there. Good as any mason! You are full of marvels, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The lady, Lady Raenemel it is, she told me where she lives. We should go there now, and speak with her. She is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place, of course.'","Lady Raenemel and Bergil are speaking intently in hushed tones","Talk to the mysterious woman","'Had I gone to Tumladen with the wains, as I was meant to... but I am an old thing, withered with grief and more at ease with my books than with living souls. Do you know, I wander the City by night, greeting ancient stones like friends, taking care never to cross the path of a living, breathing soul?\
\
'And so you must understand, ${PLAYER}, you must undertake for me - these children, though I will love them from afar, they cannot, I will not... I am old, you see, and crooked with grief...\
\
'I am like a troubled pool, ${PLAYER}, and nothing is clear to me. Let us return. I must think. Yes, think.'","You can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle.\
\
The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further. You should gather nearby stones for the task.","Bergil stands outside Lady Raenemel's house in the Fourth Circle.\
\
Lady Raenemel and Bergil were speaking as you approached. Now Bergil seems to have something to say to you.","'${PLAYER}! ${PLAYER}! I can hardly believe it. It WAS she who left the things for us. And she will come to see us now at the Old Guest-house, and we are all welcome to come here now, at any time. And she will let us see old rooms in the Houses of Lore we would never be allowed into otherwise. And any who wish it shall receive lessons!\
\
'But I am going on, aren't I? Ha ha! This is a good day, ${PLAYER}, even if tomorrow will not be so. And I thank you, for you have brought many things to light, haven't you, in the end?'","'How did Lady Raenemel stay in the City, I wonder? I don't think anyone has ever seen her before!'","The breach is within the cisterns, which can be entered at the southern end of the First Circle.\
\
Bergil has come up just as you finished blocking up the breach.","'I owe you much, ${CLASS}, but first the breach within the cisterns must be mended. You can be trusted with such a task, yes?'","'Let us not tarry, but go on along the wall-walk.'","Go to Lady Raenemel's house","Gather stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Where was I? These children have only the barest of notions what hopelessness there is, and though all should fall tomorrow, I will NOT have unquenched candles dimmed. I will not break that spell. Nor would you! I see it in your eyes. I know of how you stood up to that petty ruffian. Yes, I hear much, though I am not seen.\
\
'I heard of Lord Boromir's end and it pierced my heart, it did. And now - Lord Faramir! Though all others remember them as grown men, noble and brave, in my mind they are but boys. For I was their tutor and governess, and the memory of the light in their eyes when I showed to them knowledge, truth, and wisdom - it fades not.\
\
'But let us not tarry here.'","Bergil comes up just as you finish your work","Return to the breach in the cisterns","'These children. One can plainly see - even from afar - how they are untouched, untouched by the dark despair that has fallen over this fortress-city. Untouched by even the Enemy's pall that has darkened the skies. And I cannot, will not...\
\
'You see, it was my sons who first discovered the hole in that wall. And you should have seen the light in their eyes when they discovered what I had hidden there. Do you think, had they known it was I, the same light would have shone?\
\
'Come. Up that way.'","Step away from Lady Raenemel's House"},
[10863]={"Habla con Glamodúd en Echad Glamodúd","Has debilitado a los orcos de Ashúrz Maufulug desarmando sus trampas, dejándoles vulnerables ante un ataque.","Cortando el brazo armado","'¡Salve, ${PLAYER}, perdición de Morsharpat!'","Has derrotado a Morsharpat en Ashúrz Maufulug","Derrota a Morsharpat en Ashúrz Maufulug","'¿Morsharpat todavía vive? Hasta que no sea derrotado, los orcos de Ashúrz Maufulug seguirán siendo una amenaza para nosotros.'","Morsharpat está en Ashúrz Maufulug, al sur y poco al oeste de Echad Glamodúd.\
\
Glamodúd te ha pedido que derrotes a Morsharpat, el capitán de los orcos en Ashúrz Maufulug.","'Has hecho bien al debilitar a los orcos de esta manera. Solo hay una última e importante tarea que queda por hacer, ${PLAYER}: cortar el brazo que empuña la espada.\
\
'En lo más profundo de Ashúrz Maufulug encontrarás a su capitán, a quien hemos sabido que llaman Morsharpat. Es una criatura violenta que posee gran habilidad con las armas. Elimínalo y los orcos serán una presa fácil.\
\
'Cuando hayas conseguido realizar esta tarea, vuelve a verme y te recompensaré lo mejor que pueda.'","Glamodúd está en Echad Glamodúd, al norte y un poco al este de Ashúrz Maufulug.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Glamodúd con la noticia de tu victoria contra Morsharpat.","'¿Has derrotado a Morsharpat? ¡Entonces la victoria ya es casi nuestra! Te has ganado esta recompensa, ${PLAYER}.'","'¡No pasará mucho antes de que nuestras tropas de Echad Sirion hagan que la muerte lleva sobre los orcos de Ashúrz Maufulug!'"},
[10864]={"Defeated many foes at Kidzul-kâlah.","Shade Over Kidzul-kâlah","Explore Kidzul-kâlah","An unpleasant darkness has settled upon the Vales of Anduin. Spirits drift upon the Gladdenmere and through the old dwarf ruins of Kidzul-kâlah. These fell beings should be defeated if the Vales are to remain safe.","Destroyed shadow source (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated foes at Kidzul-kâlah (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kidzul-kâlah can be found alongside the Gladdenmere.\
\
You should destroy shadow sources and defeat any foes you find at Kidzul-kâlah.","Defeat foes at Kidzul-kâlah (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated many foes at Kidzul-kâlah, making the Vales of Anduin safer.","Completado","Lost spirits move throughout the old dwarf ruins of Kidzul-kâlah.","Destroy sources of shadow at Kidzul-kâlah (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10865]={"'Do you think you could look for my son? It may be that the Orcs of Avabárg proved too wily for him to escape, and he may be held in their fort on the island! Slay the Orcs there, and if you still do not see sign of him proceed further south into the Gladden Fields. We heard tell of shades and coloured lights among the pools, and while I forbade him from seeking them he may have been drawn in that direction after escaping from the Orcs! Please, ${PLAYER}, there is no one else to whom I can turn!'","'Are you... are you a friend?'","Badwila disappeared somewhere in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.","An injured hunter lies among the remains of a dozen Orcs","Defeat Orcs at Avabárg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Did my father... send you to me...? We were separated... and I could not get back to the village. I think the Orcs were trying... to take me alive. That is the only... the only reason I still live!'\
\
Badwila pauses to catch his breath, but when he speaks again his voice is still full of fear and his face is pale.\
\
'Look what the Orcs got for their trouble! Death! Death came for them! It was a terrifying spirit, a shade of evil countenance! It descended upon them and killed them all! It is a wonder it did not kill me too!'","One of the hunters from the village of Hultvís may know what has disturbed the shades in the Gladden Fields.","Talk to one of the hunters in Hultvís","Shades in the Swamp: Ghostly Figures","Eurik asked you to defeat the Orcs he encountered at Avabárg while you search for his son.","¿Qué es ese ruido?","'Do you think you could look for my son? We heard tell of shades and coloured lights among the pools, and while I forbade him from seeking them he may have been drawn in that direction after escaping from the Orcs! Please, ${PLAYER}, there is no one else to whom I can turn!'","Defeat shades on the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Orcs at Avabárg (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You hear a faint voice calling from the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields!","'The Woodmen live nigh to the Gladden Fields, and if some evil has stirred up the shades there they will be among the first affected. I did not fight to defend them so recently at the Old Ford for them to succumb to a new danger so soon afterward, ${PLAYER}! Go to Hultvís at Woodsedge and find someone who might know what has happened to disturb shades and spirits formerly at rest.\
\
'One of their hunters may best know, ${PLAYER}. Speak with one of them.'","Defeated shades on the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Eurik believed that you might find his son among the shades of the Gladden Fields if you did not find him with the Orcs of Avabárg.","'If some evil has stirred up the shades in the Gladden Fields, the Woodmen will be among the first affected. I did not fight to defend them so recently at the Old Ford for them to succumb to a new danger so soon afterward, ${PLAYER}! Go to Hultvís at Woodsedge and find someone who might know what has happened to disturb shades and spirits formerly at rest.\
\
'One of their hunters may best know, ${PLAYER}. Speak with one of them.'","Talk to Badwila among the Orc corpses","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. You should speak to Eurik. He and his son went hunting to fill the larders of Hultvís... but only Eurik returned.'","Look for Badwila in the north-west of the Gladden Fields","'${PLAYER}! Can it be? In my heart I hoped you would return, but I feared to send word, and in any event I did not know how to reach you. But for you to arrive at this moment... I dared not hope for it, even at my lowest point!\
\
'My son Badwila is a hunter, as I am, ${PLAYER}. We were hunting on the west bank of the river, not far from Avabárg, when we were surprised by a party of Orcs. That is not unusual in these dark days, and as is our custom we split up in order to frustrate their pursuit. Badwila knows to return to Hultvís when it is safe, but I have not yet seen him!\
\
'Do you think you could look for my son? It may be that the Orcs of Avabárg proved too wily for him to escape, and he may be held in their fort on the island! Slay the Orcs there, and if you still do not see sign of him proceed further south into the Gladden Fields. We heard tell of shades and coloured lights among the pools, and while I forbade him from seeking them he may have been drawn in that direction after escaping from the Orcs! Please, ${PLAYER}, there is no one else to whom I can turn!'","Grimbeorn has tasked you with investigating the increased presence of ghostly figures within the Gladden Fields, for his neighbours among the Woodmen may be threatened by these apparitions.","You have found Eurik's son Badwila. He has been injured, but he is surrounded by the corpses of Orcs much less fortunate than he."},
[10866]={"Shades in the Swamp: Only Half-Remembered","'My dear friend has suffered for too long. My song keeps him at peace. You have my trust, and may follow me to him.'","You have done as the Maiden of the Gladden asked. Will she now help you uncover the cause of the darkness that has settled upon the Gladden Fields?","'Tell me when you are ready, and I will bring you to see my friend. Step with care, for the way may be treacherous for mortals.'","The Maiden of the Gladden waits for you by the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah.","Talk to Gultháva and follow her into the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah"},
[10867]={"Shades in the Swamp: The Maiden of Gladden","The Maiden motions at the encircling hills with one slender arm.\
\
'Many are they who seek to harm my friend. Long have I kept him safe, granting him the peaceful slumber he needs. How am I to know you wish him well?'\
\
The Maiden falls silent, but her words hang in the air like ripples on the surface of a pond. Then she crouches and picks up a handful of soil, letting the dirt fall back to the ground between delicate fingers.\
\
'So many of my friends have gone away. Merillif and Braiglad, Silloth and Lenhwest... they planted flowers among the vales, and now their flowers are troubled by the encroaching darkness. Sprinkle this pure soil upon their flowers, in memory of my lost friends, and I will know you can be trusted.'\
\
As the Maiden gazes off to the north, beyond the still waters, images rise unbidden in your mind's eye. You see flowers growing among the camps of your foes in the Vales of Anduin, and hastily mark them on your map.","The Maiden's former distrust is gone. Now she gazes at you with fondness, and her smile sparkles like sunshine on the water.\
\
'I delight to know you have honoured my friends, though they went away so long ago. The passions of Lenhwest could not be quenched, and were not; she was the first to leave, and I missed her most of all. Merillif had a beauty all her own, and as she walked among her gardens there were none who did not love her. Silloth's laughter echoed in the dell, leaping from hearer to hearer, arousing happiness in each one. Wild Braiglad was the last to leave; she drew pleasure from even the most untamed of regions, and delighted in ferocity.\
\
'You have the trust of Gultháva. Perhaps you can help my friend.'","Sprinkle soil of purity on Silloth's flower","Defeated Orcs or goblins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Maiden of the Gladden stares at you with enigmatic eyes.","Sprinkle soil of purity on Braiglad's flower","Talk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden","The Maiden of the Gladden has reappeared further along the western path through Gladdenmere.","Catch up to the Maiden of the Gladden further to the west along the path through Gladdenmere","'Few only come this way.'","Pick up the soil of purity","The flower shines with renewed vigour","Return to Gultháva near the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah","The Maiden stares at you with enigmatic eyes","The Maiden of the Gladden waits for you by the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah.","Defeat Orcs or goblins in the Vales of Anduin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Merillif and Braiglad, Silloth and Lenhwest... they planted flowers among the vales, and now their flowers are troubled by the encroaching darkness. Sprinkle this pure soil upon their flowers, in memory of my lost friends, and I will know you can be trusted.'","The Maiden of the Gladden stares at you cryptically.","The Maiden of the Gladden asked you to pick up the soil of purity and sprinkle it on flowers planted by her friends throughout the Vales of Anduin.","Once more she disappears, and reappears further to the west","The Maiden regards you with distrust.\
\
'Few only come this way,' she says, and her voice puts you in mind of a sighing breeze among the reeds. 'My friend is not to be disturbed. Go, and let him remain at peace.'","The Maiden stares at you cryptically","The Maiden of the Gladden has reappeared further to the west along the path that runs through Gladdenmere.","Catch up to the Maiden of the Gladden further to the west in Gladdenmere","The Maiden's eyes are deep, still wells. She regards you silently, and disappears.","'So many of my friends have gone away. Merillif and Braiglad, Silloth and Lenhwest... they planted flowers among the vales, and now their flowers are troubled by the encroaching darkness. Sprinkle this pure soil upon their flowers, in memory of my lost friends, and I will know you can be trusted.'\
\
As the Maiden gazes off to the north, beyond the still waters, images rise unbidden in your mind's eye. You see flowers growing among the camps of your foes in the Vales of Anduin, and hastily mark them on your map.","Sprinkle soil of purity on Merillif's flower","You found the Maiden of the Gladden, a figure out of Woodmen legend, and followed her into the flooded wilderness. Does she have something to do with the darkness that has settled upon the Gladden Fields?","The soil feels fertile and rich between your fingers","'What do you seek?'","The flower sparkles with renewed vitality","The flower shimmers with renewed health","Sprinkle soil of purity on Lenhwest's flower","The Maiden waits for you to pick up the fertile soil","The Maiden of the Gladden asked you to find the flowers planted by her long-lost friends throughout the Vales of the Anduin and sprinkle the soil of purity on them. You have marked the locations she gave to you on your map:\
\
Merillif's Flower grows within the camp of Lúlstrok.\
Braiglad's Flower grows behind a house in Waldfast.\
Silloth's Flower grows on the sloping path that climbs up through Brafulug.\
Lenhwest's Flower grows in the camp outside the cave of Fil Sulmog.","The flower glimmers with renewed energy"},
[10868]={"Search Sharkey's Slough for Vagári the Wanderer","'You felt a watchful presence to the west of the Gladden Fields? Why then have you come here, ${PLAYER}? That way may lie the answers we seek!'","'Son-of-no-blood! Son-of-no-blood!'","Talk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden","The Island of the Flowers is quiet and still","You feel a watchful presence from the western side of the Gladden Fields","Defeat shades in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Son-of-no-blood! Son-of-no-blood!'\
\
The shade's voice is cruel and cold. It stares past you with wild eyes, seeming to address someone you cannot see, and you are overwhelmed by a feeling of dread that causes the memory of the Nazgûl to rise unbidden in your mind. But the Nazgûl are gone, destroyed alongside the Dark Lord. Your musings are cut short by an unexpected realization. The shade is weeping.\
\
'I ask for only three things!\\q it cries, its hollow voice thick with despair.\
'I ask for my life!' it pleads.\
'I ask for escape!' the shade begs, tearing at its face with spectral hands.\
\
The ghostly figure suddenly writhes and shakes. Instead of asking its unseen tormentors for a third boon, it seems to be somewhere else in its memory. 'I am sorry, I am sorry!' it cries.","Gandalf believes that the reappearance of Vagári the Wanderer may be related in some way to the darkness that has fallen on the Gladden Fields, and he has sent you to find the mysterious shade.","There is no sign of Vagári among the Orcs","Shades in the Swamp: The Wanderer Sought","The Maiden of the Gladden stands by the rocky path in Gladdenmere, watching you carefully.","You feel a watchful presence to the west","Search atop the cliff path to the north-west for the new presence","There is no sign of Vagári among the half-orcs","'¿Qué te trae a este lugar?'","Search Tûn Melen for Vagári the Wanderer","You felt something watching you from the western side of the Gladden Fields. Could it be the shade you seek?","You felt another watchful presence up the cliff path to the north-west of where you encountered Vagári the Wanderer.","The Maiden stares at you, her face betraying no emotion. At last she speaks, and her voice is like the sound of water falling over and among stones.\
\
'What has brought you to this place?' she asks quietly.","There is no sign of Vagári among the reeds","Search Lúlstrok for Vagári the Wanderer","Habla con la sombra","As you approach the shade, you are overwhelmed by a sensation of dread","'That is enough for now, ${PLAYER}. I will continue to think on it, but I ask you to conduct a search throughout the Gladden Fields for signs of this mysterious presence. If Badwila's account can be trusted, as I think it can, you may find some clues about the shade's motivations at places where the Orcs and half-orcs gather. Search too on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers, and among the mounds of Tûn Melen.\
\
'You are certain to find lesser shades among the fields as you search these places. Whether they are drawn here by the presence of the Wanderer or not, they pose a danger for the warm-blooded folk of the vales and you should defeat them if you can. It is my hope that your search will reveal why Vagári has returned to this place. If we were to learn that, we might learn much else of use to us.'","Defeated shades in the Gladden Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This must be the Maiden of the Gladden of whom the Woodmen spoke","'I ask you to conduct a search throughout the Gladden Fields for signs of this mysterious presence. If Badwila's account can be trusted, as I think it can, you may find some clues about the shade's motivations at places where the Orcs and half-orcs gather. Search too on Tol Send, the Isle of the Flowers, and among the mounds of Tûn Melen.\
\
'You are certain to find lesser shades among the fields as you search these places. Whether they are drawn here by the presence of the Wanderer or not, they pose a danger for the warm-blooded folk of the vales and you should defeat them if you can. It is my hope that your search will reveal why Vagári has returned to this place. If we were to learn that, we might learn much else of use to us.'","Search for Vagári the Wanderer on the western side of the Gladden Fields","You have found a watchful presence that seems to match Badwila's description of Vagári the Wanderer on the western side of the Gladden Fields.","The shade of Vagári the Wanderer begins to fade from view.","The shade of Vagári the Wanderer begins to fade from view","Gandalf has asked you to explore several locations in the Gladden Fields, defeating shades you find, and to search for Vagári the Wanderer.","Search Tol Send for Vagári the Wanderer","Vagári disappears from view, but you feel another presence up the cliff path to the north-west"},
[10869]={"Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús, studying the Black Book of Mordor.","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús","Talk to Elrond outside the Beorninghús","'Whether there be one shade or two at work in the Vales of Anduin, I advise you exercise caution. Whatever may be the truth of it, stories can change over the years; who can say what the original kernel may have been? Vagári the Wanderer may mean no harm to Woodmen or to Beornings, or to those who travel in their lands, but remember that even in the original story, Marhairu Winter-hair was taken from his home for a year, and returned greatly changed.\
\
'I miss my library, ${PLAYER}. If only I had access to my books, I might say more! But this will have to do. Return to Gandalf and tell him this: I know what the Wizard believes Vagári the Wanderer to be, and I caution him that it may not be so. Beware!'","Elrond is outside the Beorninghús.","Gandalf is inside the Beorninghús.","'I believe I chanced upon this very shade during my travels, long ago, and thought it gone, never to return. I will tell you of that encounter, but first I ask that you go outside and speak with Elrond. I would like to know what he thinks of Badwila's story, for he is counted highly among the Wise and I greatly value his opinion and the reach of his knowledge.'","Talk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús and tell him of Badwila's frightening encounter","'This tale you weave is of great interest to me, ${PLAYER}, but I am afraid I can provide little insight that Gandalf does not already possess. Save this, perhaps: shades linger most often in furtherance of an oath they swore in life. For a shade of such hatred to remain in this world may indicate that it served some terrible power. The Enemy is gone, but the things He set in motion may not yet have dissipated.\
\
'Whether there be one shade or two at work in the Vales of Anduin, I advise you exercise caution. Whatever may be the truth of it, stories can change over the years; who can say what the original kernel may have been? Vagári the Wanderer may mean no harm to Woodmen or to Beornings, or to those who travel in their lands, but remember that even in the original story, Marhairu Winter-hair was taken from his home for a year, and returned greatly changed. Ill intent or no, his life was altered by that encounter, and I should judge not for the better.\
\
'I miss my library, ${PLAYER}. If only I had access to my books, I might say more! But this will have to do. Return to Gandalf and tell him this: I know what the Wizard believes Vagári the Wanderer to be, and I caution him that it may not be so. Beware!'","'It was a man, or so it must have been in life. It put me in mind of the tales my people tell of Vagári the Wanderer, the spectre that stalks the vales; do you know the story? It is said he appears in the mist from time to time, but few have seen him with certainty and none have gotten near enough to hear him speak. Marhairu Winter-hair of the Northmen followed Vagári for a time, but he was missing for a year and when he returned he remembered little of the experience.'\
\
Badwila frowns at you and tests his injured leg.\
\
'Nay, it is not just this Orc-wound that troubles me, ${PLAYER}. I said the shade reminded me of the tales of Vagári the Wanderer, and it does, save one difference. As it approached I felt an overwhelming sensation of hatred, not just for the Orcs but for all living things, and it spoke without breath. It slew every Orc, chanting in its terrible voice, and I feared it would slay me as well were it to pay me any heed. But I feigned death and it did not notice me. Had it done so this Orc-wound would be the least of my troubles, and you would have only a corpse to bear back to my father!\
\
'The words it spoke were not addressed to me, nor I think to the Orcs, but as it set about dispatching its foes it muttered these words without breath: \\qson-of-no-blood,\\q it said, \\qson-of-no-blood,\\q over and over. I am chilled to remember it!\
\
'The tales my people tell of Vagári the Wanderer are different. That shade seemed to pose no ill will toward Marhairu Winter-hair, and his account contained no report of such malicious intent or frightening chant. What can it mean, ${PLAYER}? I think my leg is well-enough to carry me home now, but the memory of this encounter will haunt me until the end of my days! Will I become as Marhairu Winter-hair did, scorned by my people? But I know what I saw, and I know it is true!'","Badwila had a frightening experience in the Gladden Fields, and he related to you that something about the shade he encountered seemed different than Marhairu Winter-hair's encounter with Vagári the Wanderer.","'I said the shade reminded me of the tales of Vagári the Wanderer, and it does, save one difference. As it approached I felt an overwhelming sensation of hatred, not just for the Orcs but for all living things, and it spoke without breath. It slew every Orc, chanting in its terrible voice, and I feared it would slay me as well were it to pay me any heed. But I feigned death and it did not notice me. Had it done so this Orc-wound would be the least of my troubles, and you would have only a corpse to bear back to my father!\
\
'The words it spoke were not addressed to me, nor I think to the Orcs, but as it set about dispatching its foes it muttered these words without breath: \\qson-of-no-blood,\\q it said, \\qson-of-no-blood,\\q over and over. I am chilled to remember it!\
\
'The tales my people tell of Vagári the Wanderer are different. That shade seemed to pose no ill will toward Marhairu Winterhair, and his account contained no report of such malicious intent or frightening chant. What can it mean, ${PLAYER}? I think my leg is well-enough to carry me home now, but the memory of this encounter will haunt me until the end of my days! Will I become as Marhairu Winterhair did, scorned by my people? But I know what I saw, and I know it is true!'","'Have you learned more about the darkness that has settled upon the vales, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You recount to Gandalf the tale of Badwila the Hunter and his encounter with the hate-filled shade. Gandalf frowns.\
\
'I cannot tell what you think of this story, ${PLAYER}. Is it your belief or Badwila's that this shade he encountered is the same as that encountered by Marhairu Winter-hair, the spirit called Vagári by the Woodmen? The Gladden Fields have seen much death and tragedy over the years, and the Woodmen have long reported mysterious lights and unsettling voices in the marshes. It would not surprise me to learn that this is a second shade, as filled with rage as the first seemed benign. The aura of hatred that Badwila described reminds me of the dread that accompanied Sauron's most powerful servants: the Nazgûl.\
\
'But Sauron is gone, and the Nazgûl with him. This spectre must be something else, and indeed let us be thankful for that! In point of fact, I believe I chanced upon this very shade during my travels, long ago, and thought it gone, never to return. I will tell you of that encounter, but first I ask that you go outside and speak with Master Elrond. I would like to know what he thinks of Badwila's story, for he is counted highly among the Wise and I greatly value his opinion and the reach of his knowledge.'","Shades in the Swamp: Vágari The Wanderer","'I accept Master Elrond's warning, but it does not dissuade me from wishing to learn more about Vagári the Wanderer, and neither should it discourage you!\
\
'I told you I encountered this shade long ago, and it is true. I walked these lands for many years, watching the trials of Men and Elves and lending my aid whenever I deemed it necessary. It was some time after the Battle of Parth Celebrant and the departure of the Éothéod that I walked by the side of the Anduin, pondering who would now defend the Woodmen against the ravages of the Orcs of the Misty Mountains. Then it was that I saw this very shade.\
\
'I would have let it be, ${PLAYER}, had it not spoken. But it called me by a curious name, a name I had never heard before, and it drew me on. I pursued the shade into the swamp, and even from so great a distance I could feel the intense aura of its hatred. This spirit should not have been, and I knew that in the Éothéod's absence, such a hateful presence would endanger the Woodmen.\
\
'I cast a spell of banishment upon the shade, and it vanished. I believed it had been gone for good, but now it has returned. I know not why.'"},
[10870]={"Has derrotado a muchas sombras en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost.","Sombra derrotada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Las sombras de Perjuros, malditas a permanecer aun tras extinguirse su vida, acechan en los Campos de Fornost. Son mortiferas con su odio hacia todas las cosas que viven y respiran.","Las sombras se encuentran en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost.\
\
Debes derrotar a sombras en los Campos de Fornost.","Sombras de días pasados","Derrota sombras en el oeste de los Campos de Fornost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10872]={"Hadâd-mezer se encuentra al sureste de Anazârmekhem de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Debes derrotar a los orcos en Hadâd-mezer.","Has logrado reducir el número de orcos en Hadâd-mezer, facilitando así la entrada y salida de los enanos de Anazârmekhem.","Sombra sobre la esperanza","Derrota orcos en Hadâd-mezer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los orcos Ghâsh-hai en Hadâd-mezer","Completado","Orco derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Al llegar a Hadâd-mezer, se observa que los orcos controlan firmemente esta zona, lo que dificulta la entrada y la salida.\
\
Las fuerzas orcas son poderosas y su número debe ser reducido.","Al llegar a Hadâd-mezer, se observa que los orcos controlan firmemente esta zona, lo que dificulta la entrada y la salida."},
[10873]={"'Do you think I would allow you to reach High Priestess Ásachal? If we must fight...'","Defeated Lasairë","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should defeat Claghórd in Tûr Fúar.","Defeat Lasairë","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should defeat High Priestess Ásachal in Tûr Fúar.","'Now it is time to secure the powerful artifact the Dourhands speak of.'","Summon Múta to your side.","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Múta in the upper reaches of Tûr Fúar.","Defeated Curcúan","Múta suggests pushing further into the Drearspire, for Brathar Crack-helm has been truthful in his word, thus far.","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Múta in Tûr Fúar.","Talk to Múta in Tûr Fúar","Claghórd beckons you nearer","Defeat High Priestess Ásachal","'Hold a moment, ${PLAYER}. This place is a labyrinth of stairways and halls that seemingly go nowhere! We must scale the tower together! Here is a horn. May you use it if we become separated.\
\
'The Dourhands said that while we should defeat as many cultists as we can, only a certain four would topple their hold in Tûr Fúar. High Priestess Ásachal is the obvious target, as is her second in command, Warlord Claghórd. We are also to target two powerful priestesses, Curcúan and Lasairë. Let us hope that we are able to find all four. For Gundabad!'","'Let us enter the Drearspire and find Ásachal and her devoted followers. There is not a moment to lose.'","Múta rushes to your side!","Talk to Múta inside the entrance of Tûr Fúar","Defeat Claghórd","Claghórd flees the battle","Defeated High Priestess Ásachal","Talk to Múta in the upper reaches of Tûr Fúar","Summon Múta to your side","'We have done it! There is only but one task at hand for us to accomplish. Meet me at the base of the stairs that lead to the very top of the Drearspire.'","The tower is like a vertical labyrinth!","Shadow of the Iron Crown","Summon Claghórd","Enter Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should enter Tûr Fúar.","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should defeat Curcúan and Lasairë in Tûr Fúar.","Defeat Curcúan"},
[10874]={"Grimbriar se encuentra en la casa de piedra, cerca de El Cruce, fuera de Bree.\
\
Las notas del espía confirman bien lo que decía la carta de los bandidos, a saber, que Zarquino no es un bandido, sino un hombre influyente del sur. Sería bueno avisar a Grimbriar.","'Debemos darnos prisa, creo que sospechan algo. ¡Espera! ¿Qué es ese ruido? ¡Cuidado... vienen!'","El espía te ha entregado un manojo de notas","'¿No has podido reunirte con mi informador?'","Reúnete con el espía de Grimbriar","Tu descubrimiento corrobora lo que el espía de Grimbriar le ha estado diciendo. Grimbriar ha organizado un intercambio de documentos importantes.","El espía de Grimbriar te encontrará cerca de una roca gris en un pequeño bosque, al norte de Bree.\
\
Grimbriar te ha enviado a reunirte con un espía que ha infiltrado entre los bandidos con la esperanza de que revele información sobre Zarquino y sus planes.","Lleva las notas del informador a Grimbriar","'Ve a ver a mi espía, tal y como hablamos. Él debería poder darnos más información sobre Zarquino y sus planes para las Tierras de Bree.'","Sombra de la Mano Blanca","'Tengo un espía entre los bandidos que puede sernos de ayuda para averiguar la verdadera naturaleza de este Zarquino. Le enviaré un mensaje indicándole que se reúna en una colina no muy lejos de aquí. Encuéntralo allí y pregúntale por Zarquino y sus planes.\
\
'El lugar de encuentro es una roca gris en un pequeño bosque al norte de Bree.\
\
'Si mi espía no tiene noticias que compartir, tendremos que encontrar otro medio para conocer los planes de Zarquino.'","Habla con el Jefe de vigilancia Grimbriar","'Estas son malas noticias. Supongo que era demasiado esperar que todo resultara ser un sueño de un pequeño lider bandido por convertirse en señor.\
\
'Bueno, no debería culparte por hacer lo que te envié a hacer, aunque es una pena que no hayas vuelto con mejores noticias.\
\
'Creo que sé cuál será nuestro próximo paso en esta acción, pero es una tarea sombría la que te enviaré a realizar.'"},
[10876]={"Talk to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus","Defeat Druggavar in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Druggavar in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I do not know if we can ward off such demons as Druggavar alone... perhaps the Uch-gwirod has sent you to our aid?'","'Druggavar! Our tales tell of the demon goats, but I never thought to actually be haunted by them... you will have our friendship forever if you continue to protect us!'","You have found the evidence Grufudh requires","'You indeed saw Druggavar? This is a fell sign....\
\
'You were able to banish the spirits from our goats? You have our praise, Duvodiad... you are glûs -- holy -- among us.'","The goat-herds graze the land to the west of Gavar Cadlus.\
\
Grufudh asked you to investigate the evil shadows he and his fellow goatherds saw among their herds. They only seem to come at night, but may be found elsewhere during the day.","Druggavar have appeared among the herds of the Uch-lûth, west of Gavar Cadlus.\
\
Grufudh asked you to find a way to banish the Druggavar from their lands.","'I never believed the old tales, but now I must wonder....'","Grufudh is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd.","The Uch-lûth goatherd Grufudh accepted the gift of the Rangers, but he still does not trust you.","'My brother was right! Druggavar out of legend haunt our herd! You must have great power to drive away such demons!'","Shadows of Fear","Search for signs of the Druggavar among the goat-herds","'The gift of your duvodiad friends is welcome, but we are not prone to blindly accept the friendship of strangers. If you wish to earn our trust, you must lend us your aid.\
\
'I and my people have seen evil shadows moving among our herd at night... shadows of goat-shape, but blacker than night and with red eyes like fire. They remind us of the Druggavar, demon-goats of our legends. I had never seen such things in my childhood, and so I never believed... now it seems many things of old tales haunt us.\
\
'Perhaps you may find the truth of the matter among our goats. Our herd is there, to the west of our camp.'","'Perhaps with your help, we will learn not to be afraid of things we do not understand.'"},
[10877]={"'Once again, you have saved our goats, Glûs Duvodiad... we shall praise you always!'","Shadows of Fear -- Repeatable","Iuan is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd.\
\
You should return to Iuan with news of your victory.","Druggavar haunt the lands to the west of Gavar Cadlus.\
\
Iuan has asked you to hunt down and banish the Druggavar of Enedwaith.","'Ah! You are the Glûs Duvodiad! You have proven your power, but the banishment you performed seems only to have been temporary... the Druggavar have returned and threaten our herds!\
\
'Will you go out once more and fend off these evil demons? If you will, I will reward you. Our herds graze there, to the west.'","Impressed by your apparent power over the evil Druggavar of Enedwaith, the Uch-lûth seek your aid once more.","Defeated Druggavar or wolves in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'O Glûs Duvodiad, you come to our aid once more....'","Talk to Iuan at Gavar Cadlus","Defeat Druggavar or wolves in the Windfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10878]={"In years past, the Rangers held many refuges within the lands of North Ithilien from which to combat the Enemy's forces. Now, only Henneth Annûn remains and the rest lie abandoned or in the hands of the Enemy.","'What have you to report, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You inform Mablung of the massive size of the spiders in Thurindath, the relatively untouched state of Adab Dolen, and your suspicion that Orcs have claimed Torngroth.\
\
'I see. I shall send my Rangers to Adab Dolen at once. If we can reclaim one of our northern refuges, it shall aid us greatly in keeping the Enemy from crossing into Ithilien from Dagorlad. However, to have spiders and Orcs lurking within our lost refuges is another matter. The loss of Torngroth was a tremendous blow to our company, and I would see it returned to us.\
\
'We do not have the time to reclaim them now, but I shall have my scouts keep a careful watch on both Torngroth and Thurindath.'","Mablung can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.\
\
You have scouted the abandoned Ranger refuges and should now tell Mablung of what you discovered.","Patrol the abandoned refuge of Thurindath","Talk to Mablung","Patrol the abandoned refuge of Torngroth","Shadows of Ithilien","'For many years, the Rangers held refuges throughout the lands of Ithilien. However, as the Enemy regained his terrible might, we began to lose our footholds one by one... and now only Henneth Annûn remains. Our hidden refuge of Torngroth held long against the Enemy's forces - outlasting both Thurindath and Adab Dolen, but it, too, fell.\
\
'I wonder what has become of them since we were forced to abandon them. With all we have endured in the great battle, can we now hope to reclaim what was lost?\
\
'I would ask that you scout them, my friend. Torngroth can be found along a river-bed far to the north-west, Thurindath to the north, and Adab Dolen along the Mountains of Shadow far to the south-east.\
\
'Go with haste, and tell me what you uncover. The time of the Rangers is not yet ended!'","Patrol the abandoned refuge of Adab Dolen","Spiders have overrun the refuge!","Thurindath can be found far to the south-east of Henneth Annûn, Adab Dolen can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn, and Torngroth can be found far to the north-west of Henneth Annûn.\
\
Mablung has asked you to scout the old Ranger refuges of Thurindath, Adab Dolen, and Torngroth. You should seek them out and take note of what you discover.","You see Orkish trappings within the refuge, and something glints in the dark nearby...","Moss creeps in from the cave's entrance, but someone or something has been here recently..."},
[10880]={"'Thank you for that news. I had feared this day would come. I had hoped you would return with fairer news, but I appreciate your candor.\
\
'Hope is a cruel master, and one that has now abandoned me.\
\
'When I was a girl, my sisters and I would make shapes, shadows on the wall. We would make funny animals: ducks, and rabbits, and chickens. Oh, and the stories we would tell! The adventures those rabbits and ducks had! Such stories. My sisters have since passed, taken each by disease or famine or war. Sometimes I still see those shadows though; dancing, laughing, playing. I can still hear their laughter.\
\
'When my husband would come home, I would first see him by the shadow he cast on the wall by our home. So broad and powerful, that shadow was the harbinger of my precious Eshtali coming home to me. Just like my sisters, I sought comfort in that shadow, always steady, strangely solid.\
\
'After he was taken, I am ashamed to say I forgot what his face looked like, once so familiar to me. All I can see now of him is that shadow on the wall, insubstantial like a wraith, endlessly dancing through my memories.'","Continue searching Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.","Search around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereabouts","Mizâdi has received word from her spies that her missing husband, Eshtali, has been sighted near the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi. Make your way there and look for clues to his whereabouts.","Search the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.","Examine the man to determine if he is Eshtali","Examine the man to determine if he is Eshtali.","Give Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death","You spot something - it looks like a man tossed in the dirt","Shadows on the Wall","Give Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death.","'I have a personal matter with which I would ask your assistance, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I have received word from my spies of a rumour that my husband, Eshtali, has recently been seen outside the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi to the south of here. What he is doing there, I have no idea.\
\
'The leader of the Barkhûshim, that accursed Okhíso, claimed to take him when he drove us all from Kûr Anzar. I thought my precious Eshtali long since dead. I know it is dangerous, ${PLAYER}, but I feel a dagger of hope in my chest.\
\
'You have accomplished much with me here. There is no one I trust more with this mission than you. Please, make your way to Esh-kimâkhi and look for him. You will know him by the crimson robes he always wears. And, ${PLAYER}? If you are to return with my husband, know that you will have given me a gift worth more to me than any victory in this war.'","You search the disturbed ground here, but you find nothing","You have found Eshtali - he is dead","Search three spots around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereabouts"},
[10881]={"'I have a personal matter with which I would ask your assistance, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I have received word from my spies of a rumour that my husband, Eshtali, has recently been seen outside the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi to the south of here. What he is doing there, I have no idea.\
\
'The leader of the Barkhûshim, that accursed Okhíso, claimed to take him when he drove us all from Kûr Anzar. I thought my precious Eshtali long since dead. I know it is dangerous, ${PLAYER}, but I feel a dagger of hope in my chest.\
\
'You have accomplished much with me here. There is no one I trust more with this mission than you. Please, make your way to Esh-kimâkhi and look for him. You will know him by the crimson robes he always wears. I have sent Razâl ahead of you to scout the terrain, speak with him when you arrive.\
\
'And, ${PLAYER}? If you are to return with my husband, know that you will have given me a gift worth more to me than any victory in this war.'","Mizâdi has received word from her spies that her missing husband, Eshtali, has been sighted near the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi. Make your way there and look for clues to his whereabouts.","Continue searching around Esh-kimâkhi - Eshtali may be close","Search the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.","Examine the man to determine if he is Eshtali","Examine the man to determine if he is Eshtali.","You find a fashionable robe, burned and blood-stained","Continue searching the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali.","Shadows on the Wall","You find a ballad detailing the fall of Kûr Anzar to the Barkhûshim","Speak with Razâl at the edge of Esh-kimâkhi","'This is the worst fate we could have feared. With the way now cleared, we will recover Eshtali. We will treat him with the utmost respect. You should let Mizâdi know with all due haste, and bring what you found of Eshtali's. This is grim news indeed, but she will want to hear it, and from your lips.'","You find a piece of chest armour, gouged and warped","Find clues around Esh-kimâkhi as to Eshtali's whereabouts (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Thank you for that news, and for his effects. Hope is a cruel master, and one that has now abandoned me.\
\
'I remember when I was a girl, my sisters and I would make shapes, shadows on the wall. We would make funny animals: ducks, and rabbits, and chickens. Oh, and the stories we would tell! The adventures those rabbits and ducks had! Such stories. Those days have long passed, but when I close my eyes I can still see those shadows; dancing, vaulting, gamboling. I still hear their peals of laughter.\
\
'When my husband came home, I would first see him by the shadow he cast on the wall. So broad and powerful, that shadow was the harbinger of my precious Eshtali coming home to me. Just like my sisters, I sought comfort in that shadow, always steady, strangely solid.\
\
'After he was taken, I am ashamed to say I forgot what his face looked like, once so familiar to me. I can no longer see his face. All I see of him now is that shadow on the wall, insubstantial like a wraith, endlessly dancing through my memories.'","Meet with Razâl, Mizâdi's scout, outside of Esh-kimâkhi. The Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi can be found south-east of Urmâkh.","Meet with Razâl outside of Esh-kimâkhi","Bring Mizâdi in Urmâkh her husband's effects, and news of his death","Give Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death, and what you found of his possessions.","'This is as far as we have been able to advance. The restless dead of Esh-kimâkhi make it impossible for us to scout further.\
\
'You have shown yourself quite capable in a fight. My eyes are keen, but my sword arm is slow. Would you scout further into Esh-kimâkhi and search for signs of Eshtali? I will remain here in case you or Eshtali have need of my aid.'","You spot something - it looks like a man tossed in the dirt","You find a sword and shield, both broken beyond use","Speak with Razâl at the edge of Esh-kimâkhi.","You have found Eshtali - he is dead","A member of the Restless Dead, with fresh sword strikes carved into its bones"},
[10882]={"Sâdikiz says he can repay his debts by selling the glands of rock-worms found at the Pools of Taridím, west of Khanâg Gur, and the Seething-wells in northern An Shêru.","Shadowy Debts","Rock-worm glands collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the rock-worm glands to Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry","Sâdikiz has asked for your help to carry out his plan for a way to pay his debts.","You have collected the rock-worm glands that Sâdikiz requested. You should bring them to him at Khanâg Gur.","'Although my debt is that of coin, I devised a plan to pay it in the form of a valuable substance. However, thanks to an old injury, I find myself unable to collect it. You have helped me already once today, but I wonder if you would be willing to aid the friend of a friend again?\
\
'Here in An Shêru there are hot springs that are home to large rock-worms. These worms have glands that contain a toxin that is valuable for its use in alchemy. If you were able to collect eight of these glands, I could sell them to the right buyer for enough to cover my debt. Would you aid an old, battered dwarf?\
\
'The nearest hot spring where you can find rock-worms is the Pools of Taridím, just to the west of here. There is another hot spring in the north, the Seething-wells, where they can also be found. If you want to help, you should go there to hunt for the beasts.'","'Well, pull my beard, you got them! Thank you, ${PLAYER}, you are truly a life-saver.\
\
'While you were gone, I found myself thinking about the safety of Jiret-menêsh. Since the arrival of these new Orcs, the Ordâkhai seem more determined than ever to make everyone miserable. Tell me, do you know what defences they have in place? What is their plan, should an attack come?'\
\
You tell him that you are not privy to that information.\
\
'Ah, that is too bad then. Thank you all the same.'","Collect rock-worm glands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[10885]={"Secure the eastern and western gate controls","Secured the western gate control","Óli has asked for your assistance in retaking Bagûd-mekhem.","Defeated Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk","Defeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk and secure the Gate of Winds","'Recently there has a been a good deal of activity just North of this position. We have had reports of troops gathering near a little known entrance called Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind. These troops are being led by a goblin war-drummer known as Zhurmat with his fearsome mount: a horrible two-headed troll named Groz-and-Ulk. We fear that if this force pushes southward, it could risk the Gabil'akkâ below.\
\
'As you can see, Zhurmat and his growing forces are locked beyond the gate directly to our north. The controls for this gate are located on the eastern and western sections of this encampment. The western controls are defended by the set of Orc twins while the eastern controls are guarded by a fearsome frost-caller.'","Zhurmat and his fearsome mount - the horrible two-headed troll Groz-and-Ulk - have begun to amass forces for use against the Gabil'akkâ in the valley below. Óli has asked for your assistance in routing the forces outside Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind.","Defeat Azbauz and Maugrush","Secured the eastern gate control","Defeat Shatarkha","Shakalush, the Stair Battle -- Solo/Duo","Speak with Óli","Defeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk"},
[10886]={"Secure the eastern and western gate controls","Óli has asked for your assistance in retaking Bagûd-mekhem.","Defeated Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk","Defeat Zhurmat and Groz-and-Ulk to secure the Gate of Winds","'Recently there has a been a good deal of activity just North of this position. We have had reports of troops gathering near a little known entrance called Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind. These troops are being led by a goblin war-drummer known as Zhurmat with his fearsome mount: a horrible two-headed troll named Groz-and-Ulk. We fear that if this force pushes southward, it could risk the Gabil'akkâ below.\
